window.FWN_DIMENSIONAL_KEEPER_ALL_MY_SKILLS_ARE_AT_LEVEL_100_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_DIMENSIONAL_KEEPER_ALL_MY_SKILLS_ARE_AT_LEVEL_100_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":1701,"title":"Chapter 1701: Combat Hall!","paragraphs":["After realizing just how poor he truly was within Starfall Haven, Max finally understood that his one hundred and ten thousand Killing Points were practically nothing in the grand scheme of the Cosmic Ascension Conference.","Earlier, he had felt somewhat satisfied after seeing his Killing Points surpass one hundred thousand. After all, he had slaughtered countless participants, farmed multiple lives from demons, destroyed an entire battlefield region, and even discovered a hidden cave filled with those terrifying rainbow rabbits.","Yet after entering Starfall Haven and looking at the prices of the Divine Abilities, that confidence had completely vanished. The cheapest Tier I Divine Ability alone required ten million Killing Points.","Compared to that astronomical figure, his one hundred and ten thousand points seemed almost laughable. For the first time since entering the Eternal Hourglass, Max genuinely felt poor.","After leaving the Divine Ability Pavilion, Max began wandering throughout Starfall Haven while carefully observing the city around him. The city was far more prosperous than he had initially imagined.","Vast marketplaces stretched endlessly throughout the streets while enormous buildings rose high into the sky. Some areas were dedicated entirely to entertainment, containing restaurants, taverns, gathering halls, and various attractions where participants could temporarily relax from the constant slaughter taking place outside the city walls.","Other districts contained endless rows of shops selling treasures, cultivation resources, weapons, armor, pills, maps, inheritances, and information. Everywhere he looked, people were buying, selling, negotiating, and exchanging resources.","The city almost felt like a real civilization existing independently within the Eternal Hourglass rather than a temporary gathering point for participants in a cosmic battle royale.","However, Max was not interested in spending Killing Points.","He was interested in earning them.","As he walked through one district after another, he continuously searched for possible opportunities to increase his wealth. Unfortunately, despite the countless shops and facilities available, none of them provided the answer he was looking for.","Eventually, after spending quite some time searching, Max stopped a random human participant walking nearby and directly asked. \"Do you know the fastest way to earn Killing Points inside Starfall Haven?\"","The man immediately laughed after hearing the question, as though Max had asked something extremely obvious.","\"If you want to earn Killing Points, then there is only one place you should visit,\" the man said while pointing toward a distant part of the city. \"The Combat Hall. Most people who stay in Starfall Haven for any significant amount of time eventually end up there. Some become rich overnight while others lose everything they possess. If you have confidence in your abilities, then there is no better place in the entire city.\"","The moment Max heard those words, his interest was instantly captured.","After obtaining directions from the man, he immediately headed toward the Combat Hall. The farther he traveled through the city, the more crowded the streets became. Participants filled every visible road while excitement permeated the atmosphere.","Before long, a gigantic structure gradually appeared in the distance. The building towered high above the surrounding city like an ancient colosseum, its massive walls stretching endlessly while countless golden runes shimmered across its surface.","Above the entrance floated two enormous words formed entirely from golden light.","Combat Hall.","Yet despite the sheer size of the structure itself, what truly shocked Max was not the building.","It was the crowd.","The moment he arrived before the Combat Hall, even Max could not help but stop briefly.","People.","Everywhere he looked there were people.","The area surrounding the Combat Hall was so crowded that it resembled a sea of living beings. Hundreds of thousands of participants had gathered around the building, creating a scene unlike anything Max had witnessed since entering the Eternal Hourglass.","Humans occupied large portions of the crowd, but they were far from the only race present. Demons with dark skin and horns continuously moved through the masses while elegant elves could occasionally be seen among them as well.","The atmosphere buzzed with endless conversations, arguments, cheers, and excitement. Some participants appeared thrilled while others looked devastated. Many walked out smiling broadly while clutching newly acquired treasures. Others stumbled out looking as though they had just lost everything they owned.","The entire place felt alive.","The noise alone was overwhelming.","Cheers erupted constantly from within the Combat Hall. Heated discussions filled the surrounding streets. Participants continuously rushed inside while others hurried out to spread news regarding recent matches and results.","Looking at the enormous crowd gathered around the building, Max immediately understood why the man had directed him here.","If there truly existed a place within Starfall Haven where Killing Points changed hands in massive quantities, then it was undoubtedly this Combat Hall. Just from the sheer number of people gathered here, Max could tell that enormous fortunes were being won and lost every single moment.","A faint smile slowly appeared across his face.","It seemed that his journey toward earning the remaining three hundred and ninety thousand Killing Points required for the Genesis Trial might begin here.","After spending some time asking around and gathering information from the participants present inside the Combat Hall, Max gradually came to understand why this place had become the most crowded location in all of Starfall Haven.","The deeper he looked into the rules governing the Combat Hall, the more he realized that the place had been specifically designed to tempt participants into risking everything they possessed.","It was no wonder that such an overwhelming number of people had gathered here despite the dangers involved.","The rules themselves were surprisingly simple. Any participant could register and begin a challenge sequence. Once the challenge started, they would face one opponent after another in consecutive battles.","Every victory would reward them with Killing Points obtained from defeating their opponent, allowing their earnings to steadily increase as they continued winning. However, the true attraction of the Combat Hall was not these ordinary rewards.","The true attraction was the massive bonus granted to anyone capable of achieving ten consecutive victories.","If a participant successfully defeated ten opponents in a row without suffering a single defeat, they would immediately receive a reward of one million Killing Points on top of all the Killing Points they had already accumulated from those ten battles.","One million Killing Points.","Even Max could not help but feel his heart shake slightly after hearing that number."]},{"number":1702,"title":"Chapter 1702: Rules of the Combat Hall!","paragraphs":["Earlier, he had gone through considerable effort to gather just over one hundred thousand Killing Points. He had slaughtered countless participants, repeatedly farmed lives from demons, and wiped out an entire battlefield region.","Yet all of that combined was only a fraction of what the Combat Hall offered for ten consecutive victories. Suddenly, the prices inside the Divine Ability Pavilion no longer seemed completely impossible.","If someone possessed enough strength and enough luck, they could theoretically earn tremendous amounts of Killing Points within a relatively short period of time.","However, as Max continued listening, he soon discovered why the rewards were so generous.","There was a catch.","A very dangerous catch.","The Combat Hall was not a place where participants could safely accumulate rewards over time. Instead, it was a place where fortunes could change hands in an instant.","Every Killing Point earned during a challenge sequence remained at risk until the participant either completed all ten victories or voluntarily withdrew.","If someone lost before reaching ten victories, then all the Killing Points they had accumulated throughout their challenge would immediately transfer to the person who defeated them.","In other words, a participant could spend hours fighting their way through multiple opponents, accumulate a large amount of Killing Points, and then lose everything in a single battle.","The winner would take it all.","Because of this rule, every match became increasingly valuable as a participant’s winning streak grew longer. Someone who had already won seven or eight consecutive battles would often become a walking treasure chest worth hundreds of thousands of Killing Points.","The stronger they became and the closer they moved toward the one-million-point reward, the more attractive they became as targets for other participants hoping to claim everything they had earned.","As Max listened to the explanations and watched the excited crowds surrounding the various arenas, he finally understood why the Combat Hall had become so popular. The system was incredibly risky, yet at the same time it was impossible to ignore.","The possibility of earning one million Killing Points from a single challenge was enough to attract countless geniuses. Every participant believed they could be the next person to achieve ten consecutive victories. Every participant believed they possessed the strength to succeed where others had failed.","Naturally, that confidence continuously drove people into the arenas despite knowing the risks involved.","The Combat Hall had essentially transformed combat itself into a form of gambling. Participants wagered their strength, their confidence, and their accumulated Killing Points every time they entered an arena.","Some emerged richer than ever before. Others lost everything they had spent hours or even days earning. Yet despite those dangers, the crowds only continued growing larger. The promise of rapid wealth and glory was simply too tempting for most participants to resist.","Standing amidst the sea of people, Max slowly looked toward the enormous battle arenas located at the center of the Combat Hall. As countless participants cheered, fought, and challenged one another around him, a faint smile gradually appeared on his face.","Compared to wandering the Eternal Hourglass searching for opportunities one by one, this place seemed far more efficient.","If the rewards truly matched what he had heard, then perhaps the Combat Hall would become the fastest path toward accumulating the five hundred thousand Killing Points he needed for the Genesis Trial.","With very high expectations, Max made his way through the bustling crowds toward the registration area of the Combat Hall. The place was even busier than the rest of the building.","Thousands of participants continuously moved back and forth while enormous crystal screens displayed rankings, active challengers, ongoing battles, and the amounts of Killing Points currently at stake.","Excited cheers erupted from nearby arenas every few moments while countless spectators discussed the strengths and weaknesses of different fighters. The entire atmosphere felt charged with anticipation and greed. Here, fortunes could be won in a matter of minutes, and everyone wanted a piece of it.","Eventually, Max arrived before a long registration counter. However, what caught his attention was not the counter itself but the creature sitting behind it.","It was a strange animal unlike anything Max had ever seen before.","The creature resembled a fox and a rabbit combined together. It possessed silver fur, long ears, bright golden eyes, and a fluffy tail that lazily swayed behind it. It sat atop a floating chair while casually reading through countless glowing screens hovering before it.","Despite its small appearance, Max could sense a strange pressure coming from the creature, making it clear that it was far from ordinary.","The moment Max approached the counter, the strange animal did not even look up.","Instead, it lazily spoke.","\"Name.\"","Max raised an eyebrow slightly before replying.","\"Max Morgan.\"","The creature’s ears twitched.","Immediately, several glowing runes appeared before it as though searching through some enormous database.","A few moments later, the strange animal finally looked up.","Its golden eyes briefly examined Max from head to toe.","Then it nodded.","\"Registration successful.\"","Several glowing symbols appeared before Max before quickly disappearing.","The creature continued speaking in a calm and practiced tone.","\"You are now officially registered within the Combat Hall. As a registered participant, you have two options available to you.\"","Max listened attentively.","The strange animal flicked its tail before continuing.","\"The first option is to challenge an active participant currently undergoing the Ten Consecutive Victory Trial. If you defeat them, you immediately inherit all the Killing Points they have accumulated during their current challenge sequence.\"","At those words, Max’s eyes immediately brightened.","That sounded very profitable.","The creature continued.","\"The second option is to begin your own Ten Consecutive Victory Trial. In that case, you will be placed into the queue and wait for your turn. Once selected, you will begin fighting consecutive opponents. Every victory increases your accumulated rewards. Successfully reaching ten consecutive victories grants you the one million Killing Point bonus.\"","The creature then leaned back in its floating chair.","\"Both methods have advantages and disadvantages. Challenging active participants can be extremely rewarding if you target someone with a large accumulated pool of Killing Points. However, such opponents are usually very strong. Starting your own trial is safer, but it requires winning ten consecutive battles.\"","The strange animal then looked directly at Max.","\"So, Max Morgan.\"","Its golden eyes flashed slightly.","\"Would you like to challenge someone currently fighting, or would you like to enter the queue and begin your own Ten Consecutive Victory Trial?\""]},{"number":1703,"title":"Chapter 1703: Ten Consecutive Victory Trial","paragraphs":["Max did not immediately make a decision after hearing the explanation. Instead, he fell into thought for a few moments while weighing the advantages and disadvantages of both options.","Challenging an active participant certainly sounded tempting. If he chose the right target, he could potentially obtain a large amount of Killing Points from a single victory. However, there was also no guarantee that the participant he challenged would have accumulated enough Killing Points to make the risk worthwhile.","On the other hand, the Ten Consecutive Victory Trial offered a guaranteed reward of one million Killing Points if he could successfully clear all ten battles. Considering that he still needed hundreds of thousands of Killing Points before he could even enter the Genesis Trial, the latter option seemed significantly more attractive.","After thinking for a moment, Max looked at the strange animal and asked, \"Suppose I choose the Ten Consecutive Victory Trial. Would I still retain the right to challenge someone currently undergoing their own challenge sequence if I find a suitable target?\"","The strange animal immediately shook its head.","\"No.\"","Its answer was direct and decisive.","\"The Combat Hall does not permit participants to mix the two paths. Once you choose the Ten Consecutive Victory Trial, you remain bound to that challenge until it concludes through either victory, defeat, or voluntary withdrawal. During that period, you are not permitted to challenge active participants. Similarly, those who choose to hunt active challengers cannot simultaneously register for a Ten Consecutive Victory Trial.\"","The creature flicked its tail lazily before continuing, \"The rules were created specifically to prevent participants from abusing both systems simultaneously. Every participant must choose a single path. Either become a challenger who hunts successful fighters or become a contender seeking the one million Killing Point reward.\"","Max slowly nodded after hearing the explanation.","The rule actually made sense.","Otherwise, powerful participants would simply farm weaker challengers while also pursuing the Ten Consecutive Victory Trial at the same time, making the entire system unfair.","After understanding the restrictions, Max no longer hesitated.","A faint smile gradually appeared across his face.","\"I choose the Ten Consecutive Victory Trial.\"","The moment he said those words, the strange animal immediately nodded as though expecting that answer.","After all, most ambitious participants eventually made the same choice.","The creature quickly manipulated several glowing screens floating before it before a golden rune suddenly appeared in front of Max.","\"Registration confirmed.\"","The rune slowly merged into Max’s body.","\"You have successfully entered the queue for the Ten Consecutive Victory Trial. Please wait for your arena assignment.\"","The strange animal glanced at him briefly before adding, \"A piece of advice. The opponents selected for the Ten Consecutive Victory Trial are the ones who chose to challenge the others who have chosen to undergo ten consecutive victory trials like you. So, don’t be surprised if someone way stronger than you challenge you. They are all here to make sure you lose so that they can get the Killing Points you made so far for themselves.\"","Max merely smiled.","One million Killing Points.","That was his target.","Compared to the astronomical prices within the Divine Ability Pavilion and the five hundred thousand Killing Points required for the Genesis Trial, the reward offered by the Combat Hall was simply too good to ignore.","As the golden rune settled completely into his body, Max left the registration counter and made his way toward the waiting area designated for participants who had chosen the Ten Consecutive Victory Trial.","The area itself was enormous, large enough to accommodate thousands of challengers at once. Participants from every major race could be seen gathered there. Humans occupied a considerable portion of the crowd while demons and elves were equally common sights.","Everyone present shared the same goal. They all wished to conquer the Ten Consecutive Victory Trial and claim the coveted reward of one million Killing Points.","Because of that, the atmosphere throughout the waiting area felt tense and competitive, as though every person present was silently measuring the strength of everyone around them.","The moment Max arrived, numerous gazes immediately landed upon him. His appearance was recognizable enough that many people identified him almost instantly. Countless participants had heard stories about the genius from the Black Dragon Clan who had taken away the sword of the Sword Sovereign.","\"It’s that human who became famous recently.\"","\"Yeah, I heard he had the sword of the Sword Sovereign in his hands.\"","\"So what? He is still to weak to pose a threat to us elves. I people of his race wouldn’t take him seriously here.\"","For a brief moment, whispers spread through portions of the waiting area as people pointed him out to one another. However, that attention did not last long. The moment they sensed his cultivation at the peak of the Law Awakening Realm, many expressions changed subtly. Some looked disappointed while others openly displayed disdain.","To them, fame was one thing and strength was another. No matter how impressive Max’s achievements sounded, the reality was that his cultivation appeared significantly lower than many of the geniuses gathered here.","The majority of participants present possessed cultivation levels at the peak of Law Refinement Realm, while some even emitted a pressure that suggested they were among the strongest younger generation experts of their respective races.","Compared to them, Max’s cultivation simply did not appear threatening enough to deserve serious consideration.","Max naturally noticed those reactions but paid them no attention whatsoever. He had experienced similar situations countless times throughout his cultivation journey. People constantly underestimated him based on his cultivation level, only to regret it later.","As such, he simply ignored the surrounding gazes and quietly stood among the crowd while observing the battles occurring throughout the Combat Hall. In front of him stood ten gigantic arenas arranged in a circular formation around the center of the hall.","Each arena was protected by powerful barriers that prevented the destruction from spilling outward. The sounds of explosions, cheering crowds, clashing weapons, and battle cries continuously echoed throughout the hall as one fierce battle after another unfolded."]},{"number":1704,"title":"Chapter 1704: Conspiracy of the Starfall Haven!","paragraphs":["At the moment, all ten arenas were occupied. Some battles had only just begun while others appeared to be approaching their conclusions. Every participant present watched the ongoing fights closely, either studying potential future opponents or simply entertaining themselves while waiting for their own turn.","Max himself became somewhat interested as he watched. The quality of the combat here was noticeably higher than what he had seen in the battlefield regions outside.","The participants entering the Ten Consecutive Victory Trial all possessed considerable confidence in their own strength. Because of that, even the weaker battles displayed techniques and abilities that would have easily dominated ordinary geniuses.","It was while Max was observing one of the arenas that a voice suddenly called out from behind him.","\"You are Max, right?\"","Max turned around calmly and found a young human approaching him. The young man wore dark golden robes embroidered with symbols of war and carried a spear on his back. Unlike many of the others present, his expression did not contain the slightest trace of disdain.","\"I am Max,\" Max replied calmly. \"And who might you be?\"","The young man immediately smiled politely before cupping his fists.","\"Please pardon my abrupt approach. My name is Nick and I come from the War God Palace.\"","The moment Max heard those words, a smile appeared on his face.","\"Oh? The War God Palace?\"","His impression of the War God Palace was naturally quite positive. Ever since obtaining Saint Reiner’s Saint Token, his status within the War God Palace had become extremely special.","Although he was not an official disciple of the organization, many members treated him with considerable respect because of his connection to one of their Saints.","Nick nodded immediately.","\"Yes.\"","Max’s smile widened slightly.","\"No wonder you are being so polite.\"","Nick laughed awkwardly at those words before glancing toward the arenas.","\"Are you also here to participate in the Ten Consecutive Victory Trial?\"","\"That is the plan,\" Max replied honestly.","The moment those words left his mouth, Nick’s expression immediately changed.","Max noticed it instantly.","The young man seemed hesitant.","Concerned.","Almost as though he wanted to say something but was uncertain whether he should.","Seeing this, Max frowned slightly.","\"What is it?\"","Nick looked around cautiously.","His gaze swept across the nearby participants, particularly several demons and elves standing not far away. After confirming that many of them were paying attention to the conversation, his expression became even more serious.","Then, without another word, he switched to Divine Essence Transmission.","His voice sounded directly within Max’s mind.","\"There is a very deep conspiracy unfolding within this city.\"","The sudden statement immediately caught Max’s attention.","The casual expression on his face disappeared.","At the same time, he finally understood why Nick had suddenly become so cautious.","If the matter involved a conspiracy significant enough to warrant secrecy even inside Starfall Haven, then it was clearly not something ordinary.","Max remained outwardly calm, but his interest was thoroughly piqued.","Using Divine Essence Transmission as well, he replied, \"A conspiracy?\"","Nick nodded subtly.","His expression had become extremely solemn now.","\"What conspiracy?\"","The moment Max asked that question, Nick’s eyes darkened noticeably, as though merely thinking about the matter was enough to make him uncomfortable.","He remained silent for several moments after hearing Max’s question. His eyes carefully swept across the surroundings once more before he finally continued speaking through Divine Essence Transmission. Judging by his cautious behavior, it was clear that he did not wish for anyone nearby to overhear even a fragment of what he was about to say.","\"The conspiracy involves two demons,\" Nick transmitted. \"And they are not ordinary demons.\"","Max immediately became more attentive.","Nick continued, \"Their names are Karo and Munro. Both of them come from one of the strongest first-rate demon forces in the Divine Realm. Their father is a Star Lord.\"","At those words, Max’s eyes narrowed slightly.","He naturally knew what a Star Lord represented.","The Divine Realm was divided into countless star realms, each possessing their own rulers and dominant powers. Those capable of ruling an entire star realm stood at the very pinnacle of existence within that region. Such individuals possessed overwhelming strength, unimaginable influence, and resources beyond the comprehension of ordinary cultivators.","A Star Lord was not simply a title.","It was a symbol of supreme authority.","Nick’s expression grew increasingly grim as he continued.","\"Karo and Munro are the sons of that Star Lord. Since entering the Eternal Hourglass, the two of them have been working together. Karo practically lives inside the Combat Hall. He has become infamous among the human participants.\"","Max remained silent while listening.","Nick continued transmitting, \"The way he operates is extremely simple. He does not participate in the Ten Consecutive Victory Trial himself. Instead, he waits. Whenever a human participant reaches eight or nine consecutive victories and is on the verge of obtaining the one-million-Killing-Point reward, Karo immediately challenges them.\"","A cold light appeared within Nick’s eyes.","\"And then he defeats them.\"","Max immediately understood where this was going.","Nick clenched his fists.","\"Every single time.\"","The frustration in his voice was impossible to hide.","\"He defeats them, steals all the Killing Points they accumulated throughout their challenge sequence, and destroys their chance of obtaining the one-million-point reward. He has repeated this process so many times that many human participants have completely lost hope.\"","Max frowned.","Nick’s expression became even uglier.","\"So far, not a single human has successfully completed the Ten Consecutive Victory Trial within Starfall Haven.\"","The atmosphere around them suddenly felt much heavier.","Max could immediately understand why Nick had referred to it as a conspiracy.","This was not simply bullying.","This was systematic suppression.","Karo was intentionally targeting humans while allowing members of other races to proceed normally.","The result was that human participants continuously lost Killing Points while the demons became increasingly wealthy.","For a few moments, Max remained completely silent.","Then he finally asked a question.","\"If things are really as bad as you say, then why do humans continue staying in Starfall Haven?\"","Nick blinked.","Max continued calmly, \"The main attraction of this city is the Combat Hall. If humans cannot even enjoy the greatest opportunity available here, why not simply leave? The Eternal Hourglass is enormous. There are countless other places where Killing Points can be earned.\""]},{"number":1705,"title":"Chapter 1705: Elf Race’s Stance!","paragraphs":["The moment those words entered Nick’s ears, a bitter smile appeared on his face.","\"I thought exactly the same thing when I first arrived here,\" Nick transmitted through Divine Essence. \"And so did many other humans. Unfortunately, that is where the real conspiracy begins.\"","Max’s expression immediately became more serious.","Nick glanced around once more before continuing.","\"Humans did leave Starfall Haven.\"","His voice gradually became colder.","\"At least, they tried to.\"","Max immediately sensed that something was wrong.","Nick continued, \"Most participants are unaware of it when they first arrive, but Starfall Haven has a very peculiar layout. There are numerous ways to enter the city. Participants can arrive from countless different regions throughout the Eternal Hourglass and enter through various gates and pathways. However, there is only one official exit.\"","Max frowned slightly.","Only one exit?","Nick nodded.","\"And that single exit is precisely where the second part of the conspiracy takes place.\"","The atmosphere around them suddenly became much heavier.","Nick’s expression darkened considerably as he continued speaking.","\"Munro.\"","The name alone seemed to carry immense pressure.","\"While Karo remains inside Starfall Haven suppressing human participants within the Combat Hall, Munro stations himself outside the city’s only exit.\"","Max’s eyes narrowed immediately.","At that moment, he already had a rough idea of what came next.","Nick clenched his fists.","\"Whenever a human leaves Starfall Haven carrying a large amount of Killing Points, Munro intercepts them.\"","His voice carried obvious anger.","\"And then he kills them.\"","A cold silence followed.","Meanwhile, battles continued raging within the nearby arenas while countless participants cheered and shouted, completely unaware of the conversation taking place between Max and Nick.","Nick continued, \"At first, people believed it was a coincidence. Then they thought Munro was merely targeting certain individuals. However, after enough incidents occurred, the pattern became impossible to ignore.\"","His eyes gradually turned colder.","\"He specifically targets humans.\"","Max remained silent.","Nick continued, \"Those who lose in the Combat Hall eventually try their luck elsewhere. Those who accumulate Killing Points and wish to leave the city are forced to pass through the exit. And the moment they do, Munro takes everything.\"","A bitter laugh escaped Nick.","\"Karo farms the humans inside Starfall Haven.\"","\"Munro farms the humans outside Starfall Haven.\"","Max finally understood.","This was far more sinister than he initially imagined.","The two demon brothers had effectively transformed the entire city into a gigantic harvesting ground.","Humans entered the city hoping to earn opportunities.","Inside the Combat Hall, Karo robbed them of their rewards.","If they chose to leave instead, Munro robbed them outside the city.","No matter which path they took, the result remained the same.","The Killing Points eventually flowed into the hands of the two demon brothers.","Nick slowly exhaled before continuing.","\"Because of this, many humans now refer to Starfall Haven as a cage.\"","His eyes slowly swept across the countless human participants gathered throughout the Combat Hall.","\"A beautiful cage. Most people trapped inside do not even realize they are being farmed.\"","Max’s gaze gradually turned colder.","The more he learned about the situation, the more absurd it sounded.","A city created to provide opportunities had effectively become a trap specifically targeting human participants.","Meanwhile, Nick looked directly at Max.","\"The worst part is that nobody can stop them. Karo and Munro are already terrifying individually. Together, they are even worse.\"","A faint look of helplessness appeared on his face.","\"Many talented humans have challenged them. Every single one failed.\"","Then Nick paused briefly before adding one final sentence.","\"And because they are the sons of a Star Lord, most people do not dare provoke them even if they survive.\"","At that moment, Max finally understood why the humans within Starfall Haven looked so frustrated despite having access to one of the greatest opportunities in the Eternal Hourglass.","They were trapped.","And the ones holding the key to the cage were two demon princes named Karo and Munro.","Max remained silent for several moments after hearing Nick’s explanation. His eyes slowly swept across the enormous Combat Hall where countless participants continued cheering, fighting, and gambling away their fortunes without realizing that a far larger game was being played behind the scenes.","After pondering for a moment, Max suddenly thought of another matter.","Since the demons were targeting humans so aggressively, there was still one major race whose position remained unclear.","Turning back toward Nick, Max asked through Divine Essence Transmission, \"What about the elves? If the demons are doing this so openly, then surely the elves are affected as well?\"","Nick immediately shook his head.","\"The elves are different.\"","His expression became somewhat complicated.","\"There seems to be an unspoken understanding between the elves and demons. I would not call them allies because they do not openly cooperate with one another, but they certainly do not interfere with each other’s affairs either.\"","His gaze briefly shifted toward a group of elves standing near one of the arenas.","Several of them were calmly observing a battle while completely ignoring everything happening around them.","Nick continued, \"As far as we can tell, the demons rarely target elves, and the elves rarely provoke the demons. Both sides generally maintain a neutral stance toward one another.\"","A bitter smile appeared on his face afterward.","\"As for what happens to us humans...\"","He paused briefly.","\"The elves simply do not care.\"","His voice contained obvious dissatisfaction.","\"Whether Karo robs another human inside the Combat Hall or whether Munro kills another human outside the city makes no difference to them. As long as the situation does not affect their own interests, they pretend not to see it.\"","Nick’s eyes gradually darkened.","\"Many human participants originally hoped the elves might oppose the demons since allowing Karo and Munro to grow stronger benefits nobody except the demon race. However, those hopes quickly disappeared.\"","He looked directly at Max.","\"The elves remain completely indifferent.\"","\"Humans lose Killing Points.\"","\"Humans get hunted.\"","\"Humans get trapped inside Starfall Haven.\"","\"They simply watch from the sidelines.\"","A cold light flashed through Max’s eyes as he listened.","Meanwhile, Nick continued, \"In fact, some people suspect that the elves actually prefer the current situation. The demons suppress the humans while the elves remain untouched. Both races continue accumulating resources while the humans become weaker and weaker.\"","He then shook his head.","\"Of course, that is only speculation. Nobody has any proof.\"","The sounds of cheering suddenly erupted from a nearby arena as another participant was defeated, causing the surrounding crowd to roar with excitement.","Yet despite the noisy atmosphere surrounding them, the conversation between Max and Nick only became heavier.","At that moment, Max’s gaze slowly shifted toward the various elves scattered throughout the Combat Hall.","His expression remained calm.","However, deep within his eyes, a dangerous light briefly flashed before disappearing once again."]},{"number":1706,"title":"Chapter 1706: Nick’s Trust!","paragraphs":["After hearing everything regarding Karo, Munro, and the situation of the humans within Starfall Haven, Max remained silent for quite some time. His eyes slowly swept across the enormous Combat Hall where countless battles continued unfolding every moment.","The cheering crowds, the excited participants, and the seemingly peaceful atmosphere all appeared normal on the surface. Yet now that he knew the truth, Max could clearly see the invisible chains binding the human participants.","Whether they stayed within the city or attempted to leave it, they ultimately became prey for the two demon princes.","Eventually, a faint smile appeared across Max’s face.","Through Divine Essence Transmission, he calmly said, \"I understand the situation now. Since that is the case, I will take care of the problem here in Starfall Haven myself.\"","The moment those words entered his ears, Nick’s eyes widened slightly.","He instinctively looked toward Max. For a brief moment, he wondered whether Max truly understood what he was saying.","The opponents in question were not ordinary geniuses. They were the sons of a Star Lord. Even he, a disciple of the War God Palace, couldn’t defeat them.","Among the countless monstrous talents participating in the Cosmic Ascension Conference, Karo and Munro stood near the very top.","Yet despite that, Max’s expression remained completely calm, as though he had merely decided to handle a minor inconvenience.","Nick did not respond immediately.","Instead, he quietly observed Max.","To outsiders, Max’s cultivation at the peak of Law Awakening Realm appeared insignificant compared to the countless peak Law Refinement Realm geniuses gathered within the Combat Hall.","Normally, Nick would never place his hopes on someone with such a cultivation level.","However, Max was different.","Over the past few months, countless stories had circulated throughout portions of the War God Palace regarding the young man standing before him.","Nick personally knew several disciples who had entered the secret domain of Orion alongside Max.","When those disciples returned, they had spoken about him repeatedly.","Some claimed Max possessed combat strength completely detached from his cultivation realm.","Others described impossible battles where Max defeated opponents that should have crushed him easily.","There were even people who claimed that every time Max appeared cornered, he somehow revealed another terrifying trump card that shocked everyone around him.","The more he learned about Max, the more he felt that ordinary logic simply did not apply to him.","And because of that—","He trusted Max should be able to take care of the situation if he said he could do it.","Soon, time gradually passed within the Combat Hall as one participant after another was called from the waiting area where Max stood toward one of the ten massive arenas spread throughout the enormous structure to participate in the ten consecutive victory trial.","This caused the atmosphere to become increasingly lively and intense with every passing minute as countless spectators watched the battles unfold while discussing the strengths and weaknesses of the various challengers, placing bets, exchanging information, and evaluating which participants might have a chance of completing the Ten Consecutive Victory Trial.","Some challengers managed to win their first few battles and returned to the waiting area with renewed confidence, while others suffered immediate defeats and left with bitter expressions after losing everything they had accumulated so far.","Throughout all of this, Max remained calm and patient, silently observing everything around him while occasionally shifting his attention from one arena to another as he studied the participants present within the Combat Hall.","It was during this period of observation that Max finally noticed something unusual. At first, he did not immediately identify Karo because he had never seen him before. However, after watching several battles and paying close attention to the reactions of the crowd, he gradually began to notice a recurring pattern that appeared again and again.","Whenever a human participant managed to reach their eighth or ninth consecutive victory and stood on the verge of obtaining the one-million-Killing-Point reward, a particular demon would suddenly appear and challenge them.","The result of those battles never changed. Every single human who faced that demon ultimately lost, regardless of how strong they had appeared beforehand, and the accumulated Killing Points they had worked so hard to obtain would immediately fall into the hands of that same individual.","Eventually, Max’s attention settled entirely on the demon responsible for those challenges.","That demon was Karo.","The moment Max finally focused on him properly, he immediately understood why Karo had become such a feared figure among the human participants.","The demon’s appearance alone was enough to intimidate most people. He stood nearly three meters tall with a body that looked as though it had been forged from dark crimson metal rather than flesh and blood.","His shoulders were broad enough to make even many demons appear small in comparison, while his arms were covered in dense muscles that radiated explosive strength.","Unlike ordinary demons whose skin was usually black, Karo’s skin possessed a deep crimson color that seemed to glow faintly under the lights of the Combat Hall.","Two enormous golden horns curved backward from his forehead, and strange runes continuously moved across their surfaces like living creatures. His golden eyes were perhaps the most striking feature of all. They contained neither excitement nor anger.","Instead, they held only indifference, as though everyone around him existed on a completely different level from himself.","Strapped across his back was a gigantic black greatsword whose size alone made it appear more like a siege weapon than a personal armament. The sword was almost as tall as Karo himself, yet he carried it effortlessly, casually resting one hand upon its hilt whenever he walked.","Even from a distance, Max could feel a powerful aura radiating from both the demon and the weapon he carried.","However, what truly drew Max’s attention was not Karo’s appearance.","It was the way everyone reacted to him.","Whenever Karo stood up from his seat and began walking toward one of the arenas, the atmosphere throughout the Combat Hall changed instantly. The demon spectators would smile and laugh while openly discussing how many Killing Points Karo was about to acquire.","Meanwhile, the expressions of the human participants would immediately darken. Excitement disappeared. Hope vanished. Many people would lower their heads while others clenched their fists in frustration. It was almost as though they had already accepted the outcome before the battle even began.","Max soon witnessed this phenomenon personally."]},{"number":1707,"title":"Chapter 1707: Max’s Turn!","paragraphs":["One human swordsman fought through nine consecutive battles and finally achieved his ninth victory. The moment he won, loud cheers erupted from the human spectators throughout the Combat Hall because everyone knew he was only one battle away from obtaining the one-million-Killing-Point reward.","Even the swordsman himself appeared excited as he stood proudly within the arena while countless people watched him.","Then Karo stood up.","The cheers immediately died.","The smiles on the faces of many humans disappeared.","A heavy silence spread throughout the surrounding area.","Without saying a single word, Karo calmly walked toward the arena and accepted the challenge.","The battle began.","Three minutes later, it ended.","The swordsman, who had fought through nine difficult battles to reach that point, was killed while Karo stood above him completely unharmed. The accumulated Killing Points instantly transferred to Karo, and the giant demon simply turned around and left without even glancing at his defeated opponent. There was no celebration. No excitement. No arrogance.","To Karo, this appeared to be nothing more than routine.","A simple task he had repeated so many times that it no longer held any meaning.","Watching this scene unfold before his eyes, Max finally understood the extent of the problem within Starfall Haven. This was not merely a strong demon defeating weaker opponents. This was systematic suppression.","Karo was deliberately allowing humans to accumulate Killing Points before taking everything away from them at the last moment, ensuring that no human participant could successfully complete the Ten Consecutive Victory Trial while simultaneously enriching himself through their efforts.","Meanwhile, all around Max, countless human participants watched with expressions filled with anger, helplessness, and frustration. Some openly glared at Karo while others avoided looking at him altogether. Yet despite those emotions, nobody stepped forward to challenge him directly.","The reason was simple.","They were afraid.","Not because of Karo’s status as the son of a Star Lord.","But because of his strength.","And judging from everything Max had seen so far, that fear was not entirely unjustified.","Max continued observing the battles taking place throughout the Combat Hall while occasionally watching Karo, who remained seated in a distant section of the hall like a patient predator waiting for prey to wander into his grasp.","It was at that moment that a beam of golden light descended from above and landed directly upon Nick.","Immediately afterward, a notification appeared above his head.","His turn had arrived.","Nick looked toward the arena assigned to him and slowly exhaled before turning toward Max with a smile. \"Looks like it is finally my turn. I will go and see how far I can get. If I am lucky enough to reach the ninth battle, perhaps I will even get the chance to fight Karo myself.\"","Although he appeared relaxed, Max could easily tell that Nick was not nearly as confident as he pretended to be.","Before Nick could leave, however, Max suddenly spoke.","\"Withdraw from the trial.\"","Nick froze.","For a moment, he simply stared at Max.","Then he frowned slightly and said, \"Withdraw? The penalty for abandoning the trial is one thousand Killing Points. That is not exactly a small amount.\"","Max’s expression remained completely calm as he replied, \"One thousand Killing Points is insignificant compared to what you stand to lose. Let me handle Karo. There is no reason for you to throw away all the points you might accumulate during the trial only to have them taken by him in the end.\"","Nick fell silent afterward.","His gaze instinctively shifted toward the distant figure of Karo, who was currently watching the arenas with the confidence of someone who considered the entire Combat Hall his personal territory.","For several moments, Nick said nothing.","Eventually, he released a long sigh and shook his head helplessly. \"Honestly, I do not like this idea at all. Every warrior hates retreating before a battle, especially one that has not even begun yet. However, the more I think about it, the more I realize you are right. Losing one thousand Killing Points is unpleasant, but it is still far better than fighting my way through multiple battles, accumulating tens or even hundreds of thousands of Killing Points, and then handing everything over to Karo at the very end. Compared to that outcome, sacrificing one thousand Killing Points almost feels cheap.\"","A bitter smile appeared on his face afterward.","Then he looked at Max once more and said, \"Fine. I will trust your judgment this time.\"","With that, Nick headed toward one of the Combat Hall officials and submitted a request to withdraw from the Ten Consecutive Victory Trial.","A few moments later, a notification appeared above him.","[Participant Nick Has Withdrawn From The Ten Consecutive Victory Trial.]","[1,000 Killing Points Deducted.]","Seeing the notification, Nick shook his head once more before returning to Max’s side.","Meanwhile, Max’s gaze slowly drifted toward Karo again.","The giant demon remained completely unaware that someone had just stepped aside because another person intended to deal with him personally.","A faint smile slowly appeared across Max’s face.","Soon enough—","Karo would finally become his problem.","After Nick withdrew from the trial, several other participants went to the arena before finally Max turn came.","A brilliant pillar of golden light descended from high above and landed directly upon Max.","The moment the golden beam appeared, countless eyes within the surrounding area instinctively shifted toward its target.","Participants waiting for their turns, spectators watching the battles, and even some individuals currently fighting in nearby arenas briefly glanced toward the source of the light.","Since everyone present knew what the golden beam represented, they immediately understood that another participant had finally been selected to begin their challenge.","Meanwhile, Max calmly looked upward as the golden light enveloped his entire body.","Several notifications immediately appeared before his eyes.","[Participant Max Morgan]","[Your Turn Has Arrived.]","[Please Proceed To Arena Number 7.]","[Ten Consecutive Victory Trial Beginning.]","[Failure To Arrive Within Five Minutes Will Be Considered A Withdrawal.]","The moment Max read the notifications, a faint smile appeared across his face. He had already spent enough time observing the Combat Hall and learning about its rules.","Now it was finally his turn to step onto the stage and begin earning the Killing Points he needed. More importantly, this would also allow him to personally witness the methods Karo used to suppress the human participants within Starfall Haven."]},{"number":1708,"title":"Chapter 1708: Max’s Arrogance!","paragraphs":["Around him, numerous participants immediately recognized his name.","After all, Max Morgan was hardly an unknown figure within the Divine Realm anymore.","Many people had heard about his performance during the Smelting Trial, secret domain of Orion and from the Sword Sovereign’s sword.","Some had even personally witnessed it.","However, the moment their senses swept across his cultivation, many expressions immediately changed.","Some revealed disappointment.","Others showed amusement.","A few even displayed open disdain.","To them, fame and strength were two entirely different things. While Max’s accomplishments had certainly made him famous, his cultivation at the peak of the Law Awakening Realm simply appeared too low compared to the monstrous geniuses gathered within the Combat Hall.","Most participants here stood at the peak of the Law Refinement Realm, and many had already established impressive reputations throughout their respective races.","As a result, whispers immediately spread through the crowd.","\"So that is Max Morgan?\"","\"The one who supposedly dominated the Smelting Trial and defeated Mira, the daughter of the Sword God Palace master?\"","\"He looks too ordinary.\"","\"Peak Law Awakening Realm? He is too weak in my opinion\"","\"I expected something more impressive.\"","\"He probably will not even reach the fifth battle.\"","\"Forget the fifth battle. I would be surprised if he survives the third.\"","Similar discussions continuously echoed throughout the surroundings.","Yet Max completely ignored them.","He had long grown accustomed to people underestimating him based on his cultivation.","If anything, such reactions had become a normal part of his life.","Without wasting another moment, Max calmly stepped forward and began making his way toward Arena Number 7.","As he moved through the enormous Combat Hall, countless gazes followed him. The sea of spectators parted naturally before him while participants standing nearby occasionally glanced toward him with curiosity. Some looked interested while others clearly viewed him as nothing more than another challenger destined to fail.","Meanwhile, Nick silently watched from behind.","Unlike the others, he did not underestimate Max.","After everything he had heard from the disciples of the War God Palace and after personally speaking with Max, he possessed a strange confidence that things would not unfold as everyone expected.","Eventually, Arena Number 7 came into view.","The arena was enormous.","Like the other nine arenas spread throughout the Combat Hall, it was surrounded by powerful barriers designed to contain even the most destructive battles. Countless formations covered its surface while ancient runes continuously glowed along the outer walls.","The fighting platform itself stretched for several kilometers, providing more than enough room for high-level combatants to unleash their full strength without restrictions.","The moment Max arrived before the arena, another notification immediately appeared.","[Participant Max Morgan Has Arrived.]","[Preparing First Battle.]","[Please Enter The Arena.]","Without hesitation, Max stepped forward and passed through the barrier.","The moment his figure entered the arena, a tremendous wave of noise erupted from the surrounding audience.","Cheers.","Shouts.","Discussions.","All of it exploded simultaneously.","Countless spectators immediately focused their attention upon Arena Number 7.","Humans wanted to see whether the famous genius of the Black Dragon Clan could live up to his reputation.","Demons wanted to see how quickly he would fail.","Even many elves shifted their attention toward the arena with curious expressions.","Meanwhile, Max calmly walked toward the center of the massive platform before stopping there.","However, what happened next completely exceeded everyone’s expectations.","Instead of waiting quietly for his first opponent to arrive like every other challenger before him, Max slowly raised his head and swept his gaze across the enormous Combat Hall.","His eyes casually moved across the countless spectators occupying the stands before eventually settling upon the section where the majority of the demons were gathered. For several moments, he simply looked at them in silence. Then, a faint smile slowly appeared on his face.","The smile immediately gave many people a bad feeling.","Then Max spoke.","His voice was calm.","His tone was relaxed.","Yet because of the formations surrounding the arena, every single word echoed clearly throughout the entire Combat Hall.","\"Ever since arriving in Starfall Haven, I have continuously heard about how powerful the demon race is. I have listened to endless stories about the so-called genius demons gathered here. Yet after watching for so long, I cannot help but feel somewhat disappointed.\"","\"Aside from Karo, all I have seen are demons hiding behind the reputation of others while bullying weaker opponents. Since there are supposedly so many proud warriors among you, why not stop wasting time and send someone capable of giving me a proper fight? Surely among all the demons present here there must be at least one individual who is not completely useless.\"","The instant those words finished echoing throughout the Combat Hall, the atmosphere froze.","Complete silence descended.","Even the battles occurring in several nearby arenas seemed less important for a brief moment as countless people stared toward Arena Number 7.","Then—","The silence exploded.","The demon section immediately erupted into chaos.","\"What did that human just say?\"","\"Is he insane?\"","\"A peak Law Awakening Realm ant dares to speak to us like that?\"","\"Who gave him the courage to insult the demon race?\"","\"I will personally tear him apart.\"","\"Forget Karo. I can kill him before he manages to blink.\"","\"Let me enter that arena immediately.\"","Angry voices continuously echoed throughout the demon section as countless pairs of eyes locked onto Max with undisguised hostility. Many demons had already stood from their seats while glaring toward the arena. Several even released killing intent unconsciously due to their rage.","Meanwhile, the reactions among the humans were completely different.","Many looked shocked.","Others looked excited.","A few even struggled to hide their laughter after witnessing the demons become so furious.","Nick himself stood among the crowd with a strange expression on his face.","Even after everything he had heard about Max, he had not expected him to immediately provoke almost every demon within the Combat Hall.","This was not confidence.","This was blatant arrogance.","Meanwhile, Max simply stood in the center of the arena with a relaxed expression, completely ignoring the furious reactions around him. In fact, when he saw how angry the demons had become, the smile on his face only widened slightly.","Then he spoke again.","\"What happened? I thought demons were fearless warriors. Yet all I hear are angry complaints from the audience. If any of you actually possess the strength to back up your pride, then come down here and prove me wrong. Otherwise, sit quietly and continue watching. Your shouting is becoming rather annoying.\""]},{"number":1709,"title":"Chapter 1709: First Battle!","paragraphs":["The moment those words left his mouth, the uproar became even greater than before.","Many demons nearly exploded from anger.","Several powerful demon geniuses immediately rose from their seats.","Even the elves who had previously been observing the situation with indifference now appeared interested. After all, openly provoking an entire race inside the Combat Hall was not something one witnessed every day.","Far away, Karo’s golden eyes slowly narrowed.","For the first time since Max entered the arena, genuine interest appeared on the giant demon’s face.","Most humans who entered the Combat Hall either feared the demons or avoided drawing their attention.","Max had done the exact opposite.","Meanwhile, among the enraged crowd of demons, one individual finally stood up.","The demon was enormous.","Standing nearly two and a half meters tall, his body appeared like a fortress of muscle and steel. Dark gray skin covered every inch of his body while numerous scars crossed his arms and chest, each one evidence of previous battles.","Thick black horns curved upward from his forehead while crimson eyes burned with fury. Resting upon his shoulder was a gigantic warhammer that looked heavy enough to flatten a mountain.","The demon’s expression was incomparably ugly.","Clearly, Max’s words had completely enraged him.","Without saying a single word, he directly jumped from the spectator section.","Boom!","The floor beneath him cracked as he landed heavily before the entrance to Arena Number 7.","The sheer force of the impact caused nearby spectators to take several steps backward.","Then, under the watchful eyes of countless participants, the demon stepped through the barrier and entered the arena.","The moment he arrived inside, a savage smile spread across his face.","His crimson eyes stared directly at Max.","The killing intent within them was so obvious that even the spectators could feel it.","Slowly, the demon lifted the gigantic warhammer from his shoulder before slamming its head against the arena floor.","Boom!","The entire platform trembled violently.","Cracks immediately spread across portions of the arena as a result of the impact.","Then the demon finally spoke.","\"Human, since you are so eager to embarrass yourself, I will personally teach you the consequences of insulting the demon race. Remember my name carefully, because it will be the last thing you hear before your defeat. My name is Draven, and I promise you that this battle will end in a single move.\"","His voice echoed throughout the Combat Hall as confidence radiated from every word.","Around them, countless demons immediately began cheering.","Many already considered the battle finished.","After all, Draven was a peak Law Refinement Realm genius with a considerable reputation inside Starfall Haven.","Meanwhile, standing across from him, Max merely smiled.","There was no tension on his face.","No nervousness.","No concern.","It was as though he was not facing a powerful demon genius at all.","The atmosphere within Arena Number 7 rapidly became increasingly intense as countless spectators focused their attention entirely upon the two figures standing opposite one another.","Max’s first battle in the Ten Consecutive Victory Trial—","Was finally about to begin.","\"Now, take my attack!\" The demon roared.","The moment those words fell, the demon’s muscles bulged violently, and dark demonic energy surged around his body like a storm. He gripped the handle of his warhammer with both hands, raised it high above his head, and then slammed it down toward Max with terrifying force.","Boom!","The entire arena shook violently the instant the warhammer descended.","The attack had not even fully reached Max yet, but the overwhelming pressure created by the hammer strike had already crushed the air in front of it, causing fierce waves of force to sweep outward in every direction. The stone beneath Max’s feet cracked apart layer by layer while the surrounding battlefield trembled as if it could collapse at any moment.","Many participants watching from outside the arena felt their expressions change.","This demon was not merely relying on a large weapon.","His physical strength was truly terrifying.","The warhammer tore through the air with such brutal power that it seemed capable of smashing a mountain into pieces, and the violent demonic energy wrapped around it made the attack even more frightening. Anyone standing beneath that strike would feel as if the sky itself was falling down upon them.","Yet Max did not move.","He watched the enormous warhammer descend toward him with the same calm expression, and despite the terrifying pressure bearing down on his body.","He did not activate even one of his Seven Divine Veins, nor did he draw upon the power of his Draconic Essences, because in his eyes, this attack was not yet worthy of forcing him to reveal even the smallest part of his true strength.","The demon’s warhammer tore through the air with a horrifying roar, and the force contained within it pressed down like a collapsing mountain, causing the stone arena beneath Max to split apart before the weapon even reached him.","Cracks spread outward like a dense spiderweb, and waves of broken stone were blasted into the air as the overwhelming pressure crashed down upon the battlefield. Many of the watching participants instinctively held their breath, because from their point of view, that strike was powerful enough to smash an ordinary genius into meat paste.","Then, just as the huge warhammer was about to crash into Max’s head, Max slowly raised one hand.","His movement was casual.","It was almost lazy.","The next instant, his palm closed around the head of the descending warhammer.","Boom!","A deafening explosion erupted beneath him.","The entire section of the arena under Max’s feet was instantly obliterated, and countless fragments of stone were sent flying in all directions as the violent force of the demon’s attack poured into the ground.","Dust and debris surged upward like a storm, and the shockwave swept across the battlefield with enough power to make the barriers surrounding the arena tremble faintly.","However, within that ruined crater, Max remained exactly where he had been.","His feet had not moved.","His back had not bent.","His expression had not changed.","He stood amid the shattered arena while holding the demon’s huge warhammer in one hand, and the terrifying weapon that had seemed capable of crushing everything a moment ago now looked like nothing more than a child’s toy trapped in his grip.","For a brief moment, the entire arena fell silent."]},{"number":1710,"title":"Chapter 1710: Hundred Thousand KP!","paragraphs":["The demon’s crimson eyes widened violently.","His hands were still gripping the handle of the warhammer, and his thick arms were still bulging with strength, but no matter how hard he pushed down, no matter how much demonic energy he poured into his body, the weapon did not move even an inch. It was as if the warhammer had been caught by an immovable divine mountain.","\"Impossible,\" the demon muttered, his arrogant sneer vanishing completely from his face.","That single word came out of his mouth with raw disbelief.","He could not understand it.","He could not accept it.","A human had stopped his full-powered hammer strike with one hand, and this human had done it without releasing any terrifying aura, without revealing any divine power, and without even taking half a step back.","Max looked up at the demon and smiled faintly.","\"That is all?\"","The demon’s heart trembled the moment he heard those three words.","Before he could react, Max tightened his fingers around the head of the warhammer.","Crack.","A sharp sound echoed through the arena.","The demon’s expression changed instantly.","Crack! Crack! Crack!","More cracks spread across the massive warhammer, and the thick metal surface began to cave inward under Max’s fingers as if it were not forged from powerful demonic iron, but from soft clay.","The demon poured more strength into his arms and tried to pull the weapon back, but the warhammer remained trapped in Max’s hand, unable to move, unable to resist, unable to escape the terrifying pressure crushing it from within.","Then Max applied a little more force.","Bang!","The huge warhammer was crushed apart in his hand.","Fragments of twisted metal burst outward, and the remaining handle shook violently in the demon’s grip before becoming completely useless. The demon staggered backward with a pale face, his hands trembling as he stared at the ruined weapon, and for the first time since entering the arena, real fear appeared in his eyes.","Outside the arena, the watching participants were frozen in place.","The humans stared at Max as if they were seeing a monster hidden beneath human skin.","The demons, who had been laughing and shouting for Max to be smashed to death a moment ago, now stood with stiff expressions, their confidence crushed together with that warhammer.","Even the elves, who usually maintained their elegant calm no matter what happened, could no longer hide the shock in their eyes.","Nick was no exception.","He had always believed that Max would easily take care of the first battle, and he had never doubted that this demon would lose, but even he had not expected Max to be this overwhelming.","He had imagined Max dodging the attack, blocking it with a technique, or perhaps using one of his terrifying powers to suppress the demon, but Max had done none of that.","He had simply raised his hand.","He had grabbed the warhammer.","Then he had crushed it.","Nick stared at Max from outside the arena, his throat moving slightly as he swallowed with difficulty, and even though he knew Max was strong, this scene still shook him beyond belief.","\"This guy...\" Nick muttered under his breath, his eyes filled with disbelief. \"Just how strong is he now?\"","Max looked at the demon’s horrified expression and smiled, but that smile did not carry the slightest warmth.","\"Now leave behind your Killing Points.\"","The demon’s body stiffened the moment those words entered his ears, and before he could even recover from the shock of seeing his warhammer crushed like worthless scrap metal, Max’s figure suddenly blurred from where he stood.","There was no loud movement, no visible preparation, and no warning at all. One instant, Max was standing amid the shattered remains of the arena, and in the next instant, he had already appeared directly in front of the demon like a shadow that had crossed space itself.","The demon’s pupils contracted violently.","Too fast.","Max was far too fast.","The demon wanted to retreat, but his body could not respond in time, and the fear that had just taken root in his heart seemed to freeze his limbs in place. The same human he had mocked only moments ago now stood before him like an executioner, and the overwhelming confidence he once carried had been crushed together with his weapon.","Max slowly clenched his fist.","Brilliant star-like radiance erupted from his knuckles, and countless tiny specks of dazzling light gathered around his arm as if a small galaxy had awakened within his flesh. The glow was beautiful, but the power hidden inside it was terrifying, and the moment that stellar energy condensed, the demon felt an indescribable chill rush through his entire body.","\"Star Fist.\"","Max’s voice was calm.","Then his fist drove straight into the demon’s stomach.","Boom!","The impact exploded with terrifying force, and for a brief instant, the demon’s enormous body bent around Max’s fist as if all the strength in his body had been shattered at once. His eyes bulged, his mouth opened soundlessly, and the demonic energy around him collapsed before it could even struggle.","Then the brilliant star-like power erupted from within him, tearing through his flesh, bones, organs, and demonic core in a single devastating burst.","In the next moment, the demon was obliterated completely.","There was no corpse left behind.","There was no final scream.","His huge body vanished into scattered fragments of dark light, and only a flood of Killing Points burst out across the arena like countless blood-red sparks. The number above them was so large that the watching participants felt their hearts tremble.","One hundred thousand Killing Points.","For many participants, that was an amount they could only dream of obtaining after countless battles, but now it had scattered across the battlefield after a single punch from Max.","Max did not waste even a breath.","He raised his hand, and the scattered Killing Points immediately surged toward him like streams of crimson light being pulled by an invisible force. One after another, they entered his body, causing the number beside his name to rise rapidly while the ruined arena around him still echoed with the aftermath of that terrifying punch.","[Killing Points +100,000]","[Current Killing Points: 210,000]","In the Combat Hall, if one got killed by other participants in the arena, then they would directly lose all their Killing Points, which was different from normal situations.","Generally, if one were to get killed by another, they would only lose half the killing points at first, but here that rule didn’t apply."]},{"number":1711,"title":"Chapter 1711: Five Consecutive Victories!","paragraphs":["Outside the arena, the silence became even heavier.","The demons who had mocked him earlier no longer dared to laugh.","The elves watched with solemn expressions.","Among the elves watching from outside the arena, there was one figure who did not react in the same way as the others.","He was a young male elf with long golden hair that fell smoothly over his shoulders, and even among the naturally beautiful elves, his appearance stood out with an air of noble elegance that made him look almost like an elven prince.","His features were flawless, his posture was straight, and his emerald eyes carried a calm sharpness that did not belong to an ordinary participant. While the other elves were shocked by Max’s overwhelming strength, this golden-haired elf remained silent, but his narrowed eyes never left Max for even a single moment.","He studied Max carefully.","The way Max moved.","The way he attacked.","The way he stood in the ruined arena with that casual smile, as if destroying a powerful demon and taking one hundred thousand Killing Points was nothing worth mentioning.","The golden-haired elf’s gaze grew deeper.","For some reason, the more he looked at Max, the stronger the strange feeling in his heart became. It was not fear, and it was not simple curiosity either. It was a faint sense of familiarity, as if he had seen Max somewhere before, or as if something about Max’s aura had brushed against his memory long ago.","But that made no sense.","He was certain he had never met this human before.","\"Why does this human give me such a familiar feeling?\" the golden-haired elf thought to himself, his brows drawing together slightly.","His eyes lingered on Max’s figure, and a trace of confusion flashed through them. He could not understand where that feeling came from, but his instincts told him that Max was not merely another powerful human genius.","There was something hidden beneath that calm face, something that seemed to touch a memory buried deep within him.","The golden-haired elf did not speak.","He only continued watching Max in silence.","However, unlike the demons who now looked at Max with anger and fear, and unlike the other participants who stared at him with disbelief, this elf looked at Max as if he was trying to remember something important.","The human participants stared with wide eyes, unable to decide whether they should feel excited or terrified.","Nick stood among them, frozen in place as he watched Max calmly absorb all one hundred thousand Killing Points, and even though he had already witnessed Max crush the warhammer with his bare hand, this single punch still left his mind ringing.","The first battle had ended.","No, calling it a battle was too generous.","From beginning to end, the demon had only attacked once, lost his weapon, lost his confidence, and then lost his life.","Max lowered his hand after taking all the Killing Points, then slowly turned his gaze toward the remaining demons outside the arena.","His smile deepened.","\"Next.\"","The death of the first demon did not make the rest of the demons retreat.","Instead, it made their fury explode.","The moment Max absorbed the one hundred thousand Killing Points and calmly said the word \"Next,\" several demons outside the arena immediately roared in anger, their eyes burning with savage killing intent as they looked at the human standing in the ruined battlefield.","In their eyes, Max had not merely defeated one of their own. He had humiliated the demon race in front of humans and elves alike, and he had done so with a smile on his face, as if killing a demon genius was no different from crushing an insect beneath his foot.","\"You arrogant human bastard!\"","\"Do you really think killing one demon means you can look down on all of us?\"","\"I will tear that smile off your face!\"","One demon after another stepped forward to challenge him, and each of them carried a more brutal aura than the last. Some wielded giant axes covered in black flames, some had bodies wrapped in bone armor, some possessed claws sharper than treasured blades, and some released thick waves of demonic energy that made the surrounding participants instinctively move back.","Every demon who entered the arena looked at Max with rage and contempt, and every one of them believed that the previous demon had simply underestimated him too much.","But the result never changed.","The second demon charged at Max with a furious roar and swung a black axe that carried enough power to split the arena in half, but Max only stepped forward, avoided the blade by the smallest distance, and drove his fist into the demon’s chest with terrifying precision.","The demon’s armor shattered instantly, his body caved inward, and before his roar could even finish leaving his throat, he exploded into fragments of dark light while his Killing Points scattered across the arena.","The third demon tried to rely on speed.","His figure turned into a blur as he circled Max from all directions, leaving behind countless afterimages as his claws tore through the air again and again, yet Max did not even bother to look around.","The instant the demon appeared behind him, Max turned slightly and punched backward without hesitation, and that single casual fist struck the demon’s face with such horrifying force that his entire head disappeared before the rest of his body followed, collapsing into scattered light and vanishing from the battlefield.","The fourth demon was even larger than the first.","His skin was covered in thick scales, and the demonic energy around him formed a massive beast-like shadow that howled above the arena. He declared that Max’s fists would never break through his defense, but the moment Max arrived before him and punched once, those proud scales shattered like thin glass.","The demon’s beast shadow collapsed, his body was pierced through by the force of the strike, and he was obliterated before he could even understand how his so-called defense had failed so miserably.","The fifth demon was the strongest among those who had challenged him so far.","His aura caused the entire arena to tremble, and even some of the humans and elves watching from outside narrowed their eyes when he stepped onto the battlefield.","He did not speak much, but the hatred in his eyes was clear as he gathered all his demonic energy into both arms and unleashed a terrifying attack toward Max. The strike carried enough power to make several participants feel their scalps turn numb, yet Max only raised his fist again with activating 5000 Draconic Essences.","And...","Boom!","The demon’s attack shattered.","His arms shattered.","His body shattered.","In the next breath, he was gone.","Just like that, five demons had entered the arena one after another, and five demons had been obliterated by Max’s fists without forcing him to reveal anything beyond his raw physical strength.","What should have been a tense ten consecutive victory trial had turned into a one-sided slaughter, and the speed at which it happened was so absurd that many participants felt as if they had only blinked a few times before Max had already achieved five consecutive victories."]},{"number":1712,"title":"Chapter 1712: Elf Prince’s Test","paragraphs":["At this moment, the atmosphere inside the Combat Hall had changed completely.","Before, many demons had been furious because of Max’s arrogance.","Now, they were silent.","Before, many humans had been excited but uncertain.","Now, they were staring at him with burning eyes.","Before, most elves had watched with calm interest.","Now, even their calm expressions had become solemn.","Almost everyone in the Combat Hall had finally turned their attention toward Arena Seven. Demons, humans, and elves alike were now watching Max, and no one could pretend that he was merely an arrogant human shouting empty words anymore.","Five consecutive victories had been won in the blink of an eye, and each opponent had been crushed so brutally that even the most prideful demons had to admit one thing in their hearts.","This human was dangerous.","Far from the arena, Karo watched the scene with a faint smile on his face.","Unlike the other demons who were furious or shocked, Karo did not seem to care much about the five demons Max had killed. His expression remained calm, almost amused, as if he was watching an interesting performance rather than seeing members of his own race being destroyed one after another.","In his eyes, those demons were not worth mentioning. If they died because they were weak, then that was their own fault.","\"A little interesting,\" Karo muttered softly, his smile unchanged.","However, he still had no intention of stepping forward.","To him, interfering before Max reached the eighth battle was not worth it. The trial still had several rounds left, and if Max really had the ability to continue forward, then there would be plenty of time to deal with him later. Until then, Karo was content to watch and see how far this human could go.","Among the elves, the golden-haired male elf who looked like an elven prince continued staring at Max with narrowed eyes.","The strange feeling in his heart had not disappeared.","On the contrary, it had grown stronger with each battle.","Every time Max moved, every time he punched, every time he calmly absorbed another demon’s Killing Points, that faint sense of familiarity became harder to ignore. The golden-haired elf’s gaze grew deeper, and after a moment of silent thought, he finally turned his head toward an elven woman standing beside him.","She was a graceful young woman with silver-green hair, clear eyes, and a slender sword hanging at her waist. Her aura was sharp yet elegant, and although she had remained quiet until now, it was obvious from the way the other elves gave her space that her strength was not ordinary.","\"Go and challenge him,\" the golden-haired elf said calmly.","The elven woman was visibly surprised.","She looked at the prince for a moment, then glanced toward the arena where Max stood amid the ruined battlefield. Her brows furrowed slightly, not because she feared Max, but because she could not understand the reason behind this command.","\"Your Highness,\" she said in a low voice, \"this is a conflict between humans and demons. Why should we interfere?\"","The golden-haired elf did not answer immediately.","His eyes returned to Max.","For several breaths, he only watched that human in silence, and the thoughtful look in his emerald eyes became even more intense. Then he spoke in a calm voice that only the elves near him could hear.","\"Just go and test his strength.\"","The elven woman’s expression shifted slightly.","The golden-haired elf continued, \"Do not fight carelessly, and do not treat him like an ordinary human genius. Push him as much as you can and make sure he reveals at least part of his true strength.\"","The elven woman’s gaze sharpened.","\"Your Highness wants to test something?\"","\"Yes,\" the golden-haired elf replied softly, his eyes still fixed on Max. \"I want to confirm something.\"","The elven woman did not ask further.","Although she still did not understand why their prince cared so much about this human, she knew his judgment was rarely wrong. If he had noticed something strange about Max, then there had to be a reason behind it. She nodded once, then stepped away from the elven group and walked toward Arena Seven.","Her movement immediately attracted attention.","Many humans looked surprised.","The demons frowned.","Even Max turned his gaze slightly toward her.","Until now, only demons had challenged him one after another because of anger and humiliation, yet now an elf had suddenly stepped forward. Her expression was calm, and there was no hatred in her eyes.","Unlike the demons who had entered the arena with rage, she carried herself with composed elegance, but the aura around her was sharp enough to make the surrounding participants understand that she was not weak.","The elven woman arrived before the arena barrier and looked at Max.","\"I challenge you,\" she said.","The Combat Hall fell into a strange silence.","An elf had interfered.","The sixth battle was no longer against a demon.","Max looked at her for a moment, then smiled faintly with dark intent.","\"So the elves are joining in too?\"","The elven woman placed one hand on the hilt of her sword and stepped into the arena.","\"I am only here to test you.\"","Max’s smile turned wicked when he heard those words.","\"Then you had better test carefully.\"","Although Max tried to remain as neutral toward the elves as he could, a faint coldness still stirred deep inside his heart, because no matter how rationally he tried to look at things, he could not forget that it was the elf race that had captured his parents, and it was also because of them that the tragic accident at his home had happened in the first place.","He knew very well that not every elf was involved in that matter, and he also knew that the elves from Acaris were different from the ones who had harmed his family, but hatred was not always something that listened to reason, especially when it was born from pain, loss, and memories that had carved themselves too deeply into the soul.","Because of this, even though this was his first time seeing the elven woman in front of him, Max still felt a trace of bias toward her, and it took him a few silent breaths to calm the dark emotions rising within his chest before he finally looked at her with a steady gaze and spoke in a controlled voice.","\"Make your move.\""]},{"number":1713,"title":"Chapter 1713: Death Wind Concept!","paragraphs":["The elven woman did not respond with anger or arrogance after hearing his words, because unlike the demons who had rushed into the arena with rage and killing intent, she had come here with a clear purpose, which was to test Max’s strength under the order of her prince and force him to reveal something useful.","Her eyes remained calm, but a sharp light gradually appeared in them as she raised one hand before her body, and the pure wind element around her immediately began to gather with astonishing speed.","The air inside the arena changed at once. It no longer felt like ordinary wind. It became cleaner, sharper, colder, and far more refined, as if every strand of air had been washed by the breath of ancient forests and tempered through countless storms.","This was the natural advantage of the elves. Their connection with the elements was purer than most races, and when an elf controlled the wind, it did not appear wild and chaotic like the wind used by beasts or demons, but instead moved with a strange harmony that seemed almost alive.","Whoosh!","Seven streams of pale green wind suddenly condensed around the elven woman, and under her precise control, those streams rapidly compressed, sharpened, and transformed into seven long swords made entirely from wind element.","Each sword floated in the air behind her like a guardian blade, its form almost transparent, yet the sharpness it released was so frightening that deep marks began to appear across the already ruined arena floor without the swords even moving.","The seven wind swords hummed softly as they circled behind her, and every time they trembled, the surrounding air was sliced apart so cleanly that faint cracks seemed to appear in the space around them.","These swords were not ordinary elemental constructs. They were weapons formed from extremely pure wind energy, and because her control over the wind element had reached an extraordinary level, each sword carried enough power to cut through flesh, bone, armor, and even powerful defensive skills with terrifying ease.","However, the true danger was not merely the seven wind swords themselves.","The true danger was the concept released from within them.","A gray-green aura slowly spread across the seven swords, and the atmosphere inside the arena became colder and more suffocating in an instant. The lively sharpness of wind changed into something gloomy and sinister, something that did not merely cut the body, but seemed capable of withering life itself.","This was her fifth level wind concept, Death Wind, a terrifying variation of the wind concept that she had comprehended through years of brutal meditation inside Death Valley, a death zone located on one of the planets within the star system ruled by the elves.","Death Valley was not a place where ordinary geniuses could survive. The wind there carried traces of decay, poison, bone-chilling cold, and lingering death energy, and anyone who entered that place would constantly feel as if invisible blades were scraping against their skin while the aura of death tried to erode their body and spirit from within.","The elven woman had endured that torment again and again, sitting alone inside that deadly valley while death wind battered her body, invaded her senses, and tested her will until she finally grasped the essence hidden within that terrifying natural force.","Because of that, the seven wind swords hovering behind her did not only possess terrifying sharpness. They also carried the power of death.","The moment the Death Wind concept fully revealed, many participants outside the arena felt their expressions change. Some humans instinctively took a step back, while several demons narrowed their eyes with rare seriousness.","Even the elves watching from their side looked at the elven woman with solemn respect, because they knew very well how difficult it was to comprehend Death Wind to the fifth level, and they also understood that once her seven wind swords began to move, they would not simply slash at Max’s body.","They would attempt to invade his wounds, corrode his vitality, numb his senses, and weaken his life force with every cut.","Max stood where he was and quietly watched the seven wind swords take shape.","His expression did not change, but the coldness in his eyes deepened slightly.","The elven woman noticed that change, and although she did not know the reason behind it, she could still feel that Max’s attitude toward her was different from the way he had faced the demons.","Against the demons, his arrogance had been open, almost playful, but against her, there was a restrained hostility beneath his calmness, like a blade hidden inside a sheath. She did not understand where that hostility came from, but she did not ask. This was the arena, and in the arena, strength spoke more clearly than words.","\"I will begin,\" she said softly.","The next instant, her fingers moved.","The seven wind swords shot forward at the same time.","They did not rush toward Max in a simple straight line. Instead, they spread apart in seven different directions, slicing through the air with terrifying speed as they surrounded him from above, below, left, right, front, and behind.","Their movements were elegant, but the killing power contained within them was horrifying. Wherever the swords passed, the arena floor split apart silently, and the faint gray-green death aura trailing behind them caused the broken stones to lose their luster as if their vitality had been drained away.","In just a single breath, the seven swords sealed every direction around Max.","The elven woman’s eyes sharpened.","She had no intention of holding back too much, because her prince had ordered her to push Max into revealing some of his strength, and from what she had seen so far, ordinary attacks would never be enough to force him to take things seriously. If she wanted to test him, she had to attack with enough power to make even this arrogant human respond.","The seven wind swords descended.","Their sharpness screamed through the arena.","Their Death Wind concept spread like a silent curse.","And Max, who stood at the center of it all, slowly raised his eyes as the terrifying attack closed in around him."]},{"number":1714,"title":"Chapter 1714: Impenetrable Defense!","paragraphs":["The seven wind swords descended upon Max from every direction, and the sharpness contained within them was so terrifying that even the air around him seemed to be sliced into countless invisible fragments.","One sword came from above like heavenly punishment, one rushed straight toward his chest, two curved in from both sides, one shot toward his back, while the remaining two swept low toward his legs with enough speed and precision to tear apart any opening in his defense.","The Death Wind concept wrapped around all seven swords like a gray-green mist, spreading a cold and rotten aura that made the ruined stones beneath Max’s feet lose their color, and for an instant, it truly looked as if he had been sealed inside a cage of deathly wind blades with no path of retreat.","However, Max only gave a light smirk.","\"Dragon Scales Transformation.\"","The moment those words left his mouth, a deep and ancient power awakened inside his body.","A low dragon roar seemed to echo from within his blood, and the aura around Max changed completely. It was no longer merely the aura of a powerful human genius. It became heavier, older, and far more domineering, as if some ancient dragon sleeping inside his flesh had finally opened its eyes.","In the next instant, black dragon scales began spreading across his skin at a frightening speed. They appeared first on his arms, then crawled over his shoulders, chest, neck, face, back, and legs until his entire body was covered in a layer of dark, gleaming dragon scales.","Each scale looked like it had been forged from black divine metal, smooth yet sharp, cold yet alive, and faint chaotic patterns could be seen moving across their surface like tiny rivers of darkness.","Max lowered his gaze slightly and looked at his own body.","A faint smile appeared on his face.","\"This is the first time I have fully entered a complete Dragon Scales Transformation since my Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline evolved to its peak,\" Max muttered to himself, his voice calm, but the satisfaction hidden within it was impossible to miss.","The transformation was different from before.","Far different.","In the past, his dragon scales had already been powerful, but now that his Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline had reached its peak evolution, every scale covering his body seemed to contain an overwhelming defensive force that far surpassed his previous state.","It was not simply armor. It was a manifestation of his bloodline, his flesh, his vitality, and the tyrannical nature of a chaotic dragon compressed into physical form.","The moment the transformation was complete, Max’s entire presence became more oppressive, and even though he had not released any violent energy, the participants outside the arena felt as if a monstrous creature had suddenly appeared in human form.","Then Max smiled and began walking toward the elven woman.","His steps were not fast.","They were calm and steady.","It was as if the seven terrifying wind swords rushing toward him from every direction did not exist at all.","The elven woman’s eyes narrowed, and the moment she saw Max walking forward instead of defending or dodging, her fingers moved slightly, causing the seven wind swords to erupt with even greater speed and power.","The gray-green Death Wind concept around them became denser, and the sharpness they released turned even more frightening as they finally struck Max’s body.","Clang!","The first wind sword slashed against Max’s shoulder.","Instead of cutting through flesh, the wind sword shattered the instant it touched the black dragon scales, exploding into a raging wave of wind that swept violently across the arena.","The destructive wind rushed outward with a sharp howl, tearing apart the stones nearby, yet Max’s shoulder remained completely unharmed. Not even a scratch appeared on his scales.","The elven woman’s expression changed.","Before she could fully react, the second sword struck Max’s chest.","Clang!","It shattered as well.","The third sword pierced toward his back, but the moment its tip touched the black scales covering him, the entire blade cracked from tip to hilt before bursting apart into chaotic wind.","The fourth and fifth swords arrived at almost the same time, one targeting his neck and the other aiming at his waist, yet both were destroyed the instant they made contact.","Their sharpness, their speed, and even the terrifying Death Wind concept hidden within them failed to penetrate the defense of Max’s dragon scales.","Max did not stop walking.","His pace did not change.","His smile did not fade.","Clang! Clang!","The final two wind swords struck his legs, and just like the others, they exploded into waves of violent wind without leaving behind the slightest wound.","The Death Wind concept tried to invade his body, tried to corrode his vitality, and tried to slip through the gaps between his scales, but it could not find even the smallest opening. Max’s dragon scales were like an absolute wall, rejecting every trace of the elven woman’s power with brutal simplicity.","In only a few breaths, all seven wind swords were destroyed.","The raging wind spread across the arena, turning the battlefield into a storm of broken stone, gray-green energy, and scattered wind blades, but Max continued walking through it all as if he were merely strolling through a gentle breeze.","The storm struck his body from every side, but the black dragon scales covering him gleamed coldly beneath the light, completely untouched.","The Combat Hall fell into stunned silence.","The humans stared at Max with wide eyes, their hearts pounding violently.","The demons, who had only just recovered from seeing him obliterate five of their own with his bare fists, now felt their expressions stiffen once more, because this was no longer only terrifying strength.","This was also terrifying defense. If attacks of that level could not even scratch him, then how were ordinary participants supposed to fight him at all?","The elves were even more shocked.","They knew the power of the elven woman’s seven wind swords better than anyone. They knew how pure her wind element was, and they knew how dangerous her fifth level Death Wind concept could be once it touched a body.","Even among elven geniuses, her attack was not weak. Yet Max had not blocked it with a technique. He had not avoided it with movement. He had simply allowed the swords to strike him directly, and every single one of them had shattered against his body.","The elven woman stood frozen for a moment, her calm expression finally breaking.","Her clear eyes trembled slightly as she looked at the black dragon scales covering Max’s body. She had expected him to be strong. She had expected him to have some hidden method. She had even prepared herself for the possibility that he would destroy her seven wind swords with a powerful attack.","But she had never imagined that he would simply walk through them and remain completely unharmed.","\"How is his defense this strong?\" she thought, her heart tightening.","Among the elves, the golden-haired prince’s narrowed eyes became sharper than ever.","Max stopped only a short distance away from the elven woman.","The remnants of the destroyed wind swords still raged around him, but none of it could harm him.","He looked at her and smiled faintly.","\"Is that all the test you prepared?\""]},{"number":1715,"title":"Chapter 1715: Pseudo Cosmic Path of Death Wind Concept!","paragraphs":["The elven woman was truly shocked after seeing Max walk through her seven wind swords without suffering even the smallest injury, because although she had never believed those seven swords would be enough to defeat him, she had at least expected them to leave behind a few wounds, or at the very least force him to reveal some defensive technique beyond the black scales covering his body.","In her original thought, once her Death Wind concept entered his body through those wounds, she would be able to use the next few attacks to pressure him further, and perhaps she could even uncover a trace of the strength her prince wanted to see.","But only now did she realize how naive those thoughts had been. Her seven wind swords had not injured him. They had not slowed him down. They had not even made him raise his hand.","\"You are strong,\" she said as she looked at Max, her eyes flashing with a sharp and solemn light. \"But is this your true strength?\"","Max looked at her with a faint smile on his face, but he did not answer.","That silence made the elven woman’s gaze turn even colder.","She knew Max was looking down on her. Perhaps not openly, and perhaps not with the same mocking arrogance he had shown the demons, but that calm smile itself was a kind of contempt, because he was standing there as if nothing she had done was worthy of a proper response.","For an elf genius like her, especially one who had survived the endless torment of Death Valley and comprehended the fifth level Death Wind concept, that feeling was not pleasant at all.","Her fingers slowly moved toward the sword hanging at her waist.","The moment her hand touched the hilt, the air inside the arena changed again.","The wind that had been raging around Max suddenly became heavier, colder, and far more dangerous, and the gray-green aura that had scattered after the destruction of the seven wind swords began to gather back toward the elven woman like countless streams returning to the sea.","Her expression grew calm, so calm that it no longer carried shock, frustration, or hesitation, and even the sharpness in her eyes became quiet, as if all unnecessary emotions had been cut away in an instant.","Then she tapped into her Pseudo Cosmic Path of Death Wind Concept.","Boom!","A terrifying wave of deathly wind exploded from her body.","It did not surge outward like ordinary wind. It erupted like countless invisible blades being released from a sealed abyss, and in the next moment, blade after blade of gray-green Death Wind burst from her body without stopping.","They flew in every direction, slicing through the arena walls, tearing apart the broken stones beneath her feet, and carving deep marks into the battlefield faster than the eye could follow.","The entire arena seemed to be swallowed by a storm of deathly blades, and each blade carried a chilling aura that made the surrounding participants feel as if their skin was being scraped by unseen knives even though they were standing outside the barrier.","The ruined arena could no longer endure it.","Crack! Crack! Crack!","The floor beneath the elven woman shattered again and again as the death wind blades swept across it, and countless fragments of stone were lifted into the air before being instantly sliced into dust.","The shockwaves from the released concept slammed against the barrier surrounding the arena, causing ripples to spread across its surface, while a sharp screaming sound filled the Combat Hall as if the wind itself had turned into a dying spirit.","Many participants outside the arena instinctively stepped back.","The humans who had just been excited by Max’s overwhelming strength now felt their expressions stiffen. The demons who had been enraged by Max’s arrogance also fell silent for a moment, because even they could sense how dangerous this elven woman had become after tapping into her Pseudo Cosmic Path.","This was no longer a simple attack made from wind element. This was a path, a direction of power, a deeper form of comprehension that allowed her Death Wind concept to approach something far more terrifying than ordinary elemental mastery.","Among the elves, several geniuses stared at her with burning eyes.","They knew what this meant.","Once an elf tapped into a Pseudo Cosmic Path, their concept would no longer remain at the level of ordinary elemental usage. It would carry the beginning of a greater law, a power that could connect the element to the vast cosmic order itself.","Although it was only pseudo and had not yet reached the level of a true Cosmic Path, it was already enough to make her strength rise by a terrifying amount.","The golden-haired elven prince watched the scene in silence.","His eyes remained on Max.","He did not care how powerful the elven woman’s Death Wind had become. What he wanted to know was how Max would respond now.","Inside the arena, the elven woman slowly drew the sword from her waist.","Shing!","The blade left its sheath with a clear and chilling sound.","It was a slender elven sword, pale silver in color, with faint green patterns carved along the blade like flowing vines. The moment it appeared, the endless blades of Death Wind around her seemed to find a center.","They gathered toward the sword, coiling around the blade in dense layers, and the sword itself began to release a cold gray-green radiance that made the air around it distort. Her long silver-green hair fluttered behind her, her dress moved violently in the storm, and yet her expression remained completely calm.","She held the sword in one hand and pointed it toward Max.","\"Since ordinary attacks cannot pierce your defense,\" she said softly, her voice steady despite the raging storm around her, \"then I will use everything I have to test you.\"","Max stood within the storm of Death Wind blades, his black dragon scales gleaming under the violent gray-green light.","Blade after blade struck his body.","Clang! Clang! Clang!","Sharp metallic sounds echoed continuously as the death wind blades crashed against his scales and burst apart into wild currents of energy. Some struck his chest, some slashed at his arms, some swept across his neck, and some tried to cut into the joints between his scales, but none of them succeeded in drawing blood.","Still, unlike before, the pressure was clearly stronger now. The blades came endlessly, and each one carried the strange corrosive power of death, causing faint gray sparks to scatter every time they collided with his black scales."]},{"number":1716,"title":"Chapter 1716: Death Wind Burial Sword!","paragraphs":["Max lowered his gaze slightly and looked at the sparks bursting across his body.","His smile did not disappear.","Instead, it became a little sharper.","\"Not bad,\" he said calmly.","The elven woman’s eyes flashed.","Those two words were enough for her to understand one thing.","Even after she had tapped into her Pseudo Cosmic Path of Death Wind Concept, Max still had not taken out his true strength.","Her grip on the sword tightened.","The death wind around her became even more violent.","Then she stepped forward, and the entire arena seemed to move with her.","In the next instant, her figure turned into a streak of gray-green light and rushed toward Max, while the countless blades of Death Wind followed behind her like a storm of swords released from the depths of a death zone.","\"Good.\"","Max laughed lightly when he saw the elven woman finally release her full strength, and at that moment, the faint bias he had felt toward her because of her race slowly disappeared from his mind, because once she stood before him with her sword drawn, her Pseudo Cosmic Path of Death Wind Concept raging around her, and her entire aura pushed to its limit, she was no longer merely an elf in his eyes.","She was an opponent. She was someone strong enough to make him move beyond casual punches and simple defense. She was someone who could give him a proper battle, and that alone was enough to make the blood inside his body stir with excitement.","Max clenched his right fist.","The instant his fingers tightened, brilliant star-like energy began gathering around his knuckles, and specks of dazzling light appeared one after another, circling his fist as if tiny stars had been born around his hand.","The radiance was beautiful, almost dreamlike, but the power hidden within it was anything but gentle. It was heavy, vast, and explosive, carrying the feeling of condensed celestial force that could crush anything standing before it.","Star Fist was a third tier Divine Ability that allowed Max to gather the power of ten stars into his fist.","At first glance, that sounded simple.","It sounded like nothing more than a direct offensive ability.","But Max knew better than anyone that Star Fist was far from ordinary, because even with the strength of his current body, even with his Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline evolved to its peak, and even with his terrifying physique, he could only endure the power of seven stars without destroying himself.","He had once tried to push the power to eight stars, and that attempt had almost broken his body from the inside out. The burden of each additional star was not a simple increase. It was a terrifying leap, as if every star added another mountain of pressure onto his flesh, bones, meridians, and bloodline.","And the most absurd part was that Star Fist was only a third tier Divine Ability.","Whenever Max thought about this, even he could not help wondering just how monstrous a fifth tier Divine Ability would be. If a third tier ability already had this kind of destructive potential, then a fifth tier ability might possess power that could overturn entire battlefields or even crush worlds under the right conditions.","But now was not the time to think about that.","Max directly poured the power of five stars into his right fist.","The radiance around his hand erupted at once, and five brilliant star marks appeared faintly within the glow, each one spinning like a miniature celestial body. The light from his fist illuminated the ruined arena, pushing back the gray-green aura of Death Wind and causing the surrounding participants to feel as if a starry sky had suddenly descended into the Combat Hall.","At the same time, Max also activated the power of one thousand Draconic Essences.","Boom!","A monstrous strength awakened inside his body.","It was as if one thousand ancient dragons had opened their eyes within his flesh at the same time. His muscles tightened, his blood roared, his bones released low cracking sounds, and the black dragon scales covering his body began to shine with a deeper and more terrifying luster.","Waves of tyrannical draconic power surged through him, flowing into his limbs like molten divine iron, and the moment that power fused with the five-star force gathered in his fist, the entire arena began trembling violently.","Max did not use all five thousand of his Draconic Essences.","He knew that would be too much.","Even now, with the elven woman unleashing her strongest state, he did not believe she could survive if he combined the full strength of five thousand Draconic Essences with Star Fist. One thousand was enough. More than enough.","The elven woman felt the monstrous power rising from Max, and for the first time since she entered the arena, a trace of true danger appeared in her eyes.","That power was too heavy.","It did not feel like the strength of a human. It felt like a dragon had taken human form, wrapped its fist in starlight, and was now preparing to smash the world apart with one punch.","The pressure coming from Max forced the Death Wind around her to shake violently, and the countless blades of gray-green wind that had been cutting through the arena began to twist and break apart before his fist had even moved.","The elven woman understood at once.","If she held anything back now, she would lose without even leaving a mark behind.","Her eyes became completely calm.","She raised her sword with both hands, and the Pseudo Cosmic Path of Death Wind Concept around her surged toward the blade in a furious torrent. Endless strands of gray-green wind gathered from all directions, twisting around the sword like dying spirits trapped inside a storm.","The sword trembled violently, and the pale silver blade was soon covered in dense patterns of death wind, making it look less like a weapon and more like the core of an approaching calamity.","\"Death Wind Burial Sword.\"","Her voice was soft, but the moment she spoke those words, the air inside the arena seemed to die.","All sound vanished for an instant.","Then the wind screamed.","The elven woman stepped forward and slashed down with every bit of strength she possessed. The sword light that erupted from her blade was massive, gray-green, and terrifyingly sharp, carrying both the pure cutting power of her elven sword art and the destructive erosion of her Pseudo Cosmic Path of Death Wind Concept.","Wherever the sword light passed, the arena floor did not simply crack. It decayed. The stones lost their color, turned brittle, and were then torn into dust by the storm wrapped around the attack.","The sword light came forward like a river of deathly wind, swallowing everything in its path, and its aura was so dreadful that many participants outside the arena felt their hearts tighten.","Even the demons fell silent.","Even the humans stopped breathing.","Even the elves looked tense.","This was no ordinary strike.","This was the strongest attack of an elven genius who had survived Death Valley, comprehended Death Wind, and stepped onto a Pseudo Cosmic Path. It carried her sword, her element, her concept, her will, and every ounce of strength she could pour into one decisive attack.","For a moment, it seemed as if a part of Death Valley itself had been summoned into the arena, and the entire battlefield was about to be buried under its wind."]},{"number":1717,"title":"Chapter 1717 - 600k Killing Points!","paragraphs":["Max looked at the incoming sword light and grinned.","Then he punched forward.","\"Star Fist.\"","His fist moved.","The five-star radiance exploded.","The power of one thousand Draconic Essences roared through his body.","Boom!","The moment Max’s fist collided with the Death Wind Burial Sword, the entire arena was swallowed by a blinding burst of starry light and gray-green death wind. The shockwave slammed into the barrier with terrifying force, causing the entire Combat Hall to tremble.","The ground beneath them collapsed layer by layer, and countless cracks spread across the arena like black lightning. For an instant, no one could see what was happening inside. All they could hear was the furious collision between star power, draconic strength, sword light, and death wind.","But the stalemate lasted for only a breath.","Crack!","A sharp sound echoed through the storm.","The gray-green sword light began to break.","The elven woman’s pupils shrank.","Her strongest attack, the Death Wind Burial Sword, which carried the full force of her Pseudo Cosmic Path, was cracking under Max’s fist.","The five-star radiance tore through the death wind like a blazing celestial body piercing through rotten mist. The draconic power behind Max’s punch was even more tyrannical, crushing the sword light inch by inch, shattering the death wind, and forcing the entire attack backward with unstoppable force.","\"No...\" the elven woman whispered, her calm expression finally breaking.","Bang!","Her strongest attack shattered completely.","The Death Wind Burial Sword exploded into countless fragments of gray-green light, and before the elven woman could retreat, Max’s fist continued forward with terrifying momentum.","The remaining power of the Star Fist struck her directly, and the moment it touched her body, the five-star force and draconic strength erupted together.","Boom!","The elven woman’s body was instantly swallowed by brilliant star-like light.","There was no scream.","There was no struggle.","There was only a single burst of overwhelming power, and then her figure was obliterated into nothingness under Max’s fist. Her body vanished, her aura disappeared, and the remaining death wind scattered across the arena like broken smoke, unable to maintain its form any longer.","For a moment, the entire Combat Hall was silent.","The humans stared blankly at the ruined battlefield.","The demons looked at Max with stiff faces.","The elves were frozen in disbelief.","No one had expected the elven woman’s strongest attack to be destroyed so completely. No one had expected Max to not only break through the Pseudo Cosmic Path of Death Wind Concept, but also obliterate her in the same strike.","Among the elves, the golden-haired prince’s expression changed for the first time.","His narrowed eyes widened slightly, and his fingers tightened around the armrest beside him. The familiar feeling he had sensed from Max became even stronger after that punch, especially when the black dragon scales and star-like fist power erupted together.","\"He carries the the forbidden Divine Bloodline in his body.\" He muttered, his expression solemn. \"No wonder, he is giving me a familiar feeling.\"","Inside the shattered arena, Max slowly lowered his fist.","The black dragon scales covering his body gleamed beneath the fading starlight, and the aura of one thousand Draconic Essences gradually calmed inside him. The remnants of the elven woman’s Killing Points scattered across the battlefield, shining faintly amid the broken stones and dying wisps of death wind.","Max stood calmly in the center of the destroyed battlefield and allowed the Killing Points to enter his body.","One stream.","Then another.","Then dozens more.","The crimson lights poured into him continuously, and the number beside his name began to rise at a frightening speed. The Combat Hall’s display flickered several times as his Killing Points increased, and many participants instinctively looked up, wanting to see just how much Max had gained after defeating five demons and one powerful elf.","[Participant: Max]","[Consecutive Victories: 6]","[Killing Points: 642,000]","The moment the number appeared, a heavy silence fell over the Combat Hall.","Six hundred and forty-two thousand Killing Points.","For many participants, that was an almost absurd amount. Some had fought for days and still had not reached even a fraction of that number, yet Max had gathered this terrifying total after only six battles in the ten consecutive victory trial.","The humans stared at the display with burning eyes, and several of them could not help clenching their fists in excitement, because seeing a human dominate demons and elves in such a brutal manner made their blood boil.","The demons, however, looked as if someone had slapped them across the face again and again, because most of those Killing Points had come from their own race, and every increase in Max’s total was like another humiliation carved into their pride.","Only Karo was still calm about everything. It was as though everything that happened here didn’t affect him in anyway.","\"600k Killing Points....\" Karo sneered lightly thinking another fat sheep had appeared in the Combat Tower.","As for the elves, their expressions were far more complicated.","The elven woman had not been weak.","Everyone had seen her Pseudo Cosmic Path of Death Wind Concept, and everyone had witnessed how terrifying her strongest sword strike had been. Yet her defeat had not even looked close","Max had broken her strongest attack with one punch, obliterated her body, taken her Killing Points, and calmly stood there as if the sixth battle had merely warmed him up.","Nick stared at the number floating above the arena and felt his heart tremble again.","He had known Max would win.","He had believed that from the beginning.","But watching Max’s Killing Points jump to six hundred and forty-two thousand after only six battles still made him feel a strange pressure in his chest. This was not just winning. This was sweeping through the trial like a calamity given human form.","Inside the arena, Max looked at his current Killing Points and smiled faintly.","\"Not bad,\" he muttered.","Then he raised his eyes toward the rest of the Combat Hall.","His black dragon scales still covered his body, his right fist still carried a faint trace of fading starlight, and his calm gaze swept across demons, humans, and elves alike before finally stopping on the challengers waiting outside.","\"Four more.\""]},{"number":1718,"title":"Chapter 1718: More Victories!","paragraphs":["Soon, Max’s seventh battle began.","After seeing an elf interfere in the conflict and get obliterated by Max’s fist, the demons who had fallen silent for a short while once again found their anger burning hotter than before, because in their eyes, the fact that an elf had challenged Max before another demon could step forward was already a humiliation.","And the fact that Max had defeated her as easily as he had defeated the demons only made the situation even harder for them to accept.","This was supposed to be a trial where the strong devoured the weak, where demons could crush humans, gather Killing Points, and strengthen their reputation within the Combat Hall, but Max had turned Arena Seven into his own stage, and every battle he won made the demons look more and more pathetic.","A tall demon with dark purple skin and two curved horns finally stepped forward with a savage expression, and the moment his challenge was accepted by the trial, a beam of light descended upon him and pulled him into the arena.","His body was slimmer than the previous demons Max had killed, but the aura around him was colder and sharper, and instead of carrying a heavy weapon, he held two long black daggers that released wisps of poisonous demonic mist.","His crimson eyes stared at Max with murderous hatred, and the moment the barrier sealed the battlefield, he vanished from where he stood like a shadow melting into darkness.","The battle began almost immediately.","Inside the arena, demonic mist spread across the shattered ground, and the demon moved through it with terrifying speed, appearing and disappearing again and again as his twin daggers aimed for Max’s throat, eyes, heart, and the gaps between his dragon scales.","Each strike was vicious, precise, and filled with poison that could corrode flesh and energy alike, but Max only stood there with a faint smile, allowing the demon to circle him as if he was watching a child perform tricks. The black daggers struck his body several times, yet every collision ended with sharp metallic sounds, and not a single dagger managed to pierce through his dragon scales.","While Max’s seventh battle unfolded, outside the arena, the golden-haired elven prince remained standing among the elves with his hands behind his back, his emerald eyes fixed on Max’s figure with deep concentration.","He was not looking at the demon.","He was not interested in the battle itself.","His attention was entirely on Max.","At that moment, a faint ripple of light appeared beside him.","The silver-haired elven woman who had just been killed by Max reappeared outside the arena. She had been revived at the revival chamber present in the Combat Hall.","She did not look at the arena first.","Instead, she immediately walked to the golden-haired elven prince and knelt down on one knee before him with her head lowered.","\"I am sorry Your Highness,\" she said in a quiet voice. \"I could not do what you asked.\"","The golden-haired elven prince slowly turned his gaze away from Max and looked down at her.","There was no anger in his expression.","There was no blame either.","His calmness made the silver-haired elven woman feel even more ashamed, because she knew very well that he had only asked her to test Max’s strength, yet she had been completely overwhelmed despite using her strongest attack.","Not only had she failed to force Max to reveal his full strength, she had even been killed in front of everyone, and for an elf of her status, that was not a small humiliation.","The golden-haired elven prince looked at her for a moment before asking calmly, \"This is your first death, right?\"","The silver-haired elven woman nodded with her head still lowered.","\"Yes.\"","\"Good,\" the golden-haired elven prince said with a slight nod.","His reaction made the silver-haired elven woman raise her eyes in surprise. She had expected disappointment, or at least a few cold words about her failure, but the prince’s expression remained composed, and his tone did not carry the slightest trace of dissatisfaction.","He looked back toward the arena, where Max was still facing the seventh demon with the same careless confidence.","\"I have a few other tasks for you,\" the golden-haired elven prince continued.","At the same time, inside Arena Seven, Max’s seventh battle ended without the slightest suspense.","The demon who had challenged him had relied on speed, poison, and assassination-like attacks, but none of those methods meant anything in front of Max’s Dragon Scales Transformation.","His daggers could not pierce Max’s scales, his poison could not enter Max’s body, and his speed, which might have been terrifying to many other participants, looked almost slow in Max’s eyes.","After allowing the demon to attack several times, Max finally lost interest, and with one casual punch, he shattered the demon’s chest and obliterated him into dark fragments of light, causing another stream of Killing Points to scatter across the arena before being absorbed into his body.","[Participant: Max]","[Consecutive Victories: 7]","[Killing Points: 735,000]","The number caused another wave of shocked whispers to spread through the Combat Hall, but before those whispers could even settle, Max’s eighth opponent stepped forward. This time, the challenger was still a demon, but his aura was much stronger than the previous one.","He had four arms, a pair of curved bone blades growing from his elbows, and black flames burning around his body like a cloak of destruction.","The moment he entered the arena, he released a savage roar and declared that he would crush Max’s dragon scales with his bare hands, but his confidence lasted only until the battle began.","The four-armed demon attacked like a storm, his bone blades slashing from every direction while black flames exploded around him again and again, turning the shattered arena into a furnace of demonic fire.","His strength was truly not weak, and each of his attacks carried enough force to make the barrier tremble faintly, yet Max only walked through the flames with a faint smile, allowing the bone blades to strike his body and shatter against his scales one after another.","When the demon’s expression finally changed, Max appeared before him in a flash and drove his fist straight into the center of his chest."]},{"number":1719,"title":"Chapter 1719: Karo Makes His Move!","paragraphs":["Boom!","The four-armed demon exploded instantly.","His black flames scattered like dying embers, his body vanished into nothingness, and another large amount of Killing Points surged toward Max like crimson rivers of light.","[Participant: Max]","[Consecutive Victories: 8]","[Killing Points: 862,000]","At this moment, the entire Combat Hall had already become strangely quiet.","No one was treating Max’s victories as luck anymore.","No one was thinking that his opponents were simply too weak.","The seventh battle had been easy.","The eighth battle had been easy.","Even after the demon side sent someone stronger, even after the opponent unleashed black flames and four-armed demonic combat arts, Max had still ended the fight with a single fist. The difference in strength was so clear that even the most arrogant demons could no longer deny it.","Karo, who had earlier smiled as if everything was amusing, finally narrowed his eyes slightly when Max’s eighth victory appeared on the display.","He still did not move.","His smile remained.","But the amusement in his gaze had become sharper.","\"Eight victories already,\" Karo muttered softly, his fingers tapping once against the armrest beside him. \"Good. At least now, crushing him will be a little more meaningful.\"","Then came Max’s ninth battle.","This time, the demon who stepped into the arena was not reckless. He was tall, thin, and covered in dark red markings, and unlike the others, he did not roar or mock Max the moment he appeared.","He simply stared at Max with cold eyes, then clasped his hands together and released a strange demonic domain that spread across the arena like a pool of blood.","The moment the domain appeared, countless blood-red chains burst out from the ground and wrapped toward Max’s body, each chain releasing a thick aura of suppression that seemed designed to seal strength, restrict movement, and drain vitality.","For a brief moment, many participants thought this demon might at least force Max to take the battle seriously.","But that thought lasted only for a breath.","The blood-red chains wrapped around Max’s arms, legs, waist, and neck, yet before the demon could reveal even a trace of satisfaction, Max took one step forward.","Crack!","The chains tightened violently.","Max took another step.","Crack! Crack! Crack!","The chains began to split apart one by one.","The demon’s cold expression finally changed as he poured more demonic energy into the domain, causing even more chains to rise from the ground and coil around Max’s body like a blood-colored prison, but Max only continued walking forward.","His black dragon scales gleamed beneath the crimson light, his body stood firm under the suppression, and the terrifying physical power hidden inside him tore through the domain’s restraint with brutal force.","Then Max raised his fist.","The demon’s pupils shrank.","\"No!\"","Max punched forward.","Boom!","The blood domain shattered.","The chains shattered.","The demon shattered.","The entire arena shook as the force of the punch swept forward, and the ninth demon was obliterated into nothingness before he could even finish screaming. His Killing Points burst out like a crimson storm, and Max calmly absorbed them all while standing amid the collapsing remnants of the blood domain.","[Participant: Max]","[Consecutive Victories: 9]","[Killing Points: 1,000,000]","The moment the number appeared, the Combat Hall fell into complete silence.","One million Killing Points.","That number hung above the arena like a blazing declaration, crushing the arrogance of the demons, igniting the excitement of the humans, and making even the elves stare with solemn eyes.","For most participants, one million Killing Points was an almost unreachable amount, something that required countless battles, endless risks, and perhaps even several deaths to gather. Yet Max had reached it during his ninth consecutive victory, and he had done it with terrifying ease.","Nick stared at the display with his mouth slightly open.","Even though he had already been shocked again and again, this number still struck him hard. One million Killing Points meant Max had already entered an entirely different level from most participants in the Combat Hall. More importantly, Max had not looked exhausted.","He had not looked pressured. He had not even looked like someone who had fought nine battles in a row.","He looked calm.","He looked relaxed.","He looked as if the true battle had not even begun yet.","Inside the shattered arena, Max slowly raised his head and looked around the Combat Hall. His black dragon scales still covered his body, and the faint pressure of his bloodline spread from him like the silent breath of an ancient beast.","Demons avoided his gaze. Humans stared at him with blazing admiration. Elves watched him with narrowed eyes. Even Karo’s smile had finally become a little more dangerous.","Max looked at the floating display showing his one million Killing Points, then smiled faintly.","\"Nine victories,\" he said softly.","Then his gaze swept toward the demon side.","\"One more.\"","At this moment, the silence inside the Combat Hall did not last for long.","Just as Max’s words fell and his calm gaze swept across the demon side, a slow sound of footsteps echoed through the hall. It was not loud, but for some reason, every step seemed to fall directly upon the hearts of the watching participants, causing many of them to instinctively turn their heads toward the source of the sound.","The demons, who had been silent because of Max’s terrifying nine consecutive victories, suddenly moved aside at almost the same time, and their expressions changed from anger and humiliation to fear, respect, and a faint trace of cruel excitement.","Karo had finally stood up.","He walked forward without any hurry, his tall figure moving through the demon crowd with lazy confidence, and unlike the previous demons who had entered the arena with furious roars and savage killing intent, Karo’s expression was calm, almost pleasant, as if he was not walking toward a deadly battle but toward a prize that had already been prepared for him.","His dark hair fell loosely around his face, his crimson eyes carried a chilling amusement, and the faint smile on his lips made him look even more dangerous than those demons who shouted threats at the top of their lungs.","The moment he moved, the atmosphere changed.","The humans immediately became tense.","The elves narrowed their eyes.","Even Nick’s expression sank."]},{"number":1720,"title":"Chapter 1720: The tenth and the final battle begins!","paragraphs":["Everyone in the Combat Hall knew Karo was not like the previous demons. He had not moved when Max killed the first demon. He had not moved when Max killed five demons in a row. He had not moved when the elven woman was obliterated by Star Fist, nor had he moved when Max reached his eighth and ninth victories.","He had simply watched from the side with that faint smile, waiting as if none of the fallen demons mattered to him.","But now, Max had reached nine consecutive victories.","Now, Max had gathered one million Killing Points.","Now, there was only one battle left before he completed the ten consecutive victory trial.","And Karo had chosen this exact moment to step forward.","Many participants instantly understood his intention.","He had waited for Max to collect enough Killing Points.","He had waited for Max to become the greatest prize in the arena.","Only then had he decided to act.","Karo reached the edge of Arena Seven and looked at Max with a smile that carried neither anger nor hatred, only cold greed and confident amusement.","\"I have to admit,\" Karo said, his voice calm but clear enough for everyone nearby to hear, \"you are far stronger than I expected.\"","Max looked at him without saying anything.","Karo continued walking forward as the trial’s light descended upon him, and in the next instant, his figure appeared inside the arena, standing directly opposite Max amid the shattered battlefield.","The barrier closed around them once more, sealing the two within the ruined arena, and the moment Karo entered, the entire Combat Hall became even quieter than before.","His aura was different.","The previous demons had been brutal, violent, and filled with obvious killing intent, but Karo’s aura was deep and restrained, like a dark abyss covered by a thin layer of calm water. He did not release his full strength, yet the pressure coming from him was already enough to make several participants outside the arena feel their breathing grow heavy.","It was not the wild pressure of a beast. It was the pressure of someone who knew exactly how strong he was and had no need to prove it through noise.","Karo’s eyes moved toward the display above Max.","[Participant: Max]","[Consecutive Victories: 9]","[Killing Points: 1,000,000]","When he saw that number, the smile on his face became wider.","\"One million Killing Points,\" Karo said softly, almost as if he was admiring a treasure. \"You really did well. You crushed those useless demons, killed that elf, reached nine victories, and gathered all these points in such a short time.\"","He paused for a moment, then looked back at Max.","\"Thank you for that.\"","The moment those words left his mouth, the expressions of many participants changed.","Karo’s meaning was too obvious.","He had never cared about the demons Max killed.","He had never cared about their humiliation.","In his eyes, they had only been stepping stones used to raise Max’s value before he came to take everything for himself.","Karo raised one hand and lightly stretched his fingers, his smile still calm and arrogant.","\"You saved me quite a bit of effort,\" he said. \"Instead of wasting my time gathering Killing Points from trash, I only need to defeat you once and take everything you have collected.\"","The demon side erupted with cruel laughter after hearing his words.","Some of the demons who had been humiliated by Max’s victories finally regained their confidence, because Karo was different from the others. If the previous demons were hunters, then Karo was a predator standing above them.","His strength was acknowledged even among the demons, and many of them believed that the moment he entered the arena, Max’s arrogance had reached its end.","Nick clenched his fists outside the arena.","His face was tense.","He believed in Max’s strength, but Karo’s presence was still different from the earlier challengers. Even from outside the barrier, Nick could feel that this demon was dangerous. Not simply strong, but dangerous in a way that made one’s instincts scream.","There was something cold and calculating about him, and that made him far more frightening than the demons who had charged at Max in blind anger.","Among the elves, the golden-haired elven prince watched Karo and Max with sharp eyes. He wondered if Karo would would force Max to utilize the forbidden Divine Bloodline but he preferred Max would rather not reveal this bloodline of his.","He had his own plans for Max and that would only work if Max’s forbidden Divine Bloodline remained a secret for the rest of the elves present here.","Inside the arena, Karo slowly tilted his head and looked at Max’s black dragon scales.","\"I watched your battles,\" he said. \"Your defense is impressive. Your physical strength is even more impressive. That fist technique of yours was also not bad. But I wonder how much of your strength is left after fighting nine battles in a row.\"","Max finally smiled.","There was no fear in his expression.","There was not even caution.","Only calm amusement.","\"You waited until I reached one million Killing Points before coming in,\" Max said. \"You demons really do like dreaming.\"","Karo’s smile did not fade.","\"Dreaming?\" he repeated softly.","Max looked at him and replied, \"You are standing there as if those Killing Points already belong to you.\"","Karo’s crimson eyes narrowed slightly.","The air between them became heavier.","Max slowly raised his right hand and clenched his fist, causing a faint cracking sound to echo from his dragon-scaled fingers.","\"But there is one problem,\" Max said, his smile becoming colder. \"You still have to defeat me first.\"","Karo stared at him for a moment.","Then he laughed.","It was not a furious laugh, nor was it a mocking roar like the other demons. It was soft, controlled, and filled with chilling confidence.","\"Good,\" Karo said. \"Very good.\"","Dark demonic energy began to rise from his body.","The shattered stones around his feet trembled, and the air inside the arena seemed to sink under an invisible weight. His smile remained, but the pressure around him sharpened like a blade being slowly drawn from its sheath.","\"Then let me see,\" Karo said, \"whether the human who gathered one million Killing Points is truly worthy of keeping them.\"","Max stood across from him, his black dragon scales gleaming coldly as the faint pressure of his draconic bloodline spread around him.","The tenth and the final battle of the ten consecutive victory trial had begun."]},{"number":1721,"title":"Chapter 1721: Max’s Arrogant Words!","paragraphs":["Inside the shattered arena, the pressure between Max and Karo continued to rise, and although neither of them had made the first move yet, everyone outside the barrier could feel that this battle was completely different from the previous nine.","The earlier opponents had charged at Max with rage, greed, or arrogance, but Karo stood there with a calm smile and a dark, restrained aura that made him seem far more dangerous than all of them combined.","He was not in a hurry to attack. He was not blinded by anger. He looked at Max as if he had already measured the value of the prey before him and was simply deciding how much effort he needed to use to take everything.","Max looked at him for a moment, then slowly rolled his shoulders as the black dragon scales covering his body gave off a faint metallic sound.","\"Use your full strength,\" Max said calmly.","The words were not loud.","But in the quiet Combat Hall, they spread clearly to everyone watching.","For a brief instant, the entire demon side fell silent.","Then many demons widened their eyes, while some immediately showed furious expressions, because those words were not merely arrogant. They were almost insulting.","Karo had entered the arena after Max reached one million Killing Points, and from the way the other demons treated him, anyone could tell that his status and strength were far above the previous challengers.","Yet Max had not asked cautiously. He had not tested him first. He had directly told Karo to use his full strength, as if Karo was the weaker one who needed to prove himself.","Karo’s smile stiffened slightly.","It was a very small change, but Max noticed it.","The dark aura around Karo became colder, and a trace of irritation finally appeared in his crimson eyes. Until now, he had been watching Max with the attitude of someone looking at an entertaining opponent, but Max’s words had touched his pride.","He could accept arrogance from the strong. He could even admire it. But what he hated was when someone acted as if they were already standing above him before the battle had even begun.","\"You really are interesting,\" Karo said slowly, though the amusement in his voice had faded. \"But tell me, human, why are you acting as if you are the strongest one here?\"","Max looked at him silently.","Karo took one step forward, and the dark demonic energy around his body surged slightly, causing the broken stones near his feet to tremble.","\"Only the strongest has the right to ask another person to use their full strength,\" Karo continued, his voice becoming colder. \"Only the one standing above everyone else can speak those words without sounding like a fool. So why are you saying it to me?\"","The demons outside the arena immediately became excited again.","\"That’s right!\"","\"Who does this human think he is?\"","\"He defeated some useless trash and now thinks he can look down on Lord Karo?\"","\"Karo will make him understand what real strength means!\"","The human participants were silent, but their hearts tightened slightly. They had already seen Max display terrifying power, and many of them believed he was monstrously strong, yet Karo’s confidence was not empty either.","The aura around him alone proved that he was not someone who could be compared to the previous demons, and now that Max had provoked him so directly, the tenth battle was bound to become far more dangerous.","Among the elves, the golden-haired prince narrowed his eyes.","He was watching Max’s expression.","He wanted to see whether that arrogance was a mask or true confidence.","Then Max smiled.","No.","He grinned.","It was a wide grin filled with absolute confidence, and there was not the slightest trace of hesitation, caution, or fear in his eyes.","He looked at Karo as if the question itself was amusing, as if Karo had asked something so obvious that answering it almost felt unnecessary.","\"Because I am the strongest individual present in the Combat Hall.\"","The moment those words left Max’s mouth, the entire Combat Hall seemed to freeze.","The demons stared at him in disbelief.","The humans felt their blood boil.","The elves looked at him with solemn and complicated expressions.","Even Karo’s eyes narrowed sharply.","Max stood in the middle of the ruined arena with black dragon scales covering his entire body, his right hand loosely clenched at his side, and his smile filled with such fearless arrogance that for a moment, it felt as if he truly believed every word he had spoken.","No.","It was not belief.","It was certainty.","He was not boasting to intimidate Karo.","He was stating a fact in his own mind.","Karo stared at Max for several breaths, then slowly lowered his head and laughed. The laugh was soft at first, but it gradually became colder, deeper, and far more dangerous.","The dark demonic energy around him began to rise like black smoke from an abyss, and the air inside the arena turned heavy enough that even the barrier seemed to ripple faintly under the pressure.","\"The strongest individual in the Combat Tower?\" Karo repeated, his smile returning, though this time it carried a sharp killing intent. \"Good. Very good.\"","He raised his eyes and looked directly at Max.","\"Then I will personally tear that title from your mouth.\"","Max’s grin did not fade.","\"Try.\"","The word was simple.","But it struck the entire Combat Hall like a spark falling into a sea of oil.","In the next instant, Karo’s demonic aura erupted, and a dense wave of dark energy rushed out from his body like black smoke bursting from the mouth of an abyss.","The shattered arena trembled beneath him, the broken stones around his feet rose into the air, and the pressure he released was so much stronger than the previous demons that many participants outside the barrier immediately understood why he had been so confident.","Karo was not one of those ordinary challengers who relied on brute force and anger. His power was refined, heavy, and cruelly controlled, and the moment he released it, the atmosphere inside the Combat Hall changed as if a true predator had finally stepped onto the battlefield.","Max stood in front of him without moving, his black dragon scales gleaming coldly under the dark pressure, and the wide grin on his face did not fade even slightly."]},{"number":1722,"title":"Chapter 1722: Karo Attacks!","paragraphs":["Karo’s eyes narrowed.","\"Let us see how long that expression lasts.\"","The moment his voice fell, Karo disappeared.","He did not vanish like the earlier speed-based demon, who had relied on blurry afterimages and chaotic movement. Karo’s movement was clean, silent, and almost ghost-like, as if his body had merged with the shadow beneath his feet.","In the next breath, he appeared directly behind Max, his right arm wrapped in dense black demonic energy that twisted into the shape of a clawed beast head. The attack carried a terrifying devouring force, and the instant it descended, the air behind Max collapsed inward as if the beast head wanted to swallow everything in its path.","\"Demonic Abyss Claw.\"","Karo’s claw struck Max’s back.","Boom!","A violent explosion shook the arena, and the beast-shaped demonic energy bit down on Max’s body with enough force to tear apart a mountain of steel.","This was one of the attacks Karo normally used against humans who managed to reach the tenth battle, and in the past, many proud human geniuses had been torn open by this one strike before they even realized he had appeared behind them. Some had lost their protective armor, some had lost half their bodies, and some had died instantly.","But this time, the result was different.","Max did not even turn around.","The Demonic Abyss Claw struck his dragon scales and erupted with terrifying force, but instead of piercing through his body, the beast-shaped energy shattered against his back like a wave crashing against an unshakable cliff.","Black sparks scattered in every direction, the ground beneath Max’s feet cracked apart, and the shockwave swept forward like a storm, yet Max’s body remained completely steady. Not even his shoulders moved.","Karo’s pupils shrank slightly.","Max slowly turned his head and looked over his shoulder.","\"Is this the first attack?\"","Karo’s expression darkened for the first time.","The demons outside the arena, who had been waiting to see Max’s body torn apart, suddenly fell silent. They knew that attack. They had seen Karo use it before. They knew how many strong humans had died under it. Yet Max had taken it with his back and remained completely unharmed.","Karo pulled his hand back and retreated several steps, but the irritation in his eyes had grown stronger. He raised both arms, and the black demonic energy around him gathered above his head before rapidly condensing into nine rotating spears.","Each spear was covered in dark red runes, and their tips released a piercing aura that made the surrounding air scream. These spears did not rely on simple weight or force. They were made for penetration, and the demonic runes carved across them carried the power to drill through defenses by focusing their strength into a single point.","\"Nine Hell Piercing Spears.\"","Karo waved his hand.","The nine demonic spears shot toward Max at the same time.","They did not fly in a straight path. Instead, they crossed each other in the air, shifted directions several times, and attacked Max from different angles with terrifying speed and precision.","One aimed for his forehead, one for his throat, two for his chest, two for his shoulders, one for his heart, and the remaining two curved toward his legs. The attack was extremely vicious, and each spear released enough piercing force to make even heavily armored participants feel their scalps turn numb.","Max finally raised his hand.","But he still did not use a technique.","He simply clenched his fist and punched forward.","Bang!","The first spear shattered.","His arm moved again.","Bang! Bang! Bang!","The second, third, and fourth spears exploded into fragments of dark energy before they could touch him. Max’s movements were not flashy, but they were terrifyingly precise. Every punch landed directly on the weakest point of a spear, and each impact destroyed the condensed demonic energy with nothing more than raw physical strength.","The remaining spears tried to change direction and strike from his blind spots, but Max’s body shifted slightly, his left hand swept across the air, and three more spears were smashed apart as if they were nothing but fragile branches.","The final two spears reached his chest at the same time.","Max did not block them.","He allowed them to strike him directly.","Clang! Clang!","Two sharp metallic sounds echoed across the arena.","The demonic spears trembled violently, their sharp tips pressing against Max’s black dragon scales, but they could not enter even half an inch. A moment later, cracks spread across their bodies, and both spears shattered into black smoke.","Max looked at Karo and smiled wider.","\"Second attack.\"","Karo’s face became colder.","This time, even the humans watching from outside the arena felt a strange thrill rise in their hearts. Max was not only blocking Karo’s attacks. He was counting them. He was treating Karo’s famous killing moves as if they were test strikes from a sparring partner, and that attitude made the demons feel humiliated while making the humans feel their blood heat with excitement.","Karo’s killing intent finally sharpened.","\"Fine,\" he said coldly. \"Then try blocking this.\"","He raised one hand toward the sky, and the demonic energy around him suddenly changed. It no longer spread outward like smoke, and it no longer gathered into sharp weapons. Instead, it sank downward, pressing against the arena with a terrifying weight.","The space above Max darkened, and a huge demonic palm slowly condensed in the air, its surface covered with ancient-looking marks that seemed to carry the pressure of countless corpses buried beneath a battlefield.","The moment it appeared, the entire arena groaned under the weight, and even the barrier surrounding the battlefield rippled more violently than before.","\"Burial Demon Palm.\"","Karo pushed his hand down.","The massive demonic palm descended toward Max.","This attack was completely different from the first two. The Demonic Abyss Claw was made to tear through the body, and the Nine Hell Piercing Spears were made to pierce through defenses, but the Burial Demon Palm relied on overwhelming suppression.","It crushed everything beneath it with pure demonic pressure, burying the opponent under a force so heavy that their bones, blood, and energy would collapse at the same time.","Against other humans who had reached the tenth battle, Karo usually used this attack to end everything, because once the palm descended, even those who survived were often left kneeling, broken, and unable to fight again.","The demonic palm fell."]},{"number":1723,"title":"Chapter 1723: Karo’s Pseudo Cosmic Path!","paragraphs":["The entire arena sank.","Cracks spread across the ground beneath Max’s feet, and the ruined stones around him were crushed into powder before the attack even landed. The pressure was so overwhelming that many people outside the arena felt their chests tighten despite the barrier separating them from the battlefield.","Nick’s expression changed slightly, and even the golden-haired elven prince narrowed his eyes as he watched how Max would respond.","Max looked up.","Then he laughed.","He bent his knees slightly, clenched his right fist, and punched straight upward.","There was no Star Fist.","There was no Seven Divine Veins.","There was no additional burst of Draconic Essences beyond the physical strength already raging inside his transformed body.","It was only a punch.","A punch backed by a body so terrifyingly strong that it no longer seemed human.","Boom!","Max’s fist collided with the descending demonic palm, and the entire arena shook as if two mountains had smashed into each other. The massive palm stopped in midair for a brief instant, and the ancient marks across its surface flashed violently as Karo poured more demonic energy into it, trying to crush Max beneath its weight.","Max’s grin remained unchanged.","His fist pushed upward.","Crack!","A long crack appeared across the demonic palm.","Karo’s expression changed.","Max stepped forward, his arm muscles tightening beneath the black dragon scales, and with one more burst of raw strength, he punched through the entire Burial Demon Palm.","Bang!","The huge demonic palm exploded above him.","A storm of black energy scattered across the arena, and the pressure that had nearly buried the battlefield vanished in an instant. Broken waves of demonic force swept across Max’s body, but he stood beneath them with his fist still raised, his dragon scales untouched and his gaze locked on Karo.","\"Third attack.\"","Max slowly lowered his fist.","The Combat Hall was completely silent.","Three attacks.","Three powerful attacks that Karo had used many times before to crush humans who had reached the tenth battle.","One had struck Max’s back and failed.","One had surrounded him with nine piercing spears and failed.","One had descended from above with overwhelming suppression and failed.","Max had blocked them all with physical strength alone.","Karo stood opposite him, his face no longer carrying the same casual smile from before. His crimson eyes stared at Max with cold intensity, and the dark aura around his body slowly became deeper, more dangerous, and far more serious.","Max tilted his head slightly and looked at him with that same fearless grin.","\"Now,\" he said, his voice calm but arrogant enough to shake the pride of every demon present, \"are you ready to use your real strength? Your Pseudo Cosmic Path?\"","The moment those words echoed across Arena Seven, the atmosphere inside the Combat Hall changed once again.","Many demons outside the arena felt their expressions stiffen, because although they knew Karo was terrifyingly strong, very few of them had actually seen him use his Pseudo Cosmic Path with their own eyes.","In the Cosmic Ascension Conference, every participant treated their Pseudo Cosmic Path as one of their greatest trump cards, and unless they were forced into a dangerous situation, most geniuses would never reveal it so early.","After all, this conference was not a single battle. It was a brutal competition filled with monsters from different races, and once a powerful trump card was exposed, others would begin studying it, preparing against it, and looking for weaknesses.","Karo stared at Max for several breaths.","Then he slowly laughed.","The irritation in his eyes did not disappear, but it was gradually covered by something darker and more dangerous. It was not simple anger. It was excitement.","He had entered the arena thinking that Max was only a fat sheep carrying one million Killing Points, but after those three attacks failed, he could no longer see Max as ordinary prey.","This human’s body was absurdly strong, his dragon scales were almost impossible to break, and his confidence was not merely empty arrogance.","For the first time, Karo felt that crushing Max might actually be enjoyable.","\"I truly did not expect this,\" Karo said slowly, his crimson eyes fixed on Max. \"I never thought I would have to use my Pseudo Cosmic Path this early in the Cosmic Ascension Conference.\"","His voice was calm, but every demon outside the arena heard the weight hidden inside his words.","The humans became tense.","The elves focused their gazes.","Nick’s fists tightened again.","Among the elves, the golden-haired elven prince leaned forward slightly, and even the silver-haired elven woman beside him stared at Karo with solemn eyes, because she had already used her own Pseudo Cosmic Path against Max and had been crushed, so she understood very well that if Karo dared to reveal his at this moment, then it meant his path had to be far more terrifying than ordinary comprehension.","Karo’s grin widened.","\"But you are worthy,\" he said. \"A human who can block my three attacks with physical strength alone is at least worthy enough to witness my Pseudo Cosmic Path.\"","As soon as those words fell, the dark demonic energy around Karo disappeared.","It did not scatter.","It did not weaken.","It simply sank into his body in an instant, and for a brief moment, Karo’s aura became completely silent.","That silence was terrifying.","It felt like the moment before a corpse opened its eyes.","Then the arena darkened.","A black-red light spread from beneath Karo’s feet, and in the next breath, countless cracks appeared across the shattered battlefield. From those cracks, thick strands of abyssal mist rose slowly, and within that mist, countless faint silhouettes began to appear.","Some looked like broken warriors. Some looked like beasts. Some looked like demons. Some looked like humans. Their forms were incomplete, their faces were distorted, and their bodies seemed to be made from smoke, blood, resentment, and death.","The air became heavy with despair.","Karo slowly raised both hands.","\"Pseudo Cosmic Path,\" he said softly. \"Abyssal Grave of the Fallen.\""]},{"number":1724,"title":"Chapter 1724: Abyssal Grave of the Fallen!","paragraphs":["Boom!","The entire arena trembled.","The black-red mist exploded outward and swallowed everything around him, forming a massive grave-like domain that seemed to drag the battlefield into the depths of an ancient abyss. Tombstones made of condensed demonic energy rose from the ground one after another, each one covered in strange runes that pulsed like bleeding wounds.","The silhouettes within the mist began to move, and every time they shifted, low whispers filled the air, as if countless fallen souls were crying, cursing, and begging from the bottom of a forgotten battlefield.","This was Karo’s Pseudo Cosmic Path.","Abyssal Grave of the Fallen.","It was not a simple demonic technique.","It was a path built from slaughter, resentment, decay, and domination. Every enemy Karo had crushed, every warrior whose will he had broken, and every opponent whose pride had been buried beneath his power had become part of the idea behind this path.","It carried the terrifying concept of turning a battlefield into a grave, turning resistance into despair, and turning the strength of the fallen into nourishment for the one who ruled above them.","The moment the Abyssal Grave of the Fallen fully appeared, the pressure inside the arena rose to a frightening level.","The shattered stones around Max began sinking into the ground as if pulled by invisible hands. The air around him became thick and oppressive, and the black-red mist tried to coil around his body, searching for gaps in his dragon scales as if it wanted to drag him into the grave-like domain and bury him there forever.","The tombstones surrounding Karo released waves of suppressive force, and each wave carried a different kind of pressure. Some attacked the body. Some attacked the spirit. Some attacked the vitality. Some attacked the will.","Outside the arena, many participants felt chills run down their backs.","Even though they were protected by the barrier, they could still feel the terrifying aura of Karo’s Pseudo Cosmic Path. It was not as sharp as the elven woman’s Death Wind, but it was far more oppressive.","The Death Wind wanted to cut and corrode. The Abyssal Grave of the Fallen wanted to bury everything. It wanted to turn the entire arena into a graveyard and make anyone trapped within it feel that every step, every breath, and every heartbeat was being pulled closer to death.","Several humans turned pale.","Some demons began laughing with renewed confidence.","The elves became solemn.","The golden-haired elven prince narrowed his eyes and muttered, \"So this is his path.\"","The silver-haired elven woman beside him felt her expression tighten. Compared to her Death Wind path, Karo’s Pseudo Cosmic Path felt heavier and more complete. It was not necessarily purer, but it carried a much more brutal killing intent, and the way it suppressed the whole battlefield made it extremely difficult for an opponent to fight freely.","Inside the arena, Karo stood at the center of the grave-like domain, surrounded by tombstones, abyssal mist, and countless fallen silhouettes.","His aura had changed completely.","Before, he had looked like a dangerous demon genius.","Now, he looked like the ruler of a battlefield graveyard.","His crimson eyes glowed from within the mist, and his grin became crueler as the fallen silhouettes behind him lowered their heads as if kneeling before him.","\"Do you feel it, human?\" Karo asked softly. \"This is the grave prepared for everyone who thinks they can stand above me.\"","The black-red mist surged forward.","The tombstones pulsed.","The fallen silhouettes screamed silently.","Max stood within the oppressive domain, and the black dragon scales covering his body reflected the eerie glow of the abyssal grave. The pressure tried to push him down. The mist tried to bury him. The whispers tried to invade his mind.","But Max did not kneel.","He did not retreat.","He did not even stop smiling.","Instead, his grin became wider as he felt the terrifying power pressing toward him from all directions.","\"That is more like it,\" Max said, his voice carrying genuine excitement.","Karo’s eyes sharpened.","Max slowly clenched his fists, and the black dragon scales covering his arms gave off a deep metallic sound as the draconic power inside his body stirred once more.","Max continued, looking straight at Karo through the abyssal mist, \"this finally feels like a a good battle!\"","Karo’s grin slowly widened when he saw Max still standing calmly inside the Abyssal Grave of the Fallen, and although the human’s confidence irritated him, it also made the killing intent in his heart grow stronger, because the more Max refused to bend beneath his Pseudo Cosmic Path, the more enjoyable it would be to crush him in front of everyone.","The black-red mist around the arena surged violently, the tombstones made from condensed demonic energy trembled one after another, and the countless fallen silhouettes standing within the grave-like domain raised their heads at the same time, their hollow eyes locking onto Max as if they had all received the same command.","\"Since you like acting superior so much,\" Karo said coldly, his voice echoing through the mist like the whisper of a graveyard, \"then show me whether you can still keep smiling after this.\"","The moment his words fell, Karo raised both hands, and the entire Abyssal Grave of the Fallen answered him.","Boom!","The tombstones around the arena shattered at the same time, and the broken fragments did not scatter randomly. Instead, they rose into the air and fused with the black-red mist, gathering into a massive demonic spear above Karo’s head.","The spear was enormous, dark, and covered in countless blood-like runes, while the fallen silhouettes within the domain began to dissolve into streams of resentment that flowed into the weapon.","Every silhouette that entered the spear made its aura grow more terrifying, and in only a few breaths, the spear no longer looked like a simple attack. It looked like the condensed hatred of an entire battlefield, a weapon created to bury the living together with the dead.","\"Abyssal Burial Spear.\"","Karo’s crimson eyes burned with cruel light as he looked at Max.","\"This spear contains the suppressive force of my Pseudo Cosmic Path and the resentment of the fallen souls buried within my grave.\""]},{"number":1725,"title":"Chapter 1725: Releasing the Full Might of 5000 Draconic Essences!","paragraphs":["The massive spear trembled in the air, and its pressure descended before the attack itself moved. The ground beneath Max sank instantly, the broken stones around him were crushed into dust, and black-red mist coiled around his legs like countless hands trying to hold him in place.","The Abyssal Grave of the Fallen was not simply strengthening Karo’s attack. It was also suppressing Max’s movement, his aura, his vitality, and even the flow of power within his body, as if the entire domain wanted to pin him down and make him receive the spear like a condemned prisoner waiting for execution.","Outside the arena, many participants felt their faces turn pale.","Even the demons who supported Karo instinctively quieted down, because they could feel that this was no ordinary move. This was a killing attack born from his Pseudo Cosmic Path, a strike that had likely been prepared to destroy other peak geniuses during the later stages of the Cosmic Ascension Conference.","Yet now, because of Max’s arrogance and overwhelming defense, Karo had brought it out during this tenth battle.","The golden-haired elven prince stared at the massive Abyssal Burial Spear without blinking.","The silver-haired elven woman beside him tightened her grip, and a trace of lingering fear appeared in her eyes, because even from outside the barrier, she could sense that if this attack had been aimed at her, her Death Wind Burial Sword would have been shattered before the spear even fully descended.","Nick’s expression became extremely tense.","He had already seen Max perform impossible feats again and again, but the pressure coming from Karo’s attack was different from everything before it. It was heavy, sinister, and suffocating, and even though Nick believed in Max, his instincts still screamed that this spear was dangerous.","Karo looked at Max and sneered.","\"Where is your Pseudo Cosmic Path, human?\" he asked. \"You claimed to be the strongest individual in the Combat Tower. You said I should use my full strength. Now I have shown you my path, so show me yours.\"","Max raised his head and looked at the massive spear gathering above Karo.","For a moment, he did not speak.","Then he smiled lightly.","\"You want to see my Pseudo Cosmic Path?\"","Karo’s eyes narrowed. \"If you have one.\"","Max’s smile widened slightly, but his gaze became colder.","\"You are not worthy.\"","The entire Combat Hall seemed to fall silent.","Karo’s expression froze.","Max continued, his voice calm and direct, as if he was not insulting Karo but merely stating something obvious.","\"You are not strong enough to see it.\"","Those words struck Karo harder than any attack could have.","The black-red mist around him erupted violently, and the Abyssal Burial Spear above his head released a terrifying scream as more and more resentment poured into it. His crimson eyes became icy with killing intent, and the faint grin on his face disappeared completely. Until now, he had been angry and irritated, but this was the first time Max had truly enraged him.","\"You will regret those words,\" Karo said, his voice low and murderous.","Max did not bother answering him.","Instead, he slowly clenched both fists.","The next instant, the power inside Max’s body changed.","Until now, even though Max had used Dragon Scales Transformation and even released the strength of one thousand Draconic Essences earlier, he had still been suppressing the true depth of his physical power.","The strength slumbering inside him had not been fully awakened. The draconic essence within his body had only been partially stirred. But now, as Karo’s Abyssal Burial Spear prepared to descend, Max finally loosened the restraint he had placed upon himself.","Boom!","The full might of five thousand Draconic Essences erupted inside his body.","It was not a simple increase in strength.","It was an explosion of pure draconic force so overwhelming that the entire arena seemed to shake under the weight of his existence. Max’s blood roared like a thousand rivers of molten thunder, his bones released deep cracking sounds like ancient gates being forced open, and the black dragon scales covering his body began to shine with a darker and more terrifying light.","Each scale seemed to awaken completely, and the chaotic patterns moving across them became brighter, deeper, and more alive, as if countless black dragons were swimming beneath the surface of his skin.","The air around Max collapsed outward.","The black-red mist trying to coil around his body was torn apart instantly.","The suppressive force of the Abyssal Grave of the Fallen, which had been trying to bury him beneath its pressure, was violently pushed back by the sheer brutality of his physical aura.","The tombstone fragments floating in the air began trembling, the fallen silhouettes around Karo flickered wildly, and even the massive Abyssal Burial Spear above him shook as if it had suddenly sensed an existence far more ferocious than itself awakening below.","The Combat Hall trembled.","The barrier around Arena Seven rippled again and again, and faint cracks of light began spreading across its surface as if the protection itself was struggling to contain the monstrous pressure erupting from Max’s body.","The participants outside the arena instinctively stepped back. Some weaker humans felt their legs soften. Several demons who had been laughing moments ago turned silent with stiff faces. Even the elves, who usually maintained their composure, looked shaken as the invisible weight of Max’s unleashed draconic power pressed against their senses.","This was no longer the aura of a genius.","This was the aura of a calamity.","Max stood at the center of the destroyed arena, covered in black dragon scales, with five thousand Draconic Essences raging through his body like five thousand furious dragons roaring in unison. The ground beneath his feet could no longer bear the pressure and collapsed downward, forming a deeper crater around him.","Every breath he took caused the surrounding air to tremble, and every slight movement of his fingers released a faint shockwave that scattered the deathly mist nearby.","Karo’s eyes widened despite himself.","For the first time since entering the arena, his confidence wavered.","He had expected Max to be strong.","He had expected Max to have hidden power.","But he had not expected this.","The raw physical strength now erupting from Max was so monstrous that it made his Abyssal Grave of the Fallen feel pressured, and that was something Karo had never imagined happening against a human who had not even revealed his Pseudo Cosmic Path."]},{"number":1726,"title":"Chapter 1726: Karo’s Panick!","paragraphs":["Max slowly raised his gaze and looked at Karo through the storm of black-red mist and draconic pressure.","His smile returned.","But this time, it looked far more dangerous than before.","\"You wanted me to reveal my path,\" Max said calmly, his voice carrying through the trembling arena. \"But for someone like you, this is enough.\"","Karo’s face twisted with fury.","Above him, the Abyssal Burial Spear finally finished forming, and the massive weapon released a world-burying pressure as it pointed straight toward Max.","\"Die!\"","Karo pushed both hands down.","The Abyssal Burial Spear descended.","At the same time, Max stepped forward.","The entire arena cracked beneath that single step.","The Abyssal Burial Spear descended with world-burying pressure, and as it fell, the entire Abyssal Grave of the Fallen seemed to move with it. The black-red mist roared upward like a sea of death, the broken tombstones released waves of suppressive force, and the countless fallen silhouettes dissolved into the spear one after another, causing its aura to become heavier, darker, and far more terrifying with every passing instant.","It was no longer merely an attack thrown by Karo. It was the full wrath of his Pseudo Cosmic Path, a strike created to bury Max beneath the resentment of the dead and crush his body, spirit, vitality, and will in one blow.","Yet Max only stepped forward.","The arena cracked beneath his foot.","Then his right fist clenched.","Brilliant star-like radiance erupted around his knuckles, and five blazing star marks appeared within the light, each one spinning with terrifying force as if five miniature stars had been compressed into his fist.","At the same time, the full power of his five thousand Draconic Essences raged through his body without the slightest suppression, causing his black dragon scales to shine with a deep chaotic light, while the sound of roaring dragons seemed to echo from within his flesh.","His blood boiled like molten thunder, his bones trembled with overwhelming strength, and the power gathering in his fist became so monstrous that even the air around his arm began to collapse and twist.","Star Fist.","Power of five stars.","Full release of five thousand Draconic Essences.","The moment these two forces fused together, the entire Combat Hall seemed to lose its sound.","Even Karo’s expression changed.","For the first time, his eyes showed true fear.","He could feel it clearly now. The power gathering in Max’s fist was not something his Abyssal Burial Spear could easily suppress.","It was violent, pure, and unbelievably heavy, and when that draconic strength merged with the five-star power, it felt as if Max was not preparing to punch with a human fist, but with the crushing weight of five stars and the combined rage of five thousand dragons.","\"No...\" Karo muttered instinctively, but the word barely left his mouth before Max moved.","Max punched forward.","Boom!","The five-star radiance shot upward like a blazing celestial pillar, and the draconic power inside it roared with enough force to shake the entire arena. The fist light collided head-on with the Abyssal Burial Spear, and for a single instant, the spear seemed to stop in midair.","Black-red energy and starry light crashed against each other, deathly mist and chaotic draconic pressure tore through the battlefield, and the shockwave that erupted from their collision slammed into the barrier so fiercely that countless ripples spread across its surface.","Karo gritted his teeth and poured everything into his Pseudo Cosmic Path.","The Abyssal Grave of the Fallen trembled violently, and every remaining tombstone shattered at once, transforming into more abyssal force that surged into the spear. The fallen silhouettes screamed without sound, and their resentment poured into the attack like fuel thrown into a dying flame.","Karo’s crimson eyes became bloodshot as he tried to force the spear downward, desperate to bury Max beneath the full might of his path.","But Max’s fist did not retreat.","It rose.","One inch.","Then another.","Crack!","A sharp sound echoed from the Abyssal Burial Spear.","Karo’s pupils contracted.","A long crack appeared across the body of the massive spear, and from that crack, brilliant star-like light burst outward like dawn tearing through a grave. The black-red runes covering the spear flickered wildly, but they could not withstand the force pressing against them.","Max’s five-star fist power crushed forward, and the strength of five thousand Draconic Essences surged behind it like an endless tide, pushing through the spear’s suppressive power with brutal and unstoppable force.","Crack! Crack! Crack!","More cracks spread across the Abyssal Burial Spear.","The enormous weapon that had carried the resentment of the fallen and the pressure of Karo’s Pseudo Cosmic Path began to break apart under Max’s punch. Its tip shattered first, then the shaft split open, then the blood-red runes collapsed one after another, and the countless fallen silhouettes trapped within the spear were torn apart by the blazing star radiance before they could even struggle.","Karo’s face twisted in disbelief.","\"Impossible!\"","Max’s eyes remained cold.","His fist pushed forward completely.","Bang!","The Abyssal Burial Spear exploded.","A storm of black-red energy burst across the arena, but before it could spread, Max’s fist light tore through it and continued forward. The five-star radiance did not stop after destroying the spear.","It rushed straight into the heart of the Abyssal Grave of the Fallen, smashing through the black-red mist, shattering the remaining tombstones, and crushing the grave-like domain from the inside out.","The entire Pseudo Cosmic Path began to collapse.","The battlefield graveyard that Karo had summoned trembled violently, and the abyssal mist that had swallowed the arena was ripped apart by Max’s draconic pressure. Tombstones cracked and vanished.","Fallen silhouettes screamed and dissolved. The suppressive force that had tried to bury everything broke apart like rotten wood beneath a hammer. In only a few breaths, the terrifying Abyssal Grave of the Fallen, which had made humans, demons, and elves feel chills across their backs, was being destroyed by the raw, overwhelming might of Max’s fist.","Karo staggered backward.","Blood burst from his mouth.","His Pseudo Cosmic Path was connected to his power, his will, and his foundation. The moment Max began crushing it, the backlash struck him like a mountain collapsing onto his soul. His body trembled, his aura became chaotic, and the confident demon who had entered the arena to steal one million Killing Points finally looked as if he had seen something beyond his understanding.","Max stepped forward again.","His fist light pierced through the final layer of the Abyssal Grave of the Fallen.","Bang!","The grave-like domain shattered completely.","The black-red mist vanished.","The tombstones disappeared.","The fallen silhouettes were annihilated.","Karo’s Pseudo Cosmic Path was destroyed in front of everyone.","The Combat Hall fell into deathly silence.","Then Max appeared before Karo.","There was no warning.","There was no chance to dodge.","Karo had barely raised his head when Max’s fist, still burning with five-star radiance and the terrifying power of five thousand Draconic Essences, arrived in front of his chest.","For the first time, Karo’s face showed panic.","\"Wait...\"","Max’s expression did not change.","His fist landed.","Boom!","Karo’s body bent violently around the impact, and the remaining demonic energy protecting him shattered instantly. The five-star power erupted through his body, while the force of five thousand Draconic Essences crushed his bones, organs, and demonic core in the same breath.","His crimson eyes widened, his mouth opened, and the arrogance that had been carved into his face since the beginning vanished completely beneath the overwhelming force of Max’s punch.","Then his body exploded into nothingness.","There was no final roar.","There was no chance to resist.","Karo, the demon who had waited until Max gathered one million Killing Points, the demon who had revealed his Pseudo Cosmic Path and tried to bury Max beneath the Abyssal Grave of the Fallen, was obliterated by a single punch.","The moment he died, an enormous amount of crimson light erupted across the arena.","His Killing Points scattered like a storm of blood-red stars, filling the shattered battlefield with dazzling radiance. The amount was far greater than any opponent Max had defeated so far, and the display above the arena flickered violently as the trial recognized the end of the tenth battle."]},{"number":1727,"title":"Chapter 1727 - 8 Million Killing Points!","paragraphs":["Max stood alone in the center of the destroyed arena.","His black dragon scales gleamed.","His right fist slowly lowered.","The remnants of star radiance faded around his hand, while the monstrous power of five thousand Draconic Essences still raged inside his body like dragons unwilling to return to sleep.","Outside the arena, no one spoke.","The demons stared blankly at the place where Karo had vanished, their faces pale and frozen with disbelief.","The humans looked at Max as if they were seeing a legend being born before their eyes.","The elves remained silent, but their gazes had changed completely.","Among them, the golden-haired elven prince’s expression was no longer calm. His emerald eyes were fixed on Max, and the familiar feeling in his heart had now turned into something close to certainty, though that certainty also brought a trace of deep unease.","Nick swallowed with difficulty.","He had believed Max was strong.","But this was no longer simply strong.","Max had destroyed Karo’s strongest attack, shattered his Pseudo Cosmic Path, and killed him in one punch.","Inside the arena, Max raised his hand, and the countless Killing Points left behind by Karo surged toward him like a crimson tide.","He absorbed them all without hesitation.","Then he looked at the empty space where Karo had stood and smiled faintly.","\"You wanted my one million Killing Points,\" Max said softly. \"In the end, you only delivered yours.\"","The moment Karo’s body was obliterated, the entire ruined arena was drowned in crimson light.","It was not like the previous opponents.","When the other demons and the elven woman had died, their Killing Points had scattered like bright streams or small storms of blood-red sparks, but the amount released from Karo was on an entirely different level.","The crimson radiance that burst out from where his body had vanished spread across the arena like a sea of blood-colored stars, filling the shattered battlefield with so much light that even the black dragon scales covering Max’s body were dyed in a deep red glow.","Countless streams of Killing Points floated in the air, dense, dazzling, and overwhelming, and for a moment, the entire Combat Hall felt as if it had fallen beneath a crimson sky.","The display above the arena flickered violently.","Then Karo’s total appeared for everyone to see.","[Defeated Participant: Karo]","[Killing Points: 6,000,000]","The moment that number appeared, the Combat Hall fell into a silence so deep that even breathing seemed to stop.","Six million Killing Points.","Karo had possessed six million Killing Points.","That amount was enough to make countless participants risk their lives, enough to make demons betray one another, enough to make humans and elves feel their hearts tremble with greed and fear at the same time.","It was not the kind of number an ordinary participant could gather through a few lucky battles. It represented slaughter, domination, and the defeat of many powerful opponents before he had ever stepped into Arena Seven.","Yet now, all of it belonged to Max.","The trial’s rules activated instantly.","The crimson sea of Killing Points surged toward Max from every direction, rushing into his body like countless rivers returning to an endless ocean. One stream after another poured into him, wrapping around his dragon-scaled figure before disappearing into his body, and with every passing breath, the number beside his name began rising at a terrifying speed.","The Combat Hall’s display flashed again and again, unable to hide the absurd increase as Karo’s six million points were absorbed completely.","[Participant: Max]","[Consecutive Victories: 10]","[Previous Killing Points: 1,000,000]","[Absorbed Killing Points: 6,000,000]","[Current Killing Points: 7,000,000]","[Participant Max Morgan is awarded 1,000,000 KP for completing the Ten Consecutive Victory Trial.]","[Current Killing Points: 8,000,000]","The moment the final number appeared, a heavy pressure seemed to descend upon everyone present.","Eight million Killing Points.","Max had entered the tenth battle with one million Killing Points, and after killing Karo, that number had skyrocketed to eight million in an instant. The total was so outrageous that many participants could only stare at the display with blank expressions, unable to process what they were seeing.","A human who had just completed the ten consecutive victory trial had not only survived Karo’s Pseudo Cosmic Path, but had crushed it, killed him, and taken all six million Killing Points he had accumulated.","The demons looked as if their souls had been struck.","Some stared at the empty place where Karo had vanished, their faces pale with disbelief, while others looked at Max with fear that they could no longer hide. Karo had not been a nameless demon.","He had been someone strong enough to make them confident, someone they believed could end Max’s arrogance, someone who had carried six million Killing Points as proof of his dominance. But now, Karo was gone, and the proof of his strength had become Max’s reward.","The humans, on the other hand, felt their blood burn.","Several of them clenched their fists so hard their knuckles turned white, their eyes fixed on Max as if they were witnessing something that would be spoken of long after this trial ended. Nine victories had already made him terrifying. Killing Karo made him monstrous.","But reaching eight million Killing Points after completing the tenth battle made him something else entirely.","A calamity.","A legend.","A human genius who had stepped over demons and elves alike in front of the entire Combat Hall.","Among the elves, the golden-haired elven prince stared at the number above Max with narrowed eyes, but this time, even he could not maintain his earlier calm completely. eight million Killing Points was not the only thing that mattered.","What mattered more was how Max had obtained them. He had destroyed the Abyssal Grave of the Fallen without revealing his own Pseudo Cosmic Path, and he had killed Karo using only his Dragon Scales Transformation, his five-star Star Fist, and the full might of five thousand Draconic Essences.","That meant Max was still hiding something.","The silver-haired elven woman beside the prince also stared at Max in silence, and the memory of being obliterated by his fist returned to her mind with uncomfortable clarity.","She now understood that when Max had fought her, he truly had held back. If he had used the same power against her that he had used against Karo, there would not have even been a clash.","Inside the arena, Max slowly lowered his hand after absorbing the last stream of crimson light.","The monstrous power of five thousand Draconic Essences still raged inside him, but his expression remained calm, almost relaxed, as if killing Karo and gaining six million Killing Points had only been a natural outcome.","The black dragon scales covering his body gleamed under the fading crimson radiance, and the ruined arena beneath his feet looked like it had been crushed by the landing of an ancient beast.","Then a notification appeared before his eyes.","[Ten Consecutive Victory Trial Completed]","[Victories: 10]","[Final Killing Points: 8,000,000]","[Trial Result: Perfect Completion]","Max looked at the notification for a moment.","Then he smiled faintly.","\"Eight Million points is nice.\"","His voice was not loud, but in the silent Combat Hall, many participants heard it clearly.","The demons felt their faces burn with humiliation.","The humans almost laughed aloud.","Nick stared at Max with wide eyes, then slowly exhaled as if he had only just remembered how to breathe.","\"Eight million...\" Nick muttered under his breath, his voice filled with disbelief. \"He actually reached eight million Killing Points in one trial.\"","Max raised his eyes and swept his gaze across the Combat Hall.","This time, no demon dared to mock him.","No elf dared to underestimate him.","No human dared to think his arrogance was empty.","He had stood in Arena Seven, taken ten consecutive battles, killed Karo, shattered a Pseudo Cosmic Path, and walked out with eight million Killing Points.","At that moment, everyone understood one thing.","The name Max had truly entered the sight of every race present in the Combat Tower."]},{"number":1728,"title":"Chapter 1728: Karo went into Hiding!","paragraphs":["After the final notification faded from his vision, Max remained standing in the center of the destroyed arena for a few more moments, allowing the last traces of crimson light to disappear into his body while the number of eight million Killing Points still lingered above him like a declaration no one in the Combat Hall could ignore.","The barrier around Arena Seven slowly opened, and only then did Max loosen the power raging inside him, letting the full might of five thousand Draconic Essences settle back into the depths of his body while the black dragon scales covering him gradually lost some of their overwhelming pressure, though they did not disappear completely.","He stepped down from the arena.","The moment his foot touched the ground outside the battlefield, many participants instinctively moved away from him. It was not because Max had released any killing intent toward them, and it was not because he had said anything threatening.","It was simply because they had all seen what had happened inside the arena. They had seen demons crushed with bare fists, an elf genius obliterated by Star Fist, and Karo’s Pseudo Cosmic Path shattered completely before he himself was killed in one punch. After witnessing all of that, no one could look at Max as an ordinary participant anymore.","Max ignored their reactions.","His gaze moved across the Combat Hall.","He was looking for Karo.","Although he had killed Karo in the tenth battle, Max did not believe that the demon had been completely eliminated from the Eternal Hourglass. Just like the silver-haired elven woman had reappeared after being killed, Karo should still have more lives left.","If Max guessed correctly, Karo should have three more lives, which meant the demon should have revived somewhere inside the Combat Hall after paying the price of death.","But after scanning the demon side, Max did not see him.","He looked across the corners of the hall, toward the shadowed areas where some participants stood silently, toward the groups of demons who had gathered together, and even toward the distant exits leading away from the Combat Hall, but Karo was nowhere to be found.","The demons who had once stood proudly around him now looked tense and uneasy, and none of them dared to meet Max’s gaze for long.","A faint sneer appeared on Max’s face.","\"So he is hiding really well.\"","His voice was soft, but the mockery in it was clear.","Karo had entered the arena with confidence, waited for Max to gather one million Killing Points, and acted as if everything Max possessed already belonged to him. Yet after being killed once, he had vanished so quickly that Max could not even find his shadow in the Combat Hall. The thought made Max’s smile turn colder.","\"Then he should keep hiding well,\" Max muttered, his eyes narrowing slightly as he glanced once more across the demon side. \"Because if I see him again, I will kill him again.\"","The demons who heard those words felt their expressions stiffen.","No one dared to respond.","If another human had said such a thing after killing Karo once, the demons would have erupted in fury and ridicule. But when Max said it while standing there with eight million Killing Points, black dragon scales still covering parts of his body, and the pressure of his previous battle still lingering around him, even the most arrogant demons could only swallow their anger in silence.","Thinking along those lines, Max finally withdrew his gaze and walked back toward Nick.","The crowd parted wherever he went.","Some humans looked at him with bright eyes filled with admiration, while a few even seemed to want to speak, but none of them found the courage to step forward first. The elves watched him with complicated expressions, especially the golden-haired elven prince, whose gaze followed Max’s figure with silent intensity.","The demons, on the other hand, looked at him with resentment, fear, and humiliation, but after what had happened to Karo, none of them dared to challenge him casually.","Nick was already waiting for him.","The moment Max approached, Nick’s tense expression broke into a wide smile, and the shock in his eyes finally gave way to excitement that he could no longer suppress. He looked at Max as if he was seeing him properly for the first time, and although he had always believed Max was strong, the ten consecutive victory trial had completely shattered his previous understanding of that strength.","\"You really did it,\" Nick said, his smile widening even more. \"Ten consecutive victories, eight million Killing Points, and you even killed Karo in front of everyone.\"","Max looked at him and smiled faintly.","\"That demon wanted my points,\" Max said casually. \"So I took his instead. Besides, I already told you I would take care of him.\"","Nick stared at him for a second, then laughed under his breath.","Only Max could say something like that so casually after shaking the entire Combat Hall.","Behind them, the display above Arena Seven still showed Max’s final result, and even though the trial had ended, many participants continued staring at the number as if they wanted to carve it into their memories.","[Participant: Max]","[Ten Consecutive Victory Trial Completed]","[Final Killing Points: 8,000,000]","Nick looked at the display again, then turned back to Max with a grin that he could not hide.","\"Do you even know how insane that number looks?\"","Max glanced at the display once, then shrugged lightly.","\"It is only the beginning. I still have to kill Karo three more times and then there is also his brother Munro. I have to take care of him too. I believe they would deliver me a good amount of Killing Points for sure.\"","Nick’s smile froze for a moment.","Then he shook his head and laughed helplessly, because after everything he had just witnessed, he could not even say Max was exaggerating.","Max looked at Nick and said calmly, \"I am heading toward the exit of the city.\"","Nick’s smile faded slightly when he heard that.","\"The exit?\" he asked. \"Already?\""]},{"number":1729,"title":"Chapter 1729: Elf Prince’s Approach!","paragraphs":["Max nodded, and his expression became a little colder as the name of his next target appeared in his mind. \"I still have to take care of Munro. After that, I will be heading somewhere else.\"","Nick understood immediately.","Munro.","The moment that name appeared, Nick’s expression also turned serious. He had not forgotten the reason Max had entered this place, nor had he forgotten that Max still had enemies waiting outside the Combat Hall.","The trial had given Max an absurd number of Killing Points, but to Max, this was clearly not the end. It was only one stop along the way. There were still matters he had to settle, and knowing Max’s personality, if he said he was going to take care of Munro, then Munro’s fate was already almost decided.","Max placed one hand on Nick’s shoulder and looked at him with a faint smile.","\"Take care of yourself,\" Max said. \"Do not get dragged into unnecessary fights, and if someone troublesome comes looking for you, avoid them if you can.\"","Nick looked at him for a moment, then gave a helpless smile.","\"You say that after causing the biggest scene in the entire Combat Hall?\"","Max shrugged lightly. \"That is different.\"","Nick almost laughed, but then he sighed and nodded. \"Fine. I will be careful. You should also watch yourself. After what you did, demons, elves, and probably even some humans will start paying attention to you.\"","Max smiled faintly. \"Let them.\"","After saying that, he turned around and prepared to leave.","However, before Max could take more than a few steps, a figure suddenly appeared in front of him and blocked his path.","The surrounding atmosphere changed at once.","The person standing before him was the golden-haired elven prince.","He stood there with calm elegance, his long golden hair falling smoothly over his shoulders, his emerald eyes fixed directly on Max, and his posture carrying the natural nobility of someone who had been born above others.","He did not release any killing intent, nor did he show hostility openly, but the moment he stood in front of Max, many participants nearby instinctively quieted down. Even among the elves, his status was clearly not ordinary.","Standing beside him was the silver-haired elven woman Max had killed not long ago.","Her face was complicated knowing how she had been defeated by Max, but her eyes were calm as she stood slightly behind the golden-haired prince. When she looked at Max again, there was no hatred in her gaze, only caution, curiosity, and a lingering seriousness that had not been there before their battle.","Max stopped.","Nick’s expression immediately changed, and he stepped slightly closer to Max, his eyes moving between the golden-haired elven prince and the silver-haired woman.","The nearby humans also became tense.","The demons watched silently from a distance, some with cold smiles, as if they hoped another conflict would break out before Max could leave the Combat Hall.","Max looked at the golden-haired elven prince, then glanced at the silver-haired woman beside him.","His smile became faintly mocking.","\"What is this?\" Max asked. \"Do the elves want another test?\"","The silver-haired elven woman’s expression shifted slightly, but she did not speak.","The golden-haired elven prince looked at Max in silence for a moment, and his gaze seemed to study every part of him.","\"No,\" the golden-haired elven prince said calmly. \"I am not here to challenge you.\"","Max raised an eyebrow.","\"Then move.\"","The words were casual, but they carried enough arrogance to make several elves behind the prince frown.","The golden-haired prince did not seem offended by Max’s cold attitude. He simply stood in front of him with the same calm expression, his emerald eyes studying Max’s face as if he was looking for a reaction that could confirm the suspicion forming in his mind.","\"I only want to ask you something,\" the golden-haired prince said.","Max narrowed his eyes slightly.","\"What is it?\" he asked, his voice carrying a trace of curiosity despite the impatience in his expression.","The golden-haired prince looked at him for a brief moment, then asked in a casual tone, \"Who is Caelira to you?\"","The moment that name entered Max’s ears, everything around him seemed to stop.","His expression changed instantly.","The calmness in his eyes shattered, and an uncontrollable surge of rage exploded from deep within his chest. That name was not something he had expected to hear here, not from an elf, and certainly not from someone who looked as young as the golden-haired prince. Caelira was his mother.","Even though Max knew it was the elves who had taken his parents away, he had never thought the younger generation of the elves would know anything related to that incident, because in his mind, something so cruel and secretive should have been hidden among the higher ranks of their race.","But this elf had spoken her name.","He had spoken it casually.","\"How do you know that name?!\" Max snapped.","The words came out like a roar.","Before anyone nearby could react, Max stepped forward and grabbed the golden-haired prince by the collar. His fingers clenched tightly around the elven prince’s clothes, and a violent wave of energy burst from his body as his emotions tore through the restraint he had placed upon himself. The humans nearby froze in shock.","The elves behind the golden-haired prince immediately moved as if they wanted to act, but the silver-haired elven woman raised one hand and stopped them, her face tense as she stared at Max’s furious expression.","Max did not care about any of them.","His eyes were locked onto the golden-haired prince.","If he had known the younger generation of the elves might possess information about his mother, then his attitude toward them inside the Combat Hall would have been completely different. He might not have simply killed and ignored them.","He might have captured a few, broken their pride, and tortured the answers out of them one by one. The thought alone made the rage inside him burn even hotter.","\"Calm down,\" the golden-haired prince said, his voice still strangely steady despite being held by the collar."]},{"number":1730,"title":"Chapter 1730: Following Golden Elf Prince!","paragraphs":["\"Calm down?!\" Max raged.","The energy in his body erupted even more violently, and black dragon scales began appearing across his skin once again without his conscious command. They spread over his arms, neck, and face, gleaming with a cold chaotic light as his uncontrolled emotional state dragged his bloodline power to the surface.","His pupils sharpened, his fingers tightened, and the air around him trembled under the pressure rolling out from his body.","\"If you do not tell me how you know that name,\" Max said, his voice low and dangerous, \"I will make sure you are eliminated right here and now.\"","The golden-haired prince stared at him without fear, but before he could answer, the energy Max released reached a dangerous peak.","Then, without warning, a beam of white light descended from above and fell directly upon Max.","The light wrapped around his body in an instant.","Max frowned.","The raging energy inside him suddenly disappeared as if it had been sealed by an invisible hand, and the black dragon scales that had begun spreading across his skin stopped growing. His grip on the golden-haired prince weakened slightly, and for a brief moment, Max felt as if all the strength inside his body had been locked away.","He could still stand. He could still move. But the terrifying power that had been surging through him a moment ago was no longer responding to his will.","\"What is happening?\" Max asked, his voice still filled with anger.","Nick, who had been standing nearby with a solemn expression, immediately stepped forward and said, \"Max, it is the rules of Starfall Haven.\"","Max glanced toward him.","Nick’s expression was serious as he continued, \"You cannot use strength or release too much energy inside Starfall Haven. Remember, this is a peaceful city and a neutral zone where killing is prohibited outside the proper battle areas.\"","Max stared at him for a moment.","Then he slowly took a deep breath.","The rage in his eyes did not disappear, but he forced it down with sheer will. He understood the situation now. Starfall Haven had its own rules, and those rules were not something even he could casually ignore. If he lost control here, the city itself would suppress him before he could act.","\"I see,\" Max said coldly.","He turned back toward the golden-haired prince, released his collar, and stepped back half a pace. The white light around his body gradually faded once his energy settled, but the killing intent in his eyes remained sharp enough to make the nearby elves tense.","Max looked at the golden-haired prince again and asked, each word controlled but heavy with threat, \"How do you know that name?\"","The golden-haired prince adjusted his collar calmly, then looked at Max with a gaze that had become far more serious than before.","\"Come with me,\" he said.","After saying that, he turned and began walking toward a secluded area of the Combat Hall, one far away from the demons, humans, and most of the elven participants. The silver-haired elven woman followed beside him, but she kept glancing back at Max, clearly aware that one wrong word could make this situation explode again.","Max followed without hesitation.","He did not care whether this was a trap.","He did not care whether the golden-haired prince had some hidden motive.","The moment his mother’s name had been spoken, everything else became secondary. Munro, Karo, the Killing Points, and even the attention of the Combat Hall all faded behind the single question burning inside him.","How did this elf know Caelira?","\"Max!\" Nick called from behind.","Max stopped for a moment and looked back.","Nick’s face was filled with worry, and it was clear he wanted to say something more, but he also understood that Max would not turn away from this matter now.","Max looked at him and said solemnly, \"After this, I will take care of Munro and Karo forever. Take care out there.\"","Nick stared at him for a moment, then nodded.","\"Be careful,\" he said.","Max gave a faint nod, then turned around and continued following the golden-haired prince.","Soon, his figure disappeared from Nick’s vision, swallowed by the quieter side of the Combat Hall where fewer participants dared to linger.","The golden-haired elven prince led Max away from the crowded part of the Combat Hall, and the silver-haired elven woman followed quietly at his side, her expression calm on the surface but her eyes still carrying a trace of caution whenever she glanced toward Max.","The three of them moved past several groups of participants, crossed a wide corridor lined with pale stone pillars, and finally entered a secluded area hidden behind a curved wall of smooth white crystal.","This place was much quieter than the main hall. The roars, arguments, and shocked whispers from the Combat Hall became distant and muffled, as if they had been sealed behind layers of invisible barriers, and only a faint silver light flowed across the walls, giving the area a cold and private atmosphere.","Max stopped the moment they reached the center of that secluded space.","He simply stood there and looked at the golden-haired prince with eyes so cold that even the silver-haired elven woman felt her body tense slightly.","Although Starfall Haven’s rules had suppressed his outburst earlier, the rage inside him had not disappeared. It had only been forced under control, like a volcano sealed beneath a layer of ice.","His mother’s name still echoed in his mind, and every time he thought of an elf casually speaking that name, his blood threatened to surge again.","The golden-haired prince turned around and faced him.","For a moment, none of them spoke.","The silence stretched between them like a drawn sword.","Then Max finally opened his mouth.","\"How do you know that name?\"","His voice was calm now, but that calmness was even more dangerous than his earlier rage.","The golden-haired elven prince looked at Max for a long moment, and although his expression remained calm, there was a heaviness in his eyes that had not been there before, as if even he understood that the words he was about to speak would not be easy for Max to hear.","\"I have a guess that you hate the elf race,\" the golden-haired prince said calmly. \"And from what I know, there is indeed a valid reason behind it. I will not deny that what they did was disgustingly wrong, but I need you to trust me here, at least long enough to hear everything.\""]},{"number":1731,"title":"Chapter 1731: Max Voidwalker!","paragraphs":["Max stared at him with cold eyes.","The secluded area was quiet, and the faint silver light flowing across the crystal walls made his expression look even colder. He did not trust this elf. He did not trust his calm tone, his noble posture, or the way he seemed to know far more than he should.","But the name Caelira had already been spoken, and now that his mother’s past was being placed before him piece by piece, Max could not walk away.","\"Go on,\" Max said calmly.","The golden-haired prince nodded slightly.","\"It is like this,\" he said. \"There are currently three factions within the elf race that control almost everything. My faction remains neutral most of the time, and we rarely interfere unless the balance of the race itself is threatened. Then there is the second faction, the most aggressive of the three. Their methods are ruthless, their ambitions are extreme, and they believe the elf race should never bow to the will of any other race or compromise its purity for any reason.\"","His voice became a little lower.","\"That faction should be the one that attacked your home, Max Voidwalker, and took away your parents.\"","Max’s eyes narrowed instantly.","A chill ran down his spine.","It was not because of fear.","It was because the golden-haired prince had spoken his true name.","Max Voidwalker.","He had made sure not to reveal that name casually, and in Starfall Haven, he had not told this elven prince anything about his real identity. Yet this elf had said it as if he had already known. That single detail made Max’s heart sink slightly, while the killing intent he had just suppressed began stirring again in the depths of his chest.","\"How do you know that name?\" Max asked, his voice dangerously soft.","The golden-haired prince did not avoid his gaze. \"Because once I connected you to Caelira, your identity was no longer difficult to guess. The restricted records did not reveal everything, but they did mention the name of the human man she married and the family name connected to the child she gave birth to.\"","Max’s fingers clenched slowly.","The prince continued before Max could interrupt further.","\"The third faction,\" he said, \"is where your mother was once the leader.\"","Max’s body trembled slightly.","For a moment, the rage in his eyes was disturbed by shock.","His mother had once been the leader of an elven faction.","No.","Not merely a faction.","He knew that his mother was once an elf and she chose to give up her bloodline and her elf identity for some reason but to think she was a leader of an elf faction was shocking even to Max.","The golden-haired prince’s next words made his mind go still.","\"Caelira was once called Divine Queen Caelira,\" the prince said calmly. \"Her faction was the strongest of the three factions, and in a way, she was the true leader of the elf race, recognized by all elves, respected by every major bloodline, and feared even by the most ambitious elders of the second faction.\"","Max did not speak.","He simply stared at the golden-haired prince.","A part of him wanted to reject those words immediately. His mother, the gentle woman he remembered, the woman who had lived peacefully with his father, the woman who had smiled at him in a quiet home far away from the center of power, had once been the Divine Queen of the elf race.","It sounded absurd. It sounded impossible. Yet the way the prince spoke did not feel like a lie, and that made the revelation even harder to bear.","The golden-haired prince continued, \"But something strange happened one day. No one knows the full truth, or perhaps those who know have sealed it away too deeply, but according to the records, Divine Queen Caelira suddenly gave up her royal bloodline and abandoned her identity as an elf. After that, she disappeared.\"","Max’s breathing became heavier.","The silver-haired elven woman standing nearby lowered her gaze, clearly aware that this was no ordinary secret. Even for her, who served beside the prince, some of these details seemed shocking.","\"A few years after she gave up her bloodline and her identity,\" the golden-haired prince continued, \"the elf race received news that she had married a human and was living peacefully on a remote planet far away from the territories ruled by the elves. To many elves, that news was impossible to accept. The queen who was supposed to lead the elven race, the woman whose bloodline represented the highest purity of our royal inheritance, had chosen to live like a mortal beside a human in a distant world.\"","He paused for a moment before adding, \"It was shocking to all elves.\"","Max’s face remained cold, but his heart was no longer calm.","Images from his childhood flashed through his mind. A quiet home. His mother’s voice. His father’s presence. His sister’s playful side. The warmth of ordinary days that he had once taken for granted.","He had never imagined that behind that peaceful life was a past like this, a past filled with royal bloodlines, factions, forbidden decisions, and an entire race that had once viewed his mother as their queen.","The golden-haired prince’s expression became more solemn.","\"At first, even though some of the higher-ups of the second faction were displeased, they did not act. Your mother had already given up her royal bloodline and identity as an elf, and even though her decision was considered disgraceful by many of them, they still chose to respect it on the surface. Perhaps they feared the remnants of her old faction. Perhaps they feared the consequences of touching her. Perhaps they simply believed she no longer mattered.\"","His eyes sharpened slightly.","\"But everything changed when a piece of news leaked.\"","Max looked at him.","The prince said slowly, \"The news said that you, Max Voidwalker, had somehow inherited the Divine Bloodline, a variant born from your mother’s former royal bloodline.\"","Max’s pupils contracted slightly.","The golden-haired prince continued, \"Your mother once possessed the Heavenly Luminance Royal Bloodline, which was already one of the highest bloodlines among the elves. But what awakened in you was different. It was called the Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline. It was considered a grade above the royal bloodline your mother once held when she was the Elven Queen.\"","The secluded area became unbearably silent.","Even the silver-haired elven woman looked shaken."]},{"number":1732,"title":"Chapter 1732: Divine Queen Caelira","paragraphs":["The golden-haired prince’s voice remained steady, but the weight behind his words grew heavier. \"That was when the second faction could no longer remain still. To them, the idea that a half-human child, born far away from the elf race, had inherited a bloodline superior to the queen’s own royal bloodline was something they could not accept. It threatened their pride. It threatened their ideology. More importantly, it threatened their claim over the future of the elf race.\"","Max’s jaw tightened.","\"So they attacked,\" he said coldly.","The golden-haired prince nodded.","\"Yes,\" he said. \"They resorted to an attack, and that attack led to the catastrophe that happened around twenty ago.\"","The words fell like stones into Max’s heart.","Twenty years ago.","The catastrophe at his home.","His parents being taken away.","His life being torn apart.","All of it had happened because some faction among the elves could not accept his existence.","For a moment, Max said nothing.","His body was still, but the rage inside him was not. It rose slowly, quietly, and more dangerously than before. This was no longer blind anger. This was a cold hatred being sharpened by truth. The second faction had not merely harmed his family by accident.","They had come because of his bloodline. They had come because of his mother’s past. They had come because Max himself had become something they feared, desired, or could not tolerate.","The golden-haired prince seemed to understand what Max was thinking, because he spoke again before Max could sink fully into that rage.","\"I am not asking you to forgive the elf race,\" he said calmly. \"I would not forgive them either if I were you.\"","Max looked at him.","The prince continued, \"But you need to understand that the elf race is not united in this matter. The second faction acted, but not all elves supported them, and your mother’s old faction still exists, though it has weakened greatly after her disappearance. There are still many among them who still believe in Divine Queen Caelira and would die fighting for her.","Max’s eyes narrowed as he listened to the golden-haired elven prince speak, and the more he heard, the more complicated the image of his mother became in his mind. He had always remembered Caelira as his mother, as the gentle woman who had lived quietly with his father on a remote planet, the woman whose smile had once made their simple home feel warmer than any palace could ever be.","But now, that same woman was being described as Divine Queen Caelira, the former leader of the elf race, the ruler of the strongest faction, and someone who had once carried the responsibility of guiding an entire race.","To have that kind of position, to possess that kind of bloodline, to stand above countless elves as their queen, and yet still choose to abandon her royal bloodline and give up her identity as an elf just so she could live with her family, was not something Max could accept as a simple romantic decision.","There had to be more to it.","Max could feel it clearly.","His mother’s choice to abandon her race and bloodline could not be as simple as the surface made it seem. A queen did not give up everything without a reason. A woman who once commanded the strongest faction of the elf race would not disappear quietly unless there was something behind that decision, something heavy enough to make her cut away her past, her title, and even the bloodline that had once defined her existence.","Perhaps it was love. Perhaps it was danger. Perhaps it was betrayal. Perhaps it was all of those things together.","The golden-haired prince seemed to understand what Max was thinking, but he did not interrupt his thoughts for long.","\"But things are not going well for the faction your mother once belonged to,\" the prince continued, his voice growing heavier. \"After Divine Queen Caelira disappeared, her faction lost its strongest pillar, and although many loyal elders still tried to preserve her influence, the second faction became more aggressive with each passing year.\"","Max looked at him silently.","The golden-haired prince’s expression darkened slightly. \"Recently, they crossed a line. Without holding a proper meeting with our faction, and without receiving any consent from us, the second faction imprisoned nearly every elf belonging to your mother’s old faction. They claimed it was necessary to maintain internal order, but everyone knows that was only an excuse. Their real goal is to weaken her faction completely and make themselves the strongest power within the elf race.\"","The silver-haired elven woman standing nearby lowered her gaze slightly, and the quiet anger in her eyes showed that even she found the matter shameful.","\"Because of this,\" the golden-haired prince continued, \"your mother’s faction has suffered greatly. Their elders are restrained, their resources have been seized, their younger members are watched, and many of their supporters have been forced into silence. Those who once followed Divine Queen Caelira with pride are now treated like criminals in their own home.\"","Max’s fingers slowly curled into fists.","The golden-haired prince glanced at him, then continued in a calm but bitter tone. \"Even though my father, the leader of the first faction, wanted to interfere, he is powerless right now. The second faction has somehow managed to gain the support of several ancestors of our race, and because of that, most of our objections during the internal meetings are ignored or suppressed before they can change anything. In a way, even though it is disheartening to admit, our faction has almost become useless in the current political balance.\"","Max stared at him.","For the first time, he saw something beyond noble calm in the prince’s face.","Frustration.","Shame.","Helplessness.","This golden-haired elf was not speaking like someone who wanted to manipulate him with lies. He sounded like someone who had watched his own faction lose power little by little, while a more ruthless faction grew bold enough to crush the people who had once followed Max’s mother.","\"But there is still a chance,\" the golden-haired prince said.","Max’s gaze sharpened. \"A chance for what?\"","\"A chance for you to contact the members of your mother’s faction right now.\"","Max’s expression changed.","\"What?\" he asked, unable to hide his shock. \"I can?\""]},{"number":1733,"title":"Chapter 1733: Aunt Caroline","paragraphs":["The golden-haired prince nodded. \"Did you forget what the Cosmic Ascension Conference is? It allows young geniuses from across the Divine Realm to enter and compete, regardless of race, faction, or territory. Even though the young geniuses from your mother’s faction were imprisoned in the elven home world, the rules of the conference still pulled them into this place when the event began. That means they are somewhere in this world right now.\"","Max’s eyes shone faintly when he heard that.","For a moment, something stirred inside him that was not rage.","It was hope.","If the young geniuses from his mother’s faction were truly here, then perhaps he could finally meet someone connected to his mother’s past. Perhaps he could learn more about Caelira, about why she abandoned the elf race, about what happened twenty-two years ago, and perhaps even about where his parents were now.","But almost immediately, that hope became mixed with uncertainty. He did not know anyone from his mother’s faction. He did not know whether they would recognize him, trust him, or even accept him. To them, he might be nothing more than the half-human son of the queen who had abandoned them.","The golden-haired prince saw through Max’s concerns almost immediately.","\"I do not know whether you are aware of this or not,\" he said, \"but after your mother gave up her royal bloodline and abandoned her identity as an elf, the person who suffered the most was her younger sister, Caroline.\"","Max froze.","\"Mother has a sister?\"","The shock in his voice was impossible to hide.","He knew so little about his mother’s family that the revelation struck him harder than he expected. An aunt. His mother had a younger sister. Someone connected to Caelira by blood. Someone who might have known her before she became his mother, before she became the quiet woman living on a remote planet, before she left behind the identity of Divine Queen Caelira.","The golden-haired prince nodded.","\"Yes,\" he said. \"Caroline. She was your mother’s younger sister, and after Caelira disappeared, Caroline became one of the people who suffered the worst because of her connection to her. Many elves in the second faction hated her simply because she carried the same royal bloodline and because some members of your mother’s old faction still saw her as the closest remaining symbol of Divine Queen Caelira’s legacy.\"","Max’s expression turned colder.","The prince continued, \"Even now, Caroline and several young geniuses from her faction are being hunted by members of the second faction inside a region of this world called the Eternal Hourglass. If nothing is done, they will be eliminated from the conference. And once they are sent back to our home planet, they will once again be subjected to imprisonment, humiliation, and torture.\"","The word torture made Max’s gaze turn icy.","For a brief moment, the secluded area seemed to become colder.","The silver-haired elven woman instinctively tensed, because she could feel the killing intent rising from Max again, though this time he controlled it far better than before.","Max took a slow breath.","He thought of his mother.","He thought of the faction that had once followed her.","He thought of a woman named Caroline, his aunt, someone he had never met, someone who had suffered because of Caelira’s choice, and someone who was now being hunted down by the same faction that had destroyed his family.","Then Max made his decision.","\"Where is she?\" he asked.","The golden-haired prince looked at him.","Max’s voice was calm, but it carried an edge sharp enough to cut through bone.","\"Where is Caroline?\"","The golden-haired prince did not delay any longer, because he could already see from Max’s expression that the moment Caroline’s safety was mentioned, there was no chance of stopping him from going there.","\"She is in a very deadly place,\" the golden-haired prince said solemnly. \"A few hours ago, I received news that in order to flee from the elves of the second faction, Caroline and some members of your mother’s faction escaped into one of the most dangerous zones of the Eternal Hourglass, Witch God Valley.\"","Max’s eyes narrowed slightly.","The name alone carried a strange heaviness.","\"Witch God Valley?\" he repeated.","The golden-haired prince nodded. \"It is not an ordinary danger zone. The Eternal Hourglass itself is already filled with countless trials and death zones but Witch God Valley is dangerous even by the standards of that place. It is said that an ancient witch god once died there, and although no one knows whether that legend is true or not, the valley is filled with cursed mist, soul-devouring winds, and strange illusions that can make even powerful geniuses lose their direction. The deeper one enters, the harder it becomes to distinguish between reality and falsehood.\"","Max’s expression remained unchanged.","\"Then why would Caroline escape there?\"","\"Because she had no better choice,\" the golden-haired prince replied. \"The second faction’s hunters were closing in on her from multiple directions, and if she had stayed in the open region of the Eternal Hourglass, she would have been surrounded and eliminated. Witch God Valley is dangerous, but its danger also makes it difficult for pursuers to move freely. Caroline likely chose that place because it was the only chance she had to delay them.\"","Max’s gaze turned colder. \"Who is hunting her?\"","The golden-haired prince’s expression became heavier.","\"Two people are leading the hunt,\" he said. \"The first is Seraphine Lareth.\"","Max had already heard that name once, and now that it was spoken again, his eyes became sharper.","\"She is one of the most talented young geniuses of the second faction,\" the prince continued. \"Seraphine possesses the Heavenly Luminance Royal Bloodline, though her bloodline is far inferior to the purity your mother once possessed. Compared to Divine Queen Caelira’s original bloodline, Seraphine’s bloodline can only be considered a downgraded version, but you must not underestimate her because of that. Even a downgraded Heavenly Luminance Royal Bloodline is still powerful enough to suppress most elven bloodlines, and Seraphine has trained it to a very high level.\"","The silver-haired elven woman standing beside him also spoke for the first time, her voice quiet but serious. \"Seraphine is not only strong because of her bloodline. Her control over radiant power is extremely dangerous. She can turn light into judgment, restraint, and destruction, and among the younger generation of the second faction, very few can match her in a direct fight.\"","\"And the second?\" Max asked."]},{"number":1734,"title":"Chapter 1734: Elrian Vaelthorn!","paragraphs":["The golden-haired prince’s gaze sharpened. \"Fin Arclight.\"","The name made the silver-haired elven woman’s expression change slightly, and Max immediately noticed it.","\"He is dangerous?\" Max asked.","\"Very,\" the golden-haired prince said without hesitation. \"If Seraphine is ruthless and commanding, then Fin is silent and unpredictable. He also possesses the Heavenly Luminance Royal Bloodline, but like Seraphine, his bloodline is not on the same level as your mother’s. It is a downgraded version of the royal bloodline, but his talent in combat is terrifying, and many elves believe that his actual battle instincts are even sharper than Seraphine’s.\"","Max looked at him with narrowed eyes.","The golden-haired prince continued, \"Both Seraphine and Fin possessed Pseudo Cosmic Path and so you have to be extra careful around them.","Max’s gaze turned thoughtful for a moment.","Seraphine Lareth.","Fin Arclight.","Both possessed the Heavenly Luminance Royal Bloodline, both were from the second faction, both had mastered Pseudo Cosmic Paths, and both were hunting his mother’s younger sister inside Witch God Valley.","The golden-haired prince looked at Max carefully and said, \"I know you are strong. After watching you crush Karo, I will not insult you by pretending otherwise. But Seraphine and Fin are not ordinary participants, and they are not like the demons you destroyed in the arena. They are among the strongest geniuses of the elf race, and if they work together, even someone at Karo’s level would be in serious danger.\"","Max’s lips curved slightly.","\"Are you warning me not to go?\"","\"No,\" the golden-haired prince replied. \"I am warning you not to treat them carelessly.\"","Max’s smile faded, but the cold confidence in his eyes remained.","The prince continued, \"You may possess a bloodline even higher than theirs, but you have not lived among elves. You may not fully understand the methods of the Heavenly Luminance Royal Bloodline yet. Seraphine and Fin have trained with that power since childhood, and their Pseudo Cosmic Paths are built around it. They know how to use radiant bloodline pressure, light-based suppression, illusion, restraint, and execution techniques. If you underestimate them only because their bloodlines are downgraded versions of your mother’s, you may suffer for it.\"","Max looked at him silently for a few breaths.","Then he asked, \"Are they stronger than Karo?\"","The golden-haired prince did not answer immediately.","That silence was enough to show that the question was not simple.","\"Yes. Both of them can one shot Karo if they want to.\" The elf prince nodded solemnly.","Max slowly nodded.","\"I understand.\"","The golden-haired prince studied him. \"Do you?\"","Max’s eyes became icy.","\"I understand that two people connected to the faction that destroyed my home are hunting my aunt.\"","The silver-haired elven woman felt a chill run down her spine when she heard his tone.","Max continued, \"I understand that both of them have the Heavenly Luminance Royal Bloodline. I understand that both of them have mastered Pseudo Cosmic Paths. I understand that they are among the strongest geniuses of the elf race.\"","He paused for a moment, then smiled faintly.","\"And I understand that if they hurt Caroline before I arrive, I will make them regret entering this conference.\"","The golden-haired prince stared at him for a long moment.","Then he let out a quiet breath.","\"Then go to Witch God Valley as quickly as you can,\" he said. \"If my information is accurate, Caroline and the others are being driven deeper into the cursed region. Once they reach the inner valley, even I do not know what kind of danger they will face.\"","He added point at the silver haired woman elf. \"Also take Nancy here with you. She knows the way to the Witch God Valley and will help you locating Caroline.\"","Max turned to the silver haired woman elf before looking at the elf prince.","\"What is your name?\"","The golden-haired prince paused, as if he had not expected Max to ask that now.","\"Elrian,\" he said. \"Elrian Vaelthorn.\"","Max looked at him for a moment, then nodded faintly.","\"Elrian,\" he repeated. \"If what you told me is true, then I owe you for this information.\"","Elrian’s expression remained calm. \"Save Caroline first. We can speak of debts later.\"","Max did not say anything else.","He turned and walked away, his steps calm but filled with a silent killing intent that made even the crystal walls of the secluded area feel colder.","The silver-haired elven woman watched Max walk away from the secluded area, and after a brief silence, she turned toward the golden-haired prince with a calm but serious expression.","\"Your Highness, I will see you later.\"","Elrian looked at her for a moment, then nodded.","\"Be careful out there Nancy,\" he said quietly.","Nancy lowered her head slightly. \"I understand.\"","After saying that, she turned and followed Max without hesitation.","Elrian remained where he was, watching the two of them leave, and his emerald eyes became deeper as their figures disappeared into the distance.","He had given Max the truth, or at least the part of the truth he knew, but even he could not predict what would happen once Max reached Witch God Valley.","If Caroline truly met him, if the young geniuses of Caelira’s old faction learned that Divine Queen Caelira’s son was alive, and if the second faction discovered that Max Voidwalker had reawakened the Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline despite being the bloodline source taken away from him, then the balance among the elves might be shattered completely.","Meanwhile, Max and Nancy walked out of the Combat Hall together.","The moment they stepped outside, the loud atmosphere behind them faded, and the open streets of Starfall Haven appeared before them once again. The city was still peaceful on the surface, with pale stone roads, floating lanterns, and silent towers glowing beneath a gentle silver sky, but Max could feel the hidden currents moving beneath that calmness.","News of what had happened inside Arena Seven would not remain contained for long. Karo had died once, his six million Killing Points had been taken, and Max’s name had now entered the attention of humans, demons, and elves alike.","Max did not care about that.","His mind was already focused on Witch God Valley, Caroline, Seraphine, Fin, and the second faction that had destroyed his family.","After walking a short distance from the Combat Hall, Max glanced at Nancy and asked, \"What is the fastest way to Witch God Valley?\""]},{"number":1735,"title":"Chapter 1735: Leaving Starfall Haven!","paragraphs":["Nancy looked toward the distant western side of Starfall Haven, where the city gates stood beneath a curtain of pale light.","\"We have to pass through another neutral zone first,\" she said. \"After that, we will reach the outer path leading toward Witch God Valley.\"","Max nodded slightly.","\"I see.\"","His gaze shifted toward the exit of Starfall Haven.","For a moment, his expression remained calm, but the coldness in his eyes deepened. He had not forgotten Munro. He had not forgotten Karo either.","Karo had died once inside the arena, but he was not truly gone, and Max knew very well that a demon like him would not quietly accept such humiliation.","As for Munro, Max had already decided to settle that matter before leaving the city. If both of them were waiting near the exit, then it would actually save him the trouble of searching for them later.","\"Anyway,\" Max said, his voice calm, \"let us go and take care of Karo and Munro first.\"","Nancy’s eyes moved slightly.","\"You think they will be waiting for you?\"","Max smiled faintly as he continued walking toward the western exit.","\"If I am not wrong, they should already be waiting near the exit of Starfall Haven.\"","Nancy looked at him in silence for a moment.","She could not tell whether Max was being reckless or simply confident, but after seeing him destroy Karo’s Abyssal Grave of the Fallen with a single fist, she knew his confidence was not baseless. Still, she could not help reminding him, \"Starfall Haven is a neutral zone. They cannot attack you inside the city, but the moment you step outside, the rules will no longer protect anyone.\"","Max’s smile became colder.","\"That is exactly why they will wait there.\"","Nancy’s expression turned solemn.","The streets around them were quiet, but a few participants still recognized Max as he passed. Some humans stopped and stared with wide eyes. Several demons quickly lowered their gazes or moved aside.","A few elves looked at Nancy with surprise, as if they could not understand why she was walking beside the same human who had killed her not long ago. Max ignored all of them and continued toward the exit, his steps steady, his expression relaxed, and his killing intent hidden so deeply that only someone standing close to him could sense how dangerous he truly was at that moment.","Nancy walked beside him and said, \"Munro may not be alone. If Karo has already revived and left the Combat Hall, he might have gathered other demons.\"","\"Good,\" Max replied.","Nancy turned to him.","Max’s eyes remained fixed on the distant gate.","\"If they gather more people,\" he said softly, \"then I will not have to hunt them one by one.\"","Nancy fell silent.","For a brief moment, she remembered the scene of Karo’s Pseudo Cosmic Path shattering under Max’s fist, and she suddenly felt that the ones waiting outside the city might not understand what kind of monster they were preparing to ambush.","The western exit of Starfall Haven grew closer.","Beyond the gate, the peaceful silver light of the city gave way to a darker horizon, where the distant sands of the Eternal Hourglass shimmered like a golden sea under a strange sky. The path leading out was wide and empty, yet Max could already feel several hidden auras lingering beyond the boundary of the neutral zone.","A faint smile appeared on his face.","\"So they really are there.\"","Nancy’s eyes sharpened as she also sensed the presences waiting outside.","\"How many?\"","Max did not answer immediately.","He walked forward until he stood only a short distance from the city’s exit, where the invisible protection of Starfall Haven ended and the outside world began. Then he raised his gaze toward the shadows beyond the gate, his voice calm but filled with cold certainty.","\"Enough to make this quick.\"","With those words, Max stepped toward the exit, and the peaceful rules of Starfall Haven remained behind him.","In no time, Max stepped outside the city gates.","The moment he crossed the boundary of Starfall Haven, the strange peaceful pressure that had restrained all killing intent and violent energy inside the neutral city faded from around his body like an invisible chain being removed.","The air beyond the gate was completely different from the calm atmosphere inside the city. It was heavier, colder, and filled with the faint scent of blood, sand, and demonic energy.","Behind him, the silver-white radiance of Starfall Haven still glowed softly, while ahead of him stretched the darker road leading toward the Eternal Hourglass, where golden sands shifted beneath the distant sky like a restless ocean.","Max did not stop immediately.","He continued walking forward for some distance, as if he had not sensed anything unusual at all.","Nancy followed beside him, but her expression had already turned solemn. She could feel it now. The hidden auras surrounding the area were not few. They were everywhere, concealed behind rocks, shadows, broken ruins, and folds of demonic mist.","The moment they moved far enough from the protection of Starfall Haven, those auras began to stir like predators waiting for prey to step into the center of their trap.","Then, all at once, the world around them changed.","Boom!","Dark demonic energy erupted from every direction.","Thousands of demons appeared out of nowhere, rising from the ground, stepping out from behind distorted shadows, descending from the air, and emerging from clouds of black mist as if an entire army had been lying in wait outside the city gates.","Their bodies were different in size and shape. Some were enormous, with horns curling toward the sky and weapons resting on their shoulders. Some were lean and sharp-eyed, their claws dripping with poison. Some wore black armor covered in demonic runes, while others carried blades, spears, axes, chains, and strange bone weapons that released thick killing intent.","In only a few breaths, Max and Nancy were completely surrounded.","The road behind them was sealed.","The path ahead was blocked.","The empty land on both sides became filled with demons.","Their numbers were so great that the area outside Starfall Haven looked as if it had been swallowed by a demonic tide, and the combined pressure of thousands of hostile auras caused the ground itself to tremble faintly.","Some participants still inside the city gate noticed the sudden movement and quickly stopped to watch from a safe distance, their faces changing when they saw the size of the ambush waiting outside."]},{"number":1736,"title":"Chapter 1736: Surrounded!","paragraphs":["Nancy’s eyes narrowed.","\"So many...\" she muttered.","Max, however, only smiled faintly.","His gaze passed calmly over the thousands of demons surrounding him, and there was not the slightest trace of panic in his expression. Instead, he looked almost amused, as if the scene before him had confirmed exactly what he had expected from the beginning.","At the front of the demon army, two figures slowly walked forward.","The first was Karo.","He looked completely different from the confident demon who had entered Arena Seven with a smile, because although he had revived after death, the humiliation of being killed by Max had not disappeared.","Beside Karo stood another demon.","This demon was taller and broader, with dark red skin, sharp black horns, and a face that bore a faint resemblance to Karo’s, though his features were rougher, colder, and far more brutal. His crimson eyes carried none of Karo’s earlier playful arrogance.","Instead, there was only a deep and savage killing intent, the kind that belonged to someone who did not enjoy long conversations before slaughter. A huge black blade rested against his shoulder, and every step he took caused the ground beneath him to crack slightly.","Max looked at him once and immediately understood.","This was Munro.","The demon he had come to kill.","Karo stopped a short distance away and stared at Max with a twisted smile. \"You really came out.\"","Max looked at him calmly. \"Of course I did.\"","Karo’s eyes twitched slightly when he heard that casual reply.","Munro’s gaze moved from Max to Nancy, then back to Max, and his expression became colder. \"So this is the human who killed you once?\"","Karo’s face darkened.","The thousands of demons around them heard Munro’s words, and although none of them dared to laugh openly, the air still seemed to shift strangely. Karo felt it clearly, and the humiliation in his heart burned even hotter.","\"He used the arena rules and caught me off guard,\" Karo said coldly.","Max raised an eyebrow.","Nancy glanced at Karo with a strange expression, because she had personally seen Max crush Karo’s Pseudo Cosmic Path in front of everyone, and hearing Karo speak as if his defeat had been caused by carelessness almost made her wonder whether demons truly believed their own lies.","Max smiled faintly. \"Caught you off guard?\"","Karo’s killing intent surged.","Max continued calmly, \"I destroyed your Abyssal Grave of the Fallen, crushed your attack, killed you with one punch, and took your six million Killing Points. If that is called catching you off guard, then I suppose I can do it again.\"","The demons around them instantly became restless.","Munro’s eyes narrowed slightly.","Karo’s face turned almost savage.","\"You will not get that chance again,\" Karo said through gritted teeth. \"This is not the arena. There is no barrier. There is no trial rule. There is no one-on-one battle. Outside Starfall Haven, numbers are also strength.\"","As soon as he spoke, the thousands of demons around Max and Nancy released their aura at the same time.","Boom!","The combined pressure was terrifying.","Demonic energy rose into the sky like a black storm, covering the area outside the city gates and causing the distant golden sands to shake violently. The sheer number of demons made the scene overwhelming. Even a strong genius would feel suffocated if surrounded by so many enemies, especially with Karo and Munro standing at the front.","Nancy slowly placed one hand on the hilt of her sword.","Her expression was calm, but her eyes were serious.","\"Max,\" she said quietly, \"there are too many of them.\"","Max did not look at her.","He only stared at Karo and Munro.","\"There are a lot,\" Max admitted.","Karo sneered.","Munro gripped the huge blade on his shoulder.","Then Max smiled.","\"But not enough.\"","The moment those words fell, the air around him changed.","A faint draconic pressure began to stir beneath his skin, and although he had not yet transformed, the ground beneath his feet started cracking silently. The demons closest to him instinctively took half a step back, their bodies reacting before their minds could process why. Even Munro’s eyes sharpened, while Karo’s expression twisted with both hatred and caution.","Max slowly rolled his neck and looked around at the thousands of demons.","\"You gathered all these demons here for me,\" he said softly. \"Good.\"","His smile became colder.","\"That saves me a lot of time.\"","Karo stared at him, his eyes burning with fury. \"You still dare to act arrogant?\"","Max’s gaze returned to him.","\"I told you inside the Combat Hall,\" he said calmly. \"If I saw you again, I would kill you again.\"","Then he looked at Munro.","\"And since Munro is here too, I can finish both of you before heading to Witch God Valley.\"","Munro’s expression turned murderous.","The thousands of demons tightened their formation.","Behind them, Starfall Haven remained silent and untouchable, its peaceful light glowing beyond the city gates, while outside its protection, killing intent flooded the land like a rising tide.","Max stood at the center of the encirclement with Nancy beside him, surrounded by thousands of demons, facing Karo and Munro at the front.","Yet his expression remained calm.","No.","It was not merely calm.","It was expectant.","As if the real hunt had finally begun.","\"Do you really think you can stop me with these?\" Max asked Karo and Munro, his calm gaze sweeping over the thousands of demons surrounding him before returning to the two figures standing at the front.","\"You are arrogant,\" Munro said in a deep voice. \"But arrogance becomes stupidity when it has no place to stand.\"","Max glanced at him and raised an eyebrow. \"And you are Munro?\"","Munro’s eyes narrowed. \"You know my name.\"","\"I came out to kill you,\" Max replied calmly. \"It would be strange if I did not know the name of the person I am about to erase.\"","The surrounding demons immediately erupted with furious growls.","\"Arrogant human!\"","\"Kill him!\"","\"Tear him apart!\"","\"Let him understand what happens when he offends our demon race!\"","Nancy stood beside Max with one hand on the hilt of her sword, her silver hair fluttering slightly in the heavy demonic wind. Her expression remained composed, but her eyes moved across the countless demons surrounding them, measuring their numbers and positions.","Even though she had seen Max’s strength, the scale of this encirclement was still terrifying. Thousands of demons had gathered here, and many of them were not weak."]},{"number":1737,"title":"Chapter 1737: Dimensional Shift!","paragraphs":["Karo noticed Nancy’s cautious gaze and sneered. \"Even your elf companion understands the situation better than you do. You may have defeated me once, but do not mistake that for invincibility. Outside Starfall Haven, you can be surrounded, exhausted, and buried beneath endless attacks.\"","Max looked at him for a moment, then laughed softly.","\"Karo,\" he said, his voice carrying a trace of mockery, \"after losing six million Killing Points to me, you still dare to speak as if you understand my limits?\"","Karo’s expression twisted with fury.","Max continued, \"You hid after reviving, gathered a crowd, waited outside the city gate, and now you are talking about strength. If I were you, I would have hidden better.\"","A few demons instinctively looked toward Karo, and although none of them dared to show it openly, the words clearly struck where it hurt most.","Karo’s aura erupted violently.","\"You will regret provoking me again.\"","Max’s smile disappeared, and his eyes turned cold. \"No, Karo. You are the one who should regret showing yourself again.\"","Munro raised one hand, stopping Karo before he could lose control completely.","His gaze remained on Max, and after a moment, a cruel smile slowly appeared on his face.","\"Enough words,\" Munro said. \"Since he thinks thousands of demons are not enough, let him test it with his body.\"","He lifted his black blade and pointed it toward Max.","The killing intent of the surrounding demons surged at once, rising like a dark tide from every direction.","\"Attack,\" Munro ordered coldly. \"Do not let him leave even a bone behind.\"","The moment his command fell, thousands of demons roared at the same time.","Boom!","The earth shook as the encirclement collapsed inward.","Demons charged from every direction, their weapons raised, their claws extended, their demonic energy erupting like black flames across the battlefield. Some rushed across the ground with savage speed, some leapt into the air and descended like falling meteors, while others began releasing long-range attacks from the back, filling the sky with spears of darkness, poisonous mist, black fireballs, bone arrows, and blood-colored chains.","In an instant, the land outside Starfall Haven turned into a battlefield.","Nancy drew her sword.","Max, however, only stood there and watched the demon tide surge toward him.","Then a faint smile returned to his face.","\"Good,\" Max said softly. \"Come together.\"","His voice was calm, almost pleased, and as the tide of thousands of demons rushed toward him from every direction, he stood in the center of their encirclement with no trace of fear on his face.","Black flames, poisonous mist, bone arrows, blood chains, demonic spears, and savage killing intent filled the space around him, while Nancy tightened her grip around the hilt of her sword, fully prepared to fight her way through the storm if necessary.","But Max did not move to attack.","Instead, he smiled.","\"Now let’s try something new,\" he muttered.","The moment those words left his mouth, a golden light began to bloom from within his body.","It was not the dark chaotic radiance of his Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline, nor was it the starry brilliance of Star Fist. This light was purer, brighter, and more sacred, carrying a noble pressure that seemed to come from something ancient, divine, and immeasurably high.","Golden patterns slowly appeared across Max’s skin, flowing beneath the surface like streams of sunlight, and the air around him trembled as his Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline awakened.","Nancy’s eyes widened slightly as she sensed a pressure acting upon her body and it wasn’t just any pressure, it was bloodline pressure.","The demons charging toward Max also felt something strange, but by the time they sensed that the golden light around him was not an ordinary defensive technique, it was already too late.","\"Dimensional Shift,\" Max muttered slowly.","In the next instant, the world changed.","There was no explosion.","There was no violent tearing of space.","There was only a sudden flash of golden radiance that swallowed everything at once.","Before any demon could react, before Karo or Munro could give another order, and before Nancy could even understand what Max had done, the entire battlefield outside Starfall Haven vanished from their senses.","The city gate, the dark road, the golden sands of the Eternal Hourglass in the distance, and the familiar sky above them all disappeared as if they had been wiped away by an invisible hand.","When the demons regained their senses, they were no longer outside Starfall Haven.","They were standing inside a dimension of light.","For a moment, no one moved.","Thousands of demons who had been roaring with killing intent just a breath ago now stood frozen in place, their weapons still raised, their attacks half-formed, their expressions stiff with disbelief. Some of them looked around in confusion, while others took instinctive steps back, unable to understand how the battlefield beneath their feet had changed so suddenly.","\"What is this place?\"","\"Where are we?\"","\"The city gate... where did the city gate go?\"","\"Impossible! He moved all of us?\"","\"No, this cannot be real. This must be an illusion!\"","The demons began shouting one after another, but their voices sounded strangely small in the endless world of light around them.","Everywhere they looked, there was radiance.","The sky above was a vast sea of golden-white brilliance, without sun, moon, or stars, yet glowing with an endless light that seemed to come from every direction at once. In the distance stood hundreds of thousands of mountains and hills made entirely from condensed luminance, their peaks shining like divine crystals and their slopes flowing with soft golden mist.","Rivers ran between those light-filled mountains, but even the water did not look like water. It flowed like liquid radiance, clear, bright, and sacred, cascading down from the high cliffs like streams of melted sunlight.","The ground beneath their feet was also formed from light.","It was firm, yet strange.","Every step sent faint ripples of golden brilliance spreading outward, and every ripple carried a soft but oppressive pressure that made many demons feel deeply uncomfortable. Their demonic energy, which usually surged freely and violently, now felt heavy and sluggish in this place, as if the dimension itself rejected their existence."]},{"number":1738,"title":"Chapter 1738: Divine Light of Justice and Truth!","paragraphs":["Karo’s expression changed drastically.","He looked around with sharp eyes, and the hatred on his face was quickly replaced by shock and caution. He could still sense the demons around him. He could still sense Munro. He could still sense Nancy. But the outside world was gone, and the thousands of demons he had gathered had been dragged into this strange luminous dimension in a single instant.","\"How did he do this?\" Karo muttered, his voice low and filled with disbelief.","Munro’s eyes narrowed deeply.","Unlike the ordinary demons, he did not panic immediately, but the grip around his black blade tightened. His instincts were screaming at him that this place was not simple. It was not an illusion, and it was not a normal domain. It felt more real than a domain, wider than a battlefield technique, and far more oppressive than any ordinary spatial skill.","Nancy stood a short distance away from Max, her silver hair glowing faintly beneath the golden radiance surrounding them. She looked at the endless mountains of light, the rivers of luminance, and the sky that seemed to stretch beyond the limits of sight, and for the first time since leaving the Combat Hall, her calm expression broke completely.","\"This is...\" she whispered.","Max stood at the center of everyone, golden light flowing around his body like divine fire.","His Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline continued to shine, and beneath that light, his presence felt completely different from before. He no longer looked like a human covered in arrogance and killing intent. He looked like the master of this luminous world, a being standing inside a dimension that recognized his authority.","This was the ability of the Dimensional Sovereign Body.","Dimensional Shift.","It allowed Max to shift a portion of any dimension he had unlocked and bring it into the real world, temporarily replacing the battlefield around him with that chosen dimensional space.","It was not as simple as teleportation, nor was it merely dragging people into an illusion. He had brought a real part of a dimension into contact with reality, and everyone caught within the range had been swallowed into it before they could resist.","The demons had not entered this world willingly.","Max had pulled them in.","Thousands of demons, Karo, Munro, and even Nancy had all been shifted into this dimension of light in a single breath.","A demon with three horns suddenly roared, unable to endure the oppressive purity around him any longer, and slammed his axe into the ground with all his strength.","Boom!","The axe landed heavily, but instead of shattering the luminous ground, it only caused a ripple of golden light to spread outward. The demon’s arms shook violently from the rebound, and he staggered back with shock written across his face.","\"This place is suppressing us!\" another demon shouted.","\"My demonic energy is slower here!\"","\"Damn it, break out!\"","Several demons immediately released attacks toward the sky, sending black flames, dark spears, and demonic beams upward, but the moment those attacks rose into the golden radiance above, they were gradually weakened, dissolved, and swallowed by the endless light. The sight made the surrounding demons even more uneasy.","Karo looked at Max with an ugly expression.","\"You had this kind of ability?\"","Max smiled faintly.","\"I told you,\" he said calmly, \"you should have hidden better.\"","Karo’s face twisted.","Munro stepped forward, his heavy aura erupting around him as he stared directly at Max. \"So this is your trump card?\"","Max glanced at him, then looked around at the thousands of demons trapped inside the dimension of light.","\"No,\" Max replied with a relaxed smile. \"This is only the battlefield I chose.\"","Those words made the demons’ hearts tremble.","Only the battlefield.","That meant Max had not even begun using the true power of whatever inheritance he had activated.","Nancy looked at him from the side, and for the first time, she understood why Elrian had said Seraphine and Fin were already in danger.","If Max could drag thousands of demons into a dimension of light with a single ability, then what would happen when he faced the elves of the second faction who carried a downgraded version of the Heavenly Luminance Royal Bloodline?","The thought made her heart shake.","Max slowly raised his hand.","The rivers of light in the distance trembled.","The luminous mountains released a faint hum.","The endless golden sky brightened.","The demons surrounding him felt their bodies stiffen as a terrifying pressure descended upon them from all directions, and the same thought appeared in many of their minds at once.","They had not surrounded Max.","Max had gathered them into his own battlefield.","And now, there was nowhere left to run.","\"Divine Light of Justice and Truth.\"","Max’s voice was quiet when he muttered those words, but the moment they left his mouth, the entire Dimension of Light seemed to awaken in response.","The golden sky above the demons trembled, the rivers of light flowing between the luminous mountains began to surge violently, and the endless hills and peaks formed from condensed radiance released a low divine hum that spread across the whole dimension. Then, one after another, enormous golden constructs began appearing in the air.","They were shaped like crosses made entirely from light, and each one looked sacred, sharp, and terrifyingly pure, as if judgment itself had taken physical form. In only a few breaths, there were no longer dozens or hundreds of them.","There were hundreds of thousands of golden cross-shaped light constructs suspended across the entire sky, filling every direction above the demon army with blinding radiance.","Every single light construct released the fifth level concept of space.","That was what made them terrifying.","They did not merely shine with holy light, nor were they simple weapons of radiant energy. Each cross-shaped construct distorted the space around it, causing the air to fold, ripple, and crack under the pressure of Max’s comprehension.","The fifth level space concept wrapped around the golden light like an invisible blade, making every construct appear both near and far at the same time, as if distance itself had become meaningless under Max’s control.","Because they had been summoned inside the Dimension of Light, their power was amplified to an absurd degree, and the entire world around the demons seemed to have become a divine execution ground prepared solely for them."]},{"number":1739,"title":"Chapter 1739: Slaughter!","paragraphs":["The thousands of demons looked up.","Their faces changed instantly.","Even the most savage among them felt fear grip their hearts when they saw the endless golden crosses spread across the sky like stars of judgment. The purity of the light suppressed their demonic energy, the space concept sealed their escape routes, and the sheer number of constructs made resistance feel almost meaningless.","Some demons roared and released black flames toward the sky, some formed defensive shields around their bodies, some tried to tear open space and escape the dimension, while others charged toward Max in desperate fury, hoping to kill him before the attack descended.","But Max only lowered his hand.","\"Fall.\"","The sky collapsed in golden light.","Countless cross-shaped constructs descended at once.","They did not fall like ordinary weapons. They vanished from the sky and appeared directly above their targets through distorted space, bypassing distance and ignoring most defensive formations. A demon had just raised his shield when a golden cross appeared over his head and pierced straight through him, splitting his body apart in a burst of divine radiance.","Another demon tried to dodge to the side, but space folded around him, and the cross that should have missed appeared directly in his path, pinning him to the luminous ground before exploding into a storm of light.","Boom! Boom! Boom!","Explosions erupted everywhere.","The Dimension of Light became a world of endless judgment.","Golden crosses fell in infinite numbers, striking the demon army from above, from the sides, from behind, and even from beneath their feet as space twisted under Max’s control. Every impact released a burst of radiant force that tore through demonic bodies, shattered armor, burned away dark energy, and crushed the soul-like aura hidden within many of them.","The demons screamed, roared, and cursed, but their voices were drowned beneath the continuous thunder of divine light striking the ground.","Nancy stood beside Max, stunned into silence.","The golden light did not harm her.","It curved around her like flowing water, as if the dimension itself recognized that she was not an enemy. But everywhere else, the demons were being slaughtered. Some tried to gather together and form a huge demonic barrier, but dozens of light crosses descended upon the same point at once, their fifth level space concept overlapping until the barrier was sliced apart from the inside.","Some stronger demons attempted to counterattack, but their skills were swallowed by the endless radiance before they could even reach Max.","This was not a battle.","It was an execution.","Karo’s expression twisted with disbelief and rage as golden crosses descended toward him from every direction. He released his Abyssal Grave of the Fallen again in desperation, causing black-red mist and tombstones to rise around him as he tried to resist the incoming judgment, but compared to the power he had displayed inside the arena, his aura was clearly weaker after losing once to Max.","Even so, the Abyssal Grave still spread outward with terrifying force, forming a grave-like domain around him in an attempt to bury the falling light.","But inside the Dimension of Light, Max’s inheritance technique was far too powerful.","The first wave of golden crosses tore into the black-red mist and split it apart.","The second wave shattered the tombstones before they could fully form.","The third wave pierced directly into the heart of the Abyssal Grave of the Fallen, causing Karo’s Pseudo Cosmic Path to tremble violently. Each cross carried not only divine light, but also the fifth level concept of space, and every impact distorted the structure of Karo’s path until the grave-like domain began collapsing in pieces.","\"No!\" Karo roared, his voice filled with fury and fear. \"Not again!\"","Max looked at him from afar with cold eyes.","Then several hundred cross-shaped constructs appeared above Karo at the same time.","They fell together.","Boom!","Karo’s Abyssal Grave of the Fallen shattered completely once more, and before he could escape, the golden crosses pierced through his body from every direction. His demonic energy was torn apart, his body was pinned in the air by radiant spatial force, and in the next breath, he was swallowed by a blinding explosion of golden light.","Karo was killed again.","Munro was not spared either.","When the golden crosses began falling, Munro had already erupted with all his strength. His huge black blade released a terrifying demonic pressure, and his body swelled as dense black-red markings spread across his skin, making him look like an ancient demon war god standing within a storm of light.","He swung his blade again and again, shattering dozens of golden constructs with pure force, and for a brief moment, his strength truly surpassed most of the demons around him. Each slash tore open a dark path through the radiance, and every roar from him sent shockwaves across the luminous ground.","But the constructs did not end.","For every cross Munro shattered, ten more appeared.","For every gap he carved open, space folded and filled it again.","The fifth level space concept made the light constructs impossible to avoid through ordinary movement, and the Dimension of Light strengthened them endlessly, as if the entire world was feeding power into Max’s attack.","Munro’s arms began to tremble. Cracks appeared across his black blade. The demonic markings on his body dimmed beneath the pressure of the divine radiance. Still, he roared and charged forward, his eyes locked on Max with savage hatred.","\"Max!\" Munro thundered. \"Fight me directly if you dare!\"","Max looked at him calmly.","\"You are not worth that much effort.\"","Munro’s eyes widened with fury.","The next instant, thousands of golden crosses appeared above him.","Munro raised his blade with both hands and released one final roar, but the endless constructs descended before he could move again. The first hundred shattered his blade. The next hundred pierced through his shoulders, arms, legs, chest, and back.","Then the remaining crosses fell like a golden rain of execution, tearing through his body again and again until his enormous figure was completely drowned in radiant spatial power.","Boom!","Munro exploded into nothingness.","His aura vanished.","His roar disappeared.","Only a wave of Killing Points scattered from the place where he had stood."]},{"number":1740,"title":"Chapter 1740 - 22 Million Points - Rank 7!","paragraphs":["Across the battlefield, the slaughter continued.","Thousands of demons were erased one after another beneath the Divine Light of Justice and Truth. Some died screaming, some died trying to flee, some died while begging for mercy, and some died while still attacking in blind rage, but no matter what they did, the result did not change.","The endless cross-shaped constructs fell upon them with merciless precision, and the Dimension of Light became brighter with every demon destroyed, as if their deaths only made Max’s battlefield shine more brilliantly.","Nancy watched the scene with a pale face.","She had known Max was strong.","She had seen him kill Karo once.","But this was different.","This was the power of an inheritance technique combined with his Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline, his Dimensional Sovereign Body, the Dimension of Light, and his fifth level space concept. It was not merely personal combat strength. It was battlefield domination. Against a single opponent, Max was terrifying. Against an army, he was even more horrifying.","Within a short time, the thousands of demons who had surrounded them were gone.","The demonic tide disappeared.","The roars vanished.","The black flames faded.","Only fragments of dark energy and countless streams of Killing Points remained scattered across the luminous battlefield.","Max stood in the center of it all, golden light flowing around his body while the last cross-shaped constructs slowly faded from the sky. His expression was calm, but the coldness in his eyes had not disappeared. He looked toward the places where Karo and Munro had been killed, then raised his hand.","All the Killing Points left behind by the demons surged toward him like a crimson storm.","At first, they emerged like scattered crimson sparks across the luminous battlefield.","Then those sparks multiplied.","A moment later, they became countless streams of blood-red radiance, bursting from every place where a demon had died and filling the Dimension of Light with a storm of Killing Points so dense that it looked as if an entire crimson galaxy had been shattered and released into the air.","The golden world around them was dyed with red light, and the contrast between the sacred radiance of the dimension and the blood-colored Killing Points made the scene feel both beautiful and terrifying.","Nancy stood silently beside Max, her silver hair glowing beneath the mixture of golden and crimson light.","She could not help looking around in shock.","Thousands of demons had died here.","Karo had died again.","Munro had been killed as well.","All of them had become Max’s reward.","The trial-like system of the Cosmic Ascension Conference began calculating the points from every fallen demon, and in the next instant, the crimson lights surged toward Max from every direction.","They flowed into him like endless rivers, wrapping around his body before disappearing into his form, while the number beside his name began rising at a speed that would have made every participant in the Combat Hall lose their mind.","[Participant: Max]","[Previous Killing Points: 7,000,000]","[Absorbed Killing Points: 15,000,000]","[Current Killing Points: 22,000,000]","[Rank: 7]","The moment the final number stabilized, even Nancy’s breathing paused.","Twenty-two million Killing Points.","This was no longer the kind of amount ordinary participants could even imagine. Max had walked out of the Combat Hall with seven million Killing Points after crushing Karo in the tenth battle, and now, after wiping out the demon army waiting outside Starfall Haven, he had gained another fifteen million in one sweep.","The thousands of demons who had gathered to trap him, including Karo and Munro, had not become his executioners.","They had become his harvest.","Max looked at the number floating before him and smiled faintly.","\"Twenty-two million.\"","His voice was calm, but there was a faint trace of satisfaction in it.","Nancy turned toward him, still struggling to process what she had just witnessed. \"You gained fifteen million Killing Points from this one attack.\"","Max glanced at the fading crimson light around him. \"They gathered themselves together for me.\"","Nancy was silent for a moment.","There was nothing wrong with what he said.","Karo and Munro had truly gathered thousands of demons in one place, surrounded him outside the city gates, and believed that numbers would be enough to bury him.","But Max had dragged them all into the Dimension of Light and turned their ambush into his own execution ground. From beginning to end, they had never controlled the battlefield. They had only stepped into the place Max had chosen for their deaths.","The golden sky above them slowly calmed.","The luminous mountains stopped humming.","The rivers of light returned to their peaceful flow.","Max raised his hand slightly, and the last remaining strands of crimson Killing Points entered his body. Then the notification before him faded, leaving only the quiet brilliance of the Dimension of Light around them.","Nancy looked toward the place where Munro had been destroyed, then toward where Karo had died for the second time, and a complicated expression appeared in her eyes.","\"Munro and I think Karo too should have a life left.\" She said frowning.","\"Let it be,\" Max said calmly as the last traces of golden light around him faded and the Dimension of Light began to withdraw from reality. \"I do not think they would dare to hoard points like that again or pull the same conspiracy as last time. As for eliminating them completely, I do not think they would leave Starfall Haven after seeing my true strength, and right now, I cannot be bothered with them anyway.\"","He then turned to Nancy.","\"Let us head toward Witch God Valley.\"","Nancy nodded, and without wasting another moment, her figure turned into a beam of silver-white light as she shot toward a certain direction across the golden sands of the Eternal Hourglass.","Max followed closely behind her, his speed no slower than hers, and in only a few breaths, the area outside Starfall Haven became silent once again, leaving behind no demons, no ambush, and no trace of the army that had tried to surround him."]},{"number":1741,"title":"Chapter 1741: Proud Moment for the Black Dragon Clan!","paragraphs":["At the same time, far away in the territory of the Black Dragon Clan, a completely different scene was taking place.","Above the central region of the clan floated an enormous ranking list that seemed to cover the sky itself. It was formed from ancient black-gold light, and countless names were written upon it in shining characters that shifted and updated in real time.","Every disciple, elder, guardian, and important figure of the Black Dragon Clan could see it simply by raising their head, and because the Cosmic Ascension Conference was one of the most important events of the Divine Realm, this ranking list had become the center of everyone’s attention since the moment the conference began.","This was the Cosmic Ascension Ranking List.","It reflected the current standing of all young geniuses participating in the conference.","At first, the atmosphere in the Black Dragon Clan had been rather heavy, because although several of their disciples had entered the Cosmic Ascension Conference, none of them had managed to enter the top one hundred.","This was not because the Black Dragon Clan was weak, but because the Cosmic Ascension Conference gathered monstrous geniuses from every great race, ancient clan, divine forces, royal bloodline, and hidden inheritance across the Divine Realm.","To enter the top one hundred among such a crowd was already an extremely terrifying achievement, and not every great force could casually produce someone capable of doing it.","Because of this, many elders had been silently watching the list with complicated expressions.","Some were disappointed.","Some were patient.","Some were waiting for one of their clan geniuses to rise later in the conference.","But no one expected what happened next.","The ranking list suddenly trembled.","The massive black-gold characters floating in the sky shifted violently, and the names near the top began to rearrange themselves. At first, the elders thought another supreme genius from some ancient force had gained a large number of Killing Points, but when a new name suddenly shot upward through the rankings at an absurd speed, every gaze in the Black Dragon Clan froze.","The name did not stop at the top one hundred.","It did not stop at the top fifty.","It did not stop at the top twenty.","Instead, under the stunned eyes of everyone present, one name directly rushed into the top ten and stopped at the seventh position.","[Rank 7: Max]","[Killing Points: 22,000,000]","For a moment, the entire Black Dragon Clan fell into absolute silence.","Then the silence exploded.","\"What?!\"","\"Rank seven!\"","\"Max entered rank seven!\"","\"Twenty-two million Killing Points! How did he gain that many points all at once?\"","\"Was he not outside the top one hundred just moments ago?\"","\"This is impossible. He jumped directly to the seventh rank!\"","Countless disciples stared at the ranking list in disbelief, their voices filling the clan grounds like a rising storm. Some of them rubbed their eyes as if they thought they had seen wrongly, while others pointed toward the sky with trembling hands, unable to contain their excitement.","A disciple of their Black Dragon Clan had not merely entered the top one hundred. He had directly charged into the seventh rank of the entire Cosmic Ascension Conference.","That meant Max was now standing above countless geniuses from terrifying forces throughout the Divine Realm.","The elders of the Black Dragon Clan were even more shaken.","For the older generation, they understood the meaning of this ranking far more clearly than the younger disciples. The top ten of the Cosmic Ascension Conference was not a place ordinary geniuses could touch.","Every person ranked there was either backed by an ancient race, born with a heaven-defying bloodline, carrying a supreme inheritance, or possessing battle power strong enough to shake their generation.","For Max to enter rank seven so suddenly meant that he had either obtained an astonishing opportunity or killed a large number of powerful opponents in a very short period of time.","Either way, it was enough to make the Black Dragon Clan’s name resound.","\"Hahaha!\"","An elder with a long black beard suddenly laughed loudly, his voice shaking the hall beneath him. \"Good! Very good! This boy truly did not disappoint us!\"","Another elder’s eyes shone with excitement. \"To think that not long ago, none of our disciples were even in the top one hundred, yet now Max has directly reached rank seven. This is not just an improvement. This is a declaration to the entire Divine Realm that our Black Dragon Clan has produced a true monster.\"","\"Twenty-two million Killing Points,\" another elder muttered, still struggling to calm his heart. \"Even if he killed ordinary participants continuously, he would not have gained so many points so quickly. He must have killed someone carrying a massive number of points.\"","\"Or an entire group,\" someone else said.","The words made several elders fall silent for a moment.","Then their smiles became even wider.","If Max had truly wiped out a large force inside the conference, then his strength might be far more terrifying than even they had expected.","Among them, Lady Virelia stood with her gaze raised toward the enormous ranking list, and the moment she saw Max’s name shining at the seventh position, a rare smile appeared on her beautiful face. It was not the polite smile she usually showed before other elders, nor was it the calm expression she wore as a powerful master. It was a genuine smile filled with pride, satisfaction, and a trace of emotion that she did not bother hiding.","She had found Max in the mortal realm.","She had seen his potential when many others would have overlooked him.","She had brought him into the Black Dragon Clan and watched as his strength grew at a terrifying pace.","Now, that same disciple had entered the Cosmic Ascension Conference and reached rank seven in front of the entire Divine Realm.","How could she not feel proud?","\"Well done,\" Lady Virelia said softly, her eyes fixed on Max’s name. \"You really know how to make your master proud.\"","Not far from her, Mathew Grimes, the family leader of the Grimes family, also looked at the ranking list with bright eyes. His usually dignified expression was now filled with open admiration, and when he turned toward Lady Virelia, there was even a hint of respect in his gaze.","\"Virelia,\" Mathew Grimes said with a hearty laugh, \"your eyes are truly sharp. To think you found such a terrifying seed of potential in the mortal realm. Many people search the Divine Realm for countless years and still fail to discover such a genius, yet you brought one back from a lower world.\"","Several elders nodded in agreement.","\"That is true.\"","\"Virelia’s judgment was excellent.\"","\"Max’s rise will bring great prestige to our Black Dragon Clan.\"","\"Rank seven in the Cosmic Ascension Conference. Even if the ranking changes later, this alone is enough to make many forces remember his name.\"","Lady Virelia glanced at Mathew Grimes and smiled faintly. \"Potential alone is not enough. The path still depends on him.\"","Mathew Grimes nodded. \"Of course. But to gain twenty-two million Killing Points and jump directly to rank seven, he has already proved that his path is not ordinary.\"","The atmosphere across the Black Dragon Clan became more and more excited.","Disciples who had previously felt disappointed because no one from their clan had entered the top one hundred now felt their blood boil with pride. Some shouted Max’s name. Some began discussing how he had gained so many Killing Points.","Some even started imagining what would happen if Max continued climbing higher. If he had reached rank seven this suddenly, then could he fight for rank five? Rank three? Or perhaps even challenge the first rank later in the conference?","The elders did not stop them.","Even they were feeling the same excitement.","The entire Black Dragon Clan, which had been quiet and tense before, was now filled with a hypeful and fiery atmosphere. The ranking list above the clan shone brilliantly, and Max’s name at seventh place seemed like a blazing banner hanging over their heads.","[Rank 7: Max]","[Killing Points: 22,000,000]","To the rest of the Divine Realm, this sudden rise might have been shocking.","To the Black Dragon Clan, it was more than that.","It was pride.","It was hope.","It was proof that the disciple Lady Virelia had brought from the mortal realm was not merely talented.","He was a monster who had begun to shake the Cosmic Ascension Conference."]},{"number":1742,"title":"Chapter 1742: Sword God and War God!","paragraphs":["Max and Nancy moved across the sky like two streaks of light, one silver-white and one faintly golden, cutting through the vast expanse that stretched between Starfall Haven and the direction of Witch God Valley.","Beneath them, the land of the Eternal Hourglass spread out like a strange and ancient world, with endless golden sands shifting in slow waves, broken ruins half-buried beneath the desert, and distant storms of distorted time twisting between the horizon and the sky.","Every now and then, Max could sense dangerous auras sleeping beneath the sand, but none of them rose to stop him, perhaps because his speed was too great, or perhaps because the killing intent lingering around him after wiping out thousands of demons had not fully faded yet.","Nancy flew slightly ahead of him, guiding the way with familiar ease, though her expression had been unusually quiet ever since they left the area outside Starfall Haven.","She had seen many strong geniuses in her life, and as someone who served beside Elrian, she was not ignorant of the hidden monsters taking part in the Cosmic Ascension Conference, but what Max had done outside the city gates still remained in her mind like a scene carved by lightning.","He had not simply defeated Karo and Munro. He had shifted the battlefield itself, dragged thousands of demons into a a different domain, and slaughtered them with an inheritance technique that used the fifth level concept of space.","That kind of power was not something ordinary geniuses possessed, and the more Nancy thought about it, the more she understood why Elrian had been so certain that Max was connected to something far larger than a simple human bloodline.","There was also the bloodline pressure that caused her to feel like she stood become some elder level figure from her race or even worst. All this made her feel that Max wasn’t as simple as he seemed on the surface.","After flying in silence for some time, Nancy finally turned her head slightly and looked at Max.","\"Max,\" she said.","Max glanced at her without slowing down. \"What?\"","Nancy hesitated for a moment, as if she was thinking about whether this was the right time to ask, but in the end, she still spoke.","\"Do you want to inherit the War God legacy and become the War God of this generation?\"","Max’s expression shifted instantly.","For once, he actually looked confused.","He stared at Nancy for a moment, then frowned slightly. \"What?\"","Nancy looked at him seriously. \"The War God legacy.\"","Max’s brows drew together even more. \"What are you talking about?\"","Nancy seemed slightly surprised by his reaction. \"You do not know?\"","\"Know what?\" Max asked, his confusion becoming more obvious. \"Why are you suddenly asking me whether I want to become some War God? Is this related to the War God Palace or something?\"","Nancy’s eyes flashed with realization.","\"So you really do not know,\" she murmured.","Max narrowed his eyes slightly as he looked at Nancy, and although his speed did not slow, the confusion in his expression became much clearer than before.","\"Nancy, if you are going to bring up something strange in the middle of the journey, then explain it properly.\"","Nancy slowed down a little, though she still continued flying toward the direction of Witch God Valley, and after glancing at Max with a faintly helpless expression, she said, \"For a human, you sure are an ignorant one.\"","Max raised an eyebrow.","Nancy ignored his look and continued, \"Every time the Cosmic Ascension Conference is held, there are two titles that shine brighter than almost everything else. One is the Sword God, and the other is the War God. According to the old records, somewhere inside the world of the conference, there exist two ancient legacies, the legacy of the Sword God and the legacy of the War God.\"","Max listened silently.","The wind rushed past them, the golden sands of the Eternal Hourglass flowed beneath their feet like a vast sea, and the distant aura of Witch God Valley grew heavier with every passing moment, but Max’s attention was now partly focused on Nancy’s words.","He had heard of the War God Palace and the Sword God Palace before, but he had never cared enough to investigate their origin in detail. In his mind, they were simply two powerful forces among the many ancient powers of the Divine Realm.","Nancy continued, \"Whoever inherits the Sword God legacy during the Cosmic Ascension Conference will be recognized as the Sword God of that generation. It is not just an empty title. Once that happens, the Sword God Palace will acknowledge that person, support them fully, and even declare them as their Saint. The title itself gives status, protection, resources, and influence that most geniuses can only dream of obtaining.\"","Max’s eyes moved slightly.","Nancy glanced at him and added, \"The same is true for the War God legacy. Whoever inherits it becomes the War God of that generation and gains the full support of the War God Palace. They will also be given the Saint title of the War God Palace, which means that even many powerful forces would have to think twice before touching them openly.\"","Max was silent for a moment before saying, \"So the Sword God Palace and War God Palace were created because of these legacies?\"","Nancy nodded. \"Yes. Those two forces rose because of the ancient Sword God and War God legacies, and even now, their prestige is closely tied to them. Every generation, they send their strongest young geniuses into the Cosmic Ascension Conference to claim those legacies again, because if an outsider inherits one of them, then the palace connected to that legacy has no choice but to acknowledge that outsider.\"","Her expression turned slightly serious.","\"Because of that, countless geniuses fight for the Sword God and War God legacies. Some want the power. Some want the title. Some want the backing of the two palaces. Some simply want to prove that their talent is greater than the descendants trained by those ancient forces. But more often than not, the Sword God legacy is taken by a genius from the Sword God Palace, and the War God legacy is taken by someone from the War God Palace.\"","Max looked ahead calmly. \"That sounds expected. If they were created around those legacies, they should know more about them than anyone else.\""]},{"number":1743,"title":"Chapter 1743: Max’s Choice!","paragraphs":["\"Exactly,\" Nancy replied. \"That is why outsiders rarely succeed. The Sword God Palace and War God Palace know more clues, more trial locations, more hidden signs, and more ancient records related to these inheritances. They prepare for this from birth. Other geniuses may only stumble upon the legacies by chance, but those two palaces actively hunt for them from the moment the conference begins.\"","She then turned her gaze toward Max, her silver hair fluttering in the wind as her expression became more thoughtful.","\"But after seeing your fighting style, I thought you might also be aiming for the War God legacy.\"","Max glanced at her. \"Because I fight with my fists?\"","\"Because you dominate while fighting,\" Nancy said without hesitation. \"You do not fight like a cautious seeker trying to survive by luck. You choose the battlefield, suppress the enemy, crush their strongest attacks, and turn their confidence into despair. In the Combat Hall, you defeated ten opponents in a row and killed Karo. Outside Starfall Haven, you dragged thousands of demons into your own domain and killed them all. That kind of overwhelming battlefield presence is exactly the kind of thing people associate with the War God legacy.\"","Max gave a faint smile. \"So because I killed too many demons, you assumed I wanted to become War God?\"","Nancy shook her head. \"Not because you killed them. Because of how you killed them.\"","Max did not answer immediately.","He looked toward the distant darkness gathering near Witch God Valley, and his expression gradually became calm again. The War God legacy sounded powerful, and the support of the War God Palace was not something ordinary people could ignore.","The Sword God legacy also sounded tempting in its own way, especially since Max himself walked the path of the sword as well. But compared to saving Caroline and learning the truth about his mother, those legacies were not his priority right now.","After a while, Max said, \"I am not aiming for it.\"","Nancy looked slightly surprised. \"Not at all?\"","\"At least not right now,\" Max replied. \"If the War God legacy appears in front of me, and if it does not get in my way, then I may look at it. But I did not enter this place to become the Saint of some palace.\"","Nancy’s eyes flickered. \"Then what did you enter for?\"","Max’s gaze sharpened.","\"To become strong,\" Max said calmly. Nancy looked at him, and for a moment, the sound of the wind rushing past them seemed to fade beneath the weight of his words.","\"These legacies look strong,\" Max continued, his gaze fixed on the distant cursed mist gathering around Witch God Valley, \"and whoever obtains them may indeed become extremely powerful, but I already have my own path to follow. I realized some time ago that my path does not belong to the Sword God, nor does it belong to the War God.\"","Nancy’s eyes moved slightly.","Max’s voice remained calm, but the calmness carried a frightening certainty, the kind that did not come from ignorance or reckless arrogance, but from someone who had already looked at himself, measured his own direction, and decided what kind of existence he wanted to become. He did not sound tempted by the Sword God legacy, nor did he sound greedy for the War God legacy.","To him, those titles might be glorious in the eyes of countless geniuses, and those inheritances might be enough to make entire forces go mad with desire, but they were not the peak he was chasing.","\"They may be powerful,\" Max said, his eyes narrowing slightly, \"but they are not my destination.\"","Nancy remained silent.","For most young geniuses of the Divine Realm, the title of Sword God or War God would be enough to define their entire life. It would give them fame, resources, protection, and a path already recognized by countless generations.","Many would fight, bleed, betray, and die for even a chance to touch those legacies. But Max spoke about them as if they were not supreme opportunities, but only passing landmarks on the road ahead.","Max turned his head slightly and looked at Nancy.","\"If I want to become the strongest,\" he said, a faint grin appearing on his face, \"then the so-called Sword God and War God are only stepping stones for me.\"","Nancy’s breathing paused for half a moment. Those words were outrageous. They were so arrogant that if any disciple from the Sword God Palace or War God Palace heard them, they would probably attack Max on the spot. Even the ancient forces behind those titles might consider his words a direct insult.","The Sword God and War God were not ordinary names. They were titles that had shaken generations of the Cosmic Ascension Conference, names that countless geniuses worshiped as peaks of swordsmanship and battle. Yet Max had placed them beneath his feet in a single sentence.","But strangely, after seeing what he had done, Nancy could not immediately call his words foolish. She had seen him crush ten opponents inside the Combat Hall. She had seen him destroy Karo’s Pseudo Cosmic Path without revealing his own. She had seen him drag thousands of demons into a dimension of light and annihilate them with a single inheritance technique.","If another person had said such a thing, Nancy would have thought they were insane. When Max said it, she only felt a chill. Not because she fully believed he could surpass those ancient titles right now, but because he truly believed that he would, and the terrifying part was that his actions so far made that belief difficult to dismiss.","\"You do realize,\" Nancy said after a moment, \"that if someone from the Sword God Palace or War God Palace heard you say that, they would probably treat you as an enemy.\"","Max smiled faintly. \"Then they can treat me as one.\"","Nancy looked at him with a complicated expression. \"You are already planning to offend the second faction of the elves, demons like Karo and Munro, and perhaps even the forces hunting Caroline. Do you really want to add the Sword God Palace and War God Palace to that list?\"","Here is the continuation with the sudden ambush over the neutral city:","\"Sword God Palace is already hunting me down, and I do not believe the War God Palace will do something exactly like the Sword God Palace,\" Max said with a faint smile as he continued flying beside Nancy. \"But this is still a tournament, and if the geniuses of the War God Palace come after me, then I will not back down from them either.\""]},{"number":1744,"title":"Chapter 1744: An Ambush?!","paragraphs":["Nancy nodded slowly, but her thoughts were no longer as calm as before.","She had thought she understood Max’s strength after seeing him kill Karo, destroy thousands of demons, and gain twenty-two million Killing Points in such a short time, but the more she spoke with him, the more she felt that she might still be underestimating him.","His strength was terrifying, but what made him even more dangerous was his mentality. He did not place demons, elves, the Sword God Palace, the War God Palace, or even ancient legacies on some unreachable pedestal.","To Max, they were all things standing somewhere on the same road he had chosen to walk, and if they blocked him, then they would become enemies to be crushed rather than mountains to be worshiped.","For a brief moment, Nancy even felt that perhaps her prince had also underestimated this human.","Soon, as the two of them flew across the sky, a city came into view below them.","Unlike Starfall Haven, which had carried a bright and peaceful silver radiance, this city looked darker and more ancient. It was built between several curved stone ridges rising from the golden sands of the Eternal Hourglass, and its walls were formed from pale gray crystal engraved with countless protective runes.","A faint dome of neutral energy covered the city, preventing battles from breaking out inside, while several wide roads stretched from its gates toward different dangerous zones in the surrounding region.","Although it was much smaller than Starfall Haven, many participants could still be seen moving through its streets, resting, trading information, healing injuries, or preparing to enter the deeper parts of the Eternal Hourglass.","\"This should be another neutral city,\" Nancy said while looking down.","Max lowered his gaze toward the city.","For a moment, everything seemed normal.","Then his eyes narrowed slightly.","In the next instant, several sharp auras suddenly erupted from different directions around them.","Whoosh! Whoosh! Whoosh!","Hundreds of figures rushed into the air from the city below, from nearby ruins, from the stone ridges, and from hidden positions in the clouds. In only a few breaths, Max and Nancy were completely surrounded above the neutral city.","Some of these people were humans, some were elves, and some belonged to other races with strange appearances, but all of them had one thing in common. Their weapons were already drawn, their auras were fully prepared, and their attacks were locked onto Max and Nancy as if they had been waiting for them to arrive.","The sky became tense instantly.","Sword lights hovered in the air.","Spears of energy gathered above several hands.","Bowstrings were pulled tight.","Runes lit up across floating talismans.","A few participants held chained blades that glowed with poisonous light, while others summoned elemental formations beneath their feet, ready to unleash attacks the moment they received the order. Hundreds of killing intents pressed toward Max and Nancy at once, forming a heavy pressure that made the air around them feel as though it had turned solid.","Nancy’s expression changed.","\"This is not normal,\" she said in a low voice.","Max’s gaze swept across the people surrounding them, and his expression remained calm.","He had expected danger on the way to Witch God Valley, but he had not expected hundreds of participants to appear so suddenly around a neutral city.","More importantly, judging by the way they had positioned themselves, this was not a random encounter. They had been prepared. They had been waiting. Someone had known their route.","A tall man in dark blue armor slowly stepped forward from among the encircling crowd, his long sword held loosely in his hand, while several sharp sword lights circled around his body like obedient spirits. His gaze landed on Max first, then briefly moved to Nancy before returning to him again.","\"Max,\" the man said coldly. \"You finally arrived.\"","Nancy glanced at Max.","\"You know him?\"","Max looked at the man for a moment, then smiled faintly. \"No.\"","The dark blue armored man’s expression stiffened slightly, clearly displeased by that answer.","Max continued calmly, \"But from the way he is looking at me, I can guess he is either from the Sword God Palace or someone hired by them.\"","The man’s eyes became cold.","\"Your guess is not wrong,\" he said. \"You offended the Sword God Palace, and you still dare to fly openly above a neutral city as if no one can touch you?\"","Max raised an eyebrow. \"I have been busy killing demons. I almost forgot you people were still chasing me.\"","The surrounding participants immediately stirred.","Some of them looked angry, while others exchanged uncertain glances. The name Max had already begun spreading after his sudden rise in the Cosmic Ascension Ranking List, and some among them clearly knew that the person standing before them now had reached the seventh rank with twenty-two million Killing Points.","That number alone was enough to make many people hesitate, but greed, orders, and the prestige of the Sword God Palace had still brought them here.","Nancy’s eyes turned sharp. \"You people chose a very interesting place to block us. The city below is a neutral zone. Are you planning to attack us in full view of its protection rules?\"","The man in dark blue armor smiled coldly. \"We are not inside the city.\"","Nancy’s expression darkened.","He was right.","They were above the city, close enough to see its streets and protective dome below, but not within the actual boundary of the neutral zone. The surrounding participants had chosen their position very carefully.","If Max and Nancy descended into the city, they would be protected, but right now, in the air above the outer boundary, nothing stopped these people from attacking.","Max glanced down at the city and smiled faintly.","\"So that is why you waited here.\"","The dark blue armored man raised his sword slightly, and the hundreds of participants around them immediately tightened their formation.","\"You can still surrender,\" he said. \"Hand over your Killing Points, come with us peacefully, and perhaps the Sword God Palace will leave you with a few lives.\""]},{"number":1745,"title":"Chapter 1745: Change of Situation!","paragraphs":["Max looked at him silently for a moment.","Then he laughed.","It was not loud, but the mockery in it spread clearly across the sky.","\"You people really never learn.\"","The dark blue armored man’s eyes narrowed. \"Do not think your ranking will protect you. Rank seven only means you have gathered many Killing Points. It does not mean you can fight everyone here alone.\"","Max’s smile became colder.","\"I heard something similar not long ago,\" he said. \"Karo also thought numbers could stop me.\"","Some of the surrounding participants’ faces changed when they heard Karo’s name. Clearly, news of what had happened outside Starfall Haven had not fully reached everyone yet, but some had heard fragments. The demon Karo had been known among many participants, and if Max was mentioning him in such a tone, then something serious must have happened.","Nancy slowly drew her sword and said quietly, \"Max, we do not have time to waste here. Caroline may still be in danger.\"","Max nodded. \"I know.\"","He raised his gaze and looked at the hundreds of people surrounding them.","\"Then let us make this quick.\"","The moment those words fell, the atmosphere in the sky became even heavier.","The dark blue armored man’s expression turned cold, and he immediately lifted his sword higher. \"Attack formation!\"","In an instant, hundreds of prepared attacks brightened at once.","Sword lights screamed.","Elemental spears trembled.","Talismans burned.","Bows released sharp killing intent.","The sky above the neutral city was filled with power ready to descend, and all of it was aimed at Max and Nancy.","Max stood at the center of the encirclement with a faint smile on his face, his eyes calm, his body relaxed, and his gaze so cold that even several attackers felt a chill move through their hearts.","Below them, the neutral city remained peaceful.","Above it, battle was about to erupt.","\"Stop!\" Just as the hundreds of attacks were about to be launched, a loud shout suddenly rang across the sky, and the command carried such authority that the tense atmosphere froze in an instant.","The sword lights stopped trembling, the elemental spears halted in midair, the drawn bowstrings remained pulled tight without releasing, and even the dark blue armored man who had been preparing to give the final order turned his head with a stiff expression.","A young man appeared in the sky not far away. He wore a white and silver battle robe embroidered with faint sword patterns, and although his aura was not wildly released, the sharpness hidden within him was enough to make the surrounding air feel as if it had been filled with invisible blades.","His expression was dark, his eyes were cold, and the moment he appeared, every person involved in surrounding Max and Nancy lowered their heads at once. Even the dark blue armored man, who had acted so arrogantly before, suddenly became uncertain, and the confidence on his face faded at a visible speed.","Max looked at the newcomer with a faintly interested expression.","Nancy’s eyes moved slightly as she whispered, \"He should be someone with a higher status in this group.\"","Max did not respond, but his gaze remained calm.","The young man ignored Max and Nancy for the moment and turned his cold eyes directly toward the dark blue armored man. \"What are you doing here?\" he asked, his voice carrying obvious anger.","The dark blue armored man opened his mouth, but before he could answer, the young man’s expression became even darker. \"Did I not tell you to gather everyone who passed through the neutral city at the entrance?\" he shouted. \"Why are you blocking people in the sky and preparing to start a battle here?\"","The surrounding people lowered their heads even further.","The dark blue armored man’s face changed several times before he finally forced himself to speak. \"But he is an enemy of the Sword God Palace, and so we thought we should take care of him personally.\"","\"Personally?\" the young man repeated, his voice turning colder. \"Are you out of your mind?\" The dark blue armored man trembled slightly.","The young man’s gaze became sharper, and the invisible sword aura around him made several people nearby feel their skin sting. \"Are you trying to defy Princess Rosaline’s order?\" he demanded.","The moment the name Princess Rosaline was spoken, the expressions of everyone surrounding Max changed. Even Nancy glanced at Max, her eyes carrying a trace of surprise, while Max’s gaze sharpened slightly. He did not know who this Princess Rosaline was, but judging from the reaction of the dark blue armored man and the hundreds of people around them, her status was clearly not ordinary.","\"I dare not!\" the dark blue armored man immediately said, his voice carrying fear as he lowered his head. \"I would never dare to defy Princess Rosaline’s order.\"","\"Good,\" the young man said coldly. He then raised his hand and pointed toward Max and Nancy. \"Take the two of them to the entrance and make them stand in the line.\" The dark blue armored man hesitated for only a fraction of a second before nodding quickly.","\"Understood.\" The young man’s expression did not soften. He looked at the dark blue armored man again and said in a warning tone, \"I do not want anything like this to happen again. Princess Rosaline gave clear instructions. Anyone who passes through this neutral city is to be gathered at the entrance, not attacked without permission because of your personal judgment.\"","The dark blue armored man lowered his head even further. \"Understood.\"","\"Good.\"","After saying that, the young man gave Max a brief glance. His eyes paused on Max for a moment, as if he had also recognized something about him, but he did not say anything more. In the next instant, his figure blurred and disappeared from the sky, leaving behind only a faint trace of sword aura that slowly faded into the wind.","\"If you don’t want to die and lose all your points then come and follow us.\" The dark blue armored man then said to Max."]},{"number":1746,"title":"Chapter 1746: Emotion Severing Path!","paragraphs":["\"Is that so?\" Max smiled lightly as he looked at the dark blue armored man and the disciples of the Sword God Palace surrounding him, and although his tone sounded casual, his eyes had already become sharp enough to see through the strange situation around this neutral city.","He understood that something was wrong here. Princess Rosaline’s order might have been real, and the gathering of participants at the entrance might have had some greater purpose, but the way these Sword God Palace disciples had tried to block him in the sky and attack him before he could even reach the city entrance made it clear that they were using that order for their own convenience.","There was a conspiracy here too, perhaps smaller than what Karo and Munro had prepared outside Starfall Haven, but still troublesome enough to delay him if he followed along obediently.","Nancy noticed the faint smile on his face and immediately felt that something bad was about to happen.","\"What do you plan to do?\" she asked in a low voice while keeping her eyes on the dark blue armored man and the surrounding disciples. \"We do not have much time. I do not know how long Caroline can hold out. There are too many of them.\"","\"Do not worry,\" Max said with a relaxed smile. \"It will not take much time.\"","As soon as he said those words, he raised his hand, and a sword appeared in his grip.","The Dragonheart.","The moment the sword emerged, the atmosphere changed instantly.","The blade released a deep and ancient pressure, and the faint dragon aura sleeping within it spread outward like the breath of a beast opening its eyes. Its surface carried a dark sheen, yet hidden beneath that darkness was a powerful pulse that made the weapon feel alive, as if a dragon’s heart was truly beating inside the sword.","The surrounding disciples of the Sword God Palace immediately became alert, and several of them instinctively stepped back while tightening their grips on their own swords. Their eyes, which had been filled with hostility before, now carried greed, caution, and excitement.","The dark blue armored man’s expression changed the most.","He stared at Dragonheart with burning eyes for a split second before forcing his face to twist into anger.","\"Max, what did I tell you?!\" he snapped, his voice sharp and furious. \"If you do not want to die, then follow us obediently, and yet here you are taking out your weapon in front of the Sword God Palace!\"","Max looked at him, then lowered his gaze toward Dragonheart with a faint smile.","\"Is that not what you people are after?\"","The dark blue armored man’s face stiffened.","Max slowly swung Dragonheart through the air, and the motion caused a soft sword hum to spread across the sky. The sound was not loud, but every swordsman present felt it clearly, and many disciples of the Sword God Palace felt their own swords tremble slightly in response. That single reaction made their eyes change again.","Max noticed every change in their expressions.","His smile widened.","\"You people have been chasing me because of this sword, right?\" he asked while casually letting Dragonheart rest across his shoulder. \"It is here. Come and take it from me.\"","The words struck the Sword God Palace disciples like a direct slap to the face.","Several of them flushed with anger.","Some could no longer hide the greed in their eyes.","Others glanced toward the dark blue armored man, clearly waiting for him to make a decision.","Here is the continuation with Max revealing his Pseudo Cosmic Path and cutting down the Sword God Palace disciples:","\"If you guys do not want to make a move, then do not blame me.\"","The moment Max spoke those words, the playful smile on his face disappeared.","It did not fade slowly.","It vanished completely.","The casual arrogance in his eyes, the relaxed curve of his lips, and the faint amusement he had shown while provoking the Sword God Palace disciples were all erased in an instant, leaving behind a face so calm and empty that it looked almost inhuman.","There was no anger on his face. There was no excitement. There was no killing intent burning wildly in his eyes. There was only a deathly stillness, a cold and emotionless silence that made the surrounding air feel as if it had been cut away from the world itself.","\"Emotion Severing Path,\" Max muttered.","The moment those three words fell, an eerie aura spread from his body.","It was not like the overwhelming draconic pressure he had released against Karo, nor was it like the holy brilliance of his Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline when he had used Divine Light of Justice and Truth.","This aura was quieter than both, but far more unsettling. It did not roar. It did not blaze. It did not explode outward with violent force. Instead, it spread like an invisible blade through the sky, cutting through sound, warmth, fear, anger, pride, and even the instinctive emotions that made living beings react to danger.","The world around Max seemed to grow silent.","The wind stopped feeling like wind.","The light lost its warmth.","The sword lights of the Sword God Palace disciples trembled in the air, but even their sharpness seemed to become dull beneath the emotionless pressure that surrounded Max. His Pseudo Cosmic Path was born from the Severing Sword Concept, but it was not merely a path that cut flesh, weapons, or energy.","It severed deeper things. It severed hesitation, severed attachment, severed thought, severed emotion, and in that moment, every person standing before him felt as if something inside their hearts had been touched by a cold sword edge.","Nancy’s body trembled.","She had stood beside Max when he unleashed his Dragon Scales Transformation. She had seen him activate five thousand Draconic Essences. She had witnessed him summon the Dimension of Light and erase thousands of demons with golden cross-shaped constructs.","But this was different. Those powers had been terrifying because they were vast and overwhelming. This one was terrifying because it was quiet. It felt like death without hatred, judgment without mercy, and a sword that did not care whether its target screamed, begged, resisted, or regretted.","Her fingers tightened around the hilt of her sword without her realizing it."]},{"number":1747,"title":"Chapter 1747: Terrifying Pseudo Cosmic Path!","paragraphs":["\"This is his Pseudo Cosmic Path...\" Nancy thought, her heart shaking.","Only now did she understand why Max had told Karo that he was not worthy to see it.","The Emotion Severing Path did not feel like an ordinary Pseudo Cosmic Path at all. It felt like a blade placed against the soul, and the moment Max entered this state, even Nancy, who was not his enemy, felt as if her instincts were warning her not to stand too close to him.","The dark blue armored man, who had been rushing toward Max with his sword raised, suddenly felt his heart turn cold.","For a split second, he forgot why he had attacked.","His anger disappeared.","His greed disappeared.","Even his fear appeared late, as if it had been severed from his mind before it could fully form.","\"What is this...\" he whispered.","Max raised Dragonheart.","His movement was slow.","It was simple.","There was no dazzling sword art, no storm of sword energy, and no grand roar of power. He merely lifted the blade with that deathly calm expression on his face, and the eerie aura of the Emotion Severing Path gathered along the edge of Dragonheart.","The sword did not shine brightly. Instead, a thin, almost invisible line formed along its blade, so sharp and quiet that it seemed capable of cutting through the boundary between existence and nothingness.","The Sword God Palace disciples finally sensed danger.","\"Defend!\"","\"Move back!\"","\"Attack together!\"","Their voices rang out almost at the same time, but it was already too late.","Max swung his sword once.","A silent sword light crossed the sky.","No one saw it clearly.","There was no thunderous explosion.","There was no overwhelming wave of power.","There was only a thin line passing through the air.","The dark blue armored man froze in place first.","His sword was still raised.","His eyes were still wide.","His expression still carried the last trace of disbelief that had appeared when he sensed Max’s Pseudo Cosmic Path.","Then a straight line appeared across his body.","From his shoulder to his waist, his armor split open cleanly, his sword aura collapsed without resistance, and in the next breath, his entire body separated into two halves before dissolving into light. He did not even have time to scream. He did not have time to understand what had happened. He did not even have time to regret attacking Max.","And he was not the only one.","Behind him, the same silent sword light passed through the formation of the Sword God Palace disciples.","One by one, their bodies split apart.","Some were cut from the chest.","Some were cut through the waist.","Some had their weapons, armor, and bodies severed together in a single clean line.","Some were still preparing their attacks when their expressions froze, their eyes dimmed, and their bodies separated before they could release even a fraction of their strength. The sword light did not slow down after cutting the first few disciples.","It continued through the air with terrifying precision, cutting through every Sword God Palace disciple who had surrounded Max and Nancy, no matter where they stood, no matter what defense they raised, and no matter how quickly they tried to retreat.","In only one slash, all hundred or so disciples of the Sword God Palace were cut down.","The sky fell silent.","Their attacks disappeared.","Their sword lights vanished.","Their bodies dissolved one after another, leaving behind streams of Killing Points that scattered through the air like crimson sparks.","The participants gathered near the entrance of the neutral city stared upward in absolute shock.","Some had not even realized Max had moved.","Some had only seen him raise Dragonheart.","Some had blinked once, and when their eyes opened again, the entire group of Sword God Palace disciples had already been severed in two.","Nancy stood beside Max, her body still trembling faintly from the aura of his Emotion Severing Path. She looked at the empty sky where the Sword God Palace disciples had been moments ago, then slowly turned her gaze toward Max. His face was still emotionless. His eyes were calm. His sword was lowered slightly, and not a single drop of blood stained its edge.","The crimson Killing Points drifted toward him.","Max raised his hand and absorbed them without looking at the remains of the disciples he had just killed.","Only after the last stream of Killing Points entered his body did the eerie aura around him begin to fade. The silence that had weighed upon the sky slowly loosened, the wind returned, and the terrifying emotionless state on Max’s face softened back into a faint, casual smile.","[Participant: Max]","[Previous Killing Points: 22,000,000]","[Absorbed Killing Points: 7,000,000]","[Current Killing Points: 29,000,000]","[Rank: 7]","\"Huh? Only seven million Killing Points among these hundred or so disciples of the Sword God Palace?\" Max frowned slightly as the final crimson stream entered his body, and although the amount was not small in the eyes of ordinary participants, it still felt lower than he had expected from a group backed by a force as famous as the Sword God Palace. \"For disciples of the Sword God Palace, this is a little disappointing.\"","Nancy looked at him with a helpless expression, but there was also urgency in her eyes.","\"Max, we should go,\" she said quickly. \"We cannot waste any more time here.\"","Max glanced toward her, then nodded.","Before leaving, he looked down at the neutral city beneath them. His Dimensional Sovereign Body allowed him to sense space and hidden presences far more clearly than ordinary cultivators, and for a brief moment, he felt a terrifying aura sleeping somewhere inside the city, an aura so sharp and noble that it stood above the hundreds of Sword God Palace disciples he had just killed. Whoever that person was, they were not weak, and if Max had more time, he might have been interested in seeing what kind of person could release such a presence.","But right now, Caroline mattered more.","\"Let us go.\"","The moment he spoke, Max and Nancy turned into two streaks of light and flew past the neutral city area at terrifying speed. In only a few seconds, they vanished beyond the distant sky, leaving behind a shaken crowd near the city entrance, an empty battlefield above the neutral zone, and the lingering trace of Max’s Emotion Severing Path still cutting through the air like an invisible scar."]},{"number":1748,"title":"Chapter 1748: Princess Roseline!","paragraphs":["Only a few seconds after Max and Nancy disappeared, a figure appeared at the scene.","She was a young woman dressed in a flowing white and rose-gold gown that shone faintly beneath the light of the Eternal Hourglass, and the moment she arrived, the entire atmosphere around the city seemed to become quieter.","Her long golden-pink hair fell smoothly down her back, her eyes were clear and bright like polished gemstones, and her bearing carried a natural elegance that could not be imitated.","She did not need to announce her identity. The crown-like ornament resting above her forehead, the noble pressure surrounding her, and the way several nearby guards immediately lowered their heads all made it obvious.","She was Princess Rosaline.","And she truly looked like a princess.","Her beauty was refined, her posture was dignified, and even the slight frown on her face carried the authority of someone used to being obeyed. However, at this moment, there was no gentleness in her eyes.","She looked around the area where the Sword God Palace disciples had been cut down, and the more she observed, the more serious her expression became.","There were no bodies left.","Only fading traces of Killing Points, shattered sword intent, and a terrifying sword aura that had not fully dispersed.","Rosaline slowly raised one hand and touched the air in front of her.","The moment her fingers brushed against the remaining aura, her pupils narrowed slightly.","\"What a terrifying sword aura,\" she muttered to herself.","The aura was thin now, only a remnant left behind after the attack had already ended, but even this remnant was frightening. It was not wild, nor was it loud, yet it carried an eerie sharpness that made her feel as if something emotionless had passed through this space and severed everything in its path.","The sword aura did not feel like ordinary sword intent. It felt deeper, colder, and far more dangerous, as if the person who had released it had cut down the disciples without even allowing their emotions, thoughts, or fear to fully form.","Rosaline’s expression became solemn.","\"Could it have been Damian?\"","The name left her lips in a soft murmur.","Damian of the Sword God Palace.","Among the younger generation of the Sword God Palace, Damian was one of the few people whose sword aura could make even Rosaline feel cautious. His talent in the sword was monstrous, and if anyone in this region could leave behind such a terrifying sword trace, Damian would naturally be the first person she would suspect.","Moreover, Damian of the Sword God Palace was the one who had the highest chance of inheriting the Sword God’s Legacy this time.","But the moment that thought appeared, Rosaline’s brows furrowed even deeper.","\"That does not make sense,\" she muttered.","Her gaze swept across the empty sky where the Sword God Palace disciples had vanished.","\"Why would Damian kill disciples of his own force?\"","The question made the situation even more strange. These were disciples of the Sword God Palace. Even if Damian was arrogant, even if he had conflicts with some of them, there was no reason for him to cut down more than a hundred of his own people so cleanly near a neutral city, especially when Princess Rosaline had given clear orders to gather all passing participants at the entrance. Doing something like this would not only be cruel, it would also be foolish, and Damian was not foolish.","Rosaline closed her eyes for a brief moment and sensed the lingering sword aura again.","The more she felt it, the more unsettled she became.","The sword aura was not exactly the same as Damian’s.","Damian’s sword was proud, sharp, and domineering, like a blade that wanted all other swords to lower themselves before it.","But this aura was different. It was quiet. It was empty. It carried a strange severing force that seemed to cut away not only bodies, but also the very emotions behind resistance. It was sword power, but not the kind of sword power she associated with Damian.","Her eyes opened slowly.","\"Is there another person besides Damian who can possess such terrifying sword aura?\"","The words came out almost unconsciously, and there was deep shock in her voice.","Around her, the guards who had followed her remained silent, not daring to disturb her thoughts. They had arrived too late. Whoever had caused this had already left, and the only thing remaining was a sword trace powerful enough to make Princess Rosaline herself fall into thought.","Rosaline turned toward the direction Max and Nancy had disappeared.","She had not seen them clearly, but the fading spatial disturbance in the air told her that two figures had left only moments before she arrived.","\"One of them did this,\" she said softly.","Her eyes sharpened.","If the person responsible was not Damian, then the situation had become far more interesting than she expected.","A mysterious swordsman had appeared, killed more than a hundred Sword God Palace disciples with a single terrifying sword slash, left behind a sword aura that could rival the strongest geniuses of the Sword God Palace, and then disappeared toward the direction of Witch God Valley.","Rosaline’s expression grew thoughtful.","\"Witch God Valley...\" she murmured.","After a moment, she turned toward the guards behind her.","\"Find out who passed through this area just now. I want names, races, affiliations, and everything the witnesses saw.\"","\"Yes, Princess.\"","Several guards immediately lowered their heads and moved to obey.","Rosaline remained in the sky, still staring toward the direction where Max had gone. The wind brushed against her gown, and the last remnant of Max’s Emotion Severing Path finally began to fade from the air, but the impression it left behind remained deeply carved into her mind.","\"If this was not Damian,\" she whispered, \"then a new monster has entered the stage.\"","Her gaze became sharper.","\"And he is heading toward Witch God Valley.\"","Just at that moment, the young man who had appeared earlier to stop the dark blue armored man from attacking Max descended from the sky and appeared before Princess Rosaline. His expression was no longer as cold and commanding as it had been when he scolded the Sword God Palace disciples.","Now, there was a clear trace of apology on his face, and after landing a short distance away from Rosaline, he immediately lowered his head in respect.","\"Princess,\" he said in an apologetic manner, \"I know who did this.\""]},{"number":1749,"title":"Chapter 1749: Rosaline’s Curiosity!","paragraphs":["Rosaline slowly turned toward him.","Her eyes narrowed slightly, and the thoughtful look on her face became sharper.","\"Who is it?\"","The young man hesitated for only a moment before answering in a solemn voice, \"It is Max Morgan.\"","The moment that name was spoken, Rosaline’s gaze changed.","\"The recently popular kid who took away the Sword of the Sword Sovereign,\" the young man added. \"He was the one who passed through here with a silver-haired elf woman, and he was also the one these Sword God Palace disciples tried to stop.\"","\"Oh,\" Rosaline murmured, surprise flashing through her eyes. \"It was him.\"","She had indeed heard of Max Morgan.","Max had been a bit too popular in the Divine Realm the past few months since he had taken away the sword of the Sword Sovereign and because of this, almost every individual had heard of him in one way or another.","Rosaline was no exception.","But now, looking at the empty sky where more than a hundred Sword God Palace disciples had been cut down in one slash, Rosaline realized that Max Morgan might not be as simple as the rumors made him seem.","\"Interesting,\" she muttered, and a faint smile appeared on her lips as deep thought filled her eyes. \"So the one who left behind this sword aura was Max Morgan.\"","She looked again at the fading trace in the air.","The eerie sharpness of the sword aura still lingered faintly, and even though it was almost gone, Rosaline could feel how terrifyingly clean that slash had been. It did not resemble the clumsy swing of someone relying only on a powerful weapon. It had carried concept, path, and terrifying control.","Still, the Sword of the Sword Sovereign was not an ordinary sword.","A sword of that level could raise the threat of its wielder far beyond their normal strength.","Rosaline’s smile became more curious.","\"Is he truly that strong,\" she murmured softly, \"or is it all because of that sword?\"","The young man lowered his head even further, his expression filled with regret.","\"Forgive me, Princess,\" he said with a sigh. \"I did not think Max would be this strong. Otherwise, I would have informed you beforehand and stopped those fools more forcefully.\"","Rosaline glanced at him, then shook her head lightly.","\"It is not your fault.\"","The young man looked up slightly.","Rosaline’s smile remained calm, but the interest in her eyes had grown much clearer. \"Those disciples acted out of greed and arrogance. Even after being warned, they still chose to provoke someone they did not understand. If they died because of that, then it was the consequence of their own stupidity.\"","The young man was silent for a moment before nodding. \"Yes, Princess.\"","Rosaline turned her gaze toward the direction where Max and Nancy had disappeared.","\"They are heading toward Witch God Valley, correct?\"","\"Yes,\" the young man replied. \"From the direction they took, there is almost no doubt. They should be moving toward the valley.\"","Rosaline’s eyes narrowed slightly.","Witch God Valley.","\"And since we know where they are headed,\" Rosaline said with a faint smile, \"there is definitely a chance for us to intercept him.\"","The young man’s expression changed slightly. \"Princess, do you intend to personally meet him?\"","Rosaline did not answer immediately.","She slowly raised her hand again and touched the last remnant of sword aura in the air. The moment her fingers passed through it, a faint chill crossed her skin, and the smile on her face deepened.","\"If this sword aura came only from the Sword of the Sword Sovereign, then the sword is even more terrifying than we imagined,\" she said softly. \"But if it came from Max himself, then he is far more dangerous than the rumors suggest.\"","The young man’s eyes became serious.","Rosaline lowered her hand.","\"Either way,\" she continued, \"he is worth meeting.\"","She turned toward the guards behind her.","\"Prepare to move. We will head toward Witch God Valley.\"","The guards immediately lowered their heads.","\"Yes, Princess.\"","Rosaline looked one last time at the empty sky where the Sword God Palace disciples had been cut down, and her expression became thoughtful again.","\"Max Morgan,\" she said softly, as if testing the name on her tongue. \"A human who took the Sword of the Sword Sovereign, offended the Sword God Palace, and left behind a sword aura terrifying enough to make me think of Damian.\"","Her eyes flashed with interest.","\"Let us see what kind of person you really are.\"","——","Max and Nancy continued flying at full speed after leaving the neutral city behind, and for the next hour, neither of them wasted time speaking unnecessarily. The farther they moved into the depths of the Eternal Hourglass, the stranger the world around them became.","The golden sands beneath them gradually lost their warm color and turned dull and gray, while the air grew colder, heavier, and filled with faint whispers that seemed to come from nowhere.","Broken ruins appeared from time to time beneath the shifting sand, some half-buried, some floating in the air without support, and some surrounded by strange distortions where time seemed to flow slower than the rest of the world.","Even Max, with his confidence and strength, could feel that this region was no longer as simple as the areas near Starfall Haven.","Nancy flew slightly ahead of him, her silver hair fluttering behind her like a streak of moonlight, and her expression remained serious as she checked their direction again and again. She clearly knew that the path to Witch God Valley was not ordinary, and although they had not encountered any major enemies during the past hour, she did not relax even once.","Max noticed this, but he did not ask anything. His mind was focused on Caroline. The thought that his mother’s younger sister might be trapped somewhere ahead, hunted by Seraphine, Fin, and the second faction’s geniuses, made his eyes colder with every passing moment.","Then, after crossing a vast region of dead sand and shattered stone, Max suddenly slowed down.","Ahead of them, a shadow rose from the earth.","At first, it looked like a distant mountain standing beneath the clouds, but as they drew closer, Max realized that it was not a mountain at all.","It was a tree.","A huge tree.","No.","Calling it huge was almost an insult to its size."]},{"number":1750,"title":"Chapter 1750: Witch God Tree!","paragraphs":["The tree stood in the middle of the desolate land like an ancient pillar supporting the sky. Its trunk was so wide that even several cities placed side by side might not have been enough to cover its base, and its bark was dark brown mixed with faint traces of gray-black lines that looked almost like old scars carved by lightning.","Countless roots spread from its base and tore through the earth in every direction, some thicker than mountain ridges, some sinking deep into the sand, and some twisting upward like enormous sleeping dragons.","Strange mist coiled around the roots, and every now and then, faint green-black lights flickered within the cracks of the bark.","Max raised his head.","The top of the tree could not be seen.","Its trunk rose higher and higher, piercing through layers of mist, passing through the clouds, and vanishing into a dark sky above. The branches that could be seen were already larger than ordinary mountains, and each one stretched outward for an unknown distance, forming pathways, cliffs, and forest-like platforms high above the ground.","Some parts of the tree were covered in pale leaves that released a ghostly glow, while other parts were completely withered, as if life and death had been forced to exist together within the same ancient body.","For once, Max’s expression showed genuine surprise.","\"What kind of tree is this?\" he muttered.","He had seen many strange things since entering the Divine Realm. He had seen divine abilities, hidden dimensions, demonic armies, Pseudo Cosmic Paths, and mysterious inheritances, but the tree in front of him still managed to shock him.","It did not feel like a normal living thing. It felt like a world by itself, an ancient existence rooted into the Eternal Hourglass and stretching into places ordinary people were not meant to reach.","Nancy stopped beside him and looked up at the towering tree with a solemn expression.","\"This is the Witch God Tree,\" she said. \"Some call it the Dead Heaven Tree. Others call it the Cursed Root of the Eternal Hourglass. No one knows its true origin, but the legends say it grew from the body of the ancient witch god who died in this region.\"","Max glanced at her. \"And Witch God Valley is here?\"","Nancy nodded, then raised her hand and pointed upward.","\"Witch God Valley should be at the very top of this tree.\"","Max looked up again.","The top was hidden beyond the clouds, and even with his eyesight, he could not clearly see what lay above. The clouds around the upper part of the tree were not ordinary either.","They were dark, heavy, and faintly purple, with strands of green lightning flickering inside them like cursed veins. From time to time, strange cries drifted down from above, though it was impossible to tell whether they came from beasts, spirits, or the wind itself.","Nancy continued, \"The valley is not on the ground. It is formed between the highest branches of the Witch God Tree, where the cursed mist gathers and creates a hidden region. That place is extremely dangerous, and once someone enters it, the tree itself makes it difficult to leave. Caroline and the others must have fled upward because the lower routes were blocked by the second faction’s hunters.\"","Max’s eyes narrowed. \"So Seraphine and Fin are also up there?\"","\"If they are still chasing her, then yes,\" Nancy replied. \"They should already be somewhere above us, either climbing through the branch roads or searching the outer mist of Witch God Valley.\"","Max looked at the trunk for a moment, then smiled coldly.","\"Then we go up.\"","Nancy’s expression became more serious. \"Be careful. Flying directly upward is the fastest way, but it may also attract the attention of the creatures living on the tree. The Witch God Tree is not empty. There are cursed beasts, soul insects, illusion flowers, and strange remnants of ancient witch power hidden all over it. Some of them are dangerous even to powerful geniuses.\"","Max’s gaze remained fixed on the unseen top of the tree.","\"We do not have time to climb slowly.\"","Nancy had expected that answer.","She nodded. \"Then fly to the very top of the tree. I will guide you as much as I can, but once we enter the upper mist, even my senses may be affected.\"","Max’s body began to release a faint golden light as he prepared to accelerate again.","\"Stay close to me,\" he said.","Nancy looked at him and nodded.","In the next instant, Max shot upward like a streak of golden lightning, flying along the massive trunk of the Witch God Tree toward the clouds above. Nancy followed closely beside him, and the two of them rose rapidly past the enormous bark ridges, glowing leaves, hanging roots, and mountain-sized branches.","With Max taking the lead, the two of them shot upward along the gigantic trunk of the Witch God Tree, moving so quickly that the enormous ridges of bark around them blurred into dark streaks, while the dead lands of the Eternal Hourglass below grew smaller and smaller until even the massive roots spreading across the earth looked like twisted black veins.","The higher they flew, the thicker the cursed mist became, and the strange aura hidden within the tree also grew heavier, as if the entire ancient tree was slowly waking up because of their reckless ascent.","Nancy followed closely behind Max, her expression solemn as she watched the surrounding branches, hollows, leaves, and hanging roots with constant caution, but Max did not slow down even once.","It did not take long before the things living on the Witch God Tree noticed them.","A swarm of black-winged insects burst out from a crack in the bark, each one as large as a human head, with transparent wings covered in cursed patterns and sharp mouths that released shrill cries capable of piercing the mind.","At almost the same time, several vine-like creatures hanging from the higher branches suddenly came alive, twisting like serpents as they lashed toward Max and Nancy with thorn-covered bodies dripping green-black liquid.","Farther above, a huge demonic bird with three skull-like heads tore through the mist and dived toward them, its wings releasing waves of rotten wind that caused the surrounding clouds to churn violently.","Nancy’s eyes sharpened, and her hand moved toward her sword.","\"Max, there are too many of them!\""]},{"number":1751,"title":"Chapter 1751: Witch God Valley!","paragraphs":["Max did not even look back.","\"We do not have time for them.\"","The moment he said those words, golden light erupted from his body and expanded outward, forming a wide shield around both him and Nancy. The shield was not a simple barrier. It was formed from the power of his Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline, and its surface glowed with sacred golden patterns that moved like flowing sunlight.","The moment the black-winged insects crashed into it, their bodies were burned into ashes by the radiance before their mouths could even touch the surface. The thorn-covered vines whipped against the shield again and again, but every strike only caused ripples of light to spread across it, while the poisonous liquid they released evaporated the instant it touched the golden barrier.","The three-headed demonic bird came next.","It opened its mouths and released three beams of dark, rotten energy, each one filled with a cursed force that could corrode flesh and soul, but Max only raised one hand slightly while continuing to fly upward.","The golden shield brightened, and the three beams struck its surface with a thunderous explosion, causing the clouds around them to scatter and the nearby branches to tremble, yet the shield did not break. Not even a crack appeared.","The attack was swallowed by the golden light, and Max flew straight through the storm of rotten wind as if nothing had happened.","Nancy looked at the shield around them and felt her heart calm slightly.","She had been worried that they would be delayed by the creatures living on the Witch God Tree, but Max clearly had no intention of fighting them one by one. He simply used absolute defense and terrifying speed to ignore everything in their path.","No matter what attacked them, whether it was cursed insects, demonic birds, soul-devouring flowers, living roots, shadow beasts hidden in the bark, or strange black spirits that crawled out from the mist, all of them were blocked by the golden shield before they could reach either of them.","Boom! Boom! Boom!","Attack after attack landed against the shield.","Claws struck it.","Fangs bit into it.","Curses spread across it.","Illusion mist tried to seep through it.","Dark lightning fell from the clouds above and crashed down upon it.","Yet none of these attacks could stop Max.","The golden shield remained steady around him and Nancy, and Max continued flying upward with his eyes fixed on the unseen top of the tree. His expression was calm, but his speed only grew faster with every passing moment, as if the dangers around him were nothing more than wind brushing against his face.","Nancy followed closely within the protection of the shield, and although she kept her guard up, she soon realized that unless something truly terrifying appeared, there was no need for her to make a move at all.","The higher they went, the stranger the Witch God Tree became.","The bark around them was no longer only dark brown and gray-black. It began to show faint purple veins that pulsed like blood vessels beneath the surface. Some branches were covered in glowing white flowers shaped like tiny skulls, while other branches were completely dead, twisted, and covered in chains of black moss that moved as if alive.","Huge hollows opened in the trunk from time to time, and within those hollows, Max could sense sleeping auras that were far stronger than the creatures attacking them outside. But he did not enter. He did not investigate. Caroline was still his priority.","After what felt like a long and brutal ascent, the cursed clouds finally appeared directly above them.","They were thick, dark, and filled with green-purple lightning, but Max did not slow down. The golden shield around him brightened once more, and with Nancy following closely, he flew straight into the cloud layer.","The moment they entered, visibility dropped sharply. Everything around them became misty and distorted, and strange whispers echoed in their ears, sometimes sounding like children laughing, sometimes like old women chanting, and sometimes like someone calling their names from far away.","The cursed clouds tried to confuse their senses, but Max’s gaze remained cold and steady.","Golden light surged again.","The whispers were burned away.","The mist split open.","Max and Nancy broke through the cloud layer.","The moment they emerged above the clouds, the world changed.","The top of the Witch God Tree was not a simple treetop.","It was an entire world suspended above the sky.","Massive branches stretched outward in every direction like mountain ranges, thick enough to hold forests, rivers, ruined temples, broken towers, and valleys between them. Countless leaves, each one the size of a small house, grew across the highest branches, but their colors were strange.","Some were pale silver, some were dark purple, some were black with glowing green veins, and some looked completely transparent, reflecting faint scenes that did not seem to belong to the present. Between the branches hung streams of mist that flowed like waterfalls, pouring downward into the clouds below, while above them, the sky was neither day nor night.","It was a dim, violet expanse filled with slow-moving stars that seemed too close, as if someone could touch them by reaching upward.","At the very center of the treetop was Witch God Valley.","The valley was formed between three colossal branches that curved inward like the fingers of an ancient hand. Their surfaces joined together to create a vast basin filled with cursed mist, black grass, twisted stone pillars, and rivers of dark green liquid that flowed without sound.","Strange ruins were scattered throughout the valley, some built from bone-white stone, some carved directly into the living wood, and some floating slightly above the ground as if gravity had forgotten them. In the deepest part of the valley, a huge broken statue stood half-buried in the mist.","The statue seemed to depict a woman with six arms, a crown of branches, and eyes covered by a veil, but its face was cracked beyond recognition, and from those cracks, faint green light leaked out like the glow of something still alive inside.","Max and Nancy hovered above the edge of the valley, looking down at the scene before them.","Even Max could feel that this place was dangerous.","The air here did not simply carry cursed energy. It carried an old, decayed divinity, a power that had survived countless years and had twisted into something neither holy nor demonic. The mist below moved strangely, sometimes forming faces, sometimes forming hands, and sometimes opening like mouths before closing again.","The branches beneath the valley pulsed faintly, as if the Witch God Tree itself was breathing through this place.","Nancy’s expression became extremely solemn.","\"This is Witch God Valley,\" she said quietly. \"The highest and most dangerous region of the Witch God Tree.\"","Max’s eyes swept across the valley, and his senses spread outward as far as they could go, searching for traces of Caroline, Seraphine, Fin, or anyone connected to the second faction.","The golden shield around them slowly faded, but the light in Max’s eyes became sharper.","\"So this is where they fled,\" he said.","Nancy nodded. \"Yes. If Caroline and the others are still alive, they should be somewhere inside.\"","Max looked toward the depths of the cursed valley, where the broken statue stood beneath the violet sky and the mist twisted like living shadows.","\"Then we go in.\"","His voice was calm, but the killing intent beneath it was unmistakable.","Without waiting any longer, Max descended toward Witch God Valley, and Nancy followed closely behind him."]},{"number":1752,"title":"Chapter 1752: Cursed Roots!","paragraphs":["Max and Nancy had barely descended into the outer region of Witch God Valley when the cursed mist around them began to move strangely, and although the valley looked silent from above, the moment their feet touched the dark wooden ground formed by the highest branches of the Witch God Tree, Max immediately sensed that something hidden beneath the surface had awakened.","The black grass swayed without wind, the mist crawling across the ground gathered into thin streams, and the twisted stone pillars scattered throughout the valley released faint green light as if they were silently watching the two intruders enter a forbidden place.","Nancy’s expression changed slightly. \"Be careful.\"","Before her words fully faded, the ground beneath them exploded.","Boom!","Countless tree roots burst out from beneath the surface, thick, black, and covered in glowing green veins that pulsed like cursed blood. They did not rise slowly like ordinary roots. They shot out like spears, whips, and serpents at the same time, tearing through the dark wooden ground and rushing toward Max and Nancy from every direction.","Some roots came from beneath their feet, some twisted down from the branches above, some emerged from the mist, and some even extended from the nearby stone pillars as if the entire valley had become a living cage trying to devour them.","Max’s eyes turned cold.","Dragonheart appeared in his hand in an instant, and the Severing Sword Concept erupted from his blade like an invisible edge capable of cutting apart anything in its path.","He swung his sword once, and a sharp sword light swept outward, severing dozens of roots before they could reach him. The cut roots fell to the ground and twitched violently, leaking dark green liquid that hissed against the wooden surface like poison burning through flesh.","But more roots came.","Far more.","Max slashed again.","Then again.","Each sword strike released a terrifying severing force, and every time Dragonheart moved, hundreds of roots were cleanly cut apart. Some roots were sliced into several pieces before they could even fully emerge from the ground, while others were split lengthwise as the sword light passed through them.","The Severing Sword Concept was extremely effective against them, and under Max’s sword, even these cursed roots could not resist for long.","However, their number was simply too high.","The entire valley seemed to be producing them endlessly.","The roots did not care how many were cut down. They continued rushing forward without pause, layering over one another until the air around Max and Nancy became filled with black, twisting lines.","From a distance, it looked as if the Witch God Tree itself had opened countless veins and sent them all to swallow the intruders alive.","Max’s expression remained calm.","No matter how many roots came toward him, he cut them down with cold precision. His sword moved so quickly that it left behind only faint afterimages, and every slash carried the eerie sharpness of the Severing Sword Concept.","Roots came from above, and he cut them before they descended. Roots came from beneath, and he split them as they broke through the ground. Roots tried to wrap around his arms and legs, but they were severed before they could tighten.","Even when dozens attacked him from blind spots, Max turned slightly and swept Dragonheart around his body, forming a circular sword light that shredded everything approaching him.","Nancy, however, was having a much harder time.","She was strong, and her reaction was not slow. The moment the roots attacked, she drew her sword and released her light concept together with her Death Wind concept. Pale silver light flashed around her blade, while gray-green Death Wind wrapped around the edge, and every strike she made cut several roots apart while also corroding the vitality hidden inside them.","When the roots came too densely, she shifted her figure through the mist, dodging between attacks with elegant movements, then slashed out with crescent-shaped waves of light and death wind that tore apart the roots chasing her.","For a while, she managed to hold on.","Her sword cut down one group of roots.","Her Death Wind withered another.","Her light concept burned through several more.","But the roots were not attacking like ordinary enemies. They came endlessly, without fear, without hesitation, and without any sense of pain. Every time Nancy cut down ten, thirty more rushed from another direction.","Every time she dodged one wave, another rose beneath her feet.","Gradually, the space around her became smaller and smaller, and even her movements began to slow under the overwhelming pressure.","\"Nancy!\" Max called out coldly as he noticed her situation.","\"I can handle it!\" Nancy replied, but even as she spoke, several roots tore through the mist behind her and wrapped around her left arm.","She severed them instantly with Death Wind, but that moment of delay was enough.","More roots rushed in.","One wrapped around her waist.","Another caught her ankle.","Three more coiled around her sword arm.","Nancy’s eyes sharpened, and she released a burst of light from her body, burning several roots apart, but the surrounding roots immediately layered over her again. Their number was too great, and before she could fully break free, dozens of thick roots surged from all sides and swallowed her figure completely.","In the next instant, Nancy disappeared inside a massive cocoon of black roots.","Max’s eyes turned icy.","\"Damn.\"","His body moved instantly.","The roots tried to block him, but Max rushed forward like a sharp black shadow, Dragonheart cutting apart everything in his path.","At the same time, black flames burst into his right hand blazing with devouring intent.","Max thrust his hand forward.","Boom!","Black flames exploded across the root cocoon.","The moment the cursed roots touched the black flames, they burned violently. Their green veins flared, their surfaces cracked, and the dark liquid inside them evaporated into foul smoke before the roots could even struggle. Unlike sword cuts, which only severed them, the black flames destroyed them completely, turning them into ash and erasing the cursed vitality that allowed them to keep moving.","In only a breath, the root cocoon was burned open.","Max reached inside, grabbed Nancy by the arm, and pulled her out.","Nancy’s face was slightly pale, and several marks had been left on her arms and waist where the roots had tried to bind her, but she was still conscious. The moment Max pulled her free, she coughed once and quickly steadied herself beside him.","\"Are you injured?\" Max asked without looking away from the roots still rushing toward them.","\"Not seriously,\" Nancy said, though her breathing was a little unstable. \"Those roots were trying to drain my energy.\"","Max’s gaze became colder.","\"Then stay close.\"","The black flames around his body erupted again.","This time, Max did not use them as a simple attack. He spread them outward, forming a sphere of black flames around both himself and Nancy. The flame sphere burned silently at first, then began rotating slowly, its surface rippling like a dark sun wrapped around them.","The cursed roots continued attacking from every direction, but the moment they touched the sphere of black flames, they were burned into nothingness before they could even exert force.","Hiss! Hiss! Hiss!","One root after another vanished.","The roots came from above and turned to ash.","They came from below and were burned away.","They rushed through the mist in waves, but none could pass through the black flame sphere.","The entire area around Max and Nancy became filled with the smell of burning cursed wood, and the ground beneath them trembled as the Witch God Tree seemed to react angrily to the destruction of its roots.","More and more roots rose from the valley, but it no longer mattered. The black flames devoured all of them, leaving behind only drifting ash and shrinking trails of green smoke.","Nancy stood inside the sphere of black flames, looking at Max’s back with a complicated expression.","She had been trapped only for a moment, but she knew very well that if Max had acted even a little slower, those roots might have drained her power or dragged her deeper into the valley. This place was far more dangerous than she had expected, and they had only just entered the outer region.","Max looked at the endless roots burning outside the flame sphere and narrowed his eyes.","\"So the valley itself is trying to stop us.\"","Nancy took a slow breath and nodded. \"Witch God Valley is alive in a strange way. The deeper we go, the worse it will become.\"","Max’s expression remained cold.","\"We have to be serious here.\"","The black flame sphere expanded slightly, and every root near them was erased at once.","With Nancy close beside him, Max stepped forward into the mist, surrounded by the rotating sphere of black flames, while the cursed roots of the Witch God Tree continued rushing toward them only to be burned into nothingness the moment they touched his protection.","After another five minutes, these cursed tree roots stopped attacking them. Inside the black flaming sphere, Max didn’t underestimate the cursed roots and kept the sphere up and continued walking forward.","They walked for an hour before the region of cursed roots slowly disappeared into nothingness. Only then Max let go of the sphere of black flames."]},{"number":1753,"title":"Chapter 1753: Jessica and Lumine!","paragraphs":["Just when Max and Nancy came out of the cursed root region, the black flame sphere around them slowly shrank back into Max’s body, and the scorched smell of burned roots faded behind them as they entered a denser part of Witch God Valley.","The mist here was thicker than before, and the trees growing across the valley were twisted and pale, their branches curling downward like claws, while faint green runes appeared and disappeared across their bark as if something ancient was breathing through them.","Max had only taken a few steps forward when his eyes suddenly narrowed, and the spatial senses of his Dimensional Sovereign Body spread outward like invisible ripples, passing through the mist, the trees, and the broken ruins ahead.","\"Battles are happening ahead of us,\" Max said calmly.","Nancy immediately became alert. \"Battles?\"","Max looked into the distance. \"There are some elves there, and even some demons.\"","Nancy’s expression changed slightly. \"Demons inside Witch God Valley?\"","Max glanced at her. \"Is that unusual?\"","\"Not impossible,\" Nancy said with a frown. \"But if demons are involved with the elves here, then the situation might be worse than we thought.\"","Max’s gaze became colder. \"Then let us go and see.\"","With that, his figure moved toward the distance ahead, and Nancy followed closely behind him. The two of them passed through the cursed mist like streaks of light, avoiding the twisted trees, broken stone altars, and strange pools of dark green liquid scattered throughout the area.","Soon, faint sounds of battle entered their ears. Sword clashes, demonic roars, angry shouts, and the tremble of energy spreading through the forest all became clearer with every passing breath.","In an area enclosed by several dead white trees, a group of elves were surrounded by demons and elves.","The surrounded group numbered only five individuals, and although each of them looked injured, they were still standing back to back with their weapons raised. Their clothes were torn in many places, traces of blood marked their arms and shoulders, and their breathing was heavy, but the determination in their eyes had not faded.","These five elves belonged to the third faction, the faction that had once been led by Max’s mother, Divine Queen Caelira, and from the hatred burning in their eyes, it was obvious that surrendering was not something they would ever accept.","The ones surrounding them, however, numbered more than twenty. Some were elves with golden and pale-green hair, dressed in bright armor marked by the symbol of the second faction, while the others were demons with black horns, dark scales, and cruel smiles on their faces.","Their mixed formation looked extremely strange, yet it was clear that they had joined hands for one purpose.","They were hunting the third faction members, and if they succeeded, the members of the third faction and the others would be sent back to the Elf Prison, where torture, humiliation, and endless darkness were waiting for them once again.","Among the five surrounded elves, the leader was a blue-haired female elf.","Her long blue hair fell down her back like flowing water, but around the back of her forehead, faint specks of gold shone through the strands, making her hair look cool and noble at the same time.","Her eyes were sharp, her face was pale from exhaustion, and one side of her shoulder was stained with blood, but her sword remained steady as she pointed it toward the golden-haired female elf standing among the encircling group.","\"How shameless can you be, Lumine?\" the blue-haired female elf sneered. Her name was Jessica.","The golden-haired female elf smiled faintly.","Her name was Lumine.","She was beautiful, with long golden hair, clear green eyes, and a graceful appearance that made her seem gentle at first glance, but the coldness hidden in her smile destroyed that illusion completely.","She stood calmly among demons and elves as if there was nothing wrong with the scene at all, and when Jessica’s sword pointed at her, she did not show even the slightest anger. Instead, her expression only became more amused.","Jessica’s eyes burned with disgust. \"To join hands with demons, the mortal enemies of the elf race, Lumine, you and your faction have truly fallen too low!\"","The other four third faction elves beside Jessica also looked furious.","For elves, demons were not merely enemies competing inside the Cosmic Ascension Conference. They were old enemies of their race, creatures whose history was soaked in blood and hatred.","Even though the second faction had already committed unforgivable crimes by imprisoning and torturing the third faction members, openly cooperating with demons still crossed a line that made Jessica feel nothing but disgust.","Lumine lightly brushed a strand of golden hair behind her ear, her smile calm and cold. \"Jessica, you are still as naïve as ever.\"","Jessica’s eyes narrowed. \"Naïve?\"","\"Yes,\" Lumine said softly. \"You still speak as though honor matters. You still speak as though race matters. You still speak as though the third faction has the right to stand proudly after losing everything.\"","Jessica’s grip on her sword tightened. \"The third faction lost everything because of people like you.\"","Lumine’s smile deepened. \"No. The third faction lost everything because Caelira abandoned her duty, abandoned her bloodline, abandoned the elf race, and chose a human man over the throne that should have ruled us all.\"","The moment Caelira’s name was spoken, Jessica’s eyes became colder.","\"Do not speak her name with that filthy mouth,\" Jessica said.","Lumine laughed lightly. \"Even now, you still defend her. How touching.\"","Jessica’s voice trembled with anger. \"Divine Queen Caelira was the rightful leader of our faction. She protected us when your faction schemed in the dark, and even after she left, you were still so afraid of her shadow that you imprisoned everyone connected to her.\"","Lumine’s eyes flashed with cruelty. \"Afraid? No, Jessica. We were cautious. Your faction still carried loyalty toward Caelira. Your faction still believed she would return one day. Your faction still treated her bloodline as sacred. So yes, you were imprisoned. You were tortured. You were broken. And after this conference ends, those of you who survive will be dragged back to the Elf Prison and broken again until no one dares to speak Caelira’s name with reverence.\"","The four elves around Jessica clenched their weapons, and one of them shouted, \"You will pay for what you did to our people!\"","Lumine looked at him with cold amusement. \"Will I?\"","Jessica’s sword released a blue light mixed with faint gold, and her killing intent sharpened. \"You hunted us all the way into Witch God Valley just to send us back to that prison?\"","\"Of course,\" Lumine said without hesitation. \"Do you think we would allow the remnants of the third faction to roam freely inside the Cosmic Ascension Conference? This world gives everyone opportunities. Treasures, inheritances, legacies, bloodline resources, and perhaps even chances to contact outside forces. If your people grow strong here, you might become troublesome after leaving. So we will capture you now, send you back, and make sure your faction remains buried where it belongs.\"","Her expression turned cruel. \"As for Caroline, I believe Seraphine and Fin should have taken care of her by now.\"","\"You will regret this.\" Jessica said coldly as she heard about Caroline.","The demon leader chuckled and lifted his axe from his shoulder. \"Enough talking. Are we killing them or capturing them? The longer we delay, the more people might arrive.\"","Lumine looked at Jessica and the four elves beside her.","There was no hesitation in her eyes now.","\"Capture Jessica if possible,\" Lumine said coldly. \"She has information about Caroline. As for the others, cripple them first. If they resist too much, kill them.\"","Jessica’s group immediately became tense.","The demons grinned.","The elves of Lumine’s side raised their weapons.","But just as the surrounding group prepared to attack, a faint voice suddenly came from beyond the mist.","\"Interesting.\"","Everyone froze.","Lumine’s eyes narrowed.","Jessica turned sharply toward the direction of the voice.","The demon leader’s grip tightened around his axe.","From between the twisted white trees, Max and Nancy slowly walked out. Max’s expression was calm, but his eyes swept across the demons and the second faction elves with a coldness that made the air around him feel heavier, while Nancy, standing beside him, immediately recognized the faction marks on both sides and understood the situation at once.","Max glanced at Jessica and the four injured elves, then looked toward Nancy.","\"They are from my mother’s faction?\"","Nancy nodded with a serious expression. \"Yes. Jessica and the ones beside her belong to the third faction, the faction once led by Divine Queen Caelira. Lumine and those elves surrounding them are from the second faction.\"","Max’s gaze moved toward Lumine, then toward the demon leader.","His smile became faint and cold.","\"So the second faction is working with demons to hunt my mother’s people.\"","The moment those words fell, Jessica’s eyes widened slightly.","Lumine’s expression changed.","Nancy looked at Max’s back, and for some reason, she felt the air around him becoming colder than the cursed mist of Witch God Valley itself.","Max took one step forward.","\"Good,\" he said softly. \"This saves me the trouble of looking for you.\""]},{"number":1754,"title":"Chapter 1754: Caelira’s Son?!","paragraphs":["\"Did you just say ’my mother’...\" Lumine’s expression changed for the first time, and the cold amusement in her eyes was replaced by genuine shock as she stared at Max with disbelief. \"Are you Caelira’s son?\"","The five surrounded elves behind Jessica also froze when they heard those words.","Jessica’s eyes widened slightly, and the sword in her hand trembled for a brief moment. Caelira’s son. Those three words struck her heart with a force greater than any attack Lumine had launched against them.","She had heard rumors from the older members of the third faction, stories whispered in the darkness of the Elf Prison, stories about Divine Queen Caelira leaving the elf race, marrying a human, and giving birth to a child who should have been the hope of their bloodline.","But most of them had believed that child had died long ago during the attack arranged by the second faction. To see a young man standing here now, speaking of Caelira as his mother, felt so impossible that Jessica almost forgot the danger surrounding them.","Max looked at Lumine, his eyes cold and calm.","\"It does not matter, does it?\"","Lumine stared at him for a moment, then suddenly laughed.","\"True,\" she said, and her smile became cold again. \"It truly does not matter whether you are Caelira’s son or not. If you are, then killing you here will only make this more meaningful.\"","Her gaze shifted toward the leading demon.","\"Arnold, kill him!\"","The demon leader grinned.","Arnold’s already large body suddenly expanded further. His muscles swelled beneath his rough black armor, his demonic veins bulged across his arms, and a brutal aura erupted from him like a raging beast breaking free from its chains.","The ground beneath his feet cracked as he stepped forward, and in the next instant, he shot toward Max with terrifying speed, raising one massive fist and smashing it toward Max’s head.","\"Watch out!\" Jessica shouted instinctively.","In her eyes, Max’s cultivation aura seemed to be only at the peak of the Law Refinement Realm. Arnold, however, was at the peak of the Law Manifestation Realm, and although demons were often crude, their physical strength was terrifying among beings of the same realm.","Even an elf at the same level would not dare to casually take Arnold’s fist head-on, much less someone who seemed to be a full major realm lower.","The fist arrived before Max.","Boom!","The wind exploded outward.","The ground behind Max cracked from the pressure alone, and several nearby trees bent backward violently from the force of Arnold’s punch.","But Max did not move.","He merely raised one finger.","Arnold’s massive fist stopped.","It was not slowed down.","It was not deflected.","It was stopped completely.","Max’s single finger pressed against the center of Arnold’s fist, and the terrifying demonic force that should have crushed his head was blocked as if it had struck an immovable divine wall.","The shockwave spread in all directions, tearing through the mist and shaking the nearby cursed trees, but Max stood there without taking even half a step back. His expression remained calm, and the finger he used to block the attack did not tremble at all.","The entire area fell silent.","Jessica stared at the scene with wide eyes.","Lumine’s expression stiffened.","Even the demons behind Arnold stopped smiling.","Arnold himself looked at his fist, then at Max’s finger, and for the first time, disbelief appeared in his eyes.","Max looked at him indifferently.","\"Is that supposed to hurt me?\"","Those words were quiet, but they landed like a slap across Arnold’s face.","The demon leader’s eyes instantly turned bloodshot with anger.","\"You arrogant brat!\"","Arnold roared and swung his other fist toward Max’s chest. This punch was even stronger than the first. Demonic energy wrapped around his arm, and a dark red light gathered over his knuckles as he tried to crush Max with brute force. The air screamed beneath the punch, and the ground around them sank from the pressure.","Max raised his other hand.","Another finger moved.","Boom!","Arnold’s second fist stopped as well.","This time, Max blocked it with another finger.","The two massive fists remained frozen in front of him, each one pressed against a single finger, and the image was so absurd that even Lumine could not immediately react.","Arnold was a peak Law Manifestation Realm demon known for his physical strength, yet Max was stopping both of his fists with two fingers, standing there with the same calm expression as though Arnold’s full-powered attack was nothing more than a child throwing a tantrum.","Max looked into Arnold’s furious eyes and spoke calmly.","\"You are weak.\"","Arnold’s face twisted with rage.","Max’s gaze became colder.","\"Let me show you what true strength is.\"","The moment those words fell, the air around Max changed.","A deep, ancient, and terrifying draconic pressure erupted from his body.","One thousand Draconic Essences.","Two thousand.","Three thousand.","Four thousand.","Five thousand.","The full power of five thousand Draconic Essences surged out at once, and the entire region seemed to tremble beneath the awakening of a primordial dragon. The cursed mist around Max was blasted apart. The trees nearby groaned as if they were about to be uprooted.","The ground beneath his feet shattered instantly, cracks spreading outward like a spiderweb through the dark wooden surface of the Witch God Valley. The air became heavy, violent, and suffocating, as though an ancient dragon had opened its eyes and looked down upon everything in front of it.","Arnold’s expression changed completely.","The overwhelming demonic arrogance in his eyes vanished, replaced by shock and instinctive fear. His body reacted before his mind could. Even though his fists were still pressed against Max’s fingers, his legs trembled, and he was forced to take a step back under the crushing weight of Max’s aura.","A peak Law Manifestation Realm demon had been forced back by aura alone.","Jessica felt her heart shake violently.","\"This power...\" she whispered.","Lumine’s face also darkened, and her eyes became filled with disbelief. This was not the power of a normal peak Law Refinement Realm cultivator. This was not even close. The pressure Max released had completely broken common sense, and for a brief instant, she felt as if she was not looking at a human, but at a beast that had worn human skin.","Max smiled faintly.","He lifted one finger.","All five thousand Draconic Essences gathered toward that finger.","The golden-black draconic power condensed rapidly, becoming denser and sharper with every passing breath. The space around his fingertip distorted slightly, and the aura gathered there felt heavier than a mountain, fiercer than a storm, and more destructive than any ordinary technique Arnold had ever faced. The demon leader’s instincts screamed at him that he absolutely could not take this attack head-on.","Arnold roared and retreated half a step, then pulled out a huge axe from behind him.","The axe was enormous, almost as tall as his body, forged from dark metal and covered in demonic runes. The moment he held it in both hands, dark red energy flowed across its blade, forming several layers of defensive power. Arnold poured all his strength into the weapon and placed it in front of himself like a shield.","\"You think one finger can kill me?\" Arnold roared."]},{"number":1755,"title":"Chapter 1755: A Flick of Fingers!","paragraphs":["Max’s expression remained calm.","Then he flicked his finger.","A tiny burst of condensed draconic force shot forward.","It did not look grand.","It did not look like a divine ability.","It was only a finger flick.","But the moment that force struck Arnold’s axe, the huge demonic weapon exploded.","Crack!","The first sound was small.","Then countless cracks spread across the axe.","In the next instant, the entire weapon shattered into fragments, and the condensed force did not slow down at all. It passed through the broken axe, struck Arnold’s chest, and pierced through him with irresistible power.","Arnold’s eyes widened.","His roar stopped.","His massive body froze in place.","For a single breath, he seemed unable to understand what had happened. Then his chest cracked open with golden-black light, and his entire body began breaking apart from the point of impact. The cracks spread across his armor, his muscles, his horns, and his face, and before he could scream, his body shattered completely.","The leading demon Arnold was destroyed.","His body turned into golden fragments of Killing Points that scattered through the air like broken stars before flying toward Max.","The entire battlefield fell into absolute silence.","The demons who had been laughing a moment ago now looked as if their throats had been seized by invisible hands.","The second faction elves stared at Max with pale faces.","Jessica and the other third faction elves stood frozen, unable to reconcile the person before them with the cultivation aura they had sensed earlier.","Max lowered his hand slowly as the fragments of Killing Points entered his body.","\"Everyone attack!\"","Seeing Arnold being killed in such a terrifying way, Lumine finally felt fear crawl into her heart, and the calm arrogance she had shown earlier cracked apart almost instantly.","Arnold had been a peak Law Manifestation Realm demon with monstrous physical strength, yet Max had blocked his punches with two fingers and destroyed him with nothing more than a flick of his finger.","This was not something that could be explained by ordinary talent, nor was it something that could be ignored by pretending Max was only at the peak of the Law Refinement Realm.","The young man standing in front of her was dangerous, far more dangerous than she had expected, and if they allowed him to take the initiative again, none of them might be able to leave Witch God Valley alive.","At Lumine’s command, all the remaining second faction elves and demons moved at once.","No one dared to underestimate Max anymore.","The demons roared and released their demonic energy without holding anything back. Some charged straight toward him with heavy weapons, their axes, hammers, and bone blades wrapped in dark red killing light, while others circled to his back and sides, trying to strike from blind spots.","The second faction elves also attacked together. Golden light, green wind, pale sword aura, and sharp wood-element arrows tore through the cursed mist as they launched techniques from every direction, coordinating with the demons to seal off all possible routes of escape.","Some aimed at Max’s head, some aimed at his heart, some tried to bind his legs with glowing vines, and some released restraining light toward his arms, clearly intending to limit his movement before killing him.","The battlefield exploded into chaos.","Jessica and the four third faction elves instinctively tightened their grips on their weapons, but before they could step forward to help, Nancy raised one hand slightly and stopped them.","\"Do not interfere,\" Nancy said in a low voice.","Jessica looked at her in confusion and urgency. \"But they are all attacking him at once.\"","Nancy’s eyes remained fixed on Max’s back. \"That is why you should not interfere.\"","Jessica froze slightly.","At the center of the storm, Max looked at the attacks rushing toward him from every direction with a calm expression. The five thousand Draconic Essences still surged around his body like an invisible dragon sea, but he did not use them to crush his enemies immediately. Instead, he slowly raised his hand, and Dragonheart appeared in his grip.","The moment Dragonheart emerged, the sword hummed.","A deep sword resonance spread across the battlefield, and the weapons in the hands of several second faction elves trembled uncontrollably. Even Lumine’s sword reacted, producing a faint cry that made her expression change again.","The sword in Max’s hand was not merely powerful. It carried a natural suppression toward other swords, and the aura sleeping inside it felt ancient, noble, and dangerous.","\"I would love to play with you all,\" Max said calmly, his eyes sweeping across the incoming elves and demons, \"but I am in a hurry.\"","His fingers tightened around Dragonheart.","\"So, you guys can die.\"","As he said those words, Max executed the Saint Origin Sword Art.","At the same time, his expression changed.","The faint smile on his face disappeared, and his eyes became deathly calm. Emotion left his features like water draining from a broken vessel, and the eerie aura of his Pseudo Cosmic Path spread outward once again.","The Emotion Severing Path descended upon the battlefield, silent, cold, and terrifying, turning the already cursed air of Witch God Valley into something even more suffocating.","The demons felt it first.","Their battle intent weakened.","Their roars suddenly sounded hollow.","The second faction elves felt it next.","Their killing intent, anger, fear, greed, hatred, and confidence all seemed to be touched by an invisible blade, and for a brief but fatal instant, their minds went blank. The Emotion Severing Path did not simply pressure them.","It cut away the emotions that supported their actions, leaving their attacks moving forward while their hearts lagged behind in confusion and terror.","Then the Saint Origin Sword Art erupted.","A pure and majestic sword light rose from Dragonheart, yet because it was infused with the Emotion Severing Path, that originally sacred sword light became strangely cold and absolute.","It looked like the first light born from heaven and earth, but within that light was an emotionless severing force that judged everything before it as something to be cut down. Max stepped forward once, and the entire battlefield seemed to fall under his sword.","The first slash crossed the left side.","A crescent of saintly sword light swept through the demons charging from that direction. Their dark armor, demonic weapons, thick bodies, and defensive energy were all split apart at the same time. Several demons continued running for another step before their bodies separated, their eyes still frozen in disbelief as they dissolved into golden fragments of Killing Points.","The second slash turned toward the right.","The elves attacking from that side raised their defensive light barriers, but the Saint Origin Sword Art pierced through them cleanly. The barriers broke like thin glass, their swords snapped, and their bodies were cut open before they could even cry out.","Their golden and green light techniques vanished in the air, severed from their source by Max’s Pseudo Cosmic Path.","The third slash swept behind him.","The demons and elves who had tried to attack from his blind spot were cut down together. One demon had already raised his hammer above Max’s head, while another elf had almost completed a binding formation around his feet, but neither attack landed.","The sword light passed through them silently, and their bodies collapsed into fragments before the hammer could fall or the formation could close."]},{"number":1756,"title":"Chapter 1756: Lumine’s shock!","paragraphs":["Then Max moved faster.","Dragonheart flashed again and again.","The Saint Origin Sword Art unfolded in his hand with terrifying elegance. Every movement was smooth, precise, and filled with an ancient sword rhythm, as if Max was not fighting a group of enemies but performing a sacred execution beneath the cursed trees of Witch God Valley.","Sword light spread through the battlefield in layers, crossing, turning, rising, and descending, and every line it formed became a boundary between life and death.","The demons tried to resist with brute force.","They were cut apart.","The second faction elves tried to defend with bloodline techniques.","They were cut apart.","Some tried to retreat.","They were cut apart before they could take three steps.","Some tried to beg.","Their voices were severed before they could become words.","The Emotion Severing Path made Max’s sword merciless to a frightening degree. There was no hesitation in his strikes, no unnecessary cruelty, no rage, and no pleasure.","He simply cut down everyone who had attacked him, and because his sword carried the power to sever emotion, concept, energy, defense, and life at once, none of them could withstand even a single direct slash.","Lumine stood frozen.","Her face was pale.","Her lips parted slightly, but no sound came out.","Everything had happened too quickly. She had ordered everyone to attack because she believed numbers could at least create a chance, but the moment Max drew Dragonheart and entered that emotionless sword state, the entire battle had turned into a slaughter. No, it could not even be called a battle.","The demons and second faction elves had launched their strongest attacks, surrounded him from all sides, and tried to kill him together, yet Max had wiped them out as though they were dry leaves caught in a sword storm.","Within only a few breaths, the battlefield became quiet again.","The attacks vanished.","The roaring demons disappeared.","The second faction elves collapsed into light.","Golden fragments of Killing Points floated through the cursed mist, gathering around Max like countless sparks born from death. They streamed toward him one after another, entering his body and increasing his total once again, while Dragonheart remained lowered in his hand, its blade clean and faintly humming with the remnant power of the Saint Origin Sword Art.","Jessica and the other third faction elves stared at Max in shock.","They had thought they were about to die.","They had thought Lumine and the demons would drag them back to the Elf Prison.","But the young man who claimed a connection to Caelira had appeared, killed Arnold with one finger, and then erased the rest of the enemies with a sword art so terrifying that none of them could even understand its full depth.","Nancy’s expression was also serious.","Even though she had seen Max kill before, the Saint Origin Sword Art combined with the Emotion Severing Path still made her feel a faint chill.","This was a sword art that already carried a grand and sacred origin, yet when fused with Max’s Pseudo Cosmic Path, it became something far more terrifying. It was beautiful, but it was also absolute. It gave no mercy because mercy itself seemed to be severed before the sword even fell.","At the center of the battlefield, only Lumine remained.","She had not attacked directly, and perhaps because of that, Max had intentionally left her alive.","Her body trembled faintly as she looked around at the empty battlefield. The elves she had brought were gone. The demons she had used were gone. Arnold, her strongest helper, was gone.","The only things left around her were drifting Killing Points, scorched cursed mist, severed traces of attacks, and Max standing calmly with Dragonheart in his hand.","Max slowly turned his gaze toward her.","Lumine instinctively took a step back.","For the first time since appearing, fear completely covered her face.","Max’s emotionless expression slowly softened, but the coldness in his eyes did not disappear.","\"I guess you and the others have more lives left,\" he said with terrifying calmness in his eyes as he looked at Lumine, whose face had already lost all color. \"If you want revenge for this, then you are welcome to block me at the border of Witch God Valley down below, at the entrance of the Witch God Tree.\"","With that, Max’s sword flashed once more.","Lumine wanted to say something. Perhaps she wanted to curse him, perhaps she wanted to threaten him with the second faction, or perhaps she wanted to reveal something about Caroline to save herself, but before even a single word could leave her mouth, a golden line appeared on her body from the top of her head to the bottom of her feet.","Her eyes widened.","In the next instant, her body split cleanly into two.","There was no scream.","There was no resistance.","Her figure dissolved into golden fragments of Killing Points, scattering into the cursed mist before streaming toward Max together with the remaining fragments left behind by Arnold, the demons, and the second faction elves.","For a moment, the entire area glowed with golden light.","The demons had carried a decent amount of Killing Points, especially Arnold, whose strength and status among them had clearly been higher than the rest. The second faction elves had also gathered points during their hunt through Witch God Valley, and Lumine, being the leader among them, carried even more than the ordinary elves under her command. One by one, their points surged into Max’s body, causing the number beside his name to rise again.","[Participant: Max]","[Previous Killing Points: 29,000,000]","[Absorbed Killing Points from Arnold: 1,500,000]","[Absorbed Killing Points from Lumine: 1,200,000]","[Absorbed Killing Points from remaining demons and second faction elves: 1,900,000]","[Total Absorbed Killing Points: 4,600,000]","[Current Killing Points: 33,600,000]","[Rank: 7]","The notification appeared quietly, but to Jessica and the other third faction elves, those numbers felt thunderous.","Thirty-three million and six hundred thousand Killing Points.","That number was no longer something an ordinary genius could hope to touch. Even many powerful participants who had survived until now might not have gathered even a small fraction of that amount, yet Max had increased his total again after casually slaughtering a group that had nearly forced Jessica and her companions into despair.","Max glanced at the notification for only a moment before looking away.","\"Only four million six hundred thousand,\" he said calmly. \"Better than the Sword God Palace disciples, but still not much.\"","Jessica and the other elves stared at him in silence.","For them, that amount was already terrifying.","For Max, it was merely acceptable.","Nancy looked at him with a helpless expression, though even she could not deny that his growth in Killing Points was becoming absurdly fast. Not long ago, he had stood at twenty-two million after destroying Karo, Munro, and the demon army.","Then he had taken seven million from the Sword God Palace disciples near the neutral city. Now, after killing Arnold, Lumine, and their group, he had reached thirty-three million six hundred thousand.","At this speed, his rank in the Cosmic Ascension Ranking List would rise again soon.","Max slowly lowered Dragonheart, then turned toward Jessica and the other injured third faction elves.","\"Now,\" he said calmly, \"tell me where Caroline is.\""]},{"number":1757,"title":"Chapter 1757: Jessica’s Recognition!","paragraphs":["\"Are you truly Divine Queen Caelira’s son?\" Jessica asked, her voice still carrying the shock of what she had just witnessed.","Even now, she could not fully recover from Max’s overwhelming display of pure strength. Arnold, Lumine, the demons, and the second faction elves had all been wiped out in front of her, and Max had done it with such terrifying ease that Jessica almost felt as if she had been watching someone from a higher world descend into Witch God Valley to pass judgment.","Yet strength alone could not prove bloodline. The Divine Queen’s name was too sacred to the third faction, and Jessica could not allow herself to believe too quickly, especially when the matter involved Caelira’s child.","Before Max could answer, Nancy stepped forward and looked at Jessica.","\"He is indeed the son of Caelira,\" Nancy said seriously. \"In fact, if I am not wrong, there should also be his elder sister somewhere out there in the Divine Realm. They managed to escape the calamity all those years ago.\"","Jessica heard Nancy clearly, but disbelief still remained in her eyes.","She wanted to believe it. Every member of the third faction wanted to believe that Divine Queen Caelira’s children had survived. In the darkness of the Elf Prison, many of them had whispered about that possibility to keep themselves from breaking completely","But rumors were one thing, and seeing someone appear before her, claiming that connection while standing in the middle of Witch God Valley, was something else entirely.","Max looked at her silently for a moment.","He could see the hope in her eyes, but he could also see fear, caution, and pain. These elves had suffered because of his mother. Not because Caelira had harmed them, but because they had remained loyal to her name even after she disappeared.","They had been imprisoned, tortured, hunted, and treated as remnants that needed to be erased. Jessica’s suspicion was not disrespect. It was the caution of someone who had paid too much for misplaced trust.","Max raised his hand.","\"Then look carefully.\"","The moment those words fell, a brilliant golden light bloomed from his body.","It was not ordinary light.","It was pure, sacred, and noble, carrying a divine pressure that instantly filled the cursed forest. The green mist of Witch God Valley retreated as if burned by something holy, and the twisted trees nearby trembled faintly beneath the radiance.","Golden patterns appeared faintly across Max’s skin, flowing like ancient veins of light, while behind him, a majestic phantom of divine luminance seemed to awaken for a brief moment. It was not the Heavenly Luminance Royal Bloodline that belonged to ordinary royal elves.","It was purer, higher, and more terrifying, as though the bloodline had evolved beyond its original limit and stepped into a realm the elf race had only dreamed of.","Jessica froze.","The four elves behind her also froze.","Their weapons slowly lowered without them realizing it.","To them, this aura was unforgettable. Even though most of them had never stood before Divine Queen Caelira at her peak, every member of the third faction had grown up hearing about the Heavenly Luminance Royal Bloodline.","In the Elf Prison, the older captives had described its sacred pressure, its golden radiance, and the way it made loyal bloodlines feel warmth while making traitors feel fear. The light Max released now carried that same origin, that same noble root, and yet it was even stronger than the legends they had heard.","Jessica’s eyes trembled.","\"This aura...\" she whispered.","Her voice almost broke.","\"It is truly the Heavenly Luminance bloodline.\"","One of the injured elves behind her fell to one knee, not because Max forced him to, but because his body reacted before his mind could. Another elf’s eyes turned red as if he had seen the return of something thought lost forever.","Jessica stared at Max with shock, hope, and confusion all mixed together.","\"No,\" she muttered. \"This is not just the Heavenly Luminance Royal Bloodline. It feels different than Divine Queen’s bloodline.\"","Nancy glanced at Max, then said quietly, \"His bloodline is called the Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline. From what Prince Elrian told him, it is a variant above Divine Queen Caelira’s original bloodline.\"","Jessica’s expression changed again.","\"Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline...\" she repeated softly.","For a moment, she looked as if she might finally believe him completely.","But then something else appeared in her eyes.","Confusion.","Deep confusion.","She looked at Max with a frown, and the joy that had just begun rising in her heart was suddenly covered by doubt.","\"That should be impossible,\" Jessica said.","Max’s eyes narrowed slightly. \"Why?\"","Jessica took a slow breath and looked at the golden light around him again, as if trying to confirm what she was seeing.","\"Because from what we knew, your bloodline was taken away from you.\"","The moment those words left her mouth, the air around Max became colder.","Nancy’s expression also changed.","Jessica noticed their reactions, but she continued because this matter was too important to hide.","\"During the calamity all those years ago, the second faction did not only attack because they wanted to destroy Divine Queen Caelira’s family. They attacked because of the bloodline you carried. We heard fragments from the guards in the Elf Prison. We heard that Caelira’s son had inherited an abnormal Heavenly Luminance bloodline, something purer than even the royal line itself.\"","Her voice became heavier.","\"But we were also told that the bloodline was extracted from you and placed into an elf of the second faction.\"","Max’s eyes became deathly calm.","The golden light around him flickered once, and the pressure in the area deepened.","Jessica looked at him with uncertainty and pain in her eyes. \"That is why many of us believed you had died. A child whose bloodline was forcefully taken away could not have survived easily, especially during an attack arranged by the second faction. So I do not understand.\"","She stepped closer, her gaze fixed on the divine golden radiance surrounding Max.","\"How can you still have this bloodline?\"","Nancy turned toward Max, and for a moment, even she did not know what to say.","Max remained silent.","\"It is a long story,\" he said after a moment, shaking his head slightly. \"Now that you know it is me, can you tell me where Caroline is?\"","Jessica’s expression immediately became solemn.","She looked at Max for a few breaths, as if she still wanted to ask him many things about Caelira, about his survival, about his bloodline, and about the elder sister Nancy had mentioned, but she also knew that none of those questions mattered more than Caroline’s current danger.","If Caroline died or was captured by the second faction, then another pillar of the third faction would fall, and all the hope that had barely begun to rise in Jessica’s heart would be crushed again.","\"Follow me,\" Jessica said firmly.","Then she turned toward the other four injured elves.","\"Heal here,\" she ordered. \"We will regroup once we have saved Caroline.\"","The four elves clearly wanted to follow, but their bodies were covered in wounds, their energy was unstable, and the battle against Lumine’s group had already pushed them close to their limit. If they forced themselves deeper into Witch God Valley in their current state, they would become a burden rather than help.","One of them clenched his teeth and said, \"Jessica, be careful.\"","Jessica nodded. \"Stay alive.\"","The four elves nodded with unwilling but obedient expressions."]},{"number":1758,"title":"Chapter 1758: Caroline’s Stand!","paragraphs":["Without wasting another moment, Jessica turned and rushed deeper into the cursed forest. Max followed beside her, while Nancy kept pace slightly behind them, her silver eyes constantly scanning their surroundings.","The path Jessica chose was not a straight one. She led them between twisted white trees, around pools of dark green liquid, across cracked wooden ridges, and through narrow gaps between broken stone altars.","From time to time, cursed roots twitched beneath the ground as if preparing to attack again, but the lingering black flames around Max’s body forced them back before they could emerge fully.","As they moved deeper, the pressure inside Witch God Valley grew stronger.","The mist thickened until even ordinary sight became almost useless, and the air carried a strange sweetness that made the mind feel heavy. Faint voices echoed from the trees, sometimes sounding like crying elves, sometimes like laughing demons, and sometimes like someone whispering Max’s name from behind him.","Nancy frowned several times, clearly affected by the illusions, but Max’s Dimensional Sovereign Body continued sensing the true path through space, while the Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline within him burned quietly, keeping the cursed influence away from his mind.","Jessica glanced back once and saw Max’s calm expression.","Her heart became even more complicated.","This young man was truly Caelira’s son.","The bloodline proved it. His power proved that he was not an ordinary human. His coldness toward the second faction also proved that he already carried hatred toward the ones who had destroyed his family.","Yet the more Jessica thought about it, the more unsettled she felt. The son of Divine Queen Caelira had returned, and he had returned with strength far beyond what she could understand. Whether this was a blessing or the beginning of an even greater storm, she could not tell.","But for now, she only needed him to save Caroline.","After several minutes of high-speed movement, a violent explosion suddenly shook the forest ahead.","Boom!","A pillar of golden light rose into the sky, tearing through the cursed mist and illuminating the nearby trees. Almost immediately after, a second power descended from above, a radiant spear of judgment that carried sharp suppressive force.","Then came a third force, silent and pale, cutting through the light like an eclipse blade before vanishing again into the mist.","Jessica’s expression changed.","\"We are here.\"","Max’s eyes sharpened.","The three of them rushed through the final layer of trees and arrived at the edge of a wide battlefield formed between several enormous branches of the Witch God Tree. The ground here was cracked and scorched everywhere, and several ancient stone pillars had already collapsed into broken pieces.","Golden light burned across one side of the battlefield, pale eclipse shadows twisted on the other, and above everything, the cursed mist churned violently as if even Witch God Valley itself was afraid to approach the battle taking place there.","At the center of the battlefield, Caroline was fighting alone.","She looked similar to Caelira in a way that made Max’s eyes turn cold instantly. Her long golden hair was disheveled, her white battle dress was stained with blood, and several deep wounds marked her arms and waist, but her back remained straight.","Her eyes shone with bright golden light, and the Heavenly Luminance Royal Bloodline within her continued burning around her body like a sacred flame refusing to go out. She held a slender golden sword in one hand, while light gathered around her other hand, forming shields, arrows, chains, and blades that moved with graceful precision.","Facing her were two elves.","Seraphine and Fin.","Seraphine stood in the air above the battlefield, her long golden hair floating behind her, her expression cold and dignified. Her body was wrapped in radiant armor formed from light, and behind her, a vast golden path had manifested, filled with pillars, scales, chains, and countless shining eyes that looked down upon Caroline like judges sentencing a criminal.","This was her Pseudo Cosmic Path, the Radiant Judgment Path. Every time she raised her hand, beams of light descended from the path like divine punishment, suppressing Caroline’s movements, burning through her defenses, and trying to seal her bloodline power.","Fin moved differently.","He was almost silent.","His pale-gold hair and white cloak seemed to fade in and out of the mist, and around him spread a strange Pseudo Cosmic Path of dim light and shadow. The Pale Eclipse Path twisted perception, swallowed sound, and distorted distance.","One moment he was in front of Caroline, the next he appeared behind her, his sword cutting from impossible angles with pale crescent-shaped light that looked gentle but carried deadly sharpness. If Seraphine was judgment descending from above, then Fin was execution hidden in silence.","Caroline fought both of them at once.","A golden shield appeared above her, blocking Seraphine’s radiant spear, but the moment the spear shattered, Fin’s sword appeared near her back. Caroline turned instantly, releasing a burst of golden light from her body.","The light formed dozens of thin blades around her and forced Fin’s figure to fade back into the mist, but before she could breathe, Seraphine pressed one hand downward.","\"Radiant Judgment, Chain of Conviction.\"","Golden chains descended from the path behind Seraphine and wrapped toward Caroline from all directions. Each chain carried suppressive power that targeted her bloodline directly, and the moment they approached, the golden light around Caroline’s body flickered violently. Caroline gritted her teeth and thrust her sword upward.","\"Heavenly Luminance, Breaking Dawn.\"","A pillar of pure light erupted from her sword and shattered several chains at once, but not all of them. One chain wrapped around her left wrist, another caught her shoulder, and for a brief moment, her movements slowed.","That moment was enough.","Fin appeared behind her like a pale shadow.","His sword stabbed silently toward her heart.","Jessica’s face turned pale. \"Caroline!\"","Caroline’s eyes flashed, and a pair of golden wings made of light suddenly appeared behind her. She twisted her body at the last instant, causing Fin’s sword to pierce through her side instead of her heart. Blood scattered across the air, but Caroline did not cry out. She gathered light in her palm and slammed it toward Fin’s chest.","Boom!","Fin was forced back several steps, but his body dissolved into pale eclipse light before the attack could fully injure him.","Seraphine looked down at Caroline coldly.","\"You are still struggling,\" she said. \"How pointless.\"","Caroline pulled Fin’s sword light out of her wound with a trembling hand, and golden light immediately covered the injury to slow the bleeding. Her breathing was heavy, and her face was pale, but her eyes remained bright with defiance.","\"If you want to drag me back to the Elf Prison,\" Caroline said coldly, \"then you will have to break every bone in my body first.\"","Fin appeared beside Seraphine, his expression calm and indifferent. \"That can be arranged.\"","Seraphine raised her hand again, and the Radiant Judgment Path behind her became brighter.","\"Caroline, you are the last symbol that keeps those remnants loyal to Caelira. Once you are captured, the third faction will finally understand that hope is dead.\"","Caroline’s eyes turned colder. \"You can only wish for that.\""]},{"number":1759,"title":"Chapter 1759: Max Makes His Move!","paragraphs":["Seraphine’s gaze sharpened.","\"Then let me prove you wrong.\"","The radiant path behind her trembled, and countless spears of light began forming above the battlefield. At the same time, Fin’s Pale Eclipse Path spread outward, dimming the space around Caroline and making her figure appear isolated beneath the falling judgment.","The two Pseudo Cosmic Paths pressed down at once, one suppressing her from above and the other sealing her escape routes through distorted light and shadow.","Caroline lifted her sword with both hands.","Golden light erupted from her bloodline again, but anyone could see that she was nearly at her limit. She had already been fighting for too long. Her aura was unstable, her injuries were worsening, and against Seraphine and Fin together, even her Heavenly Luminance Royal Bloodline could not hold forever.","Jessica’s eyes turned red with urgency. \"Max, that is Caroline.\"","Max did not answer.","He was staring at the woman in the center of the battlefield.","Caroline.","His mother’s younger sister.","His aunt.","Someone who had been hunted, imprisoned, and tortured because of her connection to Caelira.","The golden light in Max’s eyes slowly brightened, and the temperature around him seemed to drop despite the divine radiance beginning to rise from his body.","Nancy felt the change in him and took a silent step back.","On the battlefield, Seraphine’s hand descended.","\"Radiant Judgment, Thousand Spears of Exile.\"","Thousands of radiant spears fell toward Caroline.","Fin’s figure vanished at the same time, reappearing behind her with his sword aimed at the wound in her side.","Caroline raised her sword, ready to endure it all.","But before the attacks could land, space rippled.","Max appeared in front of her.","He did not speak.","He simply raised one hand.","A brilliant golden barrier formed before him, carrying the aura of the Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline, and the moment the thousand radiant spears struck it, they shattered one after another like weak glass touching an unbreakable sun. At the same time, Max turned his head slightly and looked toward the empty space behind Caroline, where Fin’s blade was about to emerge.","His other hand moved.","Dragonheart flashed.","Fin’s sword strike was forced back before it could touch Caroline.","For the first time, Seraphine’s cold expression changed.","Fin also stopped moving.","Caroline stared at the figure standing before her, her exhausted eyes filled with shock.","Max did not look back yet.","His gaze remained fixed on Seraphine and Fin.","\"You two,\" he said calmly, but his voice carried a coldness that made the entire battlefield silent, \"needs to die.\"","\"And who are you, human?\" Seraphine asked with a solemn face, her eyes fixed on Max as the shattered remnants of her radiant spears faded above the battlefield. \"Why are you interfering in a fight between elves?\"","Unlike Lumine, Seraphine did not immediately lose her composure, but the seriousness in her gaze deepened. The golden barrier Max had raised just now had not merely blocked her attack. It had shattered the Thousand Spears of Exile with ease, and even more importantly, the aura released from that barrier felt strangely familiar to her.","It was light. It was pure. It was connected to the Heavenly Luminance bloodline, but it was not the same as Caroline’s. It was denser, higher, and far more oppressive, which made Seraphine’s heart sink with a faint unease she could not immediately explain.","Fin, however, was different.","He appeared beside Seraphine again, his pale cloak fluttering slightly in the mist, and instead of looking cautious, he laughed with open arrogance. His eyes swept over Max like he was looking at another prey that had conveniently delivered itself to them.","\"Haha, who cares, Seraphine?\" Fin said. \"Let us kill him too. That way we will get more points. We cannot let the Divine Son and Divine Daughter take all the fun, can we?\"","The moment the words Divine Son and Divine Daughter were spoken, Caroline’s expression changed slightly, but Max only glanced at Fin with calm eyes.","Caroline, who was standing behind Max, finally recovered from her shock. Her breathing was still uneven, and the wound at her side had not fully closed, but when she saw a human standing between her and Seraphine and Fin, her first reaction was not relief. It was alarm.","\"You should not have interfered,\" Caroline said, her voice weak but firm.","Max turned his head slightly.","Caroline looked at him with a serious expression, and despite her injuries, there was still the bearing of someone who had once stood among the core of the third faction. \"I do not know who you are, and I thank you for blocking that attack, but you need to leave. These two are not ordinary elves. Seraphine and Fin are among the strongest geniuses of the second faction. Both of them have mastered Pseudo Cosmic Paths, and both of them are peak Law Manifestation Realm experts.\"","Her eyes moved briefly toward Seraphine’s Radiant Judgment Path and Fin’s Pale Eclipse Path, then returned to Max.","\"If you stay here, you will die.\"","Jessica, who had arrived at the edge of the battlefield with Nancy, clenched her fists when she heard those words. She wanted to explain who Max was, but the atmosphere was too tense, and for a moment, she could not find the right time to speak.","Nancy also remained silent, but there was no worry in her eyes. She had already seen enough of Max’s strength to know that Caroline’s warning, while sincere, was based on a misunderstanding.","Max looked at Caroline for a moment.","There was blood on her battle dress, exhaustion in her eyes, and stubbornness in the way she still tried to stand straight even after being pushed to the edge by two powerful enemies. She did not know him.","She did not know he was Caelira’s son. She did not know that the human she was warning was not someone who had stumbled into this battle by accident, but someone who had crossed half of Witch God Valley to find her.","For some reason, that made Max’s gaze soften slightly.","Then he smiled.","\"Do not worry,\" he said. \"I will take care of them.\"","Caroline froze.","The words were spoken so casually that for a moment, she almost thought she had heard wrong.","Take care of them?","Seraphine and Fin?","Two of the second faction’s strongest young experts, both Pseudo Cosmic Path users, both peak Law Manifestation Realm geniuses, and both specifically sent to capture her?","Even when she had been at her full strength, Caroline could only barely resist them by using every advantage of her Heavenly Luminance Royal Bloodline. She had been forced into a desperate battle, suppressed from above by the Radiant Judgment","Path and hunted from the shadows by the Pale Eclipse Path. Yet this human was smiling as if he had merely been asked to remove two stones from the road."]},{"number":1760,"title":"Chapter 1760: Mocking Max!","paragraphs":["For a brief moment after Max said he would take care of them, the battlefield fell into a strange silence.","Seraphine’s eyes narrowed as she looked at Max.","The golden light that had appeared around him just now had not escaped her senses. She had felt it clearly. There was a strange bloodline aura coming from this human, and although she did not want to admit it, that aura gave her a faint pressure that should not have existed. It was related to the Heavenly Luminance bloodline.","No, it felt even purer than the bloodline power flowing inside her own body. That realization made her heart tighten for a moment, but Seraphine quickly suppressed the unease rising inside her.","She refused to believe that a human could possess something superior to the royal bloodline of the elves. It had to be the effect of some treasure, some inheritance, or perhaps a trick created by Caroline’s side to shake her confidence.","Her expression became cold again.","\"You will take care of us?\" Seraphine repeated, her voice carrying clear mockery. \"Human, do you even understand what you are saying?\"","Fin laughed from beside her, his figure flickering faintly inside the dim light of his Pale Eclipse Path. \"He obviously does not. Look at him, Seraphine. He blocked one attack and already thinks he can stand above us. Humans are always amusing when they mistake one lucky moment for strength.\"","Caroline frowned and took a step forward despite her injuries. \"You need to stop provoking them. They are not enemies you can handle with courage alone.\"","Max looked back at her and smiled faintly. \"I told you, I will take care of them.\"","That calm reply made Caroline even more anxious, but before she could say anything else, Seraphine’s cold laughter sounded across the battlefield.","\"Caroline, it seems your situation is so miserable that even a human stranger has started acting like your protector,\" Seraphine said, her golden eyes filled with disdain. \"How far the remnants of Caelira’s faction have fallen.\"","Caroline’s expression turned cold. \"Do not speak her name.\"","Seraphine ignored her and kept her gaze on Max. \"You carry a strange light aura. I will admit that much. For a moment, it almost made me think of the Heavenly Luminance bloodline, but that is impossible. A human like you cannot possess such a bloodline. At most, you obtained some imitation, some damaged treasure, or some fragment of power you do not truly understand.\"","Fin’s smile widened. \"Or maybe he stole something from someone and now thinks it belongs to him.\"","Max’s eyes remained calm.","Seraphine watched his lack of reaction, and irritation flashed in her eyes. She disliked that calmness. Most people showed fear when facing her Radiant Judgment Path. Some showed hatred. Some showed desperation. But Max was looking at her as if she and Fin were merely obstacles delaying him.","\"You are not the first person to stand in front of me with confidence,\" Seraphine said coldly. \"Many geniuses have done the same. Some relied on powerful bodies. Some relied on divine weapons. Some relied on bloodline tricks. In the end, all of them lowered their heads beneath judgment.\"","Fin slowly walked to the side, his figure splitting into several pale afterimages as the Pale Eclipse Path twisted the space around him. \"Seraphine, do not waste too many words on him. Since he wants to be a hero, let him die like one. I want to see if his expression will remain that calm after I cut his arms off.\"","Max glanced at Fin. \"You can try.\"","The simple reply made Fin’s smile stiffen.","A cold light flashed in his eyes.","\"You really are eager to die.\"","Seraphine raised her hand slightly, and the Radiant Judgment Path behind her brightened again. Golden pillars rose within the path, countless shining eyes opened in the air, and scales of light formed above her head as if the entire battlefield had become a court where she alone held the right to decide guilt and punishment.","\"Human,\" she said with a mocking smile, \"since you insist on interfering in elven matters, then I will allow you to understand the difference between borrowed courage and true power.\"","Fin’s body faded further into the dim eclipse light around him. \"And I will take his Killing Points after you break him. He looks like someone who has gathered quite a lot.\"","Seraphine’s gaze moved briefly toward Dragonheart in Max’s hand, and although she did not recognize everything about it, she could feel that it was not ordinary. Her smile became colder.","\"His sword is also interesting.\"","Fin laughed. \"Then we kill him, take the sword, take the points, and then drag Caroline back. That sounds like a good ending.\"","Caroline’s face became pale with anger and worry. \"You two are shameless.\"","Seraphine looked at her indifferently. \"The defeated do not get to complain about methods.\"","Max slowly turned Dragonheart in his hand.","The sword gave out a low hum, and the sound spread across the battlefield like a dragon waking beneath a silent mountain. Seraphine’s expression changed slightly again when she felt the power coming of Max’s sword. It was too powerful.","Even Fin could not help but feel threatened by the sword in Max’s hand.","Although he had been mocking Max a moment ago, the instant Dragonheart gave out that low hum, Fin’s instincts sharpened, and the pale light of his Eclipse Path trembled faintly around him. He was arrogant, but he was not stupid.","A sword that could make his Pseudo Cosmic Path react like that could not be an ordinary weapon, and the more he looked at Dragonheart, the more familiar it seemed, as if he had heard about it from somewhere not too long ago.","\"Wait a minute!\" Fin suddenly exclaimed, his eyes narrowing as realization flashed across his face. \"That sword... I know you! You are that human who recently became famous in the Divine Realm. Max Morgan, was it? The one who got the Sword of the Sword Sovereign.\"","\"Sword of the Sword Sovereign?\" Seraphine frowned, and for a brief moment, the caution in her eyes deepened before it was quickly replaced by disdain. She looked at Dragonheart, then looked at Max again, and a sneer slowly appeared on her face. \"So the aura he was releasing came from his sword and not from him?\"","She then laughed.","\"No wonder I felt a little threatened by him. It turns out it was all because of his sword.\""]},{"number":1761,"title":"Chapter 1761: Mocking Turn into Fear!","paragraphs":["Caroline, who stood behind Max, also frowned slightly. She had heard of the Sword of the Sword Sovereign. Anyone who had entered the Cosmic Ascension Conference and paid attention to the great inheritances and major treasures would have heard the rumors.","A human had obtained a terrifying sword connected to the Sword Sovereign, had offended the Sword God Palace, and was now being hunted by them.","Yet Caroline still could not understand why such a person would appear here, why he would interfere in a battle between elves, and why he would stand between her and two enemies powerful enough to threaten even her life. If he only relied on the sword, then his confidence was far too dangerous. If he had misjudged Seraphine and Fin, then he would die here because of her.","\"Seraphine, we should play with him a bit,\" Fin said with a smile as the Pale Eclipse Path twisted behind him like a curtain of dim light and shadow. \"Do not kill him easily.\"","Seraphine looked at Max with cold amusement. \"A human who borrowed a sword and started thinking he could interfere with the second faction. Fine. Since he wants to act brave in front of Caroline, let him understand what despair feels like.\"","Max listened to them quietly.","And then his expression changed all of a sudden.","The change was immediate.","One moment, Max looked calm and faintly amused by their arrogance. The next moment, his expression became completely emotionless. His eyes lost every visible ripple of anger, mockery, impatience, or killing intent, and what remained was so still that it felt more terrifying than rage. It was not the calm of someone suppressing emotions. It was the calm of someone who had cut them away entirely.","The air around him changed.","A silent aura spread from his body.","This time, it was different from before.","When Max had used the Emotion Severing Path against the Sword God Palace disciples and Lumine’s group, he had only revealed enough to kill them quickly, but now, for the first time, he truly released the full pressure of his Pseudo Cosmic Path.","The Severing Sword Concept inside him unfolded completely, and the Emotion Severing Path descended upon Witch God Valley like an invisible heaven-splitting blade.","The cursed mist stopped moving.","The violet sky above the treetop seemed to darken.","The golden light of Seraphine’s Radiant Judgment Path trembled.","The pale shadows of Fin’s Eclipse Path distorted violently, as if something had cut through the foundation of their illusion.","A chill crawled down everyone’s spine.","It was not cold in the ordinary sense. It did not come from ice, wind, or death energy. It came from something deeper and far more frightening. It felt as if the heart itself had been touched by a blade, as if fear, anger, pride, hatred, and hope could all be severed before they even fully formed.","The aura did not scream for destruction. It did not demand submission. It simply existed, silent and absolute, turning the entire battlefield into a place where emotions felt fragile and life felt thin.","Jessica’s body stiffened at the edge of the battlefield.","The four third faction elves who had followed behind at a distance felt their faces turn pale, and even though Max’s path was not aimed at them, their souls still trembled from the pressure.","Caroline, standing closest behind Max, felt her breath catch in her throat.","Her Heavenly Luminance Royal Bloodline instinctively flared, wrapping her injured body in golden light, but even that sacred warmth could not fully drive away the chill spreading from Max’s back.","Nancy was shaken the most.","She had seen Max use his sword before.","She had seen him kill the Sword God Palace disciples with one slash. She had seen him erase Lumine’s group with the Saint Origin Sword Art. She had seen the emotionless state that appeared when he touched his Pseudo Cosmic Path.","Yet this was still different. This was not a glimpse. This was not a restrained release. This was the true pressure of Max’s Emotion Severing Path, and the moment it descended, even Nancy felt her heart shake as if an invisible sword had been placed against it.","’So he was still holding back before,’ Nancy thought, her fingers tightening around her sword.","The realization made her feel cold.","Seraphine’s mocking smile slowly disappeared.","The laughter in Fin’s eyes also froze.","For the first time, both of them understood that something was wrong. The pressure spreading from Max was not coming from Dragonheart. The sword was resonating with him, but it was not the source. The terrifying aura, the emotionless stillness, the invisible severing force pressing down on their minds, all of it came from Max himself.","Seraphine’s eyes widened slightly. \"This is...\"","Fin’s expression turned ugly. \"A Pseudo Cosmic Path?\"","Max slowly raised Dragonheart.","The blade hummed again, but now the sound was different. It was no longer the roar of a treasure revealing its presence. It was the cry of a sword answering its master’s path. The Emotion Severing Path wrapped around the blade in thin, invisible layers, and the air near the edge split silently.","No light flashed. No storm erupted. Yet the danger carried by that raised sword made both Seraphine and Fin feel their skin tighten.","Max looked at them with eyes that held no emotion.","\"You were wrong about one thing,\" he said calmly.","His voice was quiet, but everyone heard it clearly.","\"The sword is not what made you feel threatened.\"","Seraphine’s face darkened.","Fin instinctively took half a step back, then immediately stopped himself when he realized what he had done, and humiliation flashed in his eyes.","Max continued, his tone still flat and emotionless.","\"It was me.\"","The words fell like a verdict.","Seraphine gritted her teeth, and the Radiant Judgment Path behind her erupted with stronger golden light as she forcefully suppressed the unease in her heart. \"Do not get carried away, human. A Pseudo Cosmic Path does not mean you can defeat us both.\"","Fin’s expression twisted into a cold smile again, but this time the confidence in it was no longer complete. \"Good. This makes it more interesting. If we kill you, the points and that sword will both belong to us.\"","Max did not respond.","He only took one step forward.","The moment his foot touched the cracked battlefield, the invisible pressure of the Emotion Severing Path spread even deeper, and the thin line already cut into the ground beneath him extended forward silently, as if the earth itself had acknowledged his sword before he even swung it.","Seraphine and Fin both felt their hearts tighten at the same time, and although neither of them wanted to admit it, the calmness in Max’s eyes was beginning to feel more frightening than any killing intent.","He was not looking at them like enemies who could threaten him. He was looking at them like obstacles that had not yet realized they were already dead for him."]},{"number":1762,"title":"Chapter 1762: Playing with them!","paragraphs":["Seraphine’s pride could not accept that.","\"Radiant Judgment Path, full manifestation!\"","The golden path behind her expanded violently. Pillars of light rose into the sky, countless shining eyes opened across the air, and giant golden scales appeared above the battlefield as if weighing every soul beneath them.","Chains, spears, swords, and radiant tablets appeared one after another, forming a divine court of judgment that seemed capable of suppressing an entire region. Seraphine’s body floated higher, her golden hair scattering around her like a burning halo, and the Heavenly Luminance Royal Bloodline inside her flared to its limit, wrapping her body in sacred armor that made her look like a goddess passing sentence upon sinners.","At the same time, Fin disappeared completely.","\"Pale Eclipse Path, full manifestation.\"","The light across the battlefield dimmed.","The shadows lengthened unnaturally.","The space around Max twisted, and Fin’s presence split into dozens of vague figures, each one standing at a different angle, each one holding a sword, each one looking real enough to kill.","Pale crescent moons appeared within the darkened mist, and every crescent reflected a different version of Fin’s attack, making it impossible for ordinary senses to determine which direction the true strike would come from.","His path did not suppress openly like Seraphine’s. It confused, distorted, erased sound, bent distance, and turned the battlefield into an eclipse cage where perception itself became unreliable.","Caroline’s expression changed.","\"Both of them are using their full Pseudo Cosmic Paths,\" she said in a low voice, her injured body trembling from the pressure. \"Even I could not force them to this point so quickly.\"","Jessica’s face was also pale. \"Can he handle this?\"","Nancy did not answer immediately.","She looked at Max’s back, at the deathly calm expression on his face, and at the way Dragonheart hung loosely in his hand despite the two terrifying paths pressing down on him at once.","\"Easily,\" Nancy said quietly.","The moment she said that, Seraphine attacked.","\"Radiant Judgment, Divine Court Execution!\"","The shining eyes within her Pseudo Cosmic Path released countless beams of light at the same time. Spears descended from above, chains rushed from the sides, swords of judgment appeared beneath Max’s feet, and golden tablets fell like heavenly decrees, sealing the space around him layer by layer.","Every attack carried the power of her Radiant Judgment Path, and every strand of light contained suppression, restraint, destruction, and the intent to judge Max as guilty before erasing him completely.","Fin attacked at the same instant.","Dozens of pale shadows flashed around Max, and each one stabbed toward a different vital point. One aimed for his throat, another for his heart, another for his spine, another for the tendons of his arms, while several more struck from impossible angles that ordinary movement could not avoid.","The Pale Eclipse Path twisted all of those attacks into silence, making them appear late, early, near, and far at the same time.","It was a perfect joint assault.","One path suppressed and judged.","One path distorted and assassinated.","Even a powerful genius at the same level would have been trapped, wounded, or killed in an instant.","Max only raised Dragonheart.","One slash.","A quiet sword light moved outward.","The golden spears shattered.","The chains split apart.","The swords of judgment broke into fragments.","The falling tablets were cut in half.","The dozens of pale shadows vanished like illusions touched by dawn.","The true sword strike hidden among Fin’s afterimages was also forced out, and Fin’s real body appeared several dozen meters away, his expression stiff and his sword hand trembling slightly.","The battlefield fell silent for a fraction of a breath.","Then Seraphine’s expression darkened.","\"Again!\"","Her Radiant Judgment Path erupted once more, brighter and more violent than before. The giant scales above the battlefield tilted toward Max, and a massive golden sword formed from the combined power of countless judgment runes descended from the sky.","This sword was different from the scattered spears before. It carried the full suppressive force of her path, and the moment it appeared, the ground beneath Max sank several inches, while Caroline and Jessica felt their bloodline power tremble uncontrollably.","\"Radiant Judgment, Sword of Final Sentence!\"","Fin also gritted his teeth and pushed his Pale Eclipse Path harder. The eclipse crescents around him fused into a single pale-black sword arc that vanished the moment it formed, not because it disappeared, but because it slipped into the blind spot between sight and thought. It attacked from a direction that the mind would naturally ignore, making it almost impossible to block unless one could sever the distortion of perception itself.","\"Pale Eclipse, Silent Moon Execution.\"","The two attacks came together.","Max’s eyes remained emotionless.","He swung Dragonheart again.","This slash was still simple.","There was no grand technique visible to the eyes of others, only the cold, absolute pressure of the Emotion Severing Path flowing along the blade. The moment Max’s sword moved, the Sword of Final Sentence was split cleanly from tip to hilt, and the golden judgment runes inside it lost all meaning before scattering into broken light.","At the same time, the invisible Silent Moon Execution was cut out of its hidden state, revealed as a pale sword arc for only an instant before being severed into countless fading fragments.","Seraphine’s face changed.","Fin’s eyes widened.","Their strongest coordinated attack had been destroyed with one sword slash again.","No.","It had not merely been destroyed.","It had been severed from the very source of its power.","Seraphine could feel it clearly. The golden judgment runes she had formed were not broken by brute force. They had been cut away from the law and intent that supported them. Fin felt the same thing. His Pale Eclipse distortion had not been seen through in the usual way. Max’s sword had cut through the concept of concealment itself, making his hidden attack meaningless before it could land.","\"How is that possible?\" Fin muttered.","Seraphine’s breathing grew heavier, but her pride forced her to continue.","\"Do not stop!\" she snapped.","She raised both hands, and the Radiant Judgment Path behind her trembled violently as she drew out even more power. Golden chains thicker than pillars burst from the air and wrapped toward Max, while thousands of smaller blades of light spun around them like a storm.","Fin disappeared again, this time merging deeper into his Pale Eclipse Path until even his aura nearly vanished. He gave up on direct attacks and began launching one silent strike after another from every direction, each one aimed at the gaps between Max’s movements.","But Max kept walking.","He walked forward through their attacks as if strolling through rain.","A chain came from the left.","He cut it.","A blade storm descended from above.","He cut it.","Fin’s sword appeared behind his neck.","He cut it away without even turning fully.","Radiant light formed a cage around him.","He split the cage with a casual flick of Dragonheart.","Pale shadows tried to bind his reflection and confuse his position.","He severed the distortion with a single sweep.","Seraphine and Fin attacked again and again, throwing out every technique they had refined through their Pseudo Cosmic Paths, yet nothing worked. Their light could not suppress him. Their shadows could not confuse him.","Their chains could not bind him. Their swords could not reach him. Every attack, no matter how powerful, strange, fast, or hidden, was destroyed by one slash of Max’s sword."]},{"number":1763,"title":"Chapter 1763: Max’s Threatening Words!","paragraphs":["Caroline watched in disbelief.","She had fought Seraphine and Fin for a long time and knew exactly how terrifying the combination of their paths was. Seraphine controlled the battlefield from above and forced the enemy into judgment, while Fin moved through the blind spots created by pale eclipse distortion and struck whenever the enemy’s attention wavered.","Together, they were nearly impossible to deal with. Yet Max was not countering them with complicated strategy. He was not desperately defending. He was simply cutting everything down.","Jessica swallowed, her eyes trembling. \"He is overpowering both of their Pseudo Cosmic Paths with his own path.\"","Nancy nodded slowly. \"It’s like Max’s Pseudo Cosmic Path is on a different level than ours.\"","On the battlefield, Seraphine’s face finally began to show fear.","Her Radiant Judgment Path was still shining behind her, but the brilliance was no longer stable. Every time Max cut one of her attacks, the path trembled as if it had been wounded. The shining eyes inside the path flickered. The golden scales cracked. Several of the judgment pillars were covered in thin sword marks that refused to disappear.","Fin was no better.","His Pale Eclipse Path had become chaotic. The shadows that should have obeyed him were splitting apart unnaturally, and the distorted space he relied on kept being cut open by Max’s sword. He had already retreated several times without realizing it, and each time Max took another step forward, Fin felt the distance between life and death shrink.","\"This cannot continue,\" Fin said, his voice finally losing its arrogance.","Seraphine gritted her teeth so hard that her lips trembled. \"Then use everything.\"","Fin’s eyes flashed with fear and unwillingness.","Then both of them released their final strength.","Seraphine clasped her hands together, and the entire Radiant Judgment Path condensed into one enormous golden eye above the battlefield. The eye opened slowly, releasing a pressure that made even the cursed mist of Witch God Valley sink downward. All of her judgment, all of her light, all of her bloodline power gathered inside that eye.","\"Radiant Judgment Path, Eye of Absolute Verdict!\"","Fin’s Pale Eclipse Path also collapsed inward, forming a black-white eclipse behind him. His body merged with the eclipse, and his sword became a thin pale line that seemed to exist outside normal space.","\"Pale Eclipse Path, Final Moonless Cut!\"","The enormous golden eye released a pillar of judgment toward Max.","At the same time, Fin’s moonless sword cut appeared directly before Max’s heart.","This was their strongest combined attack.","Caroline’s expression changed sharply.","Jessica held her breath.","Nancy’s eyes narrowed.","Max stopped walking for the first time.","Then he raised Dragonheart with both hands.","His Emotion Severing Path grew completely silent.","For one instant, every sound in Witch God Valley disappeared.","Then Max slashed.","A single sword light passed through the battlefield.","The pillar of judgment split apart.","The enormous golden eye cracked from the center.","Fin’s moonless sword cut shattered before it could touch Max.","The eclipse behind Fin was severed into two halves.","The Radiant Judgment Path behind Seraphine let out a sound like breaking glass as cracks spread through its golden court.","Everything they had gathered, everything they had believed in, everything they had used as their strongest power, was cut apart by one slash.","Seraphine stared at the broken golden eye above her, her face pale with disbelief.","Fin stumbled backward, his expression filled with horror.","For the first time, neither of them mocked Max.","For the first time, they truly felt helpless.","They had used their strongest forms.","They had released the full power of their Pseudo Cosmic Paths.","They had attacked together with everything they had.","And Max was still standing in the same place, untouched.","Dragonheart lowered slowly in his hand, and his emotionless eyes looked at them through the fading remnants of their shattered paths.","Seraphine’s lips trembled. \"What... are you?\"","Fin’s sword hand shook so badly that the pale light around it flickered.","Max looked at them with terrifying calmness.","\"Done?\" he asked.","Max’s emotionless eyes stared at Seraphine and Fin, and for a moment, neither of them dared to move.","The battlefield that had been filled with the radiance of judgment and the silence of eclipse now felt strangely empty. Seraphine’s Radiant Judgment Path was covered in cracks, its golden pillars broken, its shining eyes dimming one after another, and the enormous eye of absolute verdict that she had formed with all her power had already been split apart by Max’s sword.","Fin’s Pale Eclipse Path was no better. The black-white eclipse behind him had been severed into two halves, the shadows around him were unstable, and the strange distortions he relied on to hide his movements were collapsing like torn cloth.","They had used everything.","They had shown their strongest forms.","They had released the full force of their Pseudo Cosmic Paths.","Yet Max had destroyed all of it with one slash after another, and he stood before them without a wound, without a trace of exhaustion, and without the slightest emotional fluctuation on his face. That was what frightened them the most.","If Max had been angry, they could have mocked his rage. If he had been excited, they could have called him arrogant. If he had been killing them for revenge, they could have understood him as another enemy driven by hatred.","But the Max standing before them now felt like something colder than hatred, something that had already decided their end and was merely waiting for the final breath to arrive.","Seraphine’s lips trembled as she stared at him. \"You... you cannot kill us. Do you understand who we are?\"","Fin’s sword hand shook, but he still tried to force out a cold smile. \"If you kill us here, the second faction will not let you go.\"","Max looked at them silently.","Then he spoke.","\"Remember this feeling from the bottom of your heart.\"","His voice was calm, but the calmness was far more terrifying than any shout. The Emotion Severing Path still surrounded him, and every word he spoke seemed to carve itself into the air like a cold blade.","Seraphine and Fin felt their hearts tighten, and even though their pride screamed at them to resist, their instincts told them that they were no longer facing someone they could threaten.","\"One day,\" Max continued, \"I will come to your second faction and engrave this feeling into all the elves in your faction.\"","Seraphine’s eyes widened.","Fin’s expression finally changed completely.","Max took one step forward, and the broken battlefield beneath his feet split again with a thin, silent line.","\"I will make them feel what true despair means.\"","The words fell over Witch God Valley like a sentence passed by something higher than judgment."]},{"number":1764,"title":"Chapter 1764: Killing Them!","paragraphs":["Caroline stood behind him, her injured body frozen in place, and even though the threat was not directed at her, she still felt a chill move through her heart.","Jessica’s eyes trembled with shock and emotion, because for years, the third faction had lived under the terror of the Elf Prison, the torture of the second faction, and the belief that no one would ever make their tormentors pay.","Yet now Caelira’s son stood before two of the second faction’s strongest young geniuses and promised to carry that fear back to their entire faction.","Nancy remained silent, but her gaze was fixed on Max’s back.","She knew this was not an empty threat.","If Max said he would do it, then one day he truly would.","Seraphine gritted her teeth, and shame mixed with fear in her eyes. \"You dare speak about our faction like that? You are only one human. Do you think one sword, one Pseudo Cosmic Path, and one stolen reputation can make you stand against us?\"","Max’s eyes did not change.","\"Still pretending?\"","Seraphine’s face stiffened.","Fin suddenly moved.","He knew talking was useless. He knew begging would be humiliating. He knew that if he stayed still, Max’s next slash would end him.","So, in the final moment, he gathered the broken remnants of his Pale Eclipse Path around his body and tried to vanish into the distorted shadows behind him. His figure became faint, slipping between light and darkness, attempting to escape the battlefield and preserve at least one life.","Max did not even turn fully toward him.","Dragonheart moved once.","A thin sword light crossed the space where Fin was trying to disappear.","The Pale Eclipse Path split open.","Fin’s body froze halfway into the shadow, and disbelief filled his eyes as a clean line appeared across his chest. His escape technique, his path, his body, and the last trace of his confidence were all severed at the same time. He looked down at the golden line splitting him apart, then lifted his eyes toward Max with horror.","\"How...\"","Before he could finish, his body separated into two halves and dissolved into golden fragments of Killing Points.","Seraphine watched Fin die.","For the first time, pure terror covered her face.","She stepped back instinctively, and the cracked Radiant Judgment Path behind her flickered desperately, trying to gather enough strength for one final defense.","Golden chains appeared around her, forming layer after layer of protection. Scales of judgment floated before her like shields. The remaining shining eyes opened, all staring at Max as if trying to condemn him one last time.","Max looked at her calmly.","Seraphine’s voice shook despite her attempt to remain proud. \"You will regret killing me. Our Divine Son and Divine Daughter will avenge us. You will die a cruel death in the conference.\"","Max raised Dragonheart.","\"I already regret something,\" he said quietly.","Seraphine froze.","Max’s eyes became even colder.","\"I regret that I was not strong enough back then to stop you people from touching my family.\"","The moment those words entered Seraphine’s ears, something clicked in her mind.","His family.","His mother.","The strange Heavenly Luminance aura.","Caelira.","Her face turned pale.","\"You are...\" Seraphine whispered.","Max did not let her finish.","The Emotion Severing Path gathered along Dragonheart, and a silent sword light flashed through the battlefield. Seraphine’s chains of judgment split apart first. Then the scales shattered. The remaining shining eyes dimmed. The cracked Radiant Judgment Path behind her was cut through from the center, and finally, the sword light passed through Seraphine herself.","A golden line appeared across her body.","Her eyes remained wide open, filled with shock, fear, and a realization that had come too late.","Then her body split apart and dissolved into golden fragments of Killing Points.","The battlefield became silent.","The two powerful geniuses of the second faction, Seraphine and Fin, had fallen.","Their fragments of Killing Points drifted through the mist, glowing brighter than all the others Max had absorbed in Witch God Valley so far. They circled him for a brief moment before rushing into his body, one stream after another, adding to the terrifying number he had already accumulated.","Max stood still until the last fragment disappeared.","Only then did the full pressure of his Emotion Severing Path begin to fade. The deathly calm on his face softened slightly, and the world around him seemed to breathe again as the cursed mist started moving, the distant whispers returned, and the broken remnants of the two Pseudo Cosmic Paths vanished from the battlefield.","Caroline stared at him.","Jessica stared at him.","Nancy looked at him quietly.","Max slowly lowered Dragonheart and turned back toward Caroline.","Caroline took a step back seeing Max’s emotionless eyes. It felt like she was staring at a bottomless abyss.","\"You must be Caroline,\" Max said calmly, though he did not realize that his Pseudo Cosmic Path was still active.","The Emotion Severing Path had not fully withdrawn from the battlefield, and because of that, his voice sounded colder than he intended.","The invisible aura around him still carried that terrifying stillness, and the air near Dragonheart remained sharp enough to make the cursed mist split apart before it could drift too close.","His eyes were calm, almost empty, and the traces of Seraphine and Fin’s shattered Pseudo Cosmic Paths had not yet completely disappeared from around him.","To anyone else, he looked like a young swordsman who had just passed judgment on two powerful geniuses without feeling anything at all.","\"Caroline!\"","Just then, Jessica and Nancy hurried over and appeared beside Caroline.","Caroline turned her head toward them, still pale from her injuries and the shock of what she had just witnessed. \"Jessica and... Nancy?\"","She was not surprised that Jessica had come. Jessica belonged to the third faction, and Caroline knew she would never abandon her if there was still a chance to help. But Nancy’s presence made her eyes flicker with confusion.","Nancy was from the first faction, and although the first faction had not been as cruel as the second faction, they had still remained neutral for too long while the third faction suffered. Caroline could not understand why an elf from the first faction would be standing beside Jessica and this terrifying human.","Jessica, however, did not have time to explain everything slowly.","Her eyes were red with emotion, and her voice trembled as she raised her hand and pointed at Max.","\"Caroline,\" Jessica said, almost unable to keep her voice steady. \"He... He is Caelira’s son. He is the son of our Divine Queen!\""]},{"number":1765,"title":"Chapter 1765: Caroline’s Breakdown!","paragraphs":["The words struck Caroline like a bolt of lightning.","For a moment, she forgot the pain in her body.","She forgot the wounds left by Fin’s sword.","She forgot Seraphine, the second faction, Witch God Valley, and even the danger still lurking around them.","Her eyes slowly widened, and her gaze moved back to Max as if she was seeing him for the first time.","\"What?\" Caroline whispered.","Jessica took a shaky breath. \"He is Divine Queen Caelira’s son.\"","Caroline’s lips trembled.","\"WHAT?!\" she finally shouted, her voice breaking under the weight of disbelief. \"My sister’s son?!\"","She stared at Max with wide, trembling eyes.","It was impossible.","It should have been impossible.","For years, Caroline had believed that her sister’s children had died during that calamity. She remembered the day the news reached the imprisoned members of the third faction. She remembered the silence that had fallen over the Elf Prison.","She remembered how the older elves had lowered their heads, how the younger ones had cried, and how she herself had broken down after hearing that Caelira’s son and daughter had supposedly been killed.","Those children had not merely been her sister’s children. They had been the last living proof that Caelira had found happiness beyond the throne, beyond bloodline duty, and beyond the cruel politics of the elf race.","Caroline had mourned them.","She had shed tears for them.","She had hated herself for being unable to protect them.","And now Jessica was telling her that one of them was standing right in front of her.","Max looked at her silently.","He did not know what to say. The Emotion Severing Path was still affecting him faintly and he found himself unable to come out of this state for some unknown reason. It was the first time Max found himself in such a state.","Never ever was there a moment he would be in the Emotion Severing Path state without his consent and his will but now that he wanted to desperately came out of this state, he found himself unable to do so.","Caroline took one step toward him.","Then another.","Her body swayed slightly because of her injuries, but she did not stop. Her eyes moved over Max’s face, searching for traces of her sister, and the more she looked, the more her expression changed.","It was not obvious at first glance, but in the line of his eyes, in the faint golden glow of his bloodline, and in the cold strength that seemed to refuse to bend no matter what stood before him, she could see pieces of Caelira.","\"Caelira...\" Caroline whispered, and tears immediately filled her eyes.","Max’s lips parted slightly. \"I...\"","Before he could finish, Caroline stepped forward and hugged him.","The movement was sudden.","Max froze.","Caroline wrapped her arms around him tightly, burying her face against his shoulder as tears finally broke free. She was still bleeding, still exhausted, and still trembling from the battle, but in that moment, none of that mattered to her.","She held Max as if she was afraid he would vanish if she let go, as if the nephew she had thought dead for so many years might disappear like another cruel illusion of Witch God Valley.","\"You are alive,\" Caroline cried, her voice muffled against him. \"You are really alive.\"","Max stood still, his hand still holding Dragonheart loosely at his side.","The Emotion Severing Path around him flickered.","Caroline’s tears fell onto his clothes, and the warmth of her embrace reached him through the coldness of his Pseudo Cosmic Path. It was a strange feeling. A moment ago, he didn’t feel much about her. It was like he didn’t care whether Caroline was his mother’s sister or not.","Yet now, because Caroline was crying while holding him, that deathly stillness inside him began to loosen little by little.","\"You and your sister...\" Caroline said between sobs. \"We thought both of you were dead. I thought I had lost the last pieces of my sister forever.\"","Max’s eyes moved slightly.","His Pseudo Cosmic Path trembled again.","The sharp aura around Max was fading.","The invisible blade that had pressed against everyone’s hearts slowly withdrew, and the suffocating stillness that had covered the battlefield began to melt away.","The cursed mist, which had been split apart by the Emotion Severing Path, started drifting again. The air grew less heavy. Dragonheart’s hum became softer, and the cold line across Max’s expression slowly disappeared.","Jessica watched this scene with red eyes.","She had seen Max as terrifying, powerful, and almost emotionless, but now, seeing Caroline hug him and cry like this, she suddenly remembered that he was not only a monster who could kill Seraphine and Fin. He was Caelira’s son. He was family to the woman who had suffered for years because of loyalty to her sister. He was someone the third faction had believed lost forever.","Max slowly raised his free hand.","For a brief moment, he seemed unsure of what to do.","Then he placed his hand lightly on Caroline’s back.","The moment he did, the last trace of his Emotion Severing Path quietly faded from his body.","His eyes returned to normal.","The deathly calm disappeared.","What remained was a young man standing silently while his aunt cried against him.","Caroline tightened her hold on him even more. \"I am sorry,\" she whispered. \"I am so sorry. I could not protect your mother. I could not protect you. I could not protect anyone.\"","Max’s expression changed slightly.","He looked down at her and said softly, \"You do not need to apologize.\"","Caroline shook her head, still crying. \"I do. I was her sister. I should have been there.\"","Max was silent for a moment.","Then his voice became quieter. \"I came here to find you.\"","Caroline slowly lifted her head, tears still flowing down her face.","Max looked at her and continued, \"I found out you were being hunted, so I came to save you..\"","Caroline stared at him, and the emotions she had barely managed to hold back burst out again.","She hugged him once more, this time even tighter.","\"My sister’s son,\" she whispered, her voice shaking with both grief and joy. \"You are really my sister’s son.\"","Nancy stood quietly nearby, while Jessica lowered her head, tears slipping down her own face.","For the first time since entering Witch God Valley, the battlefield no longer felt like a place of death.","Seraphine and Fin were gone.","The second faction’s hunters had been cut down.","And in the middle of the broken valley, surrounded by cursed mist and shattered remnants of battle, Caroline held Max and cried for the family she had thought lost forever."]},{"number":1766,"title":"Chapter 1766: Little Talk with Caroline!","paragraphs":["Looking at Caroline, who was still crying while holding him tightly, Max did not know what to do.","Even so, he still raised his hand and gently placed it on Caroline’s back.","\"It is fine, Caroline,\" Max said, his voice quieter than before. \"Me and my sister are fine for now. And whatever happened in the past was not your fault.\"","Caroline trembled when she heard those words.","For years, she had carried guilt like a chain around her heart. She had blamed herself for failing to protect Caelira. She had blamed herself for not being there when the calamity struck. She had blamed herself for surviving when her sister’s family was torn apart, when the third faction was imprisoned, when children who should have been protected were declared dead.","Even in the Elf Prison, even while being tortured by the second faction, the thought that she had failed Caelira’s children had never left her. Now, hearing Max say that it was not her fault, something inside her finally cracked.","She tightened her arms around him again and cried harder.","\"You do not understand,\" Caroline whispered through broken sobs. \"I should have come for you. I should have found you. I should have done something.\"","Max looked down at her with a complicated expression.","\"I was a child back then,\" he said softly. \"My sister was also a child. None of this was something you could have stopped alone.\"","Caroline shook her head, tears still falling. \"But I was her sister.\"","Max was silent for a moment.","Then he said, \"And you are still alive.\"","Caroline froze slightly.","Max continued, \"That means my mother still has family waiting for her. That means my sister and I still have someone connected to her. That is enough.\"","Caroline slowly lifted her head and looked at him.","Her eyes were red, her face was wet with tears, and her breathing was unsteady, but for the first time since learning his identity, she truly looked at him not as a ghost from the past, not as a miracle she could not believe, but as the nephew standing alive before her.","She saw the shape of Caelira in his face, but she also saw someone different, someone forged by hardship, danger, and a path of his own. He was not the helpless child she had mourned. He had become a young man strong enough to cross Witch God Valley, kill the hunters sent after her, and stand before her with the promise of taking back everything that had been stolen.","\"You really are her son,\" Caroline said, her voice trembling.","Max gave a small smile. \"Of course I am.\"","For some reason, that simple reply made Caroline laugh softly through her tears.","It was a broken laugh, full of pain and relief, but it was still a laugh.","Jessica, standing nearby, lowered her head as tears gathered in her own eyes again. She had never imagined that after all the suffering the third faction had endured, she would one day see Caroline holding Caelira’s son in the middle of Witch God Valley.","Nancy stood quietly beside them, watching the scene with a softened expression, though her eyes still carried worry because she knew this reunion was happening inside one of the most dangerous regions of the Eternal Hourglass.","Caroline slowly released Max, though her hands still rested on his arms as if she needed to confirm he was truly there.","\"Your sister,\" she asked quickly, her voice filled with desperate hope. \"She is alive too?\"","Max nodded. \"Yes. She is alive. And she is also somewhere in the Divine Realm.\"","Caroline closed her eyes as another tear slipped down her face, but this time, the pain in it was mixed with relief.","\"Thank the heavens,\" she whispered. \"Caelira’s children are alive.\"","Max’s expression became serious again. \"For now, yes. But my parents are still missing, and the second faction still has answers I need.\"","Caroline’s face stiffened.","The warmth of the reunion did not disappear, but the reality of their situation returned like cold water. Seraphine and Fin had been killed, but they had other lives. Lumine and her group had been killed, but they might return.","The second faction was still out there, the Elf Prison still existed, and someone in that faction might even possess the bloodline stolen from Max during the calamity.","Caroline wiped her tears with the back of her hand and forced herself to stand straighter despite her injuries.","\"You came to the right place,\" she said, her voice still weak but firmer than before. \"There are things about that night, about your mother, and about the second faction that you need to know.\"","Max looked at her. \"Then tell me.\"","Caroline glanced toward the deeper mist of Witch God Valley, and her expression became heavy.","\"Not here,\" she said. \"This place is not safe. Seraphine and Fin were not the only ones hunting us, and if they revive outside the valley, the second faction will know that you are here.\"","Max’s gaze turned cold again. \"Let them come. I will kill however many comes.\"","Caroline nodded, then looked at Jessica. \"Where are the others?\"","Jessica answered quickly, \"The four who came with me are injured, but alive. I told them to heal and wait for us.\"","Caroline let out a faint breath of relief. \"Good.\"","Max glanced between them and then turned his eyes toward the cursed mist ahead.","\"Gather everyone,\" he said calmly. \"I believe at the bottom of the Witch God Tree, we will have a grand welcome from the second faction elves.\"","Jessica nodded.","Caroline looked at Max for a moment, and the emotion in her eyes slowly turned heavy. The joy of discovering that her sister’s children were alive had not disappeared, but it had been buried beneath years of painful memories, old hatred, and truths she had carried alone for far too long.","She took a slow breath, then glanced at the ruined battlefield where Seraphine and Fin had fallen moments ago before her gaze returned to Max.","\"In the meantime, let me tell you everything I know,\" Caroline said.","Max did not speak.","Nancy and Jessica also became silent.","Caroline walked forward slowly, her wounds still glowing faintly beneath the healing light covering her body, while Max moved beside her and listened without interrupting.","The cursed mist drifted around them, the twisted trees of Witch God Valley groaned softly in the distance, and the entire place seemed strangely quiet, as if even the valley itself wanted to hear the truth hidden beneath the calamity that had shattered Caelira’s family.","\"Your parents are alive,\" Caroline said softly.","Max’s steps paused for only the briefest moment.","His face remained calm, but the air around him grew colder."]},{"number":1767,"title":"Chapter 1767: Celestial Thorn Abyss!","paragraphs":["Caroline noticed it, and her voice became gentler. \"They are alive, Max. At least, from everything I know, they were not killed. They were taken back to the elf race and imprisoned in the highest-security prison under the control of the second faction and the ancestors supporting them.\"","Max slowly turned his head toward her. \"Where?\"","Caroline’s eyes darkened. \"The Celestial Thorn Abyss.\"","The name made Jessica’s face change.","Even Nancy’s expression became tense.","Caroline continued, \"Among the elf race, it is known as the prison that even royal blood cannot escape from. It is not a normal prison built from walls and chains. It is a sealed world hidden beneath the ancestral lands, wrapped by ancient thorn formations, bloodline suppression seals, and laws left behind by old elven ancestors. Those imprisoned there are not merely locked away. Their energy is suppressed, their bloodline is sealed, their souls are watched, and even their memories can be probed if the wardens receive permission from the ancestors.\"","Max’s eyes became deathly calm. \"They put my parents there?\"","\"Yes,\" Caroline said, her voice filled with pain. \"Your father because he was the human who dared to marry Divine Queen Caelira, and your mother because she was once the strongest symbol of the third faction and the owner of the Heavenly Luminance Royal Bloodline. The second faction could not kill her openly. Even after everything they did, Caelira’s name still carried too much weight among the older elves. If they executed her, it would shake the entire race. So they sealed her instead.\"","For a few moments, no one spoke.","Max’s hand slowly tightened.","Dragonheart was not in his grip, but Jessica still felt a terrifying sword aura rising faintly from him. It was not as overwhelming as when he used the Emotion Severing Path, but it was colder, sharper, and far more personal.","Max’s voice was frighteningly calm. \"What did they do to them there?\"","Caroline closed her eyes.","\"I do not know everything,\" she said. \"But I know the Celestial Thorn Abyss is not merciful. Your mother was likely kept under constant bloodline suppression, and your father was likely used to weaken her will. The second faction would have tried to force her to reveal hidden inheritances of the third faction, secret bloodline methods, and the things she took with her when she left. If she refused, they would hurt him. If he resisted, they would make her watch.\"","Jessica’s eyes turned red.","Nancy’s face became cold.","Max stopped walking.","For a moment, no one dared to breathe too loudly.","Caroline looked at Max, afraid of what expression she would see, but his face was calm. Too calm. It was the kind of calm that no longer needed rage to become terrifying.","After a long silence, Max asked, \"Who led the attack?\"","Caroline’s eyes hardened. \"The public name connected to that night is High Matriarch Selvaria Lareth, one of the core leaders of the second faction and Seraphine’s elder relative. But she was not alone. The extraction formation was prepared by the Bloodline Hall of the second faction, and the ancestor projection belonged to one of the old monsters supporting them from behind. The Divine Son who received your stolen bloodline was hidden afterward, and his name was never spoken openly inside the prison.\"","Max nodded slowly.","Caroline looked at him with worry. \"Max, the second faction is not like the enemies you killed here. Seraphine and Fin were geniuses, but they are still only younger-generation members. The ones behind them are far more terrifying. The Celestial Thorn Abyss is guarded by ancient formations, ancestor seals, royal wardens, and bloodline suppression laws. Even if you know where your parents are, you cannot simply rush there now.\"","Max looked at her.","\"I know.\"","Caroline was startled by how calm his voice was.","Max turned his gaze toward the mist ahead, and a faint golden light flickered deep in his eyes.","\"I am not strong enough yet.\"","That admission was calm, but no one mistook it for weakness.","Max continued, \"But one day, I will be.\"","The cursed mist around him split slightly.","\"When that day comes, I will go to the Celestial Thorn Abyss. I will break every formation, cut every chain, kill every warden, and bring my parents out.\"","His voice did not rise.","He did not shout.","But every word carried an unshakable certainty.","Caroline stared at him, and for some reason, tears filled her eyes again.","Max looked at her and said quietly, \"Until then, tell me everything you know. Names, places, factions, bloodlines, prisons, ancestors, and the Divine Son who carries what they stole from me.\"","His eyes became cold.","\"I will remember all of it.\"","Caroline did not waste any more time and told Max everything she knew, including the names of the second faction’s Divine Son and Divine Daughter.","\"The one who received your stolen bloodline is called Aurelian Lareth,\" Caroline said solemnly. \"Among the second faction, he is known as the Divine Son. They raised him in secret after that night, and most ordinary members of the elf race have never even seen his face, but inside the Elf Prison, the guards spoke of him with worship, as if he was the future ruler who would replace everything your mother once represented.\"","Max’s eyes turned colder, but he did not interrupt.","Caroline continued, \"As for the Divine Daughter, her name is Selene Vaeloria. She is also from the second faction, and from what I know, she carries an extremely pure Heavenly Luminance Royal Bloodline. She and Aurelian were trained together by the Bloodline Hall and the ancestors supporting the second faction. Seraphine and Fin were powerful, but compared to those two, they were still not the true core of the second faction’s younger generation.\"","Max silently repeated the names in his mind.","Aurelian Lareth.","Selene Vaeloria.","One carried the bloodline that might have been stolen from him.","The other was the Divine Daughter raised by the same faction that destroyed his family.","After a long moment, Max nodded slowly.","\"I will remember them.\"","Max was sure from Seraphine and Fin that both these Divine Son and Divine Daughter had participated in the Cosmic Ascension Conference and so he knew they would cross pass sooner or later.","\"Max, everyone has gathered at the entrance of the Witch God Valley.\" Jessica said at the moment. \"We are ready to depart.\""]},{"number":1768,"title":"Chapter 1768: A Cursed Pet?","paragraphs":["\"All right, let us move then,\" Max said to everyone there.","With his words, everyone began moving toward the entrance of Witch God Valley.","Caroline was still injured, but after using her light energy to stabilize her wounds, she refused to slow the group down. Jessica walked beside her with a tense expression, while Nancy stayed near Max, her senses spread outward as much as possible in the cursed mist.","Max took the lead without hesitation, and because of what they had already seen from him, no one questioned his position. Even Caroline, who was older than him and had survived years of imprisonment, hunting, and factional conflict, found herself silently following his pace.","It was not because Max had demanded obedience. It was because his presence created a strange sense of certainty, as if the path ahead would open as long as he walked first.","The cursed mist of Witch God Valley still moved around them like living breath, and from time to time, strange whispers echoed from the twisted trees, but none of them dared to attack recklessly. The roots beneath the ground twitched several times, yet the faint black flame aura still lingering around Max made them shrink back into the wood before fully emerging.","A few shadow beasts watched them from behind broken stone pillars, their eyes glowing green in the fog, but the moment Max’s gaze swept toward them, they vanished into the darkness without making a sound.","After a short while, they met up with Jessica’s group.","The four injured elves were waiting near the place Jessica had left them. Their wounds had been treated roughly, and although they were still pale, they had recovered enough to move.","The moment they saw Caroline returning alive, their eyes filled with relief, and two of them immediately stepped forward as if they wanted to kneel, but Caroline raised her hand and stopped them before they could do so.","\"There is no time for that,\" Caroline said, her voice still weak but steady. \"We are leaving Witch God Valley.\"","The four elves nodded quickly, but their eyes soon moved toward Max with awe and disbelief. Jessica had no need to explain much. The aura around Max, the absence of Lumine’s group, and Caroline’s survival already told them enough.","Their gazes toward him were no longer the gazes one gave a stranger. They looked at him with shock, reverence, and a kind of fragile hope that had not appeared in their eyes for a very long time.","Max did not pay too much attention to those gazes.","\"Stay close,\" he said calmly. \"If anything attacks, do not scatter.\"","Everyone nodded.","With Max still leading, the group continued moving toward the entrance of Witch God Valley. The closer they got to the outer boundary, the more oppressive the atmosphere became. The ground beneath their feet changed from cracked black wood to pale gray bark covered in vein-like green lines, while the cursed mist gathered in thick layers around the path ahead.","The valley seemed unwilling to let them leave. The air grew heavier, the whispers grew sharper, and occasionally, distant cries rang out from behind them as if something hidden deep inside the valley was watching their departure with hatred.","But no matter how strange the surroundings became, Max’s speed did not slow.","Caroline walked beside Jessica and quietly watched Max’s back. She still had countless questions, but she held them back. The truth about Caelira, the Celestial Thorn Abyss, the Divine Son Aurelian Lareth, and the Divine Daughter Selene Vaeloria had already opened wounds that could not be healed in a few words.","For now, survival came first. They needed to leave Witch God Valley, return to a safer region, and prepare for whatever the second faction would do once Seraphine, Fin, and Lumine revived outside with news of what had happened.","Soon, the entrance came into view.","It was a wide gap between two enormous curved branches, and beyond it lay the downward path leading along the Witch God Tree toward the lower region. From there, they could eventually return to the area below the tree, where Max had already expected the second faction to prepare a welcome.","However, just as they were about to step out of the valley, everyone stopped.","Something was blocking the entrance.","It was a huge spherical creature floating silently in the air.","Its entire body looked like a monstrous eye, round and swollen, covered in dark red veins that pulsed across its surface like living roots. Around the main body were several smaller tendrils that moved slowly in the mist, each one ending in a tiny blinking eye.","But the most terrifying part was the enormous eye at the center of the creature.","That eye was wide open, blood-red and black, with a vertical pupil that seemed to contain a deep abyss of deathly light. It did not breathe. It did not roar. It only floated at the entrance, watching the path like a guardian left behind by Witch God Valley itself.","Jessica’s face changed. \"What is that?\"","Caroline’s expression became grim. \"A cursed pet of the witch who once ruled this world. I have only heard of them. I did not expect one to appear at the entrance.\"","The moment she spoke, the huge spherical eye shifted.","Its vertical pupil locked onto them.","Max’s Dimensional Sovereign Body reacted first.","Before the others could even feel danger, before Jessica could raise her sword, before Nancy could draw her weapon, before Caroline could form a light barrier, Max’s spatial senses screamed inside him. The space in front of the giant eye twisted, compressed, and focused into a single deadly point.","The attack had not yet been released, but Max had already seen its path. It was aimed directly at the center of their group, and among those standing in that line, Jessica was the first one it would strike.","\"Move!\" Max shouted.","But his voice was slower than the eye’s attack.","A beam of deadly red light shot out from the massive pupil.","It was too fast.","To the others, it looked as if the world flashed red for an instant. They could not follow its movement. They could not react. They could not even understand that an attack had already been launched. Only Max, through the perception of his Dimensional Sovereign Body, saw the beam cutting through space toward Jessica with terrifying speed.","Dragonheart appeared in his hand.","Max stepped in front of Jessica and swung the sword horizontally."]},{"number":1769,"title":"Chapter 1769: Abyssal Witch Eye!","paragraphs":["Boom!","The red beam crashed into Dragonheart.","The impact was horrifying.","A violent shockwave exploded outward, tearing the cursed mist apart and blasting Jessica, Caroline, Nancy, and the other elves backward several steps. The ground beneath Max shattered instantly, cracks spreading in all directions across the pale bark like broken glass.","His arms trembled under the force of the beam, and even though Dragonheart blocked the attack, the power behind it did not disappear. It drove into him like a collapsing mountain.","For the first time in front of them, Max was blasted away.","His body flew backward violently, smashing through a broken stone pillar and dragging a long scar across the wooden ground before he finally twisted in midair, stabbed Dragonheart into the surface beneath him, and forced himself to stop. Even then, the remaining force pushed him several more meters before the sword carved a deep trench into the ground.","The battlefield fell into stunned silence.","Jessica stared at the place where she had been standing a moment ago, her face completely pale. If Max had not moved, that red beam would have pierced through her before she even realized she was under attack.","Nancy’s eyes widened. \"Max!\"","Caroline’s expression changed sharply. \"That attack pushed him back?\"","The four third faction elves were horrified.","They had just seen Max crush Arnold with one finger, kill Lumine’s group with his sword art, and destroy Seraphine and Fin even after they released the full strength of their Pseudo Cosmic Paths.","In their minds, Max had already become an almost unstoppable existence among the younger generation. Yet now, this strange spherical eye creature had fired a single beam, and just by blocking it, Max had been blasted away.","That alone showed how terrifying the beam of red light was.","Max slowly rose from the broken ground.","His fingers tightened around Dragonheart, and a thin trail of smoke rose from the sword’s blade where the red beam had struck. His arms were slightly numb, and his eyes narrowed as he looked toward the floating eye creature blocking the entrance.","\"Interesting,\" Max said softly.","The huge eye creature floated silently in the mist.","Its central pupil began glowing red again.","Caroline’s face turned grave. \"Everyone, get behind him!\"","Jessica and the others immediately moved back, no longer daring to stand near the creature’s line of sight.","Max stepped forward again, Dragonheart held in his hand, his gaze locked onto the massive blood-red pupil.","\"So,\" he said calmly, \"you are the thing guarding the way out.\"","\"Max, do not take that thing lightly.\"","Caroline’s voice suddenly sounded from behind him, and although she was trying to remain calm, the seriousness in her tone made everyone’s expression change. She stared at the huge spherical eye creature floating at the entrance of Witch God Valley, and for the first time since Seraphine and Fin had fallen, clear fear appeared in her eyes.","It was not the fear of someone who had lost her courage, but the fear of someone who recognized a nightmare from old legends and understood just how dangerous it truly was.","Jessica turned toward her quickly. \"Lady Caroline, you know what that creature is?\"","Caroline nodded slowly, her face pale. \"I have never seen it before with my own eyes, but I have heard of it. In the oldest records of the third faction, there were mentions of a cursed guardian that slept inside Witch God Valley. It was said that when the Witch God Tree was still ruled by the ancient Witch who once controlled this world, she raised a pet with the power to see through space, curse souls, and destroy anything that tried to escape her domain.\"","Nancy’s expression changed. \"The Witch’s cursed pet?\"","\"Yes,\" Caroline said, her eyes still fixed on the giant eye. \"That thing must be the guardian of Witch God Valley. It is not a normal cursed beast. It is something left behind by the Witch herself.\"","The moment those words were spoken, the air around the group became heavier.","The Witch who once ruled this world was not an ordinary existence. Even though countless years had passed and only broken legends remained, everything inside Witch God Valley still carried traces of her power.","The cursed roots, the living mist, the ancient ruins, the twisted trees, and even the strange pressure lingering in the valley all proved that the Witch had once reached a terrifying level. If this eye creature had truly been her pet and guardian, then it was not something they could judge by ordinary cultivation realms.","Caroline continued in a low voice, \"The records called it the Abyssal Witch Eye. It was said to be born from the Witch’s own cursed blood and fed with the souls of those who betrayed her. Its eye can release a light that does not simply burn the body. It can pierce through space, lock onto life force, and carry a curse that follows the target even after the first strike misses. If you had not blocked that beam just now, Jessica might not have only died once. The curse could have damaged her remaining lives too.\"","Jessica’s face turned completely pale.","The four third faction elves behind her also took several steps back, their eyes filled with horror as they looked at the huge floating eye.","Nancy’s hand tightened around her sword. \"No wonder the attack was so fast. It did not move like ordinary light. It cut through the distance itself.\"","Caroline nodded. \"Exactly. That is why I said not to take it lightly. Its attacks are not something most people can dodge after seeing them. By the time the eye opens and the beam is visible, it is already too late.\"","Max looked at the Abyssal Witch Eye silently.","The creature floated at the entrance without moving, but the red veins across its spherical body pulsed faster than before. Its huge central pupil remained locked onto Max, as if it had recognized him as the greatest threat among the group.","Smaller eyes at the ends of its tendrils blinked one after another, and every blink released faint waves of cursed perception that swept across the battlefield, measuring the prey before it.","Caroline stepped closer despite her injuries. \"Max, listen to me. That thing is guarding the exit. It may not chase us deep into the valley, but it will not let us leave easily. The Witch God Valley is not just a dangerous place. It is a cage. That creature is likely one of the reasons so many people enter and never return.\"","Max’s eyes narrowed slightly. \"So we cannot avoid it.\"","\"No,\" Caroline said. \"At least, not if we want to leave through this entrance.\"","The Abyssal Witch Eye’s central pupil began glowing again.","This time, the red light gathered more slowly, but the pressure was even more terrifying than before. The space in front of it compressed inward, and the cursed mist around the entrance was pulled toward the pupil like smoke being swallowed by a vortex.","Everyone felt their skin tighten, and Jessica instinctively moved behind Max, still shaken by how close she had come to being struck earlier.","Caroline’s voice became urgent. \"Max, be careful. That first attack may not have been its full power.\""]},{"number":1770,"title":"Chapter 1770: Terrifying Cursed Pet!","paragraphs":["Max slowly lifted Dragonheart.","His expression remained calm, but his grip on the sword tightened slightly.","\"I know.\"","The red light in the Abyssal Witch Eye became brighter.","The ground beneath everyone began to tremble.","Caroline looked at Max’s back and said again, her voice filled with warning, \"Do not fight it like a normal enemy. This thing belonged to the Witch who once ruled this world. If it still carries even a fragment of her cursed authority, then one mistake could be fatal.\"","Max did not look back.","A faint golden light began to gather around his body, and his Dimensional Sovereign Body spread its senses through the space before him, watching every distortion around the eye, every movement of its tendrils, and every hidden path where its attack might appear.","\"Everyone stay behind me,\" Max said calmly.","The Abyssal Witch Eye’s pupil finally opened wider.","The red beam was about to fire again.","Max’s eyes became sharp.","\"I will cut a path out.\"","The Abyssal Witch Eye’s huge central pupil widened, and the red light gathering inside it became even more intense than before.","This time, the creature did not release its attack immediately. The veins across its spherical body pulsed rapidly, and the smaller eyes at the ends of its tendrils all turned toward Max at once, blinking in a strange rhythm as if they were helping the main eye lock onto his position through space itself.","The cursed mist near the entrance was dragged toward the pupil and swallowed by the red glow, while the surrounding air twisted so violently that Jessica and the others felt their vision bend for a moment.","The first beam had already blasted Max away even though he had blocked it with Dragonheart, and now, as the second beam gathered, everyone could clearly feel that this attack would be stronger.","Caroline’s face turned pale. \"Max, it is charging more power than before.\"","Max did not answer.","His eyes remained fixed on the giant eye. The Dimensional Sovereign Body spread his perception through the distorted space around the monster, and he could clearly see the path of the beam before it was even fired.","The creature was not simply aiming at him this time. The red light was spreading across several possible spatial paths, meaning that even if Max dodged, the beam could bend its route and strike the people behind him. If he wanted to protect Caroline, Jessica, Nancy, and the other third faction elves, then he could not simply avoid the attack.","He had to block it head-on.","Max slowly exhaled.","Then his body changed.","The first Divine Vein opened.","Vein of Origin.","A deep sound echoed from within Max’s body, like the first heartbeat of an ancient beast waking from the depth of creation. His foundation surged, his aura became heavier, and the power hidden in his flesh began to stabilize and expand as if every part of his body had been strengthened from its root. The ground beneath his feet trembled as invisible force spread through him.","The second Divine Vein opened.","Vein of Vitality.","A powerful life force erupted through his body, making his blood roar like a river of molten gold. His muscles tightened, his bones seemed to become denser, and the numbness left in his arms from blocking the first beam vanished in an instant. His entire body pulsed with vitality so overwhelming that even the cursed energy of Witch God Valley was forced away from him.","The third Divine Vein opened.","Vein of Strength.","Boom!","The wooden ground beneath Max’s feet shattered violently. Cracks spread in all directions, and the branch path at the entrance of Witch God Valley sank slightly beneath the sudden pressure released by his body. His physical strength rose to a terrifying level, and the air around his arms distorted as if his flesh alone had become capable of bearing the weight of mountains.","The fourth Divine Vein opened.","Vein of Speed.","Max’s figure blurred for a fraction of a second, not because he moved, but because the power inside his body had become too fast and too violent for the air around him to remain stable.","His senses sharpened, his reaction speed soared, and the red beam that had once seemed nearly impossible for the others to perceive now appeared completely clear within his eyes. Every ripple of space, every pulse of cursed light, and every possible route of the attack became visible to him.","Behind him, Nancy’s eyes widened.","\"This is...\" she whispered.","Jessica felt her breath stop. She had already seen Max display monstrous sword power, but this was different. This was not his Pseudo Cosmic Path. This was not his Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline.","This was pure physical strength, a terrifying body power that seemed to rise from the deepest foundation of his being. Caroline also stared at him in shock, because for a brief moment, she felt as if the person standing before the Abyssal Witch Eye was no longer simply her sister’s son, but a young dragon in human form preparing to tear apart the curse of the valley with his own hands.","The Abyssal Witch Eye fired.","A second beam of deadly red light burst from its pupil.","It was faster than the first.","Stronger than the first.","The beam tore through space with a sharp scream, and the path between the eye and Max collapsed into a burning red line. Jessica and the others could not follow it at all. They only saw the eye flash, and by the time they realized the attack had been launched, Max had already moved.","Dragonheart rose.","Max stepped forward instead of retreating.","The beam crashed into his sword.","BOOM!","The impact shook the entire entrance of Witch God Valley.","The branch path beneath him exploded into countless cracks, and waves of red light swept outward like a storm, forcing Caroline, Nancy, Jessica, and the others to retreat despite standing behind him.","However, this time, Max was not blasted away. His feet dug into the shattered ground, his arms held Dragonheart steady, and the power of his first four Divine Veins roared through his body like four divine furnaces burning at once.","The beam pushed against him.","Max pushed back.","The Abyssal Witch Eye’s huge pupil trembled, and the red light became even more violent, but Max’s body did not bend. The Vein of Origin stabilized his foundation. The Vein of Vitality kept his body from breaking under the curse pressure.","The Vein of Strength gave him the force to resist the beam head-on. The Vein of Speed allowed him to see every shift in the attack and adjust his sword at the perfect angle.","Dragonheart hummed sharply.","Max’s eyes became cold.","\"You are strong,\" he said softly. \"But not strong enough.\"","The Severing Sword Concept gathered along Dragonheart.","Then Max took another step forward.","The red beam, which had been pressing against his sword like a river of death, suddenly split at the center. A thin golden-black line appeared where Dragonheart touched it, and that line stretched forward through the beam as Max pushed his sword out.","The beam screamed, distorted, and tried to repair itself, but the Severing Sword Concept continued cutting through it, dividing the deadly light into two streams that flew past Max’s sides and blasted into the distant cursed trees behind him.","The trees exploded.","The ground burned.","But Max kept moving forward.","One step.","Then another.","The beam was being cut apart.","The Abyssal Witch Eye’s tendrils thrashed wildly as if it had finally sensed danger. The smaller eyes blinked faster and faster, releasing waves of curse power into the main pupil, but Max’s strength had risen too far after opening four Divine Veins.","He pushed through the beam with terrifying force, Dragonheart cutting the red light apart inch by inch until the distance between him and the giant eye rapidly shrank."]},{"number":1771,"title":"Chapter 1771: A Small Eye","paragraphs":["Caroline stared at him in disbelief. \"He is forcing his way through the beam.\"","The Abyssal Witch Eye released a silent pulse of fear.","Its pupil contracted.","But it was too late.","Max suddenly disappeared.","The Vein of Speed erupted, and his figure crossed the remaining distance in an instant. He appeared directly before the huge central eye, Dragonheart raised above his head, the first four Divine Veins burning through his body, and the Severing Sword Concept condensed to the edge of his blade.","The Abyssal Witch Eye tried to fire again at point-blank range.","Max slashed first.","The sword descended.","A brilliant line cut through the massive pupil.","The red light inside the eye split apart, the cursed veins across its spherical body burst one after another, and the entire creature trembled violently as the slash continued downward, severing its body from top to bottom.","The smaller eyes at the ends of its tendrils exploded into red mist, and the huge spherical body released a soundless scream that made the air tremble.","Then the Abyssal Witch Eye split in two.","For a moment, its two halves floated on either side of Max, still glowing with cursed red light.","Then they began to dissolve.","The monster’s body broke apart into dark ash, red sparks, and fragments of cursed energy that scattered into the air before being swallowed by the rules of the Cosmic Ascension Conference. A massive stream of Killing Points emerged from the remains, far brighter and denser than the fragments left by ordinary enemies, and surged toward Max.","Max landed softly at the entrance of Witch God Valley.","The first four Divine Veins slowly dimmed, but the overwhelming physical pressure around him did not disappear immediately. Cracks covered the ground beneath his feet, and Dragonheart remained lowered in his hand, its blade still releasing faint smoke from having cut through the deadly beam.","Behind him, Caroline, Jessica, Nancy, and the others stood frozen.","The guardian of Witch God Valley, the cursed pet of the ancient Witch, the Abyssal Witch Eye that had nearly killed Jessica with one beam and blasted Max away with its first attack, had been cut down by Max after he opened only four Divine Veins.","Max looked at the fading remains of the eye creature, then glanced toward the path beyond the entrance.","\"Now,\" he said calmly, \"we can leave.\"","Just as the Abyssal Witch Eye was destroyed and everyone felt a wave of relief rise in their hearts, the atmosphere at the entrance of Witch God Valley changed once again.","Jessica let out a long breath and looked at Max with eyes full of shock and admiration, while the other third faction elves could barely hide the joy on their faces after seeing the guardian of the valley finally fall.","Even Caroline, whose expression had remained heavy for so long, allowed a trace of relief to appear in her eyes. For a brief moment, it felt as if the worst part was already over. The path ahead was finally open, and with Max standing at the front, the group truly believed they could leave the cursed valley.","But just when everyone was preparing to move, a strange red-black glimmer suddenly flickered among the scattered remains of the Abyssal Witch Eye.","Max noticed it first.","His Dimensional Sovereign Body immediately sensed something subtle and sinister moving through space, but before he could react, that glimmer shot out from the dissolving ashes of the giant eye creature and appeared right beside him.","In the next instant, a small eye, almost identical in appearance to the Abyssal Witch Eye but only the size of Max’s fist, floated in the air for a brief moment before sticking itself directly onto Max’s shoulder like a living parasite.","The small eye was blood-red and black, with a vertical pupil that blinked slowly, and thin dark veins spread outward from its base the moment it attached itself to him.","It did not release an overwhelming aura like the giant guardian had, yet the sight of it was far more unsettling because of how unnatural and intimate it looked, as if the curse of the Witch itself had chosen Max as its new host.","Max’s brows furrowed instantly.","He reached out with one hand and tried to tear it off.","But the moment his fingers touched the small eye, he felt a strange resistance, as if it was not truly attached to his flesh, but to something deeper. It looked like it was sitting on his shoulder, yet when he tried to grab it, the eye blurred strangely and remained exactly where it was, neither falling away nor allowing itself to be held properly.","Jessica’s expression changed. \"What is that?\"","Nancy’s face became serious. \"It came from the remains of the guardian.\"","Max’s eyes turned colder. Without hesitation, he tried again. This time he used far more force, his fingers tightening with enough strength to crush stone and metal alike, but no matter how much pressure he applied, the small eye did not break. It remained attached to him, blinking slowly, as if mocking his effort.","\"This thing is tough.\" Max’s expression darkened.","Then he activated the first four Divine Veins again.","The Vein of Origin opened first, anchoring his body with terrifying stability. The Vein of Vitality followed, flooding his flesh and blood with violent life force. The Vein of Strength awakened next, causing the ground beneath his feet to crack once again, while the Vein of Speed sharpened his reactions and made the surrounding air tremble faintly.","The moment all four Divine Veins were open, Max’s physical power rose to a terrifying level once more.","Caroline and the others immediately stepped back.","Even though he was only focusing his strength into one hand, the pressure around him was still enormous. The bark beneath his feet splintered, the air around his arm distorted visibly, and the muscles beneath his sleeve tightened with explosive force as if a dragon’s body had been compressed into human shape. Max then placed his hand over the small eye and tried to crush it directly."]},{"number":1772,"title":"Chapter 1772: A True Curse!","paragraphs":["A violent sound rang out.","The force he released was enough to shatter boulders and crush the bodies of powerful enemies, yet the small eye did not break.","Not even a crack appeared on it.","Instead, it remained there in the same place, blinking calmly while Max’s crushing grip caused the space around it to twist.","Jessica stared in disbelief. \"It did not break?\"","Nancy’s eyes narrowed. \"It is not a normal object.\"","Max’s face turned completely cold.","The first failure did not make him stop. It only made him more serious.","Max looked at the small eye in his hand and muttered. \"Let’s see how tough this eye truly is...\"","As he said those words, he released his grip for a brief moment, then the power in his body surged to an even more frightening degree.","This time, in addition to the first four Divine Veins, he also unleashed the full power of his five thousand Draconic Essences.","Boom!","A monstrous force erupted from Max’s body.","Golden-black draconic power burst outward like a storm awakening from the deepest abyss. The bark-covered ground around him collapsed into a web of cracks. The cursed mist in the surrounding area was blasted apart at once, and the air became so heavy that Jessica and the others felt their breathing turn difficult.","Max’s aura at this moment was far more devastating than before. The four Divine Veins had already pushed his physical strength to a shocking level, but with the addition of five thousand Draconic Essences, that strength rose into a completely different realm.","His body looked as though it was wrapped in the pressure of an ancient dragon.","His blood roared.","His bones hummed.","The power condensed into his arm alone was enough to make everyone present feel a chill run down their spine.","Even Caroline, who had seen Max destroy Seraphine, Fin, and the Abyssal Witch Eye, could not help but feel shaken at this moment. If Max had used this level of force against an ordinary enemy, that enemy would likely have been obliterated before even understanding what had struck them.","Max’s hand closed around the small eye again.","This time, the force he released was devastating.","The sound of compression shook the area, and the bark beneath him sank lower under the pressure. The surrounding air folded inward toward his fist, and the violent force generated by his grip caused faint cracks to appear in space itself.","The mixture of the four Divine Veins and five thousand Draconic Essences had brought his raw physical strength to an absurd level, one so terrifying that even Nancy felt that if she stood too close, she might be injured by the pressure alone.","Yet even then, the small eye did not break.","It did not shatter.","It simply remained attached to him, unchanged, its tiny vertical pupil staring outward with a calm and eerie stillness that made it look less like a creature and more like a curse given shape.","Max slowly loosened his grip.","For the first time since the small eye had attached itself to him, a real frown appeared on his face.","He had even expected it to possess some strange defensive property because of its connection to the Abyssal Witch Eye. But to endure the full force of four Divine Veins and five thousand Draconic Essences without suffering the slightest damage was something else entirely.","Caroline looked at the small eye carefully, and the relief that had briefly appeared on her face vanished completely.","Her expression became solemn and uneasy.","\"Max,\" she said slowly, \"stop for a moment.\"","Max turned toward her.","Caroline stepped closer, though she still kept a cautious distance from the attached eye. Her eyes remained fixed on the small blood-red pupil, and the more she observed it, the more troubled she looked.","\"This may not be something you can destroy with brute force,\" she said quietly.","Jessica frowned. \"What do you mean?\"","Caroline took a slow breath. \"I think this may be some sort of the Witch’s curse.\"","The words made everyone’s expression change.","Nancy’s eyes sharpened. \"A curse?\"","Caroline nodded. \"The giant guardian was not just a beast. It was the cursed pet of the Witch who once ruled this world. If that creature was truly linked to her authority, then this small eye might not be a living remnant in the normal sense. It could be a curse mark, a tracking brand, or a binding seal left behind by the Witch herself. That would explain why it cannot be crushed even with such overwhelming force. You are not trying to destroy ordinary flesh. You are trying to crush a curse attached to your existence.\"","Max looked at the eye again, his expression turning darker.","The little eye blinked once, slowly and silently, as if it was confirming Caroline’s words.","Caroline continued in a grim tone, \"If I am right, then destroying the guardian may have triggered this. Perhaps it marks the one who killed it. Perhaps it allows the deeper curses of Witch God Valley to recognize you. Or perhaps it is something even worse.\"","Jessica swallowed hard. \"Worse?\"","Caroline nodded faintly. \"The Witch’s curses were feared for a reason. Some mark the body. Some cling to the soul. Some make the cursed person easier to find, easier to track, or easier to drag into illusion and death. We cannot treat this lightly.\"","For a moment, silence fell over the entrance of Witch God Valley.","Max stood there with the small eye still attached to him, while the remnants of his power slowly settled back down. The first four Divine Veins dimmed, and the raging pressure of his five thousand Draconic Essences receded, yet the little eye remained exactly where it was, unchanged and eerily calm.","Max’s eyes narrowed.","\"So it is a curse.\"","Caroline gave a slow nod. \"Most likely.\"","Max looked toward the path beyond the entrance, then back at the eye attached to him.","His voice turned calm again, though the coldness in it made everyone still their breath.","\"Fine,\" he said. \"If it is a curse, then we will deal with it later.\"","He then looked at Caroline.","\"But first, we leave this place.\"","The others nodded, though the unease in their eyes remained."]},{"number":1773,"title":"Chapter 1773: Lunarian Kingdom!","paragraphs":["\"Let us go,\" Max said as he began to move despite the little eye still stuck to his left shoulder.","The small cursed eye blinked slowly as it shifted against him, and every now and then, its tiny red-black pupil moved as if studying the surroundings.","Sometimes it stayed on his shoulder. Sometimes it slid slightly across his upper arm. Sometimes it floated just a hair’s breadth away from his body before attaching itself again, as if it was neither fully physical nor fully illusory.","The sight was disturbing to everyone else, but Max did not pay it much attention after realizing that brute force could not destroy it for now. As long as this thing did not restrict his movement or interfere in his battles, he could not care less about it at the moment.","With that, the group once again began moving.","Max walked at the front, Dragonheart resting in his hand, while Caroline, Jessica, Nancy, and the other third faction elves followed closely behind him.","The path out of Witch God Valley was still filled with cursed mist, but after the death of the Abyssal Witch Eye, the pressure near the entrance had clearly weakened. The strange whispers in the air were still there, the black grass still moved without wind, and the twisted trees still seemed to watch them from both sides, but nothing dared to stop them openly.","Perhaps the death of the guardian had shaken the valley. Perhaps the little eye attached to Max had marked him in a way that made the other cursed things hesitate. Whatever the reason, their path became strangely smooth.","In no time, they arrived near the edge of the Witch God Tree.","The vast treetop world spread behind them like a cursed kingdom above the clouds, while ahead of them was the massive trunk descending into the lower sky. Countless enormous branches extended outward like mountain ridges, and thick clouds rolled beneath them, hiding the lower parts of the tree from sight.","From this height, the world below looked distant and unreal, and the enormous scale of the Witch God Tree became even more shocking. Its trunk fell through the clouds like a pillar holding up the heavens, while glowing veins within its bark pulsed faintly, as though the whole ancient tree was alive and watching their departure.","Max stopped at the edge and looked downward.","His Dimensional Sovereign Body spread its senses along the space below, but because the Witch God Tree was too large and covered in too many cursed distortions, he could not clearly see everything waiting near the bottom.","Still, the feeling in his heart told him that the path ahead would not be peaceful. Seraphine, Fin, Lumine, and the others had all been killed, but they still had lives left.","Once they revived outside, the second faction would quickly understand that Caroline had been rescued and that Max was involved. If those people were not stupid, then they would not let them leave so easily.","Max turned back and looked at everyone.","\"Stay cautious,\" he said calmly.","Caroline’s expression became serious. \"You think the second faction has people waiting below?\"","\"I do,\" Max said. \"They already sent Seraphine, Fin, Lumine, and others to hunt you. Since those people failed, they will either prepare an ambush or gather more people near the bottom of the Witch God Tree. Once we reach below, there is a good chance they will attack us immediately.\"","Jessica clenched her sword. \"Then we should descend carefully.\"","Max nodded. \"Do not scatter. If the second faction attacks, stay behind me unless I tell you otherwise. Their target will likely be Caroline first, but after what happened inside the valley, they will also come for me.\"","One of the injured third faction elves said with hesitation, \"Lord Max, if they have too many people...\"","Max looked at him.","The elf immediately stopped speaking.","Max’s expression remained calm, but his eyes carried a cold certainty. \"Numbers only matter when they can hurt me.\"","No one spoke after that.","Caroline looked at Max’s back, and although she wanted to remind him not to underestimate the second faction, the words did not come out. She had seen him kill Seraphine and Fin. She had seen him cut down the guardian of Witch God Valley. She had seen the power of his Divine Veins, Draconic Essences, sword path, and bloodline.","At this point, warning him like he was an ordinary young genius felt meaningless. Max understood danger, but he did not fear it. That was the difference.","Nancy moved closer to him and said quietly, \"If Princess Rosaline intercepted the news, she may also come here.\"","Max glanced at her. \"Will she be an enemy?\"","Nancy hesitated for a moment. \"I do not know. She is a princess of the Lunarian Kingdom ruling a good chunk of many star realms and her force is also considered one of the strongest 1st rate forces standing on equal terms with Sword God Palace and War God Palace.\"","She added. \"Since you have killed his men before coming here, there might be a chance she would intercept you.\"","Max looked down at the clouds below. \"Then she can speak after I deal with the ones trying to stop us.\"","The little cursed eye on his shoulder blinked once, its red-black pupil rolling slightly as if it had heard him.","Max ignored it.","\"Let us descend.\"","The moment he said that, he stepped off the edge of the treetop and began flying downward along the massive trunk of the Witch God Tree. Golden light flickered faintly around his body, not enough to reveal his full bloodline power, but enough to cut through the cursed wind rushing upward from below.","Nancy followed closely behind him, while Caroline, Jessica, and the remaining third faction elves moved in formation, keeping themselves within the range Max had indicated.","The descent began.","The clouds swallowed them almost immediately.","Cold mist rushed past their bodies, and the enormous bark of the Witch God Tree blurred beside them as they flew downward. Strange creatures hidden in the holes of the trunk watched them pass, but none dared to attack.","Some roots twitched from the bark as if tempted to lash out, but the moment Max’s gaze swept over them, they withdrew silently. The group continued falling through layer after layer of clouds, moving from the cursed upper world toward the lower regions of the Eternal Hourglass."]},{"number":1774,"title":"Chapter 1774: Surrounded - 1","paragraphs":["In no time, Max and the others arrived at the base of the Witch God Tree.","However, just when they reached the base, a golden sword flashed toward them out of nowhere.","The sword was not held by anyone. It appeared from the air itself, formed from condensed golden light, and it moved so quickly that several of the injured third faction elves did not even realize they were being attacked until the light had already crossed half the distance. Its target was not Max.","It was Caroline. The blade carried a sharp bloodline-suppressing force, and the moment it appeared, Caroline’s Heavenly Luminance Royal Bloodline trembled faintly, clearly reacting to the power hidden within the attack.","Max immediately moved forward and slashed Dragonheart at the incoming golden sword.","Boom!","The golden sword shattered into countless fragments of light, and the impact spread across the base of the Witch God Tree like a golden storm. The surrounding dust and dead leaves were swept away, the huge roots beneath their feet trembled, and several nearby stone ridges were sliced open by the stray sword light.","Max stood in front of everyone with Dragonheart lowered slightly in his hand, but his eyes had already become cold because the scene before them was much worse than they had imagined.","They were surrounded.","All around the base of the Witch God Tree, dozens upon dozens of elves stood in formation, each one wearing armor marked with the symbol of the second faction. Some stood on the giant roots spreading across the ground, some floated in the air with wings of light behind them, and some stood silently in the gaps between the ancient stones surrounding the tree’s base.","Their auras were far stronger than the ordinary hunters Max had encountered before, and unlike Lumine’s group, these elves had clearly come prepared. Light formations were already active beneath their feet, golden chains hovered in the air around the battlefield, and several bloodline-suppressing talismans had been placed around the base of the tree, forming a wide sealed region that trapped Max’s group inside.","Seraphine and Fin stood among them.","Both of them had revived after being killed in Witch God Valley, but their faces were no longer arrogant like before. Seraphine’s expression was icy, yet there was still a trace of fear hidden deep in her eyes when she looked at Max.","Fin’s usual mocking smile had disappeared completely, and although he still held his sword, his grip was tighter than before, as if his hand remembered the feeling of being cut down by Max’s Emotion Severing Path.","Their hatred was obvious, but so was their caution. They had already learned that Max was not someone they could handle alone.","At the center of the second faction formation stood a golden-haired elf woman.","The moment Caroline saw her, her face changed.","\"Max,\" Caroline said in a low and tense voice, \"be careful. The elf woman with golden hair standing at the center is Selene Vaeloria, the Divine Daughter of the second faction.\"","Max’s eyes shifted toward the golden-haired elf woman.","Selene Vaeloria truly looked different from the others.","Her golden hair flowed down her back like liquid sunlight, and her eyes were a clear, sacred gold that carried both nobility and coldness. She wore a white-gold battle dress covered in delicate divine patterns, and behind her floated a faint halo of Heavenly Luminance power.","Compared to Seraphine’s bloodline aura, Selene’s was far purer and more oppressive. The light around her did not simply shine. It seemed to command the surrounding radiance to kneel, and every second faction elf around her looked at her with unmistakable reverence.","She looked at Max calmly.","\"So you are Max Morgan,\" Selene said, her voice soft but filled with authority. \"The human who killed Seraphine, Fin, Lumine, and many others of my faction.\"","Max did not answer immediately.","The small cursed eye on his left shoulder blinked once, slowly turning its pupil toward Selene, while Dragonheart gave out a faint hum in his hand. Max noticed Selene’s Heavenly Luminance aura and felt something strange inside his bloodline stir faintly, but the reaction was not one of kinship. It was closer to disgust, as if his bloodline itself rejected the presence of the second faction’s divine radiance.","Caroline stepped closer to Max and whispered, \"She is dangerous. Seraphine and Fin are powerful, but Selene is one of the true cores of the second faction’s younger generation. She was trained directly by the Bloodline Hall and the ancestors.\"","Jessica’s face was pale as she looked at Selene. \"I did not think they would send the Divine Daughter herself.\"","Selene’s gaze moved from Max to Caroline, and a faint smile appeared on her lips. \"Caroline, you truly are troublesome. Even after hiding inside Witch God Valley, you still managed to come out alive. I suppose I should thank this human for bringing you out instead of forcing us to enter that cursed place again.\"","Caroline’s eyes turned cold. \"You should have stayed away.\"","Selene smiled lightly. \"And allow you to escape? No. The remnants of Caelira’s faction belong in the Elf Prison, and you, more than anyone else, should return there.\"","The words made the third faction elves behind Caroline tremble with anger.","Max’s gaze became colder, but before he could speak, Nancy suddenly looked toward the other side of the battlefield.","\"There are others here,\" she said quietly.","Max turned slightly.","On the opposite side of the base, away from the second faction formation, another group of people stood gathered beneath the shadow of the Witch God Tree. They were not part of the second faction.","Their armor and robes were different, more refined, and bore the emblem of the Lunarian Kingdom, one of the strongest first-rate forces in the Divine Realm. At their front stood Princess Rosaline, her white and rose-gold gown moving gently in the wind, her golden-pink hair shining faintly beneath the dim light of the Eternal Hourglass.","The young man who had stopped the Sword God Palace disciples earlier stood beside her, along with several powerful Lunarian experts and other followers."]},{"number":1775,"title":"Chapter 1775: Surrounded - 2","paragraphs":["Princess Rosaline’s gaze was fixed on Max.","She did not look surprised to see him. It was clear that she had already expected him to come out from the Witch God Tree. Her expression was thoughtful, and when her eyes moved briefly to the small cursed eye attached to his shoulder, a strange light flashed across her face.","Then her gaze shifted to Selene and the second faction elves, and her expression became slightly colder.","\"So the Lunarian Kingdom is here too,\" Caroline said, her voice heavy.","Jessica clenched her sword. \"Princess Rosaline.\"","Max glanced at Nancy. \"Is that her?\"","Nancy nodded. \"Yes. Princess Rosaline of the Lunarian Kingdom.\"","For a moment, the base of the Witch God Tree became silent in a suffocating way.","Max’s group stood in the middle.","On one side was Selene Vaeloria, the Divine Daughter of the second faction, accompanied by Seraphine, Fin, and a large number of second faction elites.","On the other side was Princess Rosaline of the Lunarian Kingdom, watching the situation with her own group.","The cursed trunk of the Witch God Tree towered behind them like a dark pillar vanishing into the clouds, while the huge roots beneath their feet formed a natural battlefield. The air was tense enough to feel like it might crack at any moment. Everyone knew that the smallest movement could turn this place into a battlefield between multiple forces.","Selene looked toward Rosaline and smiled faintly. \"Princess Rosaline, are you here to interfere?\"","Rosaline’s expression remained calm. \"I am here to observe.\"","Seraphine sneered. \"Observe? This human killed members of the second faction and helped fugitives of the Elf Prison escape. There is nothing to observe. He should be captured, and Caroline should be returned to where she belongs.\"","Rosaline’s eyes narrowed slightly. \"The Lunarian Kingdom doesn’t care what your elf faction does or doesn’t.\"","The second faction elves immediately stirred.","Selene raised one hand, and they went silent.","Then she looked at Max again.","\"You are right.\" Selene said with a smile. \"You don’t care and let it be like this.\"","She then turned to Max. \"What about you human boy?\"","Max looked at her calmly. \"You will either run away like a coward or die by my sword. That is the only outcome I can see here.\"","\"Your arrogance knows no bounds.\" Selene sneered hearing Max. \"To make me run away? You sure dream a lot.\"","\"Dream?\" Max also sneered as his Dragonheart trembled a little in his hands. \"Oh, believe me when I say out of all the opponents I have killed, you will be one of the few I would enjoy killing the most.\"","Selene’s eyes moved to Dragonheart, then to the little cursed eye on his shoulder, and finally back to his face.","\"You carry many interesting things,\" she said. \"The Sword of the Sword Sovereign, a strange curse mark from Witch God Valley, and perhaps... something else.\"","The last words carried a deeper meaning.","Max understood what she was hinting at.","Caroline’s face turned tense. She knew that if Selene sensed Max’s Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline, the situation could become even worse.","Max, however, did not look nervous at all.","He simply stepped forward.","The moment he moved, Seraphine and Fin both stiffened instinctively, and several second faction elves raised their weapons at once.","Max’s gaze swept across them, then stopped on Selene.","\"You brought a lot of people,\" he said calmly.","Selene smiled. \"Enough to stop you.\"","Max’s smile became colder.","\"Are you sure?\"","Selene sneered.","Just as she was about to release her power, her eyes suddenly shifted toward a certain direction, and the golden halo behind her trembled faintly as if it had sensed something approaching from the shadows.","Almost at the same time, Max also turned his head in that direction. His Dimensional Sovereign Body had already felt them long before they chose to reveal themselves. Three auras were hiding at the edge of the battlefield, but their attempt at concealment was almost laughable in Max’s eyes, because each of them carried a presence so strong and distinct that they appeared in his perception like three blazing suns standing in the dark.","\"Just reveal yourselves,\" Max said calmly, his voice spreading across the base of the Witch God Tree. \"The auras of you three are bright as suns in the dark. There is no use hiding.\"","The moment Max’s words fell, the air in that direction rippled.","A soft laugh sounded first.","It was gentle, elegant, and strangely eerie, as if a beautiful woman was laughing from inside an ancient dream. The cursed mist beside one of the huge roots of the Witch God Tree twisted into a spiral, and from that spiral, a young woman slowly stepped out.","She wore a long black-violet dress decorated with silver star patterns, and a pointed witch hat sat above her long midnight-blue hair. Her eyes were deep purple, filled with starlight, and several small crystal charms floated around her like tiny moons.","The moment she appeared, the cursed aura around the Witch God Tree reacted to her presence, but instead of attacking, it seemed to hesitate, as if recognizing another wielder of strange and ancient powers.","Caroline’s expression changed slightly. \"A witch...\"","Nancy’s eyes sharpened. \"Stellar Templar.\"","The woman smiled faintly and gave a graceful bow that looked playful rather than respectful. \"How sharp. I thought I had hidden myself quite well, but it seems I was wrong.\"","Her voice carried a soft charm, yet no one present dared to treat her lightly.","Stellar Templar was one of the seven strongest first-rate forces of the Divine Realm. Unlike ordinary sects, clans, kingdoms, or courts, Stellar Templar was famous for producing witches, star-seers, curse masters, fate readers, and mystic spellcasters whose methods were often difficult to understand and even harder to defend against.","Among the seven first-rate forces, they were not known for direct brute strength, but no one wanted to offend them easily, because a witch from Stellar Templar could curse an enemy, manipulate the battlefield, read hidden dangers, or guide fate itself in terrifying ways.","Selene’s eyes narrowed. \"Morgana Starveil.\"","The witch smiled. \"It seems Divine Daughter Selene still remembers me.\"","Morgana Starveil.","One of the strongest geniuses of Stellar Templar.","The moment that name spread, several elves from the second faction showed wary expressions, while even Princess Rosaline’s calm gaze became more serious. Morgana was not a weak spectator who had come to watch from the side. In this Cosmic Ascension Conference, she was one of the people truly qualified to stand on the highest stage among the younger generation."]},{"number":1776,"title":"Chapter 1776: Surrounded - 3","paragraphs":["Before anyone could speak further, another aura appeared.","The space beside Morgana folded inward silently.","There was no explosion, no light, and no grand entrance, yet the moment the space folded, everyone felt as if the distance between them and that direction had become meaningless. A young man stepped out from the folded space, dressed in a simple white robe with black edges.","His long hair was tied loosely behind him, his eyes were silver-gray, and his expression was calm to the point of indifference. Around him, faint traces of void power moved like transparent water, causing the air near his body to distort and rebuild itself again and again.","Max’s eyes narrowed slightly.","This person’s aura was different from the others. And most importantly, he could sense the aura of Void Genesis Art from this man.","Rosaline slowly said, \"Kaiden Voidmere of the Grand Void Sanctum.\"","The young man glanced at her calmly but did not respond.","The Grand Void Sanctum was another one of the seven strongest first-rate forces of the Divine Realm, and its disciples were famous for their mastery over space, void laws, and strange movement techniques that made them almost impossible to trap. Among them, Kaiden Voidmere was known as the strongest genius of his generation.","Some said he had been born inside a collapsing void rift and survived because the void itself acknowledged him. Others said he had already touched the edge of a Pseudo Cosmic Path related to emptiness and distance, making him one of the most dangerous participants in the entire Cosmic Ascension Conference.","Kaiden’s gaze moved to Max.","For a brief moment, his calm eyes flickered.","The two stared at each other for a moment.","No killing intent appeared between them, but the air around them became tense in a different way, as if two people who understood the same type of danger had recognized each other instantly.","Then the third aura descended.","Unlike Morgana’s eerie mystic presence or Kaiden’s silent void pressure, this aura was direct, grand, and overbearing. Nine points of starlight appeared in the sky above the base of the Witch God Tree, and each star shone with a different shade of silver, gold, blue, red, white, purple, black, green, and crimson.","The nine stars revolved once, then descended together, forming a stairway of starlight. From that stairway, a young man walked down step by step.","He wore dark-gold battle armor engraved with nine star marks, and his black hair moved wildly in the wind. His eyes were bright like burning stars, and every step he took caused the ground beneath the Witch God Tree to tremble faintly.","Compared to Morgana and Kaiden, he made no attempt to hide his strength. His aura was bold, sharp, and filled with absolute confidence, as if he believed that every battlefield he entered should naturally make room for him.","Caroline’s face became even more solemn. \"Nine Star Court.\"","Jessica swallowed. \"The strongest first-rate force...\"","Nine Star Court was often called the strongest first-rate force in the Divine Realm. Even among the seven strongest first-rate forces, its reputation stood at the top. Its disciples cultivated star power, body power, combat arts, and star formations, and their inheritance was famous for producing monsters who could fight across levels with terrifying ease.","Many people believed that if Nine Star Court ever produced a true supreme genius capable of uniting its nine great star inheritances, that person might one day challenge even the weakest supreme forces.","Selene’s expression finally lost some of its ease. \"Orion Starfall.\"","The young man in dark-gold armor smiled broadly. \"Selene, you look unhappy to see me.\"","Orion Starfall.","The strongest genius of Nine Star Court.","His name alone caused the battlefield to become even heavier. Even Seraphine and Fin, who had been arrogant before Max crushed them, looked deeply cautious now. They might look down on many people, but they would never dare to look down on Orion Starfall.","Among the younger generation of the seven strongest first-rate forces, his reputation was terrifying, and there were already rumors that he had defeated several peak Law Manifestation Realm geniuses without using his full strength.","With Morgana Starveil of Stellar Templar, Kaiden Voidmere of the Grand Void Sanctum, and Orion Starfall of Nine Star Court appearing at the same time, the situation at the base of the Witch God Tree instantly became far more complicated.","Max’s group stood in the center.","Selene and the second faction elves stood on one side.","Princess Rosaline and the Lunarian Kingdom stood on another.","And now, three more monsters from three of the seven strongest first-rate forces had appeared.","The base of the Witch God Tree no longer looked like a simple ambush.","It looked like the gathering point of the strongest young geniuses of the Divine Realm.","Morgana’s purple eyes moved to the small cursed eye attached to Max’s shoulder, and a trace of curiosity appeared on her face. \"A Witch’s curse mark. How interesting. I felt the death of the Abyssal Witch Eye and came to see who had the courage to kill the old guardian, but I did not expect the person to be carrying the mark so calmly.\"","Kaiden looked at Max’s shoulder as well, then at Dragonheart. \"He also carries the Sword of the Sword Sovereign.\"","Orion laughed. \"And he is the same Max Morgan whose ranking jumped like a madman. Good. I was wondering when I would meet him.\"","Selene’s face became colder.","She had intended to deal with Max and Caroline quickly, but the arrival of Morgana, Kaiden, and Orion changed the balance completely. None of these three belonged to weak powers, and none of them would obey her. Even worse, each of them had clearly come because of Max, the Witch’s curse mark, the Sword of the Sword Sovereign, or the commotion around Witch God Valley.","Max looked at the three newcomers calmly.","\"You three came to fight too?\"","Morgana smiled. \"Not necessarily. I sensed that someone destroyed the guardian here and came to check.\"","Kaiden replied flatly, \"That depends.\"","Orion grinned. \"I came to see if you are as strong as the rumors say.\"","Max’s expression did not change.","The little cursed eye on his shoulder blinked again, slowly turning from Selene to Morgana, then to Kaiden, then to Orion, as if even the curse itself was watching the arrival of these powerful geniuses with interest.","Rosaline looked at the scene and sighed softly. \"Now this has truly become troublesome.\"","Selene’s golden eyes moved between Max and the three newcomers, then her lips curled into a cold smile again.","\"Interesting,\" she said. \"It seems everyone wants a piece of you, Max Morgan.\"","Max held Dragonheart loosely at his side.","His gaze swept across Selene, Seraphine, Fin, Rosaline, Morgana, Kaiden, and Orion.","Then he smiled faintly.","\"If all of you are done introducing yourselves,\" Max said calmly, \"decide quickly whether you are here to watch or to stand in my way.\""]},{"number":1777,"title":"Chapter 1777: Max vs Selene","paragraphs":["Selene sneered at Max’s words before turning to Rosaline.","\"Remember your words.\"","\"Do as you please,\" Princess Rosaline said calmly.","She had only been interested in Max because of the terrifying sword aura he had left behind near the neutral city, and after seeing the situation at the base of the Witch God Tree, that interest had only grown deeper.","The Sword of the Sword Sovereign, the strange Witch’s curse mark clinging to his body, the rumors of his sudden rise in the Cosmic Ascension Ranking List, and now the way Seraphine and Fin looked at him with fear hidden beneath hatred all made Rosaline feel that Max was far more mysterious than the reports suggested.","If letting Selene fight him would force him to release that terrifying sword aura again, then so be it. For now, Rosaline was willing to remain an observer.","Selene understood Rosaline’s meaning, and her cold smile deepened slightly before she turned back toward Max.","Then she raised one hand.","\"All of you, step back.\"","The second faction elves immediately reacted. Some looked startled, while others hesitated because they had clearly come here prepared to surround Max and Caroline together, but none of them dared to disobey Selene’s command.","Seraphine and Fin exchanged a brief glance, and although resentment filled their eyes, their bodies moved backward more quickly than the others. They had already fought Max once.","They knew better than anyone that if Selene truly wanted to take him on herself, standing too close to the battlefield would only place them inside the range of that emotionless sword path again.","One of the second faction elves said carefully, \"Divine Daughter, should we not assist you? This human is not simple.\"","Selene’s golden eyes turned toward him.","The elf immediately lowered his head and retreated without another word.","\"I said step back,\" Selene said lightly. \"I will take care of him with my own hands.\"","Her voice was soft, but the authority inside it could not be questioned. The second faction formation slowly opened, and the elves moved away from the central battlefield, creating a wide circular space at the base of the Witch God Tree.","The golden talismans and bloodline-suppressing formations around the area remained active, but the people controlling them withdrew to the edges, leaving Selene standing alone in front of Max. Her long golden hair moved gently behind her, the halo of Heavenly Luminance power above her shoulders becoming brighter with each passing second.","The atmosphere shifted.","This was no longer an ambush.","It was a duel.","Morgana Starveil watched with bright purple eyes, her smile playful but focused. \"The Divine Daughter wants to fight him herself. How bold.\"","Kaiden Voidmere remained silent, but the space around him rippled faintly, showing that even he was paying close attention.","Orion Starfall crossed his arms and laughed. \"Good. This is better than watching a bunch of people rush him together.\"","Rosaline did not speak. Her gaze remained fixed on Max.","Max, however, only looked at Selene for a moment before turning toward Caroline and the others.","\"Retreat.\"","Caroline frowned. \"Max...\"","\"I will handle everything here,\" Max said calmly.","His tone did not leave room for argument.","Caroline wanted to say more, but when she saw the calm certainty in his eyes, she swallowed her words. She still knew too little about Max, but after everything she had witnessed inside Witch God Valley, she understood one thing clearly.","Her sister’s son was not reckless without reason. If he told them to retreat, it meant he had already decided how to face what came next.","Jessica immediately helped Caroline move back, while the other third faction elves followed with tense expressions. Nancy also retreated, though her eyes remained on Max the entire time.","Caroline stopped several dozen meters away and looked back at Max.","\"Be careful,\" she said quietly.","Max did not look back, but he nodded once.","The little cursed eye on his left shoulder blinked slowly, shifting across his shoulder as if it was also watching Selene. Max ignored it. His right hand held Dragonheart loosely at his side, and his expression remained calm, almost indifferent, while Selene’s aura continued rising in front of him.","Selene looked at him with cold interest.","\"You are quite confident,\" she said. \"You stand here alone even though you know who I am.\"","Max looked at her. \"I know enough.\"","Selene smiled. \"Then you should also know that I am not Seraphine, Fin, or Lumine.\"","\"I know,\" Max replied.","His gaze moved briefly to the golden halo behind her.","\"You are more useful than them.\"","Selene’s eyes narrowed slightly.","The words sounded simple, but she understood the meaning. Max was not treating her as a greater danger. He was treating her as someone who might carry more answers, more Killing Points, and more connection to the truth about his stolen bloodline.","The smile on Selene’s face slowly faded.","\"You truly do not know how to lower your head.\"","Max’s expression remained unchanged. \"I do not lower my head to thieves.\"","The air instantly froze.","The second faction elves at the edge of the battlefield stirred, and several of them released sharp killing intent, but Selene raised one finger without looking back, stopping them again.","Rosaline’s eyes sharpened slightly.","Morgana’s smile widened.","Kaiden’s gaze became deeper.","Orion’s expression turned more excited.","Caroline’s heart clenched because she knew exactly what Max was referring to. The bloodline stolen from him as a child. The second faction’s forbidden extraction. The Divine Son who now carried what should have belonged to Max.","By calling Selene and her faction thieves in front of everyone, Max had not merely insulted her. He had pointed directly at one of the darkest secrets of the second faction.","Selene’s golden light became colder.","\"Careful, Max Morgan,\" she said softly. \"Some words carry consequences.\"","Max slowly raised Dragonheart.","\"I am counting on it.\"","A faint sword hum spread across the battlefield.","Selene’s halo brightened.","The ground beneath them trembled.","Around the battlefield, everyone had already stepped back. Rosaline, Morgana, Kaiden, Orion, Seraphine, Fin, the second faction elves, Caroline, Jessica, Nancy, and the third faction remnants all watched the two figures standing beneath the vast shadow of the Witch God Tree.","On one side stood Selene Vaeloria, the Divine Daughter of the second faction, trained by the Bloodline Hall and the ancestors, carrying an extremely pure Heavenly Luminance Royal Bloodline.","On the other side stood Max Morgan, Caelira’s son, wielder of Dragonheart, bearer of the Witch’s curse mark, owner of the Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline, and the one who had already cut down every enemy who believed numbers, status, or reputation could stop him.","Selene took one step forward, and golden light poured from her body like a rising sun.","Max’s eyes remained calm as Dragonheart tilted slightly in his hand.","The duel was about to begin."]},{"number":1778,"title":"Chapter 1778: Divine King’s Punishment!","paragraphs":["Max did not intend to hold back in this battle.","If Selene had been someone from another force, perhaps he might have tested her slowly, measured her strength, and used the fight to sharpen one of his paths. But she was not simply another genius standing in his way.","She was the Divine Daughter of the second faction, a core figure raised by the same people who had destroyed his family, stolen his bloodline, imprisoned his parents, tortured the members of his mother’s faction, and hunted Caroline all the way into Witch God Valley.","Against an elf of the second faction, especially one standing so close to the center of its younger generation, Max saw no reason to be patient.","The air around him changed before Selene could make the first move.","Dragonheart remained in his hand, but the power rising from Max this time was not the deathly stillness of the Emotion Severing Path. It was not the ancient pressure of his Draconic Essences, nor was it the sacred golden radiance of the Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline.","A different force erupted from him, violent, majestic, destructive, and filled with the authority of punishment. Seven colors of lightning appeared around his body, red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo, and violet, each strand moving like a living divine serpent as they coiled through the air and gathered behind him into a vast lightning domain.","The sky above the base of the Witch God Tree darkened.","Thunder roared.","The huge roots beneath Max’s feet trembled as the seven-colored lightning spread outward, and even the golden light released by Selene seemed to pause for a brief moment beneath the pressure of that punishment aura.","This was Max’s Pseudo Cosmic Path of seven-colored lightning, a path he had created after considering two foundations. The first was the essence of the Storm King’s Inheritance, which had taught him the majesty of storms, thunder, heavenly pressure, and the way lightning could dominate a battlefield.","The second was the destructive and punishment nature of the seven-colored lightning itself, a force that did not merely strike, but judged, destroyed, and erased those standing beneath its wrath.","\"Divine King Punishment,\" Max said calmly.","The moment the name fell, the seven-colored lightning behind him exploded into the shape of a towering divine throne made of thunderclouds and punishment light.","No figure sat upon the throne, but everyone present felt the terrifying illusion of an unseen king looking down at all things from above. Lightning laws, punishment intent, and storm authority gathered around Max, making him look as if he had become the executor of a divine sentence.","Selene’s expression changed slightly.","She had expected Max to use his sword path, especially after hearing from Seraphine and Fin about the terrifying emotionless Pseudo Cosmic Path that had crushed them inside Witch God Valley. She had even prepared herself for his sword aura.","But instead of that, Max had released another Pseudo Cosmic Path, and this one was completely different. It was not silent. It was not cold. It was violent, majestic, and oppressively destructive.","Rosaline’s eyes narrowed from the distance. \"Another Pseudo Cosmic Path?\"","Morgana Starveil’s smile slowly faded into genuine interest. \"Seven-colored lightning with the authority of punishment. How interesting. This is not a simple lightning path.\"","Kaiden Voidmere stared at the space around Max and said nothing, but the slight ripple around his body showed that he was no longer as indifferent as before.","Orion Starfall laughed loudly, his eyes burning with fighting intent. \"Good! This Max Morgan is even better than the rumors.\"","Selene quickly suppressed the surprise in her heart. As the Divine Daughter of the second faction, she would never allow herself to show fear before so many powerful geniuses. Golden light burst from her body, and the halo behind her expanded into a radiant circle several dozen meters wide.","Unlike Seraphine’s Radiant Judgment Path, Selene’s power was purer and more regal. It did not create a divine court to judge enemies. Instead, it turned the battlefield itself into a sacred domain of light.","\"Heavenly Luminance Royal Bloodline, Divine Radiant Crown.\"","A crown of golden light appeared above Selene’s head, and the moment it formed, her aura rose sharply. Countless beams of light descended around her like pillars holding up a sacred palace, and every beam carried a suppressive power that targeted bloodlines, spiritual energy, and concepts at the same time.","She lifted one hand, and hundreds of golden swords formed behind her, each one brighter and sharper than the sword that had attacked Caroline earlier.","\"Luminance Sword Rain.\"","The golden swords shot forward.","They did not fly chaotically. They moved with perfect order, forming intersecting paths that sealed Max’s front, sides, and sky above him. Every sword contained compressed light, and as they descended, the air was burned clean, the mist was erased, and the ground beneath the Witch God Tree began glowing as if forced to reflect Selene’s radiance.","Max raised his hand.","Seven-colored lightning gathered around his fingers.","He did not swing Dragonheart.","He simply pointed forward.","A storm of lightning erupted.","Boom!","The seven-colored thunderbolts collided with the golden sword rain in midair. The first moment of impact lit up the entire battlefield, and golden light clashed with seven-colored lightning so violently that many weaker elves had to cover their eyes.","Selene’s light swords were powerful, refined, and filled with bloodline suppression, but the moment they touched Max’s Divine King Punishment, they began cracking under the destructive punishment force contained inside the lightning.","One golden sword shattered.","Then ten.","Then hundreds.","The seven-colored lightning tore through the sword rain like heavenly punishment falling upon a false sun, reducing every radiant blade into golden sparks that scattered through the air.","Selene’s eyes sharpened, and with a flick of her wrist, the remaining sword light changed direction, trying to bypass the lightning storm and strike Max from behind, but Max’s Dimensional Sovereign Body had already captured the shift in space and energy before the attack could reach him.","Lightning flashed beneath his feet.","Max disappeared.","When he reappeared, he was already above Selene.","Dragonheart descended with seven-colored lightning wrapped around its blade.","Selene reacted instantly.","A golden shield shaped like a lotus bloomed above her head, each petal made of condensed Heavenly Luminance power. Max’s sword slammed into the shield, and the collision created a shockwave that spread across the base of the Witch God Tree. The lotus shield trembled violently, several petals cracking under the combined force of Dragonheart and Divine King Punishment, but it did not break immediately.","Selene moved back, her expression finally becoming serious.","\"You have more than one Pseudo Cosmic Path,\" she said coldly.","Max’s gaze remained calm. \"You noticed quickly.\""]},{"number":1779,"title":"Chapter 1779: Storm King’s Verdict!","paragraphs":["Selene’s eyes flashed. \"Do not think that makes you invincible.\"","Her golden crown brightened, and a pair of radiant wings unfolded behind her. The wings were vast, elegant, and filled with golden runes, and the moment they appeared, Selene’s speed increased tremendously. She vanished from her original position and appeared to Max’s right, releasing a palm strike filled with condensed light.","\"Solar Luminance Palm.\"","The palm seemed to carry a small sun inside it.","Max turned and met it with a slash of lightning.","Boom!","The palm exploded into fragments of golden light, but Selene had already moved again. She appeared above him this time, both hands forming a seal as a huge golden wheel appeared behind her. The wheel rotated with terrifying speed, and every rotation released blades of light that cut toward Max from dozens of directions.","\"Heavenly Wheel of Radiant Execution.\"","The attack was far stronger than the sword rain. The golden wheel suppressed the battlefield, split the air, and created a storm of light blades so dense that it seemed impossible to avoid. The second faction elves watching from the side regained some confidence when they saw it, because this was one of Selene’s true combat techniques, and many geniuses of the same realm had fallen beneath it.","Max stood in the center of the light blade storm.","Seven-colored lightning rose around him like a divine punishment barrier.","The light blades struck the lightning.","One after another, they shattered.","Max lifted Dragonheart and slashed upward. A seven-colored lightning arc tore through the air, splitting the Heavenly Wheel of Radiant Execution from the center. The golden wheel cracked, trembled, and then exploded into a shower of light fragments.","Selene’s expression changed again.","Max did not let the chance pass.","Lightning erupted beneath his feet, and his figure rushed forward with terrifying speed. He appeared in front of Selene and thrust Dragonheart straight toward her chest. Selene’s golden wings folded in front of her, forming a layered defense, while her crown released a circle of light that pushed outward like a wave.","Max’s sword pierced through the first layer.","Then the second.","Then the third.","Selene gritted her teeth, and the halo behind her expanded suddenly. A mirror of light appeared between them, and Max’s sword struck the mirror with a thunderous sound. The mirror cracked but managed to divert his thrust slightly, causing Dragonheart to pass beside Selene’s shoulder instead of through her heart.","Even so, the lightning wrapped around the blade grazed her arm.","Selene’s sleeve was instantly destroyed, and a thin wound appeared on her fair skin. Seven-colored lightning crawled over the wound like living punishment, causing her bloodline power to tremble slightly before she forcefully dispersed it.","The second faction elves stared in disbelief.","The Divine Daughter had been injured.","Even if it was only a small wound, it was still enough to shake them.","Seraphine’s face became ugly. \"Impossible...\"","Fin’s eyes flickered with fear again. \"He can actually pressure Selene.\"","Selene’s expression turned colder than before.","The wound was not serious, but the meaning behind it was unacceptable. She had been trained by the Bloodline Hall, personally guided by powerful ancestors, and recognized as the Divine Daughter of the second faction.","Her Heavenly Luminance Royal Bloodline was extremely pure, and among the younger generation of the elf race, very few could force her into danger. Yet Max had not only blocked her techniques, but had taken the initiative to attack and wounded her.","\"You are stronger than I expected,\" Selene said softly.","Max pointed Dragonheart at her. \"You are weaker than I expected.\"","The words made the golden light around Selene flare violently.","\"Do not get arrogant.\"","Her bloodline power erupted to a new level, and the crown above her head transformed into a full divine diadem. Golden armor formed over her body, covering her arms, shoulders, chest, and legs with radiant plates carved from light itself.","Behind her, a giant phantom of a heavenly elf queen appeared, holding a spear of pure golden radiance. The aura that descended from that phantom made Caroline’s face turn grave.","Caroline said in a low voice, \"That is one of the second faction’s strongest bloodline techniques. Heavenly Luminance Queen Avatar.\"","Selene raised her hand, and the phantom behind her raised the golden spear.","The spear became enormous, stretching from the ground to the sky, and every inch of it burned with bloodline suppression and sacred destruction.","\"Heavenly Luminance, Queen’s Divine Spear.\"","The spear descended toward Max.","The pressure was terrifying.","The ground beneath Max cracked even before the attack arrived, and the golden light sealed the surrounding space to prevent him from dodging. It was clear that Selene had truly begun using her full power. She was not holding back, and the strength she displayed made everyone understand why she had the right to be called the Divine Daughter of the second faction.","Max smiled faintly for the first time since the battle began.","\"Not bad.\"","The divine throne of seven-colored lightning behind him became clearer.","Thunderclouds gathered above the battlefield, and the seven colors of lightning condensed into a massive spear of punishment in Max’s hand. It was not a weapon made from metal, but from storm authority and destructive lightning. He raised it toward the descending golden spear, and the aura around him became as majestic as a ruler announcing punishment to the heavens.","\"Divine King Punishment, Storm King’s Verdict.\"","The seven-colored lightning spear shot upward.","The two spears collided above the battlefield.","The explosion shook the base of the Witch God Tree.","Golden light and seven-colored lightning swallowed everything. The huge roots beneath the battlefield cracked open, the surrounding formations trembled, and many second faction elves were forced to retreat again and again.","Rosaline’s followers raised defensive barriers. Morgana waved her hand and formed a starry curtain before herself. Kaiden distorted the space around him. Orion stood still and let the shockwave crash against his body, his grin growing wider.","In the center of the explosion, Selene pressed down with all her strength.","Max pushed upward with Divine King Punishment.","For several breaths, the two powers seemed evenly matched.","Then the punishment lightning began to devour the golden radiance.","Crack!","The Queen’s Divine Spear cracked.","Selene’s pupils narrowed.","The seven-colored lightning spread across the golden spear like divine judgment, destroying its structure from within. The Heavenly Luminance Queen Avatar behind Selene trembled violently as the spear broke apart, and when the final surge of lightning erupted, the golden spear shattered completely.","Selene was thrown backward.","Her feet slid across the ground, leaving two long marks on the giant root beneath her.","The battlefield went silent for a heartbeat."]},{"number":1780,"title":"Chapter 1780: Furious Selene!","paragraphs":["Then Selene lifted her head, and her eyes were no longer calm.","She was furious.","But more than that, she was shaken.","Max had not used the Emotion Severing Path. He had not activated all of his hidden cards. He had only used this seven-colored lightning Pseudo Cosmic Path, yet it had suppressed every light-based attack she had released so far. Her sword rain, her lotus shield, her radiant palm, her heavenly wheel, her light mirror, and even the Queen’s Divine Spear had all failed to defeat him.","Selene clenched her hands, and the golden bloodline light around her burned even brighter.","Max stepped forward again.","The seven-colored lightning circled him, his dark hair moving wildly in the storm, Dragonheart in his hand reflecting both golden light and thunder.","He had to admit Selene was strong. She was not like Seraphine or Fin. She reacted faster, defended better, attacked with greater precision, and her Heavenly Luminance Royal Bloodline gave her an extremely stable foundation. If any other genius at her level faced her, they might truly be crushed by her divine light.","But Max was also strong.","And against the second faction, he would not yield even one step.","Selene raised both hands.","The golden halo behind her split into twelve smaller halos, each one forming a different radiant weapon: sword, spear, bow, chain, shield, axe, whip, lance, wheel, blade, hammer, and staff. At the same time, the Heavenly Luminance Queen Avatar behind her became more solid, and countless golden runes spread across the battlefield like a sacred formation.","\"Twelve Luminance Edicts.\"","The twelve weapons descended together.","Each weapon carried a different kind of light-based power. The sword cut, the spear pierced, the bow shot, the chain bound, the shield suppressed, the axe split, the whip restrained, the lance broke defenses, the wheel shredded, the blade erased, the hammer crushed, and the staff sealed. Together, they formed a terrifying all-directional attack that showed the true depth of Selene’s inheritance.","Max raised Dragonheart.","Seven-colored lightning gathered into his sword.","\"Divine King Punishment, Thousand Thunder Judgments.\"","He slashed.","One slash became ten.","Ten became a hundred.","A hundred became a thousand.","Seven-colored lightning sword lights filled the battlefield, clashing against the twelve radiant weapons in a storm of divine destruction. Every collision created a thunderous explosion. Every destroyed weapon released a burst of golden light. Every shattered lightning arc rebounded into the sky and formed new thunderbolts that descended again under Max’s control.","Selene moved through the storm with terrifying grace, her golden wings carrying her across the battlefield as she continuously formed new weapons of light.","Max moved just as quickly, using the Vein of Speed faintly beneath the surface of his body while letting Divine King Punishment dominate the clash.","He attacked when Selene formed her next seal.","He slashed when her defense shifted.","He appeared above her when her attention moved to the lightning storm, forcing her to raise three halos to block Dragonheart.","She countered with a beam of Heavenly Luminance light aimed directly at his chest.","Max cut it apart and sent a seven-colored lightning palm toward her shoulder.","Selene dodged by turning into light and reappeared behind him with a golden blade.","Max’s Dimensional Sovereign Body sensed the movement and made him turn before the blade could land.","Their attacks collided again.","Boom!","The entire base of the Witch God Tree became their battlefield.","Golden radiance and seven-colored lightning filled the sky.","The second faction elves watched with shocked eyes, because Selene was displaying power worthy of the Divine Daughter, yet Max was still matching her directly.","Caroline watched with a complicated expression, because the golden light used by Selene came from the same elven bloodline system that had once belonged to her sister’s lineage, but in front of Max’s seven-colored lightning, that light was repeatedly being broken.","Rosaline watched without blinking, realizing that the terrifying sword aura was not the only mystery surrounding Max. Morgana smiled less and less, her eyes full of calculation. Kaiden remained silent, but his gaze stayed fixed on Max’s spatial movements. Orion laughed several times, clearly enjoying the sight of two monsters colliding beneath the Witch God Tree.","The battle grew fiercer.","Selene was truly worthy of being called the Divine Daughter of the elven race’s second faction. Every time Max broke one technique, she revealed another. Every time his lightning suppressed her light, she refined her control and struck from another angle. Her combat sense was sharp, her bloodline was pure, her techniques were vast, and her foundation was strong enough that even after multiple clashes, her aura did not collapse.","But Max was not inferior.","His Divine King Punishment was too destructive. The seven-colored lightning did not merely collide with Selene’s light. It punished it. It broke through it. It carried the essence of the Storm King’s Inheritance and the destructive nature of seven-colored lightning, making every strike feel like judgment from a divine thunder ruler.","Whenever Selene’s light tried to suppress him, his lightning tore through the suppression. Whenever her bloodline tried to purify his power, his punishment lightning blasted apart the purification. Whenever she formed a sacred domain of light, Max shattered it with one storm-charged slash.","After dozens of exchanges, Selene finally retreated into the air, breathing slightly harder than before.","Max stood below her, still calm, seven-colored lightning wrapping around him like a storm cloak.","Neither of them had truly fallen.","Neither of them had been decisively defeated.","But everyone could see that Selene had used many powerful light-based techniques, while Max had used only one Pseudo Cosmic Path to answer all of them.","Divine King Punishment.","The name now felt carved into the battlefield itself.","Selene stared down at Max, her golden eyes filled with anger, caution, and something she did not want to admit.","Pressure.","Max looked up at her and smiled faintly.","\"Is that all the Divine Daughter can do?\"","The seven-colored lightning behind him roared again, and the divine thunder throne became even more imposing.","Selene’s face turned cold, and her golden aura surged once more.","The battle was far from over.","Selene floated in the air, golden light pouring from her body like a divine tide, while Max stood below her wrapped in seven-colored lightning, Dragonheart in hand, his Divine King Punishment still roaring like a heavenly storm around him.","The battlefield had already been shaken again and again by their clash. Giant roots at the base of the Witch God Tree were cracked open, nearby stone ridges had collapsed, and the space between them was still filled with scattered sparks of golden radiance and seven-colored lightning.","Selene’s expression was colder than ever, while Max’s remained calm and faintly sharp, as if he was still not pressured enough by everything she had shown so far.","That calmness was the final thing Selene could no longer endure.","She slowly raised both hands.","The halo behind her began to tremble.","The divine diadem above her head dissolved into countless strands of golden light, and those strands did not scatter aimlessly. Instead, they gathered behind her into a huge circular formation that looked like a sacred sun wheel mixed with an ancient heavenly gate.","The very moment it began to form, the entire base of the Witch God Tree grew heavy. The second faction elves immediately showed signs of awe, Rosaline’s expression turned more serious, Morgana’s purple eyes flickered faintly, Kaiden looked up with a slightly sharper gaze, and even Orion’s grin faded a little as he realized that Selene was finally about to reveal her true path.","Caroline’s face changed sharply.","\"Max,\" she called out, her voice tense, \"be careful. She is going to use her Pseudo Cosmic Path.\"","Max’s eyes narrowed slightly, but he did not look back."]},{"number":1781,"title":"Chapter 1781: A Sneak Attack","paragraphs":["Caroline continued quickly, because she knew that once Selene’s path fully unfolded, there might not be another moment to speak. \"Her Pseudo Cosmic Path is said to be one of the strongest paths among the younger generation of the second faction. Even the ancestors treated it very seriously. The only reason she does not use it freely is because it consumes too much of her power. She can only sustain it for a short period of time before it drains her energy rapidly.\"","Nancy’s face became grave.","Jessica and the other third faction elves swallowed hard.","If even Caroline, someone who had once belonged to the heart of the elven royal line, said that Selene’s path was one of the strongest, then it was not something to underestimate.","Max’s eyes remained fixed on Selene.","\"Then she should use it now,\" he said calmly.","Selene heard his words.","A cold smile touched her lips.","\"Do not regret asking for this.\"","The sacred sun wheel behind her fully opened.","Then her Pseudo Cosmic Path descended.","\"Pseudo Cosmic Path... Heavenly Luminance Genesis.\"","The moment the name fell, the world seemed to brighten.","A domain of pure golden-white radiance unfolded behind Selene, vast and grand like the birth of a divine heaven. Within that path, one could see countless layers of sacred palaces, endless rivers of luminance, golden suns rising and falling, and divine chains of law crossing the sky.","It did not feel like an ordinary path built on battle intent alone. It felt like the beginning of a holy kingdom, a genesis light capable of birthing order, authority, and divine suppression.","The air trembled.","The ground groaned.","Max’s seven-colored lightning domain was still violent and majestic, but for the first time in this battle, it encountered a radiance so pure and so overwhelmingly structured that even Divine King Punishment seemed to meet an equal in authority.","Selene’s golden hair floated upward.","Her eyes turned completely radiant, no longer showing ordinary pupils but only divine light.","The halo behind her dissolved into that Genesis Path, and in the center of the vast heavenly radiance, a single weapon slowly formed in her hands.","It was a spear.","A spear of blinding white-gold light.","But unlike her previous Queen’s Divine Spear, this weapon did not merely contain radiant bloodline power. It contained the essence of her Pseudo Cosmic Path itself. Every inch of the spear was wrapped in the beginning and order of her Heavenly Luminance Genesis.","Merely looking at it made many weaker observers feel their minds tremble, as though their thoughts were being purified and suppressed by something higher.","Seraphine’s face filled with excitement. \"Divine Daughter is finally serious.\"","Fin also looked relieved. \"This time he should fall.\"","Rosaline stared without blinking.","Morgana’s smile became thin and unreadable.","Kaiden remained silent.","Orion crossed his arms more tightly and focused harder.","Selene raised the spear.","\"Heavenly Luminance Genesis, Spear of First Dawn.\"","The giant Genesis domain behind her condensed.","Palaces of light, rivers of radiance, and suns of holy brilliance all collapsed inward toward that spear, turning it into the embodiment of beginning light. Then Selene thrust it downward at Max.","The spear descended.","Everything in its path was erased.","The air became light.","The storm around Max was split open.","The giant roots beneath the battlefield were torn apart as the attack fell with unstoppable authority. This was not just an attack of power. It was an attack carrying origin, suppression, order, and the overwhelming sanctity of Selene’s strongest path.","Caroline’s face turned pale.","\"That attack...\"","Even she had not expected Selene to use her strongest path so decisively.","But Max did not retreat.","The moment the Spear of First Dawn descended, Max’s eyes became colder, and his seven-colored lightning erupted again. Divine King Punishment roared around him, the thunder throne behind him becoming even more imposing as he prepared to answer Selene’s strongest path head-on. Lightning condensed around Dragonheart, and the destructive, punishing essence of his path gathered to an extreme.","He was ready to counter.","He was ready to destroy Selene together with her Heavenly Luminance Genesis.","But just as Max was about to move, something unexpected happened.","The ground beneath him exploded.","Countless roots of the Witch God Tree burst out from below like living serpents. They moved too suddenly, too quietly, and too unnaturally. Their timing was perfect, striking at the exact instant all of Max’s attention had been focused upward on Selene’s descending Pseudo Cosmic Path attack.","Even with his Dimensional Sovereign Body, the interference came too abruptly and from too close. Before he could completely shift away, the giant roots wrapped around his legs, his waist, his sword arm, and his other shoulder, binding him in place.","Max’s eyes changed instantly.","This sneak attack had come completely out of nowhere.","For the briefest moment, even he was caught off guard.","Caroline gasped. \"Max!\"","Jessica’s face turned pale. Nancy’s expression changed sharply.","Orion’s eyes widened slightly.","Kaiden’s gaze became deeper.","Rosaline’s brows furrowed.","And then everyone’s eyes turned toward one person.","Morgana Starveil.","The witch stood at the edge of the battlefield with one hand slightly raised, and around her fingers, faint violet star-charms were revolving slowly. Her expression remained graceful and calm, but the meaning of what had happened was clear to everyone present.","The roots of the Witch God Tree had not acted on their own. They had been controlled, guided, or awakened by her witchcraft.","Even Selene seemed momentarily surprised by the timing, but she did not stop her attack.","If Max was bound, then better.","The Spear of First Dawn descended completely.","Max was still restricted.","And in the next instant, Selene’s full-powered attack landed on him while he was completely defenseless.","Boom!","The explosion was world-shaking.","Golden-white radiance swallowed the battlefield whole. The entire base of the Witch God Tree trembled violently, countless nearby roots were blown apart, and the force of the clash spread outward in a ring of destructive light that forced even the surrounding observers to retreat or raise defenses.","The second faction elves stumbled backward, Rosaline’s group activated barriers, Kaiden distorted the incoming shockwave, Morgana raised a curtain of purple starlight before herself, and Orion only planted his feet harder as the explosion crashed into him with a wide grin.","The third faction elves were horrified.","Caroline nearly stepped forward on instinct, but Jessica and Nancy stopped her.","Dust, light, shattered bark, and broken roots filled the battlefield.","For several breaths, no one could see anything.","Seraphine’s face lit up. \"He took it head-on while restricted.\"","Fin laughed in relief. \"This time there is no way he survived that without heavy injuries.\"","Selene remained in the air, breathing slightly harder now.","Caroline’s warning had been true.","Using Heavenly Luminance Genesis drained her power quickly. Even though she stood straight, there was a faint instability in her aura now, and the vast radiance behind her had already dimmed somewhat after unleashing that terrifying attack.","Yet in her eyes, there was still confidence. Max had been restrained at the critical moment. Her full-powered strike had landed directly. Even if he was absurdly strong, there was no reason for him to emerge unscathed from that.","The battlefield slowly began to clear.","The light faded.","The dust settled.","And then everyone saw him.","Max was still standing in the center of the ruined battlefield.","The roots binding him had already been shattered, broken into blackened fragments around his feet. His body had not been pierced. His flesh had not been burned. His clothes were torn and partly destroyed from the explosion, but beneath them, his body was now covered in golden-black dragon scales from head to toe.","Every scale gleamed with a terrifying luster.","They were neither purely golden nor purely black, but a fusion of both, carrying an ancient, noble, and chaotic aura at the same time.","The remaining traces of Selene’s Genesis light were still crawling across those scales, but they could not penetrate them at all. Instead, the light slid away or shattered apart as though it had struck the body of an ancient dragon king rather than a human cultivator.","For a moment, no one spoke.","Caroline’s eyes widened.","Jessica looked stunned.","Nancy slowly exhaled, though the shock in her face remained.","Seraphine’s expression froze.","Fin’s smile vanished.","Rosaline’s pupils narrowed.","Kaiden’s gaze became serious.","Orion let out a low whistle.","Even Morgana’s calm smile wavered slightly.","At the center of it all, Max slowly raised his head.","Golden-black scales covered his face and neck, leaving only his eyes fully visible, and those eyes were now colder than before. Lightning still coiled around him. Dragonheart remained in his hand. The small cursed eye clung to his left shoulder as if even the Witch’s mark was watching in silence.","Max looked first at Selene.","Then his gaze slowly moved toward Morgana.","His voice was calm, but terrifying.","\"So,\" he said softly, \"that is how you want to play.\""]},{"number":1782,"title":"Chapter 1782: Shameless Morgana!","paragraphs":["\"So, what of it?\" Morgana sneered.","Her earlier graceful smile had disappeared, and what remained on her beautiful face was a cold, mocking expression that made the charm around her feel poisonous.","The small crystal charms floating around her fingers spun slowly, and faint violet threads connected them to the roots of the Witch God Tree beneath the battlefield, revealing that her interference had not been accidental at all.","She had been waiting. She had watched Max and Selene clash, waited until Selene released her strongest Pseudo Cosmic Path, waited until Max was about to counterattack, and only then had she chosen the most disgusting moment to strike from the shadows.","\"This is a battle royale,\" Morgana continued, her voice carrying no shame at all. \"You did not expect us to be mere spectators, did you?\"","Her words made the expressions of many people change.","Even some of the second faction elves looked at her with strange eyes. They had been Max’s enemies from the beginning, so they naturally wanted him dead, but even they had not expected Morgana, who had introduced herself with such elegance and had claimed to be only curious about the Witch’s curse mark, to interfere so suddenly in another person’s duel.","Her timing had been too vicious. She had not challenged Max openly. She had not even attacked him directly. She had used the roots of the Witch God Tree to bind him from below when his attention was fully occupied by Selene’s strongest attack, deliberately trying to make him take that blow without defense.","Caroline’s eyes turned cold with anger. \"Shameless.\"","Jessica clenched her sword. \"You call that battle? You hid behind the Witch God Tree and stabbed from the dark like a rat.\"","Morgana glanced at Jessica, then smiled with cruel amusement. \"A rat that succeeds is still alive. A proud fool who fails is still dead. Which one do you think matters more in this conference?\"","Jessica’s face darkened.","Caroline looked at Morgana with undisguised disgust. \"Stellar Templar is one of the seven strongest first-rate forces of the Divine Realm. Is this how its strongest genius conducts herself?\"","Morgana laughed softly, and that laugh made her even more hateful than if she had simply been cruel. There was no guilt in it. There was no trace of embarrassment. Instead, she looked almost entertained by their anger, as if the disgust of others was another form of applause.","\"Please, do not speak to me about honor,\" Morgana said lightly. \"Honor is a word used by people who need others to admire the way they lose. I prefer winning. If binding him for a moment gives me a chance to see whether Selene’s strongest attack can break his body, then why would I not do it?\"","Her purple eyes moved back to Max, and a thin smile appeared on her lips.","\"Besides, he did not die. So why are all of you so angry?\"","That sentence made the atmosphere even colder.","Even Rosaline frowned slightly.","Kaiden’s gaze toward Morgana became more distant.","Orion’s smile vanished for the first time, and he looked at the witch with clear displeasure. \"You really are unpleasant.\"","Morgana turned her head slightly and smiled at him. \"Unpleasant people live longer, Orion.\"","Orion snorted coldly. \"Not always.\"","Selene, who had just used Heavenly Luminance Genesis and was still recovering from the drain, looked at Morgana with a complicated expression. Although Morgana’s interference had helped her attack land on Max, even Selene did not enjoy the feeling of having her duel dirtied by someone else’s trick. Yet she did not speak against it either.","In a battle royale, results mattered, and if Max had truly been injured by that attack, Selene would not have refused the advantage.","Max looked at Morgana silently.","The golden-black dragon scales covering his body gleamed faintly, and the seven-colored lightning around him had become quieter, but that quietness was more dangerous than the storm from before. His eyes were calm, yet the calmness now carried a weight that made the air around him feel sharper.","Then he nodded his head.","\"Fair.\"","Morgana raised an eyebrow.","Max continued calmly, \"This is indeed a battle royale, and your actions are justified.\"","For a brief moment, Morgana’s smile widened.","She seemed to think Max had accepted her logic, or perhaps she thought he was trying to suppress his anger because too many strong people were present. Her expression became even more mocking, and the violet charms around her fingers revolved lazily as if she was already preparing another trick.","But Max’s next words made her smile pause.","\"Since your actions are justified,\" Max said softly, \"then whatever I do to you next is also justified.\"","The battlefield fell silent.","Morgana’s eyes narrowed slightly.","Max slowly turned his body toward her.","The broken roots around his feet burned away under black flames, and the golden-black dragon scales covering him released a deep draconic pressure that spread across the base of the Witch God Tree. The little cursed eye on his left shoulder blinked once, its pupil turning toward Morgana as if even the Witch’s mark was waiting to see what he would do.","Morgana’s smile did not fully disappear, but a trace of caution entered her eyes.","\"Oh?\" she said, still trying to sound amused. \"Are you planning to attack me now while Selene is still standing before you?\"","Max looked at her.","\"You joined the battle first.\"","Morgana’s fingers twitched slightly.","Max continued, his voice calm and cold. \"You did not interfere to test me. You waited for the worst possible moment and tried to make someone else’s strongest attack land while I was bound. If my defense had been weaker, Caroline and the others would now be watching my body torn apart, and you would still be smiling as if you had done something clever.\"","Caroline’s expression tightened.","Nancy’s eyes became cold.","Jessica glared at Morgana with hatred.","Morgana’s expression finally changed a little because Max had described her intention perfectly. She had not cared whether he died. She had not cared whether it was fair. She had wanted to see his secrets, and if he died in the process, then that would only mean he had not been worth her attention.","Max took one step toward her.","The ground beneath his foot cracked.","\"So I will remember you, Morgana Starveil.\"","His voice was still calm, but everyone could hear the threat inside it."]},{"number":1783,"title":"Chapter 1783: Dealing with Selene First!","paragraphs":["Max then turned to look at Selene.","The golden radiance around her was still bright, and the vast image of Heavenly Luminance Genesis had not fully vanished behind her, but anyone with sharp eyes could already see the truth. The sacred palaces of light in her Pseudo Cosmic Path were flickering.","The golden rivers flowing through the radiant domain were breaking apart into unstable fragments. Even the divine sun wheel behind her had become dimmer than before, and the Spear of First Dawn she had unleashed had drained far more of her strength than she wanted others to notice.","Max looked at her calmly.","\"I won, right?\"","Selene’s eyes turned colder.","Max continued before she could answer, his voice spreading clearly across the base of the Witch God Tree. \"You are already trembling from the use of your Pseudo Cosmic Path. And as Caroline said, you cannot maintain this form for too long. You are barely holding on.\"","The moment those words came out, many people finally noticed Selene’s condition.","Her fingers were indeed trembling slightly. Her breathing had become heavier, and although she stood straight with the pride of the Divine Daughter, her aura was no longer as stable as before.","The Pseudo Cosmic Path of Heavenly Luminance Genesis was terrifyingly powerful, but that power came at an equally terrifying cost. It could overwhelm most enemies in a short period of time, yet if the first few attacks failed to secure victory, the burden would turn against Selene herself.","Caroline’s expression became serious. \"He is right. Her path is weakening.\"","Seraphine’s face changed. \"Divine Daughter...\"","Fin’s expression also became ugly, because the confidence he had felt when Selene unleashed her strongest path had disappeared the moment Max emerged from the dust without a single injury.","Even after being bound by the roots of the Witch God Tree and struck directly by Selene’s strongest attack, Max was still standing there unharmed, covered in golden-black dragon scales, while Selene was the one who had exhausted a great amount of power.","Selene gritted her teeth.","\"Do not act as if this is over.\"","Her voice was cold, but there was now a trace of strain hidden inside it. She raised both hands again, and the weakened Heavenly Luminance Genesis behind her trembled violently as she forcefully tried to gather another wave of golden-white radiance.","The twelve halos around her reappeared, though they were no longer as solid as before, and sacred weapons of light began to form inside them once more. Even in her weakened state, Selene still refused to retreat.","She was the Divine Daughter of the second faction. She had been trained by the Bloodline Hall and the ancestors. She could not accept defeat before so many geniuses, especially not against Caelira’s son.","Max looked at her and shook his head slightly.","\"You should have stopped.\"","Selene’s eyes flashed with anger. \"I have not lost.\"","\"Then I will make it clearer.\"","Just as Max said those words, his Vein of Speed came to life.","The air around him twisted.","The next instant, his figure vanished from where he stood.","Selene’s pupils contracted.","Fast.","Too fast.","Even with her Heavenly Luminance Genesis still active, even with her golden eyes strengthened by her royal bloodline, she could barely catch the trace of Max’s movement. One moment he was standing several dozen meters away, and in the next, he had appeared right before her, the golden-black scales on his body reflecting the dim light of her collapsing Pseudo Cosmic Path.","His speed was not just ordinary movement. It was the explosive burst of the Vein of Speed combined with his terrifying physical foundation, making him cross the distance like a dragon tearing through space.","Selene reacted instantly.","Despite her shock, her combat instinct was worthy of the Divine Daughter.","A radiant shield formed in front of her chest. Then a second shield appeared. Then a third. Golden-white light surged around her, forming overlapping barriers shaped like divine lotus petals, sacred mirrors, and bloodline runic circles. The remnants of Heavenly Luminance Genesis also gathered around her body, trying to turn the space between her and Max into a protected domain of light.","But Max was faster.","The moment he appeared before her, the Vein of Strength awakened inside his body.","Boom!","His muscles tightened beneath the golden-black dragon scales, and the pressure released from his flesh alone caused the light around Selene to shake violently.","Then five thousand Draconic Essences erupted through him at the same time, pouring into his arm like the condensed might of an ancient dragon. The power gathered in his fist was devastating, heavy, and brutally simple, without the elegance of sword arts or the mystic complexity of Pseudo Cosmic Paths.","It was pure destruction.","Selene’s expression changed completely.","\"Wait...\"","Max punched.","Bang!","His fist slammed into Selene’s defensive shield.","The first radiant barrier exploded instantly.","The second shattered before it could even release its full power.","The third cracked apart like thin glass beneath a mountain’s weight.","The divine lotus petals broke. The sacred mirrors burst. The bloodline runic circles collapsed one after another, and the remaining light of Heavenly Luminance Genesis was crushed under the overwhelming combination of the Vein of Strength and five thousand Draconic Essences.","Selene’s eyes widened in disbelief as every defense she had raised was destroyed in a single instant.","Then Max’s fist reached her.","The impact struck her body head-on.","For a fraction of a second, the entire battlefield became silent.","Selene’s golden eyes stared at Max from only a few inches away, still filled with shock, unwillingness, and disbelief. She had never imagined that after revealing Heavenly Luminance Genesis, after using one of the strongest Pseudo Cosmic Paths of the second faction, after forcing Max to reveal his dragon scales, she would be taken out by one punch.","But Max’s power had already passed through every defense she possessed, and there was nothing left to protect her.","Her body shattered into light.","Golden cracks spread across her form.","Then, with a burst of radiant fragments, Selene Vaeloria, the Divine Daughter of the second faction, disappeared from the battlefield and turned into a dense stream of Killing Points that surged toward Max.","The golden light vanished.","Her Heavenly Luminance Genesis collapsed.","The sacred palaces, divine rivers, sun wheel, and radiant halos all broke apart like an illusion being destroyed by force, leaving only scattered motes of light drifting through the air before they faded completely.","For a long moment, no one spoke.","The second faction elves stared blankly at the empty place where Selene had stood.","Seraphine’s face turned deathly pale.","Fin took an unconscious step back.","Caroline, Jessica, Nancy, and the third faction elves were equally stunned, even though they had already seen Max do impossible things inside Witch God Valley.","This was different. Selene was not Lumine. She was not Arnold. She was not even Seraphine or Fin. She was the Divine Daughter, one of the strongest geniuses of the second faction, yet Max had ended her the moment he chose to stop playing defense.","Rosaline’s eyes narrowed deeply.","Morgana’s expression became much more serious.","Kaiden Voidmere remained silent, but the space around him rippled once.","Orion Starfall let out a slow breath, and the excitement in his eyes grew even stronger.","At the center of everyone’s gaze, Max slowly lowered his fist.","The golden-black dragon scales still covered his body, and faint seven-colored lightning flickered around him. The small cursed eye attached to his left shoulder blinked silently, as if it too had witnessed the fall of the Divine Daughter.","Dragonheart remained in his other hand, but he had not even needed to use it to finish Selene."]},{"number":1784,"title":"Chapter 1784: Three Moves to Morgana!","paragraphs":["The entire base of the Witch God Tree fell into a silence so heavy that even the cursed wind seemed to stop moving.","Selene was gone.","The Divine Daughter of the second faction, the golden-haired genius trained by the Bloodline Hall and guided by the ancestors, the young woman who had unleashed the terrifying Pseudo Cosmic Path known as Heavenly Luminance Genesis, had been destroyed by a single punch after Max decided to close the distance.","It had not been a desperate struggle where both sides exhausted everything. Max had simply used the Vein of Speed to appear before her, activated the Vein of Strength, poured five thousand Draconic Essences into his fist, and shattered her defenses along with her body.","Rosaline stared at the empty space where Selene had disappeared, and for the first time since arriving at the base of the Witch God Tree, her calm expression showed clear shock. She had known Max was dangerous.","She had come here precisely because of the terrifying sword aura he had left behind near the neutral city, but seeing him kill Selene in one punch was something else entirely.","Selene was not some unknown genius. She was one of the strongest names among the younger generation of the elven race, and even Rosaline would have needed to treat her seriously if they fought. Yet Max had ended her after enduring her strongest Pseudo Cosmic Path attack without injury.","The young man standing beside Rosaline also looked stunned. \"Princess... he killed Selene Vaeloria.\"","Rosaline did not answer immediately.","Her gaze remained fixed on Max’s golden-black dragon scales, then shifted to the faint seven-colored lightning still flickering around him, then finally moved to Dragonheart in his other hand.","The strange thing was that Max had still not released the sword aura that had originally drawn her here. Even after fighting Selene, even after being ambushed by Morgana, even after killing the Divine Daughter, he had relied on other powers.","That realization made Rosaline’s shock turn into something deeper.","’He still has not used that sword path,’ Rosaline thought, her eyes narrowing slightly. ’Just how many hidden cards does he have?’","Morgana Starveil was also silent.","Her earlier mocking smile had vanished after Selene’s death. The witch from Stellar Templar stared at Max with narrowed purple eyes, and although she quickly regained her composure, the brief stiffness in her expression had already revealed that she had not expected Selene to fall so suddenly.","Kaiden Voidmere’s gaze remained calm, but the space around him rippled faintly, as if his body had instinctively reacted to Max’s burst of speed.","Orion Starfall, on the other hand, looked excited, but even his excitement was mixed with caution now. Max had just shown that if he wanted to end a fight quickly, his close-range killing power was terrifying.","The second faction elves were in even worse condition.","Seraphine’s face had become pale to the point of looking bloodless. Fin no longer had any desire to speak. The other elves stared at Max as if looking at a monster in human form, because the person they had trusted the most, the person they believed could suppress Max, had been turned into Killing Points before their eyes.","The confidence created by their numbers, formations, and bloodline suppression talismans cracked apart at that moment.","Caroline, Jessica, Nancy, and the third faction elves were equally shaken, but their shock carried a completely different emotion.","Max did not pay attention to the silence around him.","He slowly turned his head.","His gaze moved away from the place where Selene had died and landed on Morgana Starveil. \"Let us finish what you started, shall we?\"","Morgana heard him and immediately sneered.","\"Humph, do you really think if you can handle Selene, you can also kill me?\" Morgana said, her voice sharp with cold arrogance. \"You have got it all wrong.\"","Her words broke the silence and made many people look at her.","Even after seeing Selene die, Morgana still did not step back. Violet starlight gathered around her body, and the crystal charms floating beside her began spinning faster, forming faint circles of witchcraft power around her.","Unlike Selene, who fought with open radiance and overwhelming bloodline power, Morgana’s strength was strange, hidden, and poisonous.","She was a witch from Stellar Templar, one of the seven strongest first-rate forces of the Divine Realm, and her methods were not meant to be fair, beautiful, or direct. They were meant to make enemies die without understanding how they had been trapped.","Max smiled lightly.","\"If it were the real world, I would have surely killed you by now in pure rage,\" he said calmly. \"I hate sneak attackers the most.\"","Morgana’s eyes narrowed.","The air around her became colder.","Max continued arrogantly, \"But since this is a battle royale, I will allow you three moves.\"","The moment those words came out, the expressions of everyone present changed again.","Rosaline’s pupils tightened slightly.","Caroline was stunned.","Nancy looked at Max with surprise.","Orion Starfall’s eyes widened, then he suddenly laughed. \"Three moves? He is even more arrogant than I thought.\"","Kaiden Voidmere remained expressionless, but his gaze became much sharper.","Morgana stared at Max for a moment, then her lips curled into a cold smile. \"You will allow me three moves?\"","Her voice was filled with disbelief and mockery, but beneath that mockery, a trace of anger had clearly appeared. She was Morgana Starveil, one of the strongest geniuses of Stellar Templar. People feared her curses, her witchcraft, her fate-reading, and her ability to control a battlefield from the shadows. Yet Max was speaking as if she were someone he could casually test, tolerate, and then cut down whenever he pleased.","Max raised Dragonheart slightly.","The seven-colored lightning around him slowly faded, and in its place, a quieter and more terrifying sword aura began to stir. It was not fully released yet, but the moment it appeared, Rosaline’s expression changed. She recognized it. This was the very aura that had made her come all the way here.","Max looked at Morgana and spoke in an even calmer voice.","\"If you cannot kill me in three moves, my sword will sever your existence in two.\"","The battlefield went completely still.","The word sever made Seraphine and Fin instinctively tremble.","They had felt that sword path before. They knew what it meant. They have experienced it themselves. No matter how hard they tried, they simply couldn’t get past the severing power of Max’s sword.","Morgana’s smile stiffened for a heartbeat.","Then her expression turned cold and hateful.","\"You are truly courting death, Max Morgan.\"","Max’s smile did not disappear.","\"First move,\" he said.","Morgana’s eyes flashed with killing intent.","The violet charms around her body suddenly stopped spinning.","Then, one by one, they cracked open, releasing threads of purple starlight that spread into the air like a spiderweb woven from fate and curse power. At the same time, the roots beneath the Witch God Tree trembled again, and faint witch runes appeared across the ground around Max.","Rosaline stared at the scene with a serious expression, still shocked by Max’s arrogance but unwilling to blink.","Morgana was not Selene.","She would not fight openly if there was a more vicious way to win.","And now Max had given her three moves.","Whether that was confidence or madness, everyone was about to find out."]},{"number":1785,"title":"Chapter 1785: Witch Attacks!","paragraphs":["Morgana’s killing intent spread silently.","Unlike Selene’s golden radiance, Morgana’s power did not erupt in a bright and majestic manner. It seeped into the battlefield like poison entering water.","The violet charms around her body cracked one after another, and thin threads of purple starlight stretched outward, connecting to the roots of the Witch God Tree, the scattered pieces of cursed bark, the remnants of Selene’s shattered light, and even the dust floating in the air. In the eyes of ordinary people, it looked beautiful. In the eyes of those who understood witchcraft, it was terrifying.","A witch was most dangerous when she attacked first with preparation.","Everyone in the Divine Realm knew this.","Witches of Stellar Templar did not fight like ordinary cultivators. They did not always compete in strength, speed, or direct power. They studied curses, fate, soul marks, bloodline weaknesses, spiritual threads, and the hidden connections between people and the world around them.","Once a witch was given time to prepare, she could turn the environment into a trap, turn the enemy’s shadow into a prison, and turn the opponent’s own aura into the medium of a curse. Many geniuses who could fight warriors stronger than themselves had died miserably after allowing a witch to move first.","And Max had just given Morgana three moves.","Rosaline stared at the battlefield without blinking. \"He is too confident.\"","Kaiden Voidmere said quietly, \"Or perhaps he wants to see her strongest methods.\"","Orion Starfall grinned, but even he did not laugh this time. \"Either way, letting Morgana Starveil attack three times without interruption is something most people would never dare to do.\"","Morgana heard their words and smiled coldly.","\"First move.\"","The witch raised one finger.","The purple starlight threads around the battlefield suddenly tightened.","\"Stellar Witchcraft, Thousand-Fate Needle Burial.\"","The moment she spoke, countless violet needles appeared in the air around Max. They were not ordinary needles made of energy. Each one was formed from curse power, star divination, and a faint thread of fate.","They did not simply aim at Max’s body. They aimed at the openings in his aura, the tiny pauses between his breaths, the flickers of energy around his joints, and even the spiritual rhythm hidden beneath his dragon scales.","The attack covered every direction, leaving no space to dodge, and more importantly, the needles seemed to adjust themselves according to Max’s movements before he even moved.","Jessica’s face turned pale. \"They are predicting his movement.\"","Caroline’s heart tightened. \"No. They are not predicting. They are using the connection between his aura and the battlefield to guide the attack.\"","Morgana’s smile became cruel.","The Thousand-Fate Needles descended.","Max stood still.","The golden-black dragon scales covering his body gleamed faintly, and the little cursed eye on his left shoulder blinked once as if watching the violet rain fall around him.","Max did not use Divine King Punishment. He did not use the Vein of Speed to escape. He did not even raise Dragonheart at first. He simply allowed the countless violet needles to close in until they were only a short distance away from his body.","Only then did he move.","Dragonheart turned in his hand.","A thin sword circle appeared around him.","It was not a wide slash. It was not a grand technique. It was one simple rotation of the blade, but the moment it formed, a quiet and emotionless sword intent spread outward. The violet needles entering that sword circle began to lose their direction.","Their fate threads were severed. Their curse guidance was cut. Their connection to Morgana, to the Witch God Tree, and to the battlefield itself was sliced apart cleanly.","Needle after needle fell apart.","The first layer dissolved into starlight.","The second layer shattered into dust.","The third layer collapsed before touching his scales.","Within a breath, the Thousand-Fate Needle Burial had vanished.","Max remained exactly where he was, unharmed.","Morgana’s eyes narrowed.","The surrounding geniuses stared silently.","Even Rosaline’s gaze became sharper. She had finally felt it clearly now. That terrifying sword aura, that emotionless severing power, was truly coming from Max. He had not relied on the Sword of the Sword Sovereign alone. It was his own path.","\"He is strong!\" Even Orion and Kaiden were a little surprised sensing Max’s sword aura.","Max lowered Dragonheart slightly.","\"Second move,\" he said calmly.","Morgana’s expression turned colder.","She had not expected the first move to kill Max. But she had expected it to test the weakness in his defense, leave a faint curse mark, or at least force him to reveal instability. Yet Max had severed the fate-guidance of her attack so cleanly that the entire technique had collapsed before it could touch him. It was as if her witchcraft had met something that did not care about its hidden structure and simply cut the connection supporting it.","\"Good,\" Morgana said softly. \"Then let me see if you can cut this too.\"","She raised both hands this time.","The ground beneath Max darkened.","His shadow stretched unnaturally, then split into many black shapes. Each shadow rose from the ground like a thin, twisted figure, and every one of them had Max’s outline. The shadows opened their eyes, revealing small violet pupils similar to the witch marks Morgana used. At the same time, a huge starry circle appeared above Max’s head, while the roots of the Witch God Tree beneath him pulsed with cursed light.","\"Stellar Witchcraft, Mirror Curse of the Seven Dead Shadows.\"","The seven shadows moved at once.","One attacked his body.","One attacked his bloodline.","One attacked his soul.","One attacked his senses.","One attacked his movement.","One attacked his energy flow.","And the last one attacked the cursed eye on his shoulder, trying to use the Witch’s curse mark as a bridge to drag the entire curse deeper into Max’s existence.","Caroline’s expression changed completely. \"Max, careful! She is trying to use the Witch’s mark against you.\"","For the first time, Nancy’s hand tightened around her sword with real anxiety.","A witch using an existing curse as a medium was far more dangerous than creating a curse from nothing. The little eye attached to Max had already proven impossible to remove or destroy with brute force. If Morgana managed to connect to it, then even Max’s dragon scales might not be able to protect him fully.","Morgana’s eyes flashed with cold delight.","The seven shadows reached Max.","The one targeting the cursed eye arrived first.","But just as its shadowy hand touched the little eye, something unexpected happened.","The little eye blinked.","A faint red-black ripple spread from it.","The shadow froze for an instant.","Max looked down slightly, and his expression remained calm.","\"You chose the wrong bridge.\""]},{"number":1786,"title":"Chapter 1786: Her Three Moves!","paragraphs":["Black flames suddenly erupted from his shoulder, wrapping around the cursed eye without burning it. At the same time, seven-colored lightning flickered once around his body, and the golden-black dragon scales released a deep draconic pressure.","The shadow trying to touch the curse mark began twisting violently, as if the Witch’s curse itself refused Morgana’s control. Before Morgana could react, Max lifted his left hand and crushed the frozen shadow with raw physical pressure.","Then Dragonheart moved again.","This time, Max slashed seven times.","Each slash was short, accurate, and merciless.","The first shadow was severed at the neck.","The second was split from shoulder to waist.","The third was pierced through the forehead.","The fourth had its violet eyes cut apart.","The fifth was cut through the knees.","The sixth was divided at the core where its curse threads gathered.","The seventh, the one that had tried to touch the Witch’s mark, was cut last. Max’s blade passed through it silently, and the shadow broke apart into red-black sparks and violet dust.","The Mirror Curse of the Seven Dead Shadows collapsed.","The blackened ground returned to normal.","The starry circle above Max shattered.","Morgana’s face finally changed.","This time, she could not hide it.","Max had not merely defended against the curse. He had broken every part of it and even used the strange resistance of the Witch’s own mark to ruin her attempt to control it. The very curse she had wanted to exploit had refused to become her tool.","Max looked at her calmly.","\"Third move.\"","The words were simple, but they struck Morgana’s pride like a slap.","The witch from Stellar Templar clenched her fingers.","Her purple eyes became icy, and the playful cruelty on her face disappeared completely. The first move had been cut. The second had failed. She had one move left, and everyone was watching.","Rosaline, Kaiden, Orion, Selene’s remaining faction members, Caroline’s group, and even the second faction elves who hated Max were all waiting to see whether Morgana Starveil, one of Stellar Templar’s strongest geniuses, could do anything to him after being given three prepared moves.","Morgana took a slow breath.","Then she bit her finger.","A drop of purple-red blood appeared.","The moment that blood fell into the air, the sky above the Witch God Tree darkened. Stars appeared in the daytime gloom, one after another, forming a vast constellation shaped like a closed eye. The air became cold.","The giant roots beneath the battlefield trembled. The cursed remnants of Witch God Valley stirred in the distance, and countless invisible threads gathered around Max, connecting to his footprints, his breath, his sword aura, the lightning traces left from his battle with Selene, and the tiny fragments of power that had spread from his dragon scales.","Morgana’s voice became low and dangerous.","\"Stellar Witchcraft, Star-Coffin Curse of the Nameless Witch.\"","A coffin made of starlight and curse runes formed around Max.","It did not close from the outside.","It formed directly around him, using the traces he had left in the battlefield as anchors. Violet chains wrapped around the coffin, and ancient witch symbols appeared across its surface.","The moment it manifested, Max felt a force trying to bury his body, seal his energy, silence his soul, and erase his name from the battlefield. It was not a simple damaging technique. It was a burial curse, one meant to trap the target between star fate and witchcraft until their existence weakened enough to be killed.","Morgana’s face was pale after using it, but her eyes were filled with cold confidence.","\"This is my third move,\" she said. \"Let me see you walk out of this unscathed.\"","The Star-Coffin Curse closed.","Boom!","Violet starlight surged like a tide.","The coffin swallowed Max completely.","For several breaths, no one could see him. Only the giant coffin stood in the middle of the battlefield, covered in countless curse runes. The pressure it released made even the second faction elves retreat. Caroline’s face became pale, Jessica looked terrified, and Nancy’s eyes were filled with concern.","Even Rosaline, Kaiden, and Orion looked serious because this was clearly no ordinary witchcraft. Morgana had used blood as a price, the battlefield traces as anchors, and the lingering cursed aura of the Witch God Tree as support.","This was exactly why witches were feared.","When they attacked first with preparation, they were the deadliest.","The coffin trembled once.","Then again.","Morgana smiled faintly despite her pale face.","But the smile lasted only a moment.","A crack appeared on the coffin.","Then another.","A thin sword light leaked out from within, not bright, not violent, but quiet enough to make everyone’s heart turn cold. The crack widened. The violet chains broke one after another. The curse runes on the coffin started vanishing, not because they were being destroyed by brute force, but because the connection holding them together was being severed from within.","Morgana’s pupils shrank.","\"No...\"","The coffin split open.","Max walked out.","He was completely unscathed.","His golden-black dragon scales remained flawless. His aura had not weakened. His eyes were calm, and Dragonheart rested in his hand with faint traces of Emotion Severing Path lingering along its edge. The Star-Coffin Curse collapsed behind him, breaking into starlight and dust that scattered into the air like the remains of a failed funeral.","The entire battlefield went silent.","Rosaline stared at Max with clear shock.","Kaiden’s expression finally changed slightly.","Orion’s grin slowly returned, but now it carried genuine amazement.","Seraphine and Fin looked as if they had seen a nightmare.","Caroline exhaled shakily, relief flooding her face.","Jessica stared at Max with wide eyes.","Nancy whispered, \"He came out... without even a scratch.\"","Everyone understood what that meant.","Morgana had not been ambushed. She had not been rushed. She had not been forced to defend. Max had given her three moves, and she had used three of her strongest prepared witchcraft techniques.","For a witch of Stellar Templar, that should have been the most dangerous situation for any opponent. When a witch attacked first with preparation, even stronger enemies could die without touching her.","Yet Max had defended against all three.","He had walked out unscathed.","Max stopped several steps away from Morgana and looked at her calmly.","\"Three moves are over.\"","Morgana’s face turned pale.","The violet charms around her trembled faintly, and for the first time, true fear flickered in her eyes.","Max raised Dragonheart.","His voice remained calm.","\"Now it is my turn.\"","Morgana’s face turned pale the moment Max raised Dragonheart.","The confidence she had displayed earlier, the mocking arrogance she had used when she sneered about the rules of the battle royale, and the cruel amusement that had filled her eyes when she bound Max with the roots of the Witch God Tree were all gone now. She had used three of her strongest witchcraft moves with preparation, and each one had failed.","Worse than that, Max had not merely survived them. He had walked out without a single injury, as if her curses, fate needles, shadow mirrors, and star coffin had been nothing more than interesting tricks placed before his sword.","Now it was his turn."]},{"number":1787,"title":"Chapter 1787: Max’s One Attack!","paragraphs":["Morgana understood that better than anyone.","The violet charms around her body began spinning wildly, and her hands moved so quickly that they left trails of purple afterimages in the air. One defensive spell after another appeared around her, forming layers so densely packed that the space between her and Max became a fortress of witchcraft.","A curtain of starlight unfolded first, then a circular barrier made of thirteen witch runes appeared inside it. After that came a veil of purple mist, a mirror formed from cursed moonlight, a cage of black roots summoned from the Witch God Tree, a shield made from condensed fate threads, and finally a strange starry doll that floated before her like a substitute body.","She was desperate.","Everyone could see it.","Morgana Starveil, one of the strongest geniuses of Stellar Templar, the witch who had made so many people wary simply by appearing at the battlefield, was now using every defensive method she could gather in the short moment before Max attacked. She did not even bother pretending to be calm anymore.","Her pride had been pushed aside by survival instinct. Her fingers trembled as she formed seals, and her purple eyes remained locked on Dragonheart as if the sword in Max’s hand was no longer a weapon, but the edge of death itself.","\"Stellar Witchcraft, Thirteen Star Sanctuary.\"","A barrier of thirteen rotating stars appeared around her.","\"Mirror Curse, False Body Reflection.\"","Three illusory Morganas stepped out from her body and stood around her.","\"Fate Veil, Life-Thread Reversal.\"","Countless thin purple threads wrapped around her true body, trying to redirect any fatal attack toward the false reflections.","\"Witch Root Coffin, Guardian Form.\"","The roots of the Witch God Tree rose again, this time not to bind Max, but to protect Morgana in a thick, twisting wall of cursed wood.","She was fast.","She was skilled.","She was indeed worthy of being one of Stellar Templar’s strongest geniuses. In only a few breaths, she had created more defensive layers than most geniuses could break through with their strongest attack.","Each layer carried different properties. Some blocked physical strikes, some resisted energy, some twisted curses, some redirected fate, some concealed her true body, and some tried to confuse the enemy’s senses. Against any ordinary opponent, this defense would have been enough to make them hesitate, waste strength, or fall into another hidden trap.","But Max did not hesitate.","The seven-colored lightning around him faded completely.","The draconic pressure around his golden-black scales also became quiet.","Even the air around him seemed to lose its movement.","Then the Emotion Severing Path descended.","It did not arrive like thunder.","It did not spread like fire.","It did not roar like a dragon.","It fell upon the battlefield in absolute silence.","The moment Max activated the Emotion Severing Path, the atmosphere at the base of the Witch God Tree changed in a way that made every observer feel a chill sink into their bones.","The anger, fear, excitement, hatred, and killing intent filling the battlefield all seemed to dim at once, as if an invisible blade had passed through the hearts of everyone present and cut away the emotions feeding their thoughts.","Rosaline’s pupils contracted. Kaiden Voidmere’s expression finally changed. Orion Starfall stopped smiling. Caroline clenched her hands tightly. Seraphine and Fin trembled instinctively, because they had already felt this terrifying path once before.","Morgana felt it most clearly.","Her fear did not vanish.","It was severed.","Her panic did not calm.","It was cut away.","The desperation that had been driving her hands suddenly broke apart, and for a fraction of a second, her mind became frighteningly blank. That blankness was more terrifying than fear itself, because it meant Max’s sword had not even moved yet, but his Pseudo Cosmic Path had already reached into the foundation of her battle will.","Max took one step forward.","Dragonheart rose.","\"One sword,\" he said calmly.","Morgana’s eyes widened.","She bit the tip of her tongue and forcefully awakened herself from that terrible stillness. Blood flowed from the corner of her mouth as she poured everything she had into her defenses. The thirteen stars spun faster.","The false bodies shifted positions. The fate threads tightened. The cursed root coffin thickened. The mirror curse glowed. The moonlight shield brightened. Every layer of protection around her reached its strongest state.","Max swung Dragonheart.","There was no grand explosion.","There was no dazzling light.","There was only a thin, silent sword line.","The sword line moved forward.","The curtain of starlight was severed first, not shattered by force but cut away from the power that sustained it. The thirteen-star sanctuary split cleanly, each star losing its connection to the others before falling apart like dead embers.","The false bodies vanished without even being struck directly, because the illusionary link connecting them to Morgana had been severed. The fate threads tried to redirect the attack, but the sword line cut the fate itself, making the reversal meaningless.","The cursed moonlight mirror cracked down the center. The purple mist parted. The Witch God Tree roots that had once caught Max off guard were sliced open as if their will to bind and protect had been removed before the blade touched them.","Layer after layer fell.","Morgana watched the sword line approach.","Her lips parted, and for the first time, there was no mockery in her voice.","\"Impossible...\"","The final starry doll floated in front of her, trying to take the attack in her place.","The sword line passed through it.","The doll did not explode. It simply split in half and lost all meaning as a substitute.","Then the sword reached Morgana.","Dragonheart passed through her from head to waist in one smooth motion.","For a moment, Morgana stood perfectly still.","Her purple eyes stared at Max with disbelief, fear, regret, and hatred, but even those emotions were fading, because the sword that had cut her body had also severed the threads of emotion clinging to her existence.","She had prepared three killing moves. She had used countless defensive layers. She had relied on Stellar Templar’s witchcraft, fate manipulation, curse arts, false bodies, root protection, and star barriers. Yet in front of Max’s Emotion Severing Path, all of it had been useless.","A thin line appeared down the center of her body.","Then Morgana Starveil split in half.","Her body dissolved into fragments of violet starlight and Killing Points before the two halves could even fall to the ground. The witch charms around her shattered one after another, releasing faint ringing sounds that quickly faded into silence.","The roots she had controlled collapsed limply against the ground, and the remaining curse symbols around the battlefield vanished like smoke under the wind.","Morgana was gone.","The strongest genius of Stellar Templar who had sneak-attacked Max from the shadows, mocked him with the excuse of the battle royale, and used three prepared moves against him had been cut down by one sword.","The battlefield remained silent.","Rosaline stared at Max, her eyes filled with shock that she could no longer hide. She had finally seen the sword aura that had drawn her here, but seeing it from afar and witnessing it sever through one of Stellar Templar’s strongest witches were two completely different things.","Kaiden Voidmere’s gaze became deeply solemn. Orion Starfall’s excitement was still there, but now it was mixed with genuine wariness. The second faction elves had become deathly quiet, and Seraphine and Fin looked as if the nightmare they had feared had returned before their eyes.","Caroline slowly exhaled.","Jessica stared at Max with trembling eyes.","Nancy’s expression was complicated, but there was also a strange certainty in her gaze now.","Max lowered Dragonheart.","The Emotion Severing Path slowly faded, but the chilling silence it left behind still lingered over the battlefield. The small cursed eye on his left shoulder blinked once, its red-black pupil staring at the place where Morgana had disappeared.","Max did not look pleased.","He did not look angry either.","He simply turned his gaze toward the remaining geniuses and spoke in a calm voice.","\"Anyone else?\""]},{"number":1788,"title":"Chapter 1788: Kill Yourselves!","paragraphs":["The silence after Morgana’s death did not last for long.","\"You are good, Max Morgan,\" Orion laughed at this moment.","His voice broke the frozen atmosphere at the base of the Witch God Tree, and unlike the others, there was no fear in his eyes. There was shock, yes, and there was also caution, but above both of them was a fierce excitement that made his aura burn even brighter. He looked at Max as if he had finally found something worth remembering in the Cosmic Ascension Conference.","The strongest genius of the Nine Star Court had come here to measure the truth behind the rumors, but after seeing Max destroy Selene, survive Morgana’s three strongest witchcraft moves, and cut Morgana down with a single sword, the answer had already become obvious.","\"But now is not the time for our battle,\" Orion continued, his grin widening. \"I only came here to see if you were really that strong or just overhyped, but you exceeded my expectations.\"","Max looked at him calmly.","Orion crossed his arms and laughed again. \"We will have a battle for sure, but not right now. Until then, I hope you do not get eliminated.\"","With that, the nine stars behind him revolved once. Starlight wrapped around his body, and his figure disappeared from the base of the Witch God Tree, leaving only a faint pressure in the air and a few sparks of star power drifting behind him. His departure was simple, but no one treated it as retreat.","Orion had not left because he was afraid. He had left because he had already gained what he wanted from this place, and his battle with Max had merely been postponed to a better stage.","Kaiden Voidmere remained for a moment longer.","He stared at Max silently, and the space around him rippled gently like water disturbed by a falling leaf. His gaze was not hostile. It was calm, deep, and faintly complicated, especially after he had sensed the familiar aura inside Max’s body during the previous exchanges.","He had not interfered with the battle, and he had not said much before, but now that Morgana and Selene were gone, he finally spoke.","\"Master once said that he had taken in another disciple from a mortal world,\" Kaiden said slowly, \"but he did not mention much about him. However, after looking at you, I feel the disciple he was talking about was you. I can feel the Void Genesis Art inside you.\"","The moment those words fell, Caroline, Nancy, Jessica, and even Rosaline looked at Max with surprise.","Void Genesis Art.","The name itself was enough to carry weight, especially when spoken by Kaiden Voidmere, the strongest genius of the Grand Void Sanctum","Max’s expression did not change much, but his eyes narrowed slightly as he looked at Kaiden. The aura of Void Genesis Art inside him had always been hidden deeply, but Kaiden had still sensed it. That alone proved that this man was not ordinary.","Kaiden continued, \"In that case, you are my junior brother, and I do not wish to fight you unless there is no other choice. I hope to see you around until the end of the first round of the Cosmic Ascension Conference. Until then, see you.\"","After saying that, he gave Max a small nod.","The space behind him folded inward silently, and his figure vanished as if swallowed by an invisible doorway. There was no grand light and no violent fluctuation, yet his departure felt even more mysterious than Orion’s. One moment he was there, and the next, the distance around him had lost meaning and removed him from the battlefield.","Max watched the place where Kaiden had disappeared for a brief moment, then slowly turned his gaze toward the remaining elves from the second faction.","The second faction elves stiffened instantly.","Selene was dead for now. Morgana was gone. Orion had left. Kaiden had left. The only powerful outsiders remaining were Rosaline and her people, and Rosaline had already declared herself an observer.","That meant the second faction elves now had to face Max directly, and after everything they had witnessed, none of them still had the courage to attack him.","Max looked at them calmly.","\"If you do not want me to take action,\" he said, \"kindly kill yourself.\"","The words were spoken in a casual tone, but to the second faction elves, they sounded like a sentence from hell.","For a moment, no one moved.","Then the first elf gritted his teeth, raised his own weapon, and pierced his heart without hesitation. His body dissolved into light and Killing Points, disappearing from the battlefield.","The second followed. Then the third. Then the fourth. In only a few breaths, the remaining second faction elves began committing suicide one after another, choosing to lose one life by their own hands rather than be cut down by Max and possibly suffer a far more terrifying death under his sword path.","The sight shocked everyone.","Even Rosaline’s followers could not hide their disbelief.","These were proud elves from the second faction, many of them geniuses or elite hunters who looked down on others. Yet after Max spoke, they actually killed themselves without daring to resist. It was not because they respected him. It was because they feared him.","Caroline watched them disappear one by one, her expression cold and unreadable.","Jessica’s eyes were filled with hatred, but also relief.","Nancy quietly stood beside Max, her gaze sweeping over the dissolving figures of the second faction elves.","In the end, only Seraphine and Fin remained.","The two of them stood in place, faces pale and twisted with humiliation. They had already died once to Max inside Witch God Valley, and now they were being forced to end themselves again in front of everyone. Seraphine’s eyes burned with hatred, while Fin’s expression was full of resentment and fear. Neither of them wanted to die again, but neither of them dared to attack Max either.","Max’s gaze moved to them.","That was enough.","Seraphine clenched her teeth until blood almost appeared at the corner of her mouth. \"Max, our Divine Son will take revenge for us. Just you wait.\"","Fin also glared at Max and said in a threatening tone, \"The Divine Son is not like us. When he comes, you will understand what true despair means.\""]},{"number":1789,"title":"Chapter 1789: Leaving!","paragraphs":["Max looked at them without any change in expression.","Seraphine and Fin seemed to want to say more, but the pressure in Max’s eyes made them swallow the rest of their words. In the end, both of them raised their weapons and killed themselves at the same time.","Their bodies shattered into golden light and Killing Points before disappearing from the base of the Witch God Tree.","The second faction was gone.","For the first time since Max and the others had descended from Witch God Valley, the battlefield became truly quiet.","Now, only Max, the elves from the third faction, and Rosaline with her people remained.","Rosaline’s gaze remained fixed on Max.","She had watched everything from beginning to end. She had seen him force Orion to postpone the fight, make Kaiden acknowledge him as a possible junior brother, frighten the second faction elves into killing themselves, and stand there as if all of it was natural.","The more she looked at him, the more her original curiosity changed into a far more serious interest. The terrifying sword aura she had chased here was real. The strength behind it was also real. More than that, Max had shown enough power to stand among the strongest geniuses in the first round of the Cosmic Ascension Conference.","Rosaline finally stepped forward.","Her followers immediately became alert, but she raised one hand and stopped them from moving.","Max turned his eyes toward her.","\"Are you done observing?\" he asked.","Rosaline looked at Dragonheart in his hand, then at the faint golden-black scales still fading from his body, and finally at the little cursed eye moving slowly around his left shoulder.","\"For now,\" she said calmly. \"But I have a question.\"","Max said nothing.","Rosaline’s eyes became sharper. \"With your strength, you should already be qualified to compete for one of the great legacies in this conference. Are you aiming for the Sword God Legacy?\"","The moment she said those words, Caroline and Nancy both looked at Max.","Jessica also became quiet.","Rosaline continued before Max answered, \"Or perhaps the War God Legacy? Considering your body strength, your draconic power, your Divine Veins, and the way you crushed Selene’s defenses with one punch, you might have a chance there as well.\"","Max’s expression remained calm, but the air around him changed slightly.","Rosaline noticed it and continued in a measured tone, \"Do not misunderstand me. I am not asking because I want to stop you. I am asking because someone with your strength will not stay unnoticed for long. After what happened here, every major force will begin paying attention to you. The Sword God Palace will not ignore you because of Dragonheart. The elves will not let you go because of Selene. Stellar Templar will remember Morgana’s death. And if you truly aim for one of the supreme legacies, then even Orion and Kaiden may become your opponents sooner or later.\"","Max looked at her quietly.","Rosaline’s tone became more serious. \"So I want to know, Max Morgan. Are you aiming for the Sword God Legacy, the War God Legacy, or something even greater?\"","For a moment, no one spoke.","The base of the Witch God Tree was still ruined from the earlier battles. Shattered roots, broken light fragments, fading curse marks, and traces of seven-colored lightning still covered the battlefield. Max stood at the center of it all, Dragonheart in hand, the cursed eye still circling near his left shoulder, while everyone waited for his answer.","Then Max smiled faintly.","\"Why should I tell you?\"","Rosaline paused.","Max turned slightly, looking toward Caroline and the others as if preparing to leave.","\"I have no obligation to explain my goals to someone who only came to watch.\"","Rosaline’s eyes narrowed slightly, but she did not get angry.","Instead, her interest deepened.","Max glanced back at her and added calmly, \"And just so you know, I have no interest in any of these so called legacies.\"","Rosaline stared at him.","The answer was arrogant.","It was also perfectly in line with everything she had just witnessed.","Rosaline slowly smiled.","\"I see,\" she said softly. \"Then this conference will become very interesting.\"","Max did not respond.","He turned away from her and looked toward Caroline, Jessica, Nancy, and the third faction elves.","\"We are leaving.\"","Caroline nodded, though her eyes were still filled with many emotions after what had happened.","Rosaline did not stop them.","She simply watched Max begin to move, her gaze lingering on his back, Dragonheart, and the strange cursed eye that continued to move around his body like a living mark of Witch God Valley.","The battle at the base of the Witch God Tree had ended.","After leaving the base of the Witch God Tree, Max led Caroline, Jessica, Nancy, and the remaining third faction elves away from that cursed region without stopping.","The journey was much quieter than before. No one spoke much, and even the wind seemed calmer after the chaos they had survived. Behind them, the Witch God Tree slowly disappeared into the distance, its enormous trunk fading into the clouds like a dark pillar connecting heaven and earth.","The cursed eye attached to Max continued moving around his left shoulder and upper arm from time to time, blinking silently as if it had no intention of leaving him. Max still did not pay much attention to it.","As long as it did not restrict his movement, interfere with his battles, or try to attack those around him, he decided to ignore it for now.","In time, they reached a neutral city.","Unlike the deadly silence surrounding Witch God Valley, the neutral city was filled with movement, lights, voices, and cultivators from many races. Tall stone walls surrounded the place, and defensive formations shone faintly above the gates, separating the city from the dangers of the wilderness.","Participants of the Cosmic Ascension Conference moved through the streets in groups, some injured, some excited, some cautious, and some openly watching others as if looking for targets.","This was a temporary safe region, but even here, the atmosphere remained tense because everyone knew that the first round was still ongoing and that safety only existed as long as the rules allowed it.","Max stopped near a quiet street after entering the city.","Caroline looked at him and immediately sensed something from his expression. \"You are leaving.\"","Max nodded.","Jessica’s face changed slightly. \"Already?\"","\"Yes,\" Max said calmly. \"I still have something to do.\"","Caroline’s expression became serious."]},{"number":1790,"title":"Chapter 1790: Genesis Trial!","paragraphs":["Max looked at Caroline and said, \"For now, take care of yourselves.\"","Caroline’s eyes softened slightly.","Max continued, \"The second faction will not stop after what happened. Selene, Seraphine, and Fin all lost lives because of me, and the Divine Son they mentioned will probably come sooner or later. Until then, stay in neutral cities as much as possible. Do not move alone. Do not trust anyone from the second faction. Survive until the end of the first round.\"","The third faction elves behind Caroline listened seriously.","Jessica clenched her fists and nodded. \"We understand.\"","Caroline looked at Max with complicated emotions in her eyes. \"You saved us, Max. If not for you, Jessica and the others would have been taken back, and I would likely have remained trapped inside Witch God Valley until they found another way to capture me. I know you do not like emotional words, so I will not say too much, but I want you to remember one thing. Your mother’s faction is not dead. As long as even a few of us survive, we will stand with you.\"","Max was silent for a brief moment.","Then he nodded. \"Stay alive first. Everything else can wait.\"","Caroline gave a faint smile, though worry still remained in her eyes. \"You too. Do not be careless. You have made too many enemies now.\"","Max looked at the cursed eye that had shifted from his shoulder to hover near his collarbone, then glanced back toward the direction of the Witch God Tree.","\"I know.\"","Nancy stepped forward. \"Do you want me to come with you?\"","Max shook his head. \"No. Stay with them for now. You know more about the elven factions and the neutral cities than they do, and Caroline is still recovering.\"","Nancy hesitated, but after a moment, she nodded. \"Then be careful.\"","Max gave a small nod in response.","For a few seconds, no one moved.","Caroline seemed to want to say something else, perhaps about Caelira, perhaps about the Celestial Thorn Abyss, perhaps about the Divine Son Aurelian Lareth and the stolen bloodline, but in the end, she held back.","This was not the right time. Max had his own path in the Cosmic Ascension Conference, and she knew that if she tried to hold him here out of worry, she would only slow him down.","Max turned away.","Golden light gathered beneath his feet.","Then, without wasting any more time, he rose into the air and flew out of the neutral city.","Caroline, Jessica, Nancy, and the other third faction elves watched him leave until his figure became a streak of light in the sky. The little cursed eye remained attached to him, blinking faintly as it moved around his shoulder, while Dragonheart rested at his side.","The city walls passed beneath him, the streets disappeared behind him, and soon the noise of the neutral city faded into the distance.","Max flew alone.","His destination was clear.","He was heading back toward the region where he had first spawned in this world, the place where the Cosmic Ascension Conference had begun for him, and the place where a trial had been waiting since the very beginning.","Back then, because of insufficient Killing Points, Max had not been able to participate in the trial, but things were completely different now.","At that time, five hundred thousand Killing Points had seemed like a large amount, especially when he had only just entered this world and was still trying to understand the rules of the Cosmic Ascension Conference.","But after everything that had happened since then, he had more than enough now, and if this hidden trial was called the Genesis Trial, then its value was likely far above the cost required to enter.","A few hours later, Max arrived at the broken castle.","The ruins still looked the same as before. Half-collapsed walls stood beneath the dim sky, cracked stone towers leaned at strange angles, and ancient battle marks remained carved into the ground as if some forgotten war had once torn through this place.","Compared to the Witch God Tree, the neutral cities, and the battlefields filled with powerful geniuses, this broken castle looked almost quiet. Yet Max did not underestimate it.","The hidden trial inside this place had been waiting for him from the moment he entered the Eternal Hourglass, and anything labeled by the system in such a way was never ordinary.","Max entered the cave hidden inside the broken castle.","The air in the cave was cold and still, carrying the faint smell of stone dust and ancient energy. His footsteps echoed softly in the narrow passage, while the little cursed eye attached to his left shoulder blinked from time to time, its pupil turning toward the dark walls as if it could sense something hidden in the depths.","Max ignored it and continued walking deeper.","Once he reached deeper into the cave, the system prompt came again.","[Hidden Trial Detected.]","[Genesis Trial]","[Requirement To Enter: 500,000 Killing Points]","[Would You Like To Spend 500,000 Killing Points To Begin The Genesis Trial?]","This time, Max did not think much and accepted the trial.","[500,000 Killing Points Deducted...]","[Current Killing Points: 55.3 Million]","[Entering the Genesis Trial in 10, 9, 8...]","Max looked at the prompt calmly. Even after deducting five hundred thousand Killing Points, he still had fifty-five point three million left, a number that would be enough to make many participants of the Cosmic Ascension Conference lose their minds with envy.","Yet Max was not focused on the number. His attention was on the name of the trial. Genesis Trial. The word Genesis had already appeared in many powerful contexts around him, and every time it did, it seemed to involve something related to origin, creation, foundation, or the beginning of a path.","\"I wonder what benefits will be in this trial,\" Max muttered as he waited for the countdown to reach zero.","[Entering the Genesis Trial in 3, 2, 1...]","Just when the countdown reached one, his figure disappeared from the cave.","Before he knew it, Max appeared in a cubic room.","The room was strange.","It was not large, yet it did not feel small either. The walls, floor, and ceiling were all made of smooth dark-gray cubes fitted together without any visible cracks, and the space inside seemed to shift subtly every time Max looked away.","Around the room, countless cubes of different colors floated silently in the air. Some were red, some blue, some gold, some silver, some black, some white, and some carried colors Max had never seen before, colors that seemed to change depending on the angle from which he looked at them.","Each cube released a faint aura, and although none of them appeared dangerous at first glance, Max could sense that each one contained a different kind of law, energy, or hidden rule.","The room felt less like a battlefield and more like the inside of a massive mechanism.","Max’s eyes narrowed slightly.","But he was not alone in that room.","Four other figures were already there.","And to Max’s surprise, two of them were people he knew."]},{"number":1791,"title":"Chapter 1791: Meeting Two Familiar Figures!","paragraphs":["The two familiar figures were Revona and Tamara.","Revona stood near a floating silver-black cube, her expression as calm and unreadable as it had been in the past. Her eyes, however, were different from ordinary eyes.","They carried a deep void-like radiance, and when Max looked at them, he immediately recognized the familiar power of the Void Origin Eyes. Back during his early days of ascension in the Black Dragon Clan, he had met Revona and seen the strangeness of those eyes with his own vision.","At that time, the Divine Realm had still felt distant, almost unreachable, and the higher stages of the Cosmic Ascension Conference had been something he had only just begun to understand. Yet now, after so many battles, after tearing through demons, elves, geniuses, hidden trials, and dangerous legacies, he had unexpectedly met her again in a place like this.","Revona also looked at Max.","For a moment, even her calm eyes showed faint surprise.","\"Max,\" she said softly. \"long time no see.\"","Max nodded. \"I did not expect to meet you again here.\"","Revona’s gaze moved briefly over his body, on the small cursed eye moving near his left shoulder. A faint change passed through her expression, but she did not ask about it immediately. Perhaps she understood that too many things must have happened to him since they last met, just as too many things must have happened to her.","The second familiar figure was Tamara.","She stood with her arms crossed, her posture firm and domineering, while a heavy battle aura surrounded her like an invisible war drum. She was a war lord of the War God Palace, and compared to Revona’s quiet and mysterious presence, Tamara felt far more direct and oppressive.","Her body seemed built for battle, her eyes carried the confidence of someone who had survived countless life-and-death fights, and the war intent around her was so dense that the floating cubes near her trembled faintly from time to time.","The moment Tamara saw Max, her lips curled into a faint smile.","\"So it really is you,\" she said. \"I heard some ridiculous rumors about a young man called Max Morgan, but I wondered if it was the same person.\"","Max looked at her calmly. \"Depends on which rumors.\"","Tamara laughed. \"The ones where you keep offending powerful forces and somehow continue walking away alive.\"","Max glanced at the cursed eye near his shoulder. \"Some things are harder to walk away from.\"","Tamara’s gaze shifted to the little eye, and even her smile faded slightly. \"That is not something ordinary.\"","\"I know,\" Max replied.","Revona looked at the eye with her Void Origin Eyes for a moment, then her expression became a little more solemn. \"That thing is attached deeper than the body.\"","Max’s eyes narrowed slightly, but before he could ask anything, his attention shifted toward the other two figures in the room.","One of them was a demon.","He was tall, broad-shouldered, and covered in dark bronze armor that looked as though it had been forged from volcanic stone and demon bone. Two curved black horns rose from his head, and crimson markings ran across his neck and jaw like living veins. His aura was violent but controlled, carrying the smell of blood, abyssal fire, and countless battles.","Unlike the demons Max had slaughtered before, this one did not rush to speak or release killing intent. He only stood there, silently watching Max with a pair of dark red eyes that carried sharp interest.","The last figure was a handsome young man with black hair.","He wore a simple black robe without any obvious symbol of a force, and at first glance, he looked almost ordinary compared to the others. His face was calm, his features were handsome, and his eyes were dark and quiet. Yet the moment Max’s gaze landed on him, something inside Max’s instincts reacted.","It was a strange feeling.","For the first time among those of his peers, Max felt as if he was staring into an abyss.","Not a dark pit that could be measured.","Not a void rift that could be sensed with spatial perception.","But a true abyss whose depth was bottomless.","The young man’s aura was not loud like Tamara’s war intent. It was not mysterious like Revona’s Void Origin Eyes. It was not violent like the demon’s bloodline pressure. It was simply deep. Fathomless. Quiet to the point of being terrifying.","Max could not clearly sense its end, and the more his perception tried to measure it, the more it felt as if it was sinking into something endless.","That shocked him.","Max had met many powerful geniuses by now.","Seraphine and Fin had possessed terrifying Pseudo Cosmic Paths. Selene had carried Heavenly Luminance Genesis. Morgana had possessed deadly witchcraft.","Orion Starfall had the overwhelming aura of the Nine Star Court’s strongest genius, and Kaiden Voidmere had the deep, unreachable presence of the Grand Void Sanctum. Yet this black-haired young man gave Max a completely different feeling.","It was not that his aura was exploding outward.","It was that his aura seemed to contain far more than it revealed.","The black-haired young man noticed Max’s gaze and smiled faintly.","\"Hello, I am Ervin.\" He reached out with his hand. \"It’s nice to finally meet you.\"","Max also smiled shook hands with him. \"The pleasure is all mine.\"","At that moment, the floating cubes around the room trembled.","A system prompt appeared before everyone.","[Genesis Trial Initiated.]","[Participants: 5]","[Trial Type: Cooperative And Competitive]","[Objective: Survive The Genesis Cube Sequence And Obtain As Many Genesis Marks As Possible.]","[Warning: Participants May Cooperate, Compete, Or Eliminate One Another.]","[The Trial Will Begin Shortly.]","The moment the prompts appeared, the atmosphere inside the cubic room changed.","Revona’s Void Origin Eyes became deeper.","Tamara’s war intent slowly stirred.","The demon’s crimson markings glowed faintly.","The black-haired young man’s eyes remained calm and unreadable.","Max looked at the system prompt, then at the floating cubes surrounding them. Cooperative and competitive. That meant the Genesis Trial would not simply test strength. It would also test judgment, timing, greed, and trust.","The cubes of different colors began to rotate faster, and a deep mechanical sound echoed from the walls. Then the floor beneath the five participants lit up with countless square patterns, each one forming a path toward a different side of the room.","Max smiled faintly.","\"It seems this trial will be interesting.\""]},{"number":1792,"title":"Chapter 1792: First Trial!","paragraphs":["The floating cubes continued rotating around the cubic room, and the deep mechanical sound echoing from the walls grew heavier with every passing breath.","Max looked at the system prompt calmly, but his mind was already moving.","Cooperative and competitive. That meant the trial would not simply reward the strongest person, nor would it allow someone to rely entirely on the others and pass safely.","If the system had brought five participants into one space, then there had to be a reason, and since the objective was to obtain Genesis Marks, these marks were likely the true reward of the trial.","As if responding to his thoughts, a new prompt appeared before everyone.","[Genesis Trial Structure Confirmed.]","[Total Trials: 3]","[Maximum Genesis Marks Obtainable: 100]","[Trial One: Genesis Cube Labyrinth]","[Trial Type: Teamwork Assessment And Individual Performance Assessment]","[Maximum Genesis Marks Obtainable In Trial One: 30]","[Warning: Failure Of Cooperation May Result In Reduced Genesis Marks Or Immediate Elimination.]","The moment the prompt appeared, the expressions of the five participants changed slightly.","Tamara narrowed her eyes. \"Only thirty marks in the first trial.\"","The demon crossed his thick arms, his dark red eyes flashing with interest. \"That means the later trials will be even more valuable.\"","Revona’s Void Origin Eyes moved across the floating cubes, and her calm voice followed. \"It also means this first trial is likely designed to measure our foundations. If we fight among ourselves too early, all of us may lose marks.\"","The black-haired young man smiled faintly. \"A cooperative trial that still assesses individual performance. That is a clever way to make allies compete without openly betraying each other.\"","The demon gave a sharp grin. \"Since there is cooperation, I think I should share my name. It’s Varkhon.\"","Tamara looked at him briefly. \"A demon genius who gives his name so easily?\"","Varkhon laughed deeply. \"Names are not the dangerous part of me.\"","No one responded to that, because at that moment, the cubic room trembled.","The walls began to separate.","The smooth dark-gray cubes forming the room shifted outward one by one, and the space around them expanded with terrifying speed. The floor broke into hundreds of square platforms floating above an endless void, and the ceiling vanished, revealing a dark sky filled with cubic stars. Pathways of glowing lines stretched between the platforms, but none of them stayed still.","Some moved left and right. Some rotated. Some disappeared for a breath before reappearing in another place. Around the entire space, countless cubes of different colors floated like living mechanisms, each one releasing a different aura.","Then the system prompt appeared again.","[Trial One Begins.]","[Genesis Cube Labyrinth.]","[Objective: Reach The Genesis Gate At The Center Of The Labyrinth.]","[Condition One: At Least Three Participants Must Reach The Gate.]","[Condition Two: Participants Must Prevent The Collapse Of The Labyrinth Core.]","[Condition Three: Individual Contributions Will Be Assessed Separately.]","[Genesis Marks Will Be Distributed According To Cooperation, Combat Performance, Perception, Adaptability, And Survival Contribution.]","As soon as the prompt ended, the far center of the labyrinth lit up.","There, suspended above the void, stood a massive white cube gate. It slowly rotated in the distance, and around it floated rings of smaller cubes moving in complex patterns. Between the five participants and that gate stretched a maze of shifting platforms, cube bridges, rotating walls, and countless hidden dangers.","Tamara let out a breath and tightened her grip around her spear. \"So this is not only about reaching the center.\"","Revona nodded. \"The Labyrinth Core must not collapse. If we rush blindly, the route itself may break.\"","Varkhon cracked his neck. \"Then someone needs to clear the path.\"","Ervin raised one hand, and a long spear appeared in his grasp. The spear was black from shaft to blade, but faint silver lines ran along its edge like veins of abyssal light.","The moment he held it, his entire aura changed. The fathomless feeling around him did not become louder, but it became sharper, as if the bottomless abyss Max had sensed earlier had suddenly revealed a single spear point rising from its depths.","Max’s eyes moved to him for a brief moment.","Ervin noticed his gaze and smiled slightly. \"I am better with a spear.\"","Tamara snorted. \"Then do not fall behind.\"","Her own spear appeared in her hand, long, heavy, and covered with war runes. Compared to Ervin’s quiet abyssal sharpness, Tamara’s spear carried the pressure of a battlefield commander. The moment she gripped it, her war intent surged, and the air around her seemed to fill with invisible soldiers marching beneath a banner of conquest.","Revona stood quietly, her Void Origin Eyes glowing faintly.","Varkhon clenched his fists, and the crimson markings across his arms burned brighter.","Max did not draw Dragonheart immediately. Instead, he activated his Dimensional Sovereign Body.","The world changed in his perception.","The cubic labyrinth unfolded before him in countless layers. Every platform, every moving bridge, every rotating cube, every hidden spatial crack, and every concealed attack mechanism appeared within his senses. There was no blind spot. His vision did not rely only on his eyes.","Space itself became his field of awareness, and through that field, he could see through almost everything. He could sense which platforms were real, which were traps, which cubes would attack, which paths would collapse, and which invisible lines connected the labyrinth to its core.","Max’s expression became serious.","\"This place has hidden attack sequences,\" he said. \"Do not step on the blue-black platforms. They are linked to spatial blades. The red cubes on the left will release heat beams if we cross too slowly. The silver platforms ahead are safe, but only for three breaths after someone touches them.\"","Tamara glanced at him. \"You can see that?\"","Max nodded. \"I can see more than that. Follow my route.\"","No one argued.","Even Varkhon, who looked like the type who preferred smashing through trials, only grinned and said, \"Then lead.\"","Max moved first.","The moment his foot touched the first silver platform, the labyrinth awakened.","Hundreds of cubes around them lit up at once, and sharp rays of light shot out from multiple directions. Max’s Dimensional Sovereign Body captured every trajectory before the beams fully formed, and he immediately shifted his position while giving short commands.","\"Tamara, left side. Three attacks.\"","Tamara moved without hesitation.","Her spear swept outward, and three incoming cube spears were smashed aside with precise and brutal force. Each strike carried war intent, and every time her spear moved, the air trembled as if an army had advanced behind her. She did not merely block the attacks. She crushed them with dominance, then stepped forward and anchored her spear into the platform, stabilizing it just as it began to tilt.","\"Varkhon, break the red cube above.\"","The demon laughed and leapt upward.","His body shot into the air like a cannonball. A red cube opened above them, preparing to release a beam of destructive heat, but Varkhon reached it first. He did not use a complicated technique. He simply punched it. The impact produced a thunderous explosion, and the red cube shattered into burning fragments that scattered into the void.","Varkhon landed heavily on another platform, causing cracks to spread beneath his feet, but he grabbed the edge of the platform with one hand and forcefully held it in place before it could collapse.","\"Revona, right side. Hidden void pulse.\"","Revona’s eyes glowed brighter.","A transparent wave emerged from a dark cube to her right, completely invisible to ordinary perception, but Revona saw it clearly with her Void Origin Eyes. She did not dodge. She simply turned her gaze toward it.","The moment the wave entered the range of her eyes, it began to fade, as if its existence had been erased from the trial itself. The attack that should have struck the group from the side turned into nothingness without making a sound.","Max’s eyes sharpened slightly.","Revona’s Void Origin Eyes were still as strange as he remembered.","No, they were stronger than before.","’Her ability to nullify all attacks is terrifying!’ Max thought silently."]},{"number":1793,"title":"Chapter 1793: Working Together!","paragraphs":["The labyrinth continued shifting.","Platforms moved. Bridges twisted. Cubes opened and closed like mechanical beasts. Attacks came from above, below, behind, and even from angles that should not have existed. Yet with Max standing at the center of the formation, no attack truly came as a surprise. His Dimensional Sovereign Body gave him a complete view of the battlefield, and he guided the group through the shifting maze with calm precision.","\"Ervin, forward.\"","Ervin moved.","His spear thrust out once.","The motion was simple.","Too simple.","But the result was terrifying.","A line of black-silver spear light pierced through seven floating cubes in a row. Each cube had been moving at a different speed and angle, yet his spear strike passed through all of them perfectly, as if he had seen the exact point where their paths would align before they aligned.","The cubes split open silently, and the broken mechanisms inside them fell into the void. His spearmanship was monstrous, not because it was flashy, but because it was absurdly accurate. Every thrust carried depth. Every sweep contained hidden force. Every step placed him at the perfect range to attack again.","Tamara saw it and smiled coldly. \"Not bad.\"","Ervin smiled back. \"You are not bad either.\"","The next wave came stronger.","A massive cube wall rose before them, blocking the route, while dozens of smaller cubes around it opened and released chains of light toward the group. At the same time, the platforms behind them began collapsing one after another, forcing them to move forward or fall.","Max immediately understood the problem.","\"If that wall stays, the Labyrinth Core will lose stability,\" he said. \"We break it together.\"","Tamara’s war intent erupted first.","\"Then move.\"","She rushed forward, spear raised, and the war runes on her weapon blazed. Her spear struck the cube wall with enough force to make the entire structure tremble. Varkhon arrived beside her in the next instant, his fist smashing into the same point with raw demonic strength. The combined impact cracked the outer layer of the wall, but the wall immediately began repairing itself.","Revona’s Void Origin Eyes flashed.","The repairing energy flowing through the cracks vanished.","Ervin’s spear then thrust into the weakened center, and a black-silver line pierced deep into the wall.","Max followed last.","He raised his hand, and instead of using overwhelming force, he struck the exact cubic node that his Dimensional Sovereign Body had identified as the wall’s control point. The moment his attack landed, the entire wall stopped repairing itself.","Tamara shouted and thrust her spear again.","Varkhon roared and punched with both fists.","Ervin’s spear flashed three times in a row.","Revona erased the final layer of defensive energy.","The cube wall exploded.","Fragments flew in every direction, but Max had already seen the path of the debris and guided everyone through the safe gap before the broken cubes transformed into another attack sequence.","Their cooperation was not perfect because none of them truly trusted one another yet, but all five of them were too strong and too experienced to miss the rhythm of battle once it appeared. Max perceived. Tamara suppressed. Varkhon destroyed. Revona erased. Ervin pierced.","Together, they advanced.","The system’s cubic stars above them glowed brighter.","[Team Coordination Increased.]","[Labyrinth Core Stability: 87%]","[Individual Performance Assessment Ongoing.]","More attacks came after that.","A rain of golden cubes turned into falling blades.","Tamara met them head-on, spinning her spear so violently that a storm of war intent formed above the group.","A black cube released a wave of devouring darkness.","Varkhon stepped forward and tore through it with both hands, roaring as his raw strength ripped the darkness apart.","A silver cube created false platforms to mislead them.","Revona looked once, and the illusions were reduced to nothing under her Void Origin Eyes.","A rotating prism cube released attacks from blind angles.","Max saw them all before they arrived, moved through the group like a commander on a battlefield, and redirected everyone with short, precise instructions.","A line of indigo cubes formed a killing corridor.","Ervin stepped forward alone, his spear moving so quickly that it became a black-silver rain. Every thrust struck the core of a cube, and every pierced cube shut down instantly.","His spearmanship made even Max feel that this young man was far more dangerous than his calm appearance suggested. It was not only skill. It was depth. His spear carried something abyssal, something that seemed to fall endlessly even after reaching the target.","The closer they came to the Genesis Gate, the more dangerous the labyrinth became.","The final stretch consisted of nine floating platforms arranged in a broken spiral, and each platform could only hold one person at a time.","Above them, a massive cube constellation formed, preparing to release a combined attack. Below them, the void began rising like dark water, devouring the platforms behind them. At the center, the white cube gate rotated slowly, only a short distance away.","Max’s Dimensional Sovereign Body spread to its limit.","He saw the sequence.","The trial wanted to separate them, test them individually, and then force them to reconnect at the gate.","\"Each of us takes one path,\" Max said quickly. \"Do not slow down. The attacks will target your weakness.\"","Tamara grinned. \"Good.\"","Varkhon laughed. \"Finally.\"","Revona remained calm. \"Understood.\"","Ervin looked at Max. \"And the gate?\"","Max’s eyes locked onto the core mechanism behind the Genesis Gate. \"I will open it when all of you reach the final platform.\"","The five moved at once.","Tamara’s path was filled with heavy cube soldiers wielding square shields and spears. She charged through them like a war lord leading an invisible army, her spear breaking shields, crushing formation lines, and forcing open a route with overwhelming battle intent.","Varkhon’s path was a collapsing series of platforms struck by crushing cubes from above. He used no elegance at all. He grabbed the falling cubes, smashed them aside, punched through obstacles, and forced his way forward with brutal demonic strength.","Revona’s path was covered in invisible attacks, false exits, and void traps. Her Void Origin Eyes glowed continuously, and every attack that approached her faded into nothingness. She walked through the path as if the trial itself could not decide whether she truly existed within its rules.","Ervin’s path was the narrowest, filled with moving cube needles and spinning spear shadows. His black spear danced in silence, each strike landing with frightening perfection. Not a single movement was wasted, and not a single attack came close enough to touch his robe.","Max’s own path had no obvious enemies.","That made it the most dangerous.","The trial attacked him with blind spots, spatial distortions, hidden cube shifts, reversed directions, and invisible walls meant to confuse perception. But before his Dimensional Sovereign Body, there were no blind spots.","He saw through the false spaces, stepped only on real platforms, avoided the invisible walls, and reached the core node of the Genesis Gate just as the others arrived at their final platforms.","The cube constellation above them fired.","A combined beam descended toward all five at once.","Max raised his hand and struck the core node.","\"Now.\"","Tamara thrust her spear upward.","Varkhon punched into the sky.","Revona erased the beam line targeting her and weakened the connection between the remaining beams.","Ervin pierced the central point of the descending attack with one perfect spear strike.","Max activated the gate mechanism and used his Dimensional Sovereign Body to redirect the remaining spatial pressure away from the group.","The combined beam shattered.","The Genesis Gate opened.","White light flooded the labyrinth.","[Trial One Completed.]","[Labyrinth Core Stability: 79%]","[Teamwork Assessment: Excellent.]","[Individual Performance Assessment Completed.]","[Genesis Marks Distribution In Progress...]","The five figures appeared before the white cube gate as the shattered labyrinth froze behind them. For a moment, none of them spoke. They had not trusted one another completely, but they had still worked together well enough to clear the first trial without losing anyone.","More importantly, every one of them had shown why they were qualified to stand inside the Genesis Trial.","Max looked at the system prompt calmly.","The first trial had only been the beginning.","And there were still seventy Genesis Marks left to fight for."]},{"number":1794,"title":"Chapter 1794: Second Trial","paragraphs":["The white light from the Genesis Gate washed over the five participants, and for a brief moment, the shattered labyrinth behind them became completely still.","Max stood at the front, his Dimensional Sovereign Body slowly calming down as the endless layers of space, hidden mechanisms, and invisible attack routes withdrew from his perception. Revona stood quietly beside him, her Void Origin Eyes dimming slightly but not fully closing.","Tamara rested her spear against her shoulder, her war intent still rising and falling like the breathing of a battlefield. Varkhon cracked his knuckles, looking more excited than tired, while Ervin remained calm, his black spear lowered at his side as if everything that had happened had only been a warm-up.","Then the system prompt appeared before all of them.","[Trial One Completed.]","[Genesis Cube Labyrinth Cleared.]","[Labyrinth Core Stability: 79%]","[Teamwork Assessment: Excellent.]","[Survival Contribution Assessment: Completed.]","[Combat Performance Assessment: Completed.]","[Perception And Guidance Assessment: Completed.]","[Adaptability Assessment: Completed.]","[Genesis Marks Distribution Completed.]","A second prompt followed immediately.","[Max Morgan: 9 Genesis Marks]","[Ervin: 7 Genesis Marks]","[Revona: 6 Genesis Marks]","[Tamara: 5 Genesis Marks]","[Varkhon: 3 Genesis Marks]","[Total Genesis Marks Distributed In Trial One: 30/30]","The moment the distribution appeared, the cubic space became quiet.","Varkhon looked at the prompt, then let out a rough laugh. \"Only three? This trial really does not appreciate honest strength.\"","Tamara glanced at him and said bluntly, \"You smashed what you were told to smash. That was useful indeed but that was it. If you hadn’t been guided you would have been useless.\"","Varkhon snorted, though he did not look truly angry. \"You sound happy with your five.\"","Tamara smiled faintly. \"I did my part.\"","Revona looked toward Max. \"Nine marks. The highest.\"","Max glanced at the prompt without much surprise. \"The trial valued perception and guidance more than raw destruction.\"","Ervin’s eyes rested on Max for a moment, and the abyss-like calm in them deepened slightly. \"Without you seeing the route, the Labyrinth Core would have collapsed much faster. Nine marks are reasonable.\"","Max looked at Ervin. \"You pierced the main sequence several times without needing instructions. You also did a good job.\"","Ervin smiled faintly. \"I only pierced what I could see.\"","His tone was calm, but no one believed that was all there was to it. Among the five of them, Ervin had revealed the least, yet his performance had been terrifyingly stable.","His spear had not missed once. Every strike had landed where it needed to land, and his aura still felt as fathomless as when Max first noticed him. Even now, Max could not accurately measure his depth.","Before anyone could say more, the Genesis Gate in front of them opened completely.","The five were pulled through.","Their surroundings changed again.","The cubic labyrinth vanished, and they appeared inside a vast circular arena made of countless interlocking cubes. The arena floated above a dark void, but unlike the first trial, this place was not a simple path toward a gate.","It was divided into five outer regions and one central region. Each outer region had a different color: silver, black, crimson, blue, and gold. At the very center of the arena floated a massive transparent cube, and inside that cube were dozens of glowing marks shaped like small white flames.","Max’s eyes narrowed slightly.","Those were likely Genesis Marks.","But before anyone could move, the system prompt descended.","[Trial Two Initiated.]","[Trial Two: Genesis Core Dominion.]","[Trial Type: Cooperative And Competitive.]","[Maximum Genesis Marks Obtainable In Trial Two: 35]","[Objective: Obtain Genesis Flames From The Central Core And Preserve Them Until The End Of The Trial.]","[Rules: Genesis Flames Can Be Obtained By Breaking The Central Core Seals.]","[Rules: Central Core Seals Require Multiple Forms Of Power To Break Efficiently.]","[Rules: Participants May Cooperate To Break The Core Faster.]","[Rules: Participants May Also Steal Genesis Flames From One Another.]","[Rules: Trial Can Be Completed Alone Or As A Team.]","[Warning: The More Genesis Flames A Participant Holds, The More Trial Beasts Will Target Them.]","[Warning: If All Participants Fail To Hold At Least One Genesis Flame Before The Timer Ends, Trial Two Will Be Considered Failed.]","[Time Limit: 30 Minutes.]","The moment the prompts finished, a timer appeared in the sky above the arena.","[30:00]","The five participants immediately understood the cruelty of the second trial.","This was not like the first trial, where they only had to work together to reach a gate. This trial encouraged cooperation and betrayal at the same time. The central core held the Genesis Flames, but its seals required multiple forms of power to break efficiently. If they cooperated, they could obtain the flames faster.","But once the flames were obtained, each person could steal from the others. Even worse, the more flames someone held, the more trial beasts would target them. That meant being too greedy would turn the entire trial against them, while being too cautious might leave them with too few marks.","Tamara’s eyes sharpened. \"Interesting.\"","Varkhon laughed, his demonic aura rising. \"Now this is more like it.\"","Revona calmly studied the central cube. \"The seals are layered. They are not all the same.\"","Ervin looked at the arena beneath them. \"The outer regions are likely temporary territories. Holding one may give defensive advantages.\"","Max’s Dimensional Sovereign Body spread outward again, and the structure of the arena unfolded in his perception. He could see the central core clearly now. It had five seals wrapped around it, each seal corresponding to a different type of power.","One was spatial. One was destructive. One was perception-based. One was battle-force-based. One was origin-force-based. No single participant could break all five quickly unless they possessed several different abilities, but the five of them together could dismantle the seals much faster.","Max said calmly, \"The core has five seals. If we break them together, we can save time.\"","Varkhon grinned. \"And after that?\"","Tamara’s spear tapped against the ground. \"After that, everyone takes what they can keep.\"","Revona’s Void Origin Eyes glowed faintly. \"If we waste too much time fighting before opening the core, the trial beasts may become the real problem.\"","Ervin nodded. \"Then we cooperate first.\"","Max looked at the timer.","[29:34]","\"Agreed,\" he said. \"Break the core first. Compete after.\"","No one objected.","The five moved toward the center at the same time."]},{"number":1795,"title":"Chapter 1795: Core Seal Broken!","paragraphs":["The moment they entered the central region, the transparent cube reacted. Five rings appeared around it, and each ring began rotating in a different direction.","A deep humming sound filled the arena, and then the surrounding void trembled as dozens of cubic beasts emerged from below. Some looked like wolves made of black cubes. Some looked like birds with razor-edged wings. Others looked like armored giants with cube-shaped heads and glowing white cores in their chests.","[Genesis Guardians Awakened.]","[Core Seal Integrity: 100%]","Varkhon laughed and rushed forward first. \"I will handle the big ones.\"","A cube giant stepped toward him, raising both arms like falling pillars. Varkhon met it head-on, his fist crashing into the giant’s arm with raw demonic strength.","The cube arm shattered, and before the guardian could reform, Varkhon grabbed its head with both hands and smashed it into the ground. The impact shook the arena, but more guardians immediately rushed toward him.","Tamara moved to the other side, her spear sweeping in a wide arc. War intent erupted from her body, forming a faint battlefield domain around her. Every thrust of her spear struck with commanding power, pushing back several guardians at once.","Unlike Varkhon’s brutal destruction, Tamara fought like a general controlling the rhythm of war. She forced the beasts into certain paths, blocked their advance, and created openings for the others.","Revona stood near the central cube and raised her eyes.","A silver seal on the core brightened, releasing invisible pulses meant to disrupt the participants’ senses and confuse their energy flow.","Revona’s Void Origin Eyes flashed, and those pulses began to vanish before they could spread. Each time she looked at a weak point in the seal, the energy there turned faint, as if it was being erased from existence. The silver ring slowed down almost immediately.","Ervin stepped forward with his black spear.","The gold ring around the core released spear-like beams of Genesis energy, each one aimed at his vital points. Ervin moved through them with terrifying calm. His spear flickered once, twice, three times, and every strike pierced a tiny node on the rotating ring.","His spearmanship was so precise that he did not waste even the smallest movement. With each thrust, the gold ring’s rotation became unstable.","Max did not rush to attack immediately.","He looked through the core.","His Dimensional Sovereign Body allowed him to see how all five seals connected, and after a few breaths, he found the problem. If they broke the seals one by one, the remaining seals would strengthen. The trial wanted them to coordinate the timing. They had to weaken all five seals at once, then destroy them together.","Max’s voice spread across the central arena. \"Do not break your seals yet. Weaken them to the edge and wait for my signal.\"","Tamara thrust her spear through a guardian’s chest and shouted back, \"How long?\"","\"Fifteen seconds.\"","Varkhon smashed two guardians aside. \"Make it ten.\"","Max ignored him and placed his hand against the core barrier.","The black ring represented destructive power. The red ring represented origin pressure. The blue ring represented spatial structure.","Max could handle more than one, but he did not reveal everything at once. Seven-colored lightning gathered around his right hand, while his Dimensional Sovereign Body locked onto the spatial nodes within the blue ring.","The Divine King Punishment surged.","The black ring trembled.","At the same time, Max’s spatial perception pressed into the blue ring, identifying every hidden point that stabilized it. He did not need to tear space apart. He only needed to strike the correct places. His fingers moved like lightning, tapping several invisible nodes in succession, and the blue ring immediately slowed.","Revona glanced at him from the side.","\"He can handle two seals at once,\" she said softly.","Ervin’s spear paused for a fraction of a second before continuing. \"Maybe more.\"","The core hummed violently.","[Core Seal Integrity: 62%]","More guardians emerged.","This time, they did not attack randomly.","They targeted the person closest to breaking a seal.","Several winged cube beasts shot toward Revona, while two armored giants charged at Ervin. A massive black lion made of cubic plates appeared before Max, its white core burning with Genesis fire.","Tamara immediately moved to support Revona, her spear sweeping through the winged beasts before they could descend.","\"Keep working,\" Tamara said. \"I will cover you.\"","Revona did not look away from the seal. \"Thank you.\"","Varkhon rushed toward Ervin’s side, grabbing one of the armored giants by the waist and throwing it into the second.","\"Do not let your spear slow down, abyss boy,\" Varkhon laughed.","Ervin smiled faintly. \"My spear will never get slowed down.\"","His black spear pierced through both giants in the next instant, striking their cores through the gap Varkhon had created.","Max faced the black lion alone.","The beast leapt at him with terrifying speed, its claws tearing through the air. Max’s body shifted slightly, avoiding the first claw by a hair’s breadth, then he raised Dragonheart and cut through the lion’s front leg. The beast tried to reform, but Max’s seven-colored lightning struck its core and exploded from within.","The lion shattered.","[Core Seal Integrity: 41%]","\"Ready,\" Revona said.","\"Ready,\" Ervin followed.","Tamara stabbed her spear into the ground and used her war intent to hold back a wave of guardians. \"My side is clear.\"","Varkhon grinned. \"Say the word.\"","Max’s eyes narrowed.","The five rings around the core were all unstable now. Each one was trembling at the edge of collapse, but if they failed to destroy them at the same time, the core would repair itself and possibly summon stronger guardians.","Max lifted his hand.","\"Now.\"","Five powers struck at once.","Revona’s Void Origin Eyes erased the silver seal’s final connection.","Tamara’s spear carried war intent into the battle-force ring and shattered it from the front.","Varkhon punched the destructive-force ring with enough strength to crack the arena beneath him.","Ervin’s spear pierced the gold ring’s deepest node.","Max used his Dimensional Sovereign Body to collapse the spatial ring while Divine King Punishment destroyed the red origin-pressure ring.","The five seals broke together.","[Core Seal Integrity: 0%]","The transparent cube opened.","Dozens of white Genesis Flames shot out.","For a moment, everyone moved.","The cooperation ended almost instantly."]},{"number":1796,"title":"Chapter 1796: Stabilizing Genesis Flames!","paragraphs":["Varkhon laughed and grabbed three Genesis Flames with one hand, but the moment he did, six guardians turned toward him at once.","Tamara captured two flames with her spear aura, then spun around and blocked Varkhon from grabbing a fourth.","Varkhon grinned at her. \"Already competing?\"","Tamara answered with a spear thrust. \"You said you wanted this kind of trial.\"","Their attacks collided, and the shockwave scattered several nearby flames.","Revona did not rush greedily. Her Void Origin Eyes locked onto two flames drifting between several cube beasts, and she made the attacks around them vanish just long enough to step through and take them calmly.","Ervin moved like a shadow with his spear, piercing the air around three flames and pulling them toward himself through precise spear force.","Max’s Dimensional Sovereign Body saw every flame at once.","He knew which ones were bait, which ones would attract stronger guardians, and which ones were about to vanish into the arena floor. Instead of grabbing the nearest flames, he moved toward the far side of the core where five flames were drifting into a dangerous cube storm. He stepped through the shifting space, avoiding three hidden traps, and caught all five flames in one motion.","The system reacted immediately.","[Genesis Flame Count Increased.]","[Participant Max Morgan Has Obtained 5 Genesis Flames.]","[Guardian Aggression Toward Participant Max Morgan Increased.]","The arena trembled.","A larger guardian began forming above Max.","It looked like a knight made of white cubes, holding a massive sword of Genesis light. At the same time, two smaller guardians appeared behind him, while the cube storm in front of him turned into a rotating prison.","Tamara saw it and shouted, \"Taking five at once was greedy.\"","Max glanced at her. \"I can hold them.\"","The Genesis knight descended.","Max moved.","Dragonheart flashed, seven-colored lightning erupted, and his Dimensional Sovereign Body guided him through the rotating cube prison without taking a single hit. He did not destroy the knight immediately. Instead, he led it toward the area where several loose Genesis Flames were drifting near Varkhon and Tamara’s clash.","Varkhon noticed and cursed. \"Human, do not bring that thing here.\"","Max smiled faintly. \"This is also part of the trial.\"","The Genesis knight swung its sword.","Varkhon and Tamara were forced to stop fighting each other and block together.","Boom!","The giant sword crashed down, and the impact blasted both of them backward. Max used that instant to take one more Genesis Flame that had been floating between them.","Tamara’s eyes sharpened. \"Max.\"","Varkhon laughed angrily. \"Now I like this trial.\"","Revona watched all this and quietly moved to take another flame that everyone had ignored.","Ervin saw her move and smiled faintly, then pierced the ground with his spear. A hidden pulse pushed the flame slightly away from Revona and toward him. Revona’s Void Origin Eyes flashed, and the pulse vanished, allowing her to take the flame after all.","Ervin looked at her. \"Well done.\"","Revona replied calmly, \"You too.\"","The trial had become exactly what the system intended.","They cooperated when the guardians became too dangerous.","They competed when flames became available.","They blocked each other without fully trying to kill.","They stole opportunities without destroying the team structure entirely.","For several minutes, the arena became chaotic.","Max fought the Genesis knight while holding several flames, forcing him to display terrifying adaptability. His Dimensional Sovereign Body allowed him to avoid blind attacks, see through shifting cube traps, and choose the safest route while still stealing more flames whenever an opening appeared.","Tamara and Varkhon clashed several times over the same flames, but whenever too many guardians attacked, they fought back-to-back with surprising efficiency. Revona used her Void Origin Eyes to erase attacks, traps, and even the pull of several Genesis Flames when others tried to steal from her.","Ervin’s spear moved like an abyssal line through the battlefield, sometimes protecting the group, sometimes stealing flames, sometimes forcing guardians into the paths of others with subtle precision.","Then the timer reached the final five minutes.","[05:00]","[Genesis Flame Possession Will Now Stabilize Every 60 Seconds.]","[Stabilized Genesis Flames Cannot Be Stolen.]","The rule changed the entire battle.","Everyone immediately understood that the next few minutes mattered most. Flames held long enough would become safe, and that meant the competition would become more aggressive before each stabilization.","Varkhon grinned widely. \"Now this is fun.\"","Tamara’s war intent surged. \"Then hold what you can.\"","The guardians roared.","The Genesis knight turned toward Max again.","Revona’s Void Origin Eyes glowed deeper.","Ervin lifted his spear.","Max held the Genesis Flames around him and looked at the timer.","The moment the final five minutes began, the entire Genesis Core Dominion arena changed.","The cubic floor beneath them lit up with white patterns, and each participant’s Genesis Flames began circling their bodies like small burning stars. Max had the most flames around him, and because of that, the pressure on him became the heaviest.","The Genesis knight that had been chasing him suddenly grew larger, its white cube armor rearranging into thicker plates, while a second sword of Genesis light formed in its other hand.","At the same time, several smaller guardians turned toward Max, their glowing cores locking onto the flames surrounding him as if the trial itself had decided that his greed needed to be punished.","Tamara glanced toward him while sweeping her spear through two cube beasts. \"You really attracted half the arena.\"","Max avoided the Genesis knight’s first sword by shifting half a step to the side, then turned Dragonheart and blocked the second sword head-on. The collision sent a shockwave across the platform, but his body did not move back.","\"Only half?\" he said calmly. \"Then the trial is not that hard.\"","Varkhon laughed loudly from the other side of the battlefield. He was holding several Genesis Flames of his own, and a group of cubic wolves were tearing toward him from three directions.","Instead of dodging, he charged directly into them with his demonic markings blazing. His fist smashed the first wolf into pieces, his shoulder rammed through the second, and his hand grabbed the third by its cube-shaped neck before hurling it toward Tamara’s side.","Tamara’s eyes narrowed. \"Varkhon.\"","The demon grinned. \"Teamwork.\"","Tamara snorted coldly, but she still thrust her spear forward and destroyed the flying wolf before it could crash into her. However, the brief distraction gave Varkhon a chance to rush toward a drifting Genesis Flame nearby. He almost grabbed it, but before his fingers touched it, a thin black spear light pierced the air and knocked the flame away.","Ervin stood several platforms away, his spear lowered as if he had done nothing.","Varkhon turned toward him with a dangerous smile. \"You are annoying.\"","Ervin smiled faintly. \"You were too slow.\""]},{"number":1797,"title":"Chapter 1797: Five Minutes Timer!","paragraphs":["The flame that Ervin had knocked away drifted toward Revona’s side, but Revona did not reach for it immediately. Her Void Origin Eyes flashed, and an invisible cube trap around the flame vanished.","Only then did she stretch out her hand and take it calmly. The moment she obtained it, two guardians rushed toward her from the void below, but before they could reach her, she looked at them once. Their bodies became faint, then the attacks forming inside their cores disappeared into nothingness.","A breath later, Ervin’s spear pierced through both weakened cores from afar, destroying them before they could recover.","Revona looked at him. \"Thank you.\"","Ervin replied, \"You removed the dangerous part. I only finished the rest.\"","Even while competing, none of them fully ignored cooperation. That was the cruel balance of the trial. If they focused only on stealing from one another, the guardians would overwhelm them. If they focused only on helping one another, the marks would not be distributed in their favor.","Every movement had to carry two meanings, survival and advantage, defense and theft, assistance and calculation.","The timer continued falling.","[04:12]","The Genesis Flames around everyone trembled faintly, and the first stabilization was approaching.","Max had already understood the rhythm of the trial. The flames needed to be held for sixty seconds before becoming stable, but the closer the stabilization came, the more aggressive the guardians became.","The system was not giving them free rewards. It was forcing them to defend their gains under increasing pressure while tempting others to steal at the last moment.","The Genesis knight raised both swords.","The space around Max shifted.","Dozens of cube blades appeared from every side, and the knight itself vanished from his front, reappearing behind him through a sudden spatial shift. If it had been anyone else, that attack might have struck before they even sensed the danger.","But Max’s Dimensional Sovereign Body had no blind spot. He saw the spatial shift from the moment it began, saw the cube blades forming around him, and saw the hidden flame behind the knight that the trial had placed as bait.","Max moved.","His body slipped through the smallest gap between the cube blades, Dragonheart curved behind him without looking, and his sword edge met the knight’s twin swords with perfect timing. Sparks of Genesis light burst outward.","The knight’s attack was redirected to the side, and Max’s left hand reached through the gap between two shifting cubes, pulling the bait flame into his possession before the trap fully activated.","[Participant Max Morgan Has Obtained 1 Genesis Flame.]","[Guardian Aggression Toward Participant Max Morgan Increased.]","Varkhon looked over and laughed. \"You are insane. You are still taking more?\"","Max’s eyes remained calm as he kicked off the platform and moved away from the Genesis knight’s next strike. \"The trial placed it there.\"","Tamara shouted, \"It placed it there to kill you.\"","Max slashed apart three cube blades and replied, \"Then it should try harder.\"","The words made Varkhon laugh again, while even Tamara’s mouth twitched slightly. Revona only shook her head faintly, and Ervin’s smile deepened as if he found Max’s response interesting.","Then the first stabilization arrived.","[04:00]","[Genesis Flame Stabilization Initiated.]","White light descended on the arena.","Several flames around each participant changed color, becoming more solid and sinking into their trial marks. The unstable flames that had been circling them became divided into two types. The stabilized ones could no longer be stolen, while the unstable ones still remained vulnerable.","[Stabilized Genesis Flames Cannot Be Stolen.]","Max felt several of his flames become safe, but he did not relax. The moment stabilization ended, the trial released a new wave of guardians.","This time, the guardians were different.","Five Genesis knights appeared, one for each participant.","Each knight carried a weapon reflecting the person it targeted. The one facing Tamara held a cube spear. The one facing Varkhon had massive gauntlets. The one facing Revona had mirror-like eyes that seemed designed to resist erasure. The one facing Ervin held a long black-white spear. The one facing Max carried a sword, but its body was wrapped in faint spatial distortions.","[Personal Genesis Guardians Awakened.]","[Warning: Personal Guardians Will Adapt To Participant Combat Style.]","Tamara’s smile became fierce. \"Now this is better.\"","Her spear collided with the cube spear of her personal guardian, and the sound rang across the arena like two armies crashing together. The guardian’s spear arts were not weak. It copied the rhythm of Tamara’s war spear, using formation-like footwork and heavy battlefield pressure to match her advance.","Tamara’s eyes grew sharper, and her war intent surged as she began overpowering it through sheer dominance.","Varkhon’s guardian rushed at him with both gauntlets raised.","The demon met it with a punch.","The two fists collided, and the platform beneath them cracked. Varkhon’s grin turned savage as the guardian punched again and again, each strike growing heavier as it adapted to his raw strength. Instead of retreating, Varkhon became even more excited. His demonic markings burned brighter, and he started trading blows with the guardian like a beast enjoying a storm.","Revona’s guardian was the strangest.","It did not attack immediately. Its mirror-like eyes stared directly at her Void Origin Eyes, and the space between them became distorted as erasure and reflection fought in silence. Revona’s expression became more serious than before.","The guardian had been created to resist her, and each time she tried to erase part of its attack structure, the mirror-like surface reflected part of that power back toward her. She stepped back, adjusted her gaze, and began targeting the gaps between the reflection layers instead of the surface itself.","Ervin faced his spear guardian calmly.","For several breaths, neither moved.","Then both attacked at once.","Two spear lights crossed in the air, one black-silver and one white-black. Their movements were so fast and precise that even Tamara glanced over for a moment. Ervin’s spear was monstrous, but the guardian was learning with every exchange.","It copied his angles, mirrored his distance, and tried to predict his next point of attack. Ervin’s smile did not vanish. If anything, it became a little more genuine.","Max’s personal guardian attacked last.","Its sword cut through space.","The slash did not travel normally. It vanished halfway and appeared near Max’s neck. At the same time, the guardian’s body blurred, creating three false spatial positions around him. The trial had understood that ordinary attacks would not work against his perception, so it used spatial distortion, false position, and delayed sword cuts to interfere with his senses."]},{"number":1798,"title":"Chapter 1798: Outer Regions!","paragraphs":["Max’s Dimensional Sovereign Body expanded.","He saw the real sword.","He saw the false cuts.","He saw the delayed attack hidden beneath the platform.","He saw the guardian’s core shifting between its chest, head, and sword hilt.","\"No blind spots,\" Max said softly.","Dragonheart moved.","One slash destroyed the delayed attack beneath him.","The second blocked the sword near his neck.","The third pierced the false spatial body on his left and forced the real guardian to reveal itself.","The fourth struck the guardian’s sword hilt and cracked the hidden core inside.","The guardian staggered back.","Max stepped forward and kicked it in the chest, sending it flying into the Genesis knight that had been chasing him earlier. The two guardians collided, and before they could separate, Max raised his hand and sent a seven-colored lightning bolt through both of their bodies.","The lightning did not fully destroy them, but it disrupted their structure long enough for him to move toward two unstable flames drifting near the center.","Ervin saw Max going for them.","His spear flashed.","A thin spear force shot toward one of the flames, trying to pull it away.","Max’s left hand moved slightly, and space distorted around the flame, shifting it out of the spear force’s path.","Ervin’s eyes flickered.","Max caught the flame.","Revona’s Void Origin Eyes then targeted the second flame, erasing the guardian’s pull around it. But before she could take it, Tamara’s spear struck the ground, sending a wave of war intent that pushed the flame toward her side.","Varkhon appeared from the opposite direction and punched the platform, causing the flame to bounce upward. For a brief instant, all four of them competed for the same flame.","Then Max used his Dimensional Sovereign Body to step into the precise point where all their forces canceled each other.","He took the flame.","Four gazes turned toward him.","Max looked calm. \"Good teamwork.\"","Varkhon stared at him for a moment, then burst into laughter. \"You shameless human.\"","Tamara shook her head, though her war intent rose again. \"Do not think you can keep stealing like that.\"","Revona did not seem angry, but her Void Origin Eyes became deeper. \"Then we should stop creating openings for him.\"","Ervin smiled faintly. \"Agreed.\"","For the next minute, the competition grew sharper.","Tamara, Varkhon, Revona, and Ervin began subtly limiting Max’s opportunities, but they could not fully ignore the guardians either. Max, meanwhile, had to deal with the highest guardian aggression because he still held the most unstable flames.","The trial pressed him with increasing force, sending his personal guardian, the Genesis knight, and several smaller beasts against him at once. He moved through the attacks with terrifying precision, but even he had to admit that the trial was becoming troublesome.","The second stabilization approached.","[03:02]","The arena floor shifted again.","Several platforms began sinking into the void.","The central core released a pulse, and the remaining loose Genesis Flames scattered toward the five outer regions.","[Genesis Flame Scatter Initiated.]","[Outer Regions Activated.]","[Participants May Claim Outer Regions To Increase Stabilization Speed.]","The five colored outer regions lit up fully.","Max immediately understood the new rule. If someone controlled an outer region, the flames they held would stabilize faster, but staying in one region also made them easier to target. It was another balance of risk and reward.","Tamara was the first to move.","She flew toward the crimson region and planted her spear into the ground. War runes spread outward, and the region accepted her power.","[Participant Tamara Has Claimed Crimson War Region.]","[Stabilization Speed Increased.]","Varkhon laughed and charged into the black region.","[Participant Varkhon Has Claimed Black Destruction Region.]","Revona calmly stepped into the silver region.","[Participant Revona Has Claimed Silver Void Region.]","Ervin moved toward the blue region, his spear resting against his shoulder.","[Participant Ervin Has Claimed Blue Abyss Region.]","Max looked at the remaining gold region.","The Genesis knight and his personal guardian were between him and that region, while several smaller guardians moved to block the path. The trial had clearly made his route harder because he had the highest flame count.","Max smiled faintly.","His Vein of Speed came to life.","In the next instant, he disappeared.","The guardians attacked empty air.","Max appeared inside the gold region and placed his foot on the glowing cubic platform.","[Participant Max Morgan Has Claimed Gold Dominion Region.]","[Stabilization Speed Increased.]","The second stabilization began almost immediately.","[03:00]","White light descended once again, and several more flames became fixed into the participants’ marks. Max felt another portion of his flames stabilize, and the pressure around him finally lessened slightly. The others also secured part of their gains, but the remaining unstable flames still circled them, waiting for the final stage of the trial.","[Remaining Time: 03:00]","[Final Phase Initiated.]","[Rule Update: Participants May Invade Outer Regions.]","[Rule Update: Defeating A Personal Guardian Grants 1 Bonus Genesis Flame.]","[Rule Update: Final Genesis Flame Will Appear At 01:00.]","The moment the final phase began, the arena became even more dangerous.","Tamara looked toward Max’s region.","Varkhon looked toward Ervin’s.","Ervin looked toward the center.","Revona looked at all of them.","Max’s personal guardian slowly rose again, its cracked sword hilt glowing as the hidden core repaired itself.","Then the final battle of the second trial began.","Varkhon invaded Ervin’s Blue Abyss Region first.","The demon crossed three platforms in a single leap, his fist descending like a meteor toward Ervin’s head. Ervin did not retreat. His spear rose and met the fist at an angle, redirecting most of the force while the ground beneath him cracked apart.","The two clashed violently, raw demonic strength against abyssal spearmanship. Varkhon’s strikes were heavy enough to crush platforms, but Ervin’s spear always found the weakest point of each attack, turning aside what could be turned aside and piercing what could not.","Tamara did not invade immediately.","She focused on killing her personal guardian.","Her spear moved with brutal discipline, and her war intent formed the faint image of a battlefield behind her. The guardian copied her spear rhythm, but it could not copy her command. Tamara suddenly changed from direct combat to battlefield suppression, forcing the guardian into a corner of her crimson region where war runes had already gathered. Then she thrust her spear through its core.","[Participant Tamara Has Defeated Personal Guardian.]","[Bonus Genesis Flame Awarded.]","Revona used that moment to invade Varkhon’s black region while he was fighting Ervin.","Her Void Origin Eyes erased the defensive pull of his claimed region, allowing her to step inside without triggering the full penalty. She did not try to steal all his flames. She only reached for one unstable flame that had not yet stabilized.","But Varkhon sensed it and roared from Ervin’s region, punching across the distance. A wave of demonic strength tore toward Revona, but she looked at the weakest part of the force and erased enough of it to let the remaining impact pass around her.","She took the flame.","Varkhon laughed furiously. \"All of you are thieves.\"","Tamara replied from her region, \"You started with three stolen opportunities.\"","Max watched the movements of all four while facing his own personal guardian."]},{"number":1799,"title":"Chapter 1799: End of the Second Trial!","paragraphs":["The guardian had fully adapted to his earlier response. This time, its sword did not simply cut through space. It created multiple overlapping spaces, each one containing a different attack timing. For a normal cultivator, it would have been nearly impossible to identify which attack was real. For Max, it was only troublesome, not fatal.","His Dimensional Sovereign Body saw the entire structure.","He stepped through the first false space.","Cut the second.","Ignored the third.","Then thrust Dragonheart into the fourth, where the real core was hidden.","The guardian froze.","Max twisted the blade.","The core shattered.","[Participant Max Morgan Has Defeated Personal Guardian.]","[Bonus Genesis Flame Awarded.]","At the same time, Ervin’s spear pierced through his own personal guardian, which had tried to interfere in his battle with Varkhon.","[Participant Ervin Has Defeated Personal Guardian.]","[Bonus Genesis Flame Awarded.]","Varkhon saw two bonus flames appear and grinned wildly. \"Good. More to steal.\"","He abandoned Ervin for a moment and rushed toward Max’s Gold Dominion Region, clearly deciding that the person with the most flames was the best target. Tamara also moved at the same time, not directly attacking Max but heading toward the boundary between her region and his. Revona remained near the center, her eyes glowing as if calculating the final flame’s appearance.","Max stood inside the Gold Dominion Region, several stabilized flames already secured and several unstable flames still circling him.","Varkhon arrived like a meteor.","His fist came down with all his strength.","Max raised his left arm and blocked it.","Boom!","The Gold Dominion Region shook violently, and the cubic ground beneath Max’s feet cracked in a wide circle. Varkhon’s raw strength was terrifying. Even among demons, he was clearly a monster, and his body seemed to contain enough brute force to tear apart ordinary geniuses.","But Max’s golden-black dragon scales appeared faintly on his arm, and with the support of his physical foundation, he held the punch without being forced back.","Varkhon’s grin widened. \"Your body is strong too.\"","Max looked at him. \"Strong enough.\"","Tamara’s spear suddenly came from the side, aiming not at Max’s body but at one of the unstable flames circling him. Max’s Dimensional Sovereign Body detected it instantly. He tilted his body, shifted the flame with spatial pressure, and let Tamara’s spear pass between him and Varkhon.","Varkhon immediately tried to grab the shifted flame.","Max kicked his wrist aside.","Ervin’s spear light arrived from the distance and struck another unstable flame near Max, pushing it toward the center.","Revona appeared there first.","Her Void Origin Eyes erased the flame’s resistance, and she took it.","Max glanced toward her.","Revona said calmly, \"You were occupied.\"","Max smiled faintly. \"Fair.\"","The timer reached the final minute.","[01:00]","A brilliant white flame appeared above the central core.","It was larger than the others.","The moment it appeared, every participant felt its value.","[Final Genesis Flame Appeared.]","[Final Genesis Flame Value: 3 Genesis Marks.]","The entire arena stilled for a fraction of a breath.","Then all five moved.","Varkhon abandoned Max and charged toward the center.","Tamara flew from the crimson region with her spear surrounded by war intent.","Revona’s Void Origin Eyes locked onto the space around the final flame.","Ervin’s spear pointed straight at its core path.","Max activated his Vein of Speed.","All five reached the central area almost at the same time.","Varkhon punched first, trying to blast everyone away.","Tamara’s spear met his fist and diverted the force upward.","Ervin’s spear pierced through the gap between them, aiming to hook the flame away.","Revona erased the spear force’s pull for an instant.","Max appeared above them and reached down.","The final flame reacted by splitting into five shadows, only one of which was real.","Max’s Dimensional Sovereign Body saw through it immediately.","But so did Revona’s Void Origin Eyes.","And somehow, Ervin’s abyss-like gaze also seemed to find the real one.","Three hands, one spear force, and one void gaze converged on the true flame at once.","The trial core trembled.","The final flame could not choose a direction.","Then Tamara made an unexpected move.","Instead of competing for the flame, she stabbed her spear into the platform and released a burst of war intent that froze Varkhon’s movement for a split second. Varkhon roared, but that instant was enough to keep him from reaching the flame first.","Ervin smiled faintly.","His spear force wrapped around the flame.","Revona’s eyes erased part of that pull.","Max’s hand passed through the gap between both powers, and for a moment, he almost took the flame.","But the black-haired Ervin suddenly changed his spear angle.","The abyssal aura around him deepened.","Max felt that bottomless feeling again, and the flame sank slightly as if pulled toward an unseen depth.","Max’s eyes sharpened.","His Dimensional Sovereign Body twisted space around the flame.","Revona’s Void Origin Eyes flashed brighter.","The final flame trembled violently between three powers.","Then the timer reached the final ten seconds.","[00:10]","The trial suddenly released a shockwave.","Everyone was pushed back half a step.","The final flame shot upward.","Max moved first.","Ervin moved second.","Revona moved third.","Their powers collided in the air, and the final flame cracked into three smaller white flames under the pressure of their simultaneous capture.","[Final Genesis Flame Split Due To Equal Claim Conflict.]","[Value Distributed Among Valid Claimants.]","Each of the three obtained one fragment.","Max landed back in the Gold Dominion Region.","Revona appeared near the silver region.","Ervin lowered his spear with a faint smile.","Varkhon stared at the result, then burst into loud laughter. \"Even the trial could not decide.\"","Tamara pulled back her spear and exhaled. \"Better than letting one person take all three.\"","The timer reached zero.","[00:00]","[Trial Two Completed.]","[Genesis Core Dominion Cleared.]","[Team Cooperation Assessment: High.]","[Competitive Performance Assessment: Exceptional.]","[Survival Contribution Assessment: Completed.]","[Genesis Flame Stabilization Completed.]","[Genesis Marks Distribution In Progress...]","The arena stopped moving.","The guardians froze and dissolved into cube dust.","The outer regions dimmed one by one.","For a moment, the five stood in silence, each surrounded by the fading glow of the flames they had secured. None of them had truly trusted the others, and none of them had held back from competing, yet the trial had forced them into a strange balance where cooperation and conflict had both been necessary.","A new prompt appeared.","[Trial Two Results:]","[Max Morgan: 12 Genesis Marks]","[Ervin: 8 Genesis Marks]","[Revona: 7 Genesis Marks]","[Tamara: 5 Genesis Marks]","[Varkhon: 3 Genesis Marks]","[Total Genesis Marks Distributed In Trial Two: 35/35]","[Current Genesis Mark Totals:]","[Max Morgan: 21/100]","[Ervin: 15/100]","[Revona: 13/100]","[Tamara: 10/100]","[Varkhon: 6/100]","Varkhon looked at the totals and clicked his tongue. \"Again with three.\"","Tamara glanced at him. \"You spent half the trial trying to punch people instead of reading the rules.\"","Varkhon grinned. \"Punching people is how I read rules.\"","Revona looked at Max’s total calmly. \"You are far ahead.\"","Ervin also looked at the prompt, then at Max. \"For now.\"","Max did not respond immediately. His gaze moved from the system prompt to the cubic sky above them. The first two trials had already distributed sixty-five Genesis Marks, and there were only thirty-five left. That meant the third trial would decide the final ranking, and judging by the structure so far, it would likely be far more dangerous than the previous two.","As if confirming his thought, the arena beneath them began to sink into the void.","The central core broke apart.","The five participants were swallowed by white light once again.","[Preparing Final Trial.]","[Trial Three: Genesis Sovereign Descent.]","[Maximum Genesis Marks Obtainable In Trial Three: 35]","[Warning: Final Trial Will Determine Genesis Ranking.]","[Warning: Death Or Elimination In Final Trial Will Result In Loss Of Unstabilized Genesis Marks.]","[Warning: The Final Trial May Be Completed By One Participant, Multiple Participants, Or No Participants.]","The white light deepened.","Max’s eyes became sharper.","The third trial was coming."]},{"number":1800,"title":"Chapter 1800: Last Trial - 1","paragraphs":["Just at that moment, a while light descended upon them.","The white light swallowed the five participants completely.","For a moment, Max could not see the arena, the Genesis Core, the outer regions, or even the others beside him. Everything around him became pure whiteness, but unlike ordinary light, this whiteness did not feel warm or sacred. It felt empty. It felt unfinished.","It was the kind of light that existed before color, before form, before direction, and for a brief instant, Max felt as if he had been thrown back into the beginning of something vast and unknown.","Then the system prompt appeared.","[Final Trial Initiated.]","[Trial Three: Genesis Sovereign Descent.]","[Maximum Genesis Marks Obtainable In Trial Three: 35]","[Trial Type: Sovereign Assessment.]","[Objective: Climb The Genesis Sovereign Platform And Obtain Recognition From The Genesis Throne.]","[Rules: Participants May Cooperate, Compete, Or Eliminate One Another.]","[Rules: Genesis Marks Will Be Awarded According To Ascent Height, Combat Contribution, Willpower, Path Manifestation, And Throne Recognition.]","[Warning: The Genesis Sovereign Platform Will Continuously Suppress All Participants.]","[Warning: The Higher One Climbs, The Stronger The Suppression Becomes.]","[Warning: At The Final Stage, Only One Participant May Stand Before The Genesis Throne.]","[Trial Three Begins Now.]","The white light shattered.","Max appeared in a vast open space that looked nothing like the previous two trials.","There was no cubic room this time. There was no labyrinth and no circular arena. Instead, they stood at the base of an enormous platform rising into a starless sky. The platform was made of countless layered cubes, each layer wider than a city and higher than a mountain.","Every cube was engraved with ancient white-gold patterns, and the entire structure gave off a pressure that made the air feel heavy enough to crush weaker cultivators into the ground. At the very top of the platform, far beyond ordinary sight, a faint throne could be seen floating above everything, surrounded by a halo of colorless light.","The Genesis Throne.","Even before the system named it again, everyone understood that the throne was the true center of the final trial.","Max looked upward silently.","His Dimensional Sovereign Body spread through the space around him, but this time, his perception could not cover the whole structure. The Genesis Sovereign Platform seemed to resist being seen completely.","Whenever his senses climbed too high, the white-gold patterns on the cubes shifted and pushed his perception back down. It was not like the first trial, where he could read the labyrinth and guide everyone through hidden routes. Here, the trial was openly telling them one thing.","Climb.","Endure.","Prove yourself.","Beside him, Revona’s Void Origin Eyes glowed softly, but even she frowned slightly after looking toward the top. \"My eyes cannot see the throne clearly.\"","Tamara tightened her grip on her spear. \"So the final trial is a pressure ascent.\"","Varkhon grinned, but the grin was heavier than before. \"Good. No more chasing flames. No more strange rules. Just climb and crush whatever stands in the way.\"","Ervin stood quietly, black spear in hand, his fathomless aura still calm. His gaze remained fixed on the distant throne, and for the first time, Max felt a faint ripple in that bottomless presence, as if even Ervin was genuinely interested in what waited at the top.","Then another prompt appeared.","[Current Genesis Mark Totals:]","[Max Morgan: 21/100]","[Ervin: 15/100]","[Revona: 13/100]","[Tamara: 10/100]","[Varkhon: 6/100]","[Final Trial Genesis Marks Available: 35]","[Notice: Current Ranking Does Not Guarantee Final Ranking.]","[Notice: Genesis Throne Recognition May Alter Final Distribution.]","Varkhon looked at the prompt and laughed. \"So I still have a chance.\"","Tamara glanced at him. \"Only if you climb better than you read rules.\"","Varkhon’s grin widened. \"I understand climbing.\"","Revona remained calm. \"The final stage only allows one participant before the throne. That means cooperation will eventually end.\"","Ervin nodded faintly. \"But perhaps not at the beginning. A platform this large will not only suppress us. It will likely send guardians, illusions, path trials, and attacks based on our foundations.\"","Max looked at the steps rising ahead.","The first layer of the Genesis Sovereign Platform was already releasing a steady pressure, and they had not even begun climbing yet. His body could easily endure it, but the nature of the pressure was strange. It did not only weigh on flesh. It pressed against aura, bloodline, soul, will, comprehension, and even the Pseudo Cosmic Paths hidden within them.","Max said calmly, \"We climb first. Compete when we have to.\"","Tamara nodded. \"Agreed.\"","Revona said, \"Agreed.\"","Varkhon snorted. \"Fine. But if the trial says only one can reach the throne, do not blame me when I start punching.\"","Ervin smiled faintly. \"No one here expected otherwise.\"","With that, the five began moving.","The moment Max stepped onto the first layer of the Genesis Sovereign Platform, the pressure descended.","Boom!","The air around them sank violently.","Tamara’s war intent flared at once. Varkhon’s demonic markings glowed. Revona’s Void Origin Eyes deepened. Ervin’s abyss-like aura became sharper. Max’s golden-black scales did not appear yet, but the strength of his body stirred instinctively as the Genesis pressure tried to force him to lower his head.","Max did not slow down.","He took another step.","Then another.","The others moved with him.","At first, the ascent seemed simple. The pressure grew with each layer, but none of the five were ordinary. They climbed steadily, their footsteps echoing across the massive cube steps. The lower layers only tested basic endurance, and even Varkhon, who had the fewest Genesis Marks, moved with ease because his raw physical body was terrifyingly strong.","Tamara’s war intent surrounded her like an invisible army, making every step feel like a march into battle.","Revona used her Void Origin Eyes to erase part of the pressure pressing against her soul. Ervin walked as if the abyss beneath his aura swallowed the weight before it could truly affect him. Max relied on his body, his foundation, and the subtle support of his Dimensional Sovereign Body to sense which parts of the pressure were physical and which were conceptual.","After the tenth layer, the first obstacle appeared.","The cubes ahead shifted, and from the white-gold patterns carved into the platform, five figures emerged.","Each figure looked like one of the participants."]}]);
